window.TWG_L1C={"level":1,"exam":{"questions":30,"minutes":45,"pass":70,"written":false,"tasting":false,"trueFalse":true},"ch":{"p1":{"it":"L'uva, la vite e il clima","fr":"Le raisin, la vigne et le climat","en":"Grapes, vines and climate"},"p2":{"it":"Come si fa il vino","fr":"Comment on fait le vin","en":"How wine is made"},"w1":{"it":"Tipi e stili di vino","fr":"Types et styles de vins","en":"Types and styles of wine"},"w2":{"it":"I quattro bianchi principali","fr":"Les quatre grands blancs","en":"The four key white grapes"},"w3":{"it":"I quattro rossi principali","fr":"Les quatre grands rouges","en":"The four key black grapes"},"w4":{"it":"Vini famosi dai vitigni principali","fr":"Vins célèbres des grands cépages","en":"Famous wines from the key grapes"},"w5":{"it":"Altri vini da conoscere","fr":"Autres vins à connaître","en":"Other wines to know"},"t1":{"it":"Conservare e servire il vino","fr":"Conserver et servir le vin","en":"Storing and serving wine"},"t2":{"it":"Cibo e vino","fr":"Mets et vins","en":"Food and wine"},"t3":{"it":"Degustare: i primi passi","fr":"Déguster : premiers pas","en":"Tasting: first steps"}},"groups":[{"k":"p","w":6,"n":{"it":"Dalla vigna al vino","fr":"De la vigne au vin","en":"From vine to wine"},"c":["p1","p2"]},{"k":"w","w":18,"n":{"it":"Tipi, stili e vitigni","fr":"Types, styles et cépages","en":"Types, styles and grapes"},"c":["w1","w2","w3","w4","w5"]},{"k":"t","w":6,"n":{"it":"Conservare, servire, abbinare","fr":"Conserver, servir, accorder","en":"Store, serve, pair"},"c":["t1","t2","t3"]}],"bank":[{"id":"l1713c3a1","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale definizione descrive meglio il vino?","Quelle définition décrit le mieux le vin ?","Which definition best describes wine?"],"o":[["Succo d'uva fermentato","Du jus de raisin fermenté","Fermented grape juice"],["Succo d'uva distillato","Du jus de raisin distillé","Distilled grape juice"],["Succo d'uva concentrato","Du jus de raisin concentré","Concentrated grape juice"],["Succo d'uva pastorizzato","Du jus de raisin pasteurisé","Pasteurised grape juice"]],"e":["Il vino si ottiene facendo fermentare il succo dolce dell'uva.","Le vin s'obtient en faisant fermenter le jus sucré du raisin.","Wine is made by fermenting the sweet juice of grapes."],"d":["Per fare il vino si schiaccia l'uva per liberarne il succo dolce. Poi la fermentazione alcolica, grazie ai lieviti, trasforma lo zucchero di quel succo in alcol. Senza fermentazione resterebbe semplice succo d'uva; la distillazione o la concentrazione non fanno parte della definizione di base del vino.","Pour faire du vin, on écrase le raisin afin de libérer son jus sucré. Ensuite, la fermentation alcoolique, grâce aux levures, transforme le sucre de ce jus en alcool. Sans fermentation, il ne resterait qu'un jus de raisin ; la distillation ou la concentration ne font pas partie de la définition de base du vin.","To make wine, grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice. Alcoholic fermentation, carried out by yeast, then turns the sugar in that juice into alcohol. Without fermentation you would simply have grape juice; distilling or concentrating the juice is not part of the basic definition of wine."]},{"id":"l122a0219","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In quale parte dell'uva nera si trovano i tannini?","Dans quelle partie du raisin noir trouve-t-on les tanins ?","Which part of a black grape contains tannins?"],"o":[["Nella buccia","Dans la peau","The skin"],["Nella polpa","Dans la pulpe","The pulp"],["Nel succo","Dans le jus","The juice"],["Nel fiore","Dans la fleur","The flower"]],"e":["La buccia delle uve nere contiene sia il colore sia i tannini.","La peau des raisins noirs contient à la fois la couleur et les tanins.","Black grape skins hold both the colour and the tannins."],"d":["La buccia è la parte che distingue davvero le uve nere da quelle bianche: è intensamente colorata e contiene tannini, che lasciano in bocca una sensazione di secchezza. La polpa invece contiene il succo, fatto di acqua, zucchero e acido, ed è dello stesso colore in tutte le uve.","La peau est ce qui distingue vraiment les raisins noirs des blancs : elle est très colorée et contient des tanins, qui donnent une sensation de sécheresse en bouche. La pulpe, elle, contient le jus, fait d'eau, de sucre et d'acide, et elle a la même couleur dans tous les raisins.","The skin is what really sets black grapes apart from white ones: it is deeply coloured and contains tannins, which leave the mouth feeling dry. The pulp, by contrast, holds the juice, made of water, sugar and acid, and it is the same colour in all grapes."]},{"id":"l168e9f05","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Da che cosa è composto principalmente il succo della polpa?","De quoi est principalement composé le jus de la pulpe ?","What is the juice in the pulp mainly made of?"],"o":[["Acqua, zucchero e acido","Eau, sucre et acide","Water, sugar and acid"],["Acqua, tannini e colore","Eau, tanins et couleur","Water, tannin and colour"],["Alcol, zucchero e lievito","Alcool, sucre et levures","Alcohol, sugar and yeast"],["Acqua, alcol e anidride carbonica","Eau, alcool et gaz carbonique","Water, alcohol and carbon dioxide"]],"e":["Il succo d'uva è soprattutto acqua, zucchero e acido.","Le jus de raisin est surtout composé d'eau, de sucre et d'acide.","Grape juice is mostly water, sugar and acid."],"d":["La polpa è la parte morbida dell'acino e contiene il succo, formato in gran parte da acqua, zucchero e acido. Tannini e colore stanno invece nella buccia. Alcol e anidride carbonica compaiono solo più tardi, quando i lieviti fermentano lo zucchero del succo.","La pulpe est la partie tendre du grain et contient le jus, composé en grande partie d'eau, de sucre et d'acide. Les tanins et la couleur se trouvent dans la peau. L'alcool et le gaz carbonique n'apparaissent que plus tard, quand les levures font fermenter le sucre du jus.","The pulp is the soft part of the grape and holds the juice, which is mostly water, sugar and acid. Tannin and colour are found in the skin instead. Alcohol and carbon dioxide only appear later, when yeast ferments the sugar in the juice."]},{"id":"l11f3fcad","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Che sensazione lasciano in bocca i tannini?","Quelle sensation les tanins laissent-ils en bouche ?","What do tannins do to your mouth?"],"o":[["La fanno sentire secca","Ils l'assèchent","Make it feel dry"],["La fanno salivare","Ils la font saliver","Make it water"],["La fanno sentire calda","Ils la réchauffent","Make it feel hot"],["La fanno sentire dolce","Ils l'adoucissent","Make it feel sweet"]],"e":["I tannini della buccia danno una sensazione di secchezza in bocca.","Les tanins de la peau donnent une sensation de sécheresse en bouche.","Tannins from the skins leave the mouth feeling dry."],"d":["I tannini provengono dalla buccia delle uve nere e si percepiscono più come una sensazione che come un sapore: asciugano la bocca. Non vanno confusi con l'acidità, che invece fa salivare: sono due sensazioni opposte, da imparare a distinguere in degustazione.","Les tanins viennent de la peau des raisins noirs et se perçoivent davantage comme une sensation que comme un goût : ils assèchent la bouche. Il ne faut pas les confondre avec l'acidité, qui fait saliver : ce sont deux sensations opposées, à apprendre à distinguer en dégustation.","Tannins come from black grape skins and are felt more than tasted: they dry out the mouth. When tasting, they should not be confused with acidity, which makes your mouth water instead; these are two opposite sensations worth learning to tell apart."]},{"id":"l1bbb6c87","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Che colore ha la polpa di un'uva nera?","Quelle est la couleur de la pulpe d'un raisin noir ?","What colour is the pulp of a black grape?"],"o":[["Lo stesso di quella di un'uva bianca","La même que celle d'un raisin blanc","The same as in a white grape"],["Rosso intenso, come la buccia","Rouge intense, comme la peau","Deep red, like the skin"],["Viola, ma solo a piena maturità","Violette, mais seulement à maturité","Purple, but only when fully ripe"],["Rosa, più chiara della buccia","Rose, plus claire que la peau","Pink, paler than the skin"]],"e":["La polpa ha lo stesso colore in tutte le uve; il colore sta nella buccia.","La pulpe a la même couleur dans tous les raisins ; la couleur est dans la peau.","Pulp is the same colour in all grapes; the colour is in the skin."],"d":["All'interno uve bianche e nere si somigliano molto: la polpa ha lo stesso colore, qualunque sia il colore della buccia. È proprio per questo che il colore di un vino rosso viene dalle bucce, e che da uve nere si può persino ottenere un vino bianco separando subito il succo dalle bucce.","À l'intérieur, raisins blancs et noirs se ressemblent beaucoup : la pulpe a la même couleur, quelle que soit celle de la peau. C'est pour cela que la couleur d'un vin rouge vient des peaux, et qu'on peut même faire un vin blanc avec des raisins noirs en séparant tout de suite le jus des peaux.","Inside, white and black grapes look very alike: the pulp is the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. This is exactly why a red wine gets its colour from the skins, and why a white wine can even be made from black grapes if the juice is separated from the skins straight away."]},{"id":"l1bbb5fa6","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In quale stagione fiorisce la vite?","À quelle saison la vigne fleurit-elle ?","In which season does the grape vine flower?"],"o":[["In primavera","Au printemps","Spring"],["In estate","En été","Summer"],["In autunno","En automne","Autumn"],["In inverno","En hiver","Winter"]],"e":["La vite fiorisce in primavera; l'uva matura poi in estate.","La vigne fleurit au printemps ; le raisin mûrit ensuite en été.","Vines flower in spring; the grapes then ripen in summer."],"d":["Il ciclo annuale della vite segue le stagioni. In primavera compaiono i grappoli di fiori, ciascuno dei quali diventerà un acino. In estate l'uva matura e verso la fine dell'estate si vendemmia. In inverno, invece, la vite riposa, e ha bisogno di un freddo sufficiente per farlo.","Le cycle annuel de la vigne suit les saisons. Au printemps apparaissent les grappes de fleurs, dont chacune deviendra un grain. En été, le raisin mûrit, et vers la fin de l'été on vendange. En hiver, en revanche, la vigne se repose, et elle a besoin d'un froid suffisant pour cela.","The vine's yearly cycle follows the seasons. In spring the clusters of flowers appear, and each flower will become a grape. During summer the grapes ripen, and they are picked towards the end of summer. In winter the vine rests, and it needs enough cold to do so."]},{"id":"l13597bf0","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa diventa ogni fiore della vite?","Que devient chaque fleur de la vigne ?","What does each individual vine flower become?"],"o":[["Un acino d'uva","Un grain de raisin","One grape"],["Un nuovo germoglio","Une nouvelle pousse","A new shoot"],["Un'intera foglia","Une feuille entière","A whole leaf"],["Un grappolo intero","Une grappe entière","A whole bunch"]],"e":["Dopo la fioritura ogni singolo fiore si trasforma in un piccolo acino.","Après la floraison, chaque fleur se transforme en un petit grain.","After flowering, each single flower turns into a small grape."],"d":["I fiori della vite si presentano a grappoli formati da tanti fiori piccolissimi. Dopo la fioritura ognuno di essi diventa un acino: il grappolo di fiori diventa quindi un grappolo d'uva. All'inizio questi acini sono piccoli, duri e verdi, e solo durante l'estate cresceranno e matureranno.","Les fleurs de vigne forment des grappes composées de nombreuses fleurs minuscules. Après la floraison, chacune devient un grain : la grappe de fleurs devient donc une grappe de raisin. Au début, ces grains sont petits, durs et verts ; ils ne grossiront et ne mûriront qu'au cours de l'été.","Vine flowers come in clusters made up of many tiny flowers. After flowering, each one becomes a grape, so the cluster of flowers turns into a bunch of grapes. At first these grapes are small, hard and green; they only grow and ripen as the summer goes on."]},{"id":"l13008e68","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Come sono gli acini subito dopo la fioritura?","Comment sont les grains juste après la floraison ?","What are grapes like just after flowering?"],"o":[["Piccoli, duri e verdi","Petits, durs et verts","Small, hard and green"],["Piccoli, morbidi e dorati","Petits, mous et dorés","Small, soft and golden"],["Grossi, duri e viola","Gros, durs et violets","Large, hard and purple"],["Grossi, morbidi e dolci","Gros, mous et sucrés","Large, soft and sweet"]],"e":["Tutti gli acini giovani sono piccoli, duri e verdi, bianchi o neri che siano.","Tous les jeunes grains sont petits, durs et verts, blancs ou noirs.","All young grapes are small, hard and green, white or black."],"d":["Appena formati, gli acini non sono ancora pronti: sono piccoli, duri e verdi, e in questa fase uve bianche e nere non si distinguono. Solo con la maturazione estiva si gonfiano d'acqua, diventano più dolci e cambiano colore, verso il dorato per le bianche e verso il viola per le nere.","Juste formés, les grains ne sont pas encore prêts : ils sont petits, durs et verts, et à ce stade on ne distingue pas les raisins blancs des noirs. Ce n'est qu'avec la maturation estivale qu'ils gonflent d'eau, deviennent plus sucrés et changent de couleur, vers le doré pour les blancs et vers le violet pour les noirs.","Newly formed grapes are not ready yet: they are small, hard and green, and at this stage white and black grapes look the same. Only during summer ripening do they swell with water, become sweeter and change colour, towards golden for white grapes and purple for black ones."]},{"id":"l12811d78","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Durante la maturazione, che cosa succede ai livelli di zucchero e di acido nell'uva?","Pendant la maturation, que deviennent les niveaux de sucre et d'acide du raisin ?","As grapes ripen, what happens to their sugar and acid levels?"],"o":[["Lo zucchero sale e l'acido scende","Le sucre augmente et l'acide diminue","Sugar rises and acid falls"],["Lo zucchero scende e l'acido sale","Le sucre diminue et l'acide augmente","Sugar falls and acid rises"],["Salgono entrambi allo stesso ritmo","Les deux augmentent au même rythme","Both rise at the same rate"],["Restano entrambi invariati","Les deux restent stables","Both stay the same"]],"e":["Maturando l'uva diventa più dolce e meno acida.","En mûrissant, le raisin devient plus sucré et moins acide.","Ripening makes grapes sweeter and less acidic."],"d":["Mentre l'uva matura in estate avvengono diversi cambiamenti: gli acini si gonfiano d'acqua, lo zucchero aumenta, l'acido diminuisce e i sapori diventano più maturi. È questo equilibrio tra zucchero e acido che, più tardi, influenzerà l'alcol e la freschezza del vino.","Pendant que le raisin mûrit en été, plusieurs changements se produisent : les grains gonflent d'eau, le sucre augmente, l'acide diminue et les saveurs deviennent plus mûres. C'est cet équilibre entre sucre et acide qui influencera plus tard l'alcool et la fraîcheur du vin.","While grapes ripen over the summer, several things change: they swell with water, sugar goes up, acid goes down and the flavours become riper. This balance between sugar and acid will later influence the alcohol and freshness of the wine."]},{"id":"l1bb25208","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Di che colore diventano le uve bianche quando maturano?","Quelle couleur prennent les raisins blancs en mûrissant ?","What colour do white grapes turn as they ripen?"],"o":[["Dal verde al dorato","Du vert au doré","From green to golden"],["Dal verde al viola","Du vert au violet","From green to purple"],["Dal giallo al verde","Du jaune au vert","From yellow to green"],["Dal dorato al rosa","Du doré au rose","From golden to pink"]],"e":["Le uve bianche passano dal verde al dorato; le nere dal verde al viola.","Les raisins blancs passent du vert au doré ; les noirs du vert au violet.","White grapes go from green to golden; black ones from green to purple."],"d":["All'inizio tutti gli acini sono verdi. Con la maturazione la buccia cambia colore: nelle uve bianche diventa dorata, nelle uve nere diventa viola. Il cambiamento di colore accompagna gli altri segni della maturazione, cioè più acqua, più zucchero, meno acido e sapori più maturi.","Au départ, tous les grains sont verts. Avec la maturation, la peau change de couleur : elle devient dorée chez les raisins blancs et violette chez les raisins noirs. Ce changement accompagne les autres signes de maturation : plus d'eau, plus de sucre, moins d'acide et des saveurs plus mûres.","At first all grapes are green. As they ripen, the skin changes colour: it becomes golden in white grapes and purple in black grapes. This colour change goes hand in hand with the other signs of ripening, namely more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours."]},{"id":"l1c26259b","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi cambiamenti NON avviene quando l'uva matura?","Lequel de ces changements ne se produit PAS quand le raisin mûrit ?","Which of these does NOT happen as grapes ripen?"],"o":[["L'acidità aumenta","L'acidité augmente","Acidity increases"],["Gli acini si gonfiano d'acqua","Les grains gonflent d'eau","Grapes swell with water"],["Lo zucchero aumenta","Le sucre augmente","Sugar increases"],["I sapori diventano più maturi","Les saveurs deviennent plus mûres","Flavours become riper"]],"e":["Con la maturazione l'acidità scende, non sale.","En mûrissant, l'acidité baisse, elle n'augmente pas.","During ripening acidity falls, it does not rise."],"d":["La maturazione porta più acqua negli acini, più zucchero e sapori più maturi, ma l'acido segue la direzione opposta e diminuisce. Per questo un'uva acerba è aspra, mentre un'uva matura è dolce e meno acida. Ricordare questa tendenza aiuta anche a capire l'effetto del clima.","La maturation apporte plus d'eau dans les grains, plus de sucre et des saveurs plus mûres, mais l'acide suit le chemin inverse et diminue. C'est pourquoi un raisin vert est acide, tandis qu'un raisin mûr est sucré et moins acide. Retenir cette tendance aide aussi à comprendre l'effet du climat.","Ripening brings more water into the grapes, more sugar and riper flavours, but acid moves the other way and drops. That is why an unripe grape tastes sour, while a ripe one is sweet and less acidic. Remembering this trend also helps you understand the effect of climate."]},{"id":"l15a7a1c1","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quando si vendemmia di solito, secondo il ciclo della vite?","Quand vendange-t-on habituellement, selon le cycle de la vigne ?","In the vine's yearly cycle, when are the grapes usually picked?"],"o":[["Verso la fine dell'estate","Vers la fin de l'été","In late summer"],["All'inizio della primavera","Au début du printemps","In early spring"],["In pieno inverno","En plein hiver","In midwinter"],["Subito dopo la fioritura","Juste après la floraison","Just after flowering"]],"e":["L'uva matura durante l'estate e si raccoglie verso la fine dell'estate.","Le raisin mûrit pendant l'été et se récolte vers la fin de l'été.","Grapes ripen through summer and are picked in late summer."],"d":["La vite fiorisce in primavera, i fiori diventano acini e questi maturano durante l'estate. Quando sono abbastanza maturi, verso la fine dell'estate, si raccolgono. Subito dopo la fioritura gli acini sono ancora piccoli, duri e verdi, quindi troppo acerbi per fare vino.","La vigne fleurit au printemps, les fleurs deviennent des grains, et ceux-ci mûrissent pendant l'été. Lorsqu'ils sont assez mûrs, vers la fin de l'été, on les récolte. Juste après la floraison, les grains sont encore petits, durs et verts, donc beaucoup trop peu mûrs pour faire du vin.","The vine flowers in spring, the flowers become grapes and these ripen during the summer. Once they are ripe enough, towards the end of summer, they are picked. Just after flowering the grapes are still small, hard and green, far too unripe to make wine."]},{"id":"l1b4557c0","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché la vite cresce meglio dove l'inverno è freddo?","Pourquoi la vigne pousse-t-elle mieux là où l'hiver est froid ?","Why do vines grow best where winters are cold?"],"o":[["Perché il freddo le permette di riposare","Parce que le froid lui permet de se reposer","The cold lets the vine rest"],["Perché il freddo aumenta lo zucchero","Parce que le froid augmente le sucre","The cold raises sugar levels"],["Perché il freddo fa fiorire la vite","Parce que le froid fait fleurir la vigne","The cold makes the vine flower"],["Perché il freddo colora le bucce","Parce que le froid colore les peaux","The cold colours the skins"]],"e":["Un inverno abbastanza freddo dà alla vite un periodo di riposo.","Un hiver assez froid offre à la vigne une période de repos.","A cold enough winter gives the vine a period of rest."],"d":["Oltre alla giusta quantità di sole e calore durante la stagione di crescita, la vite ha bisogno di un inverno abbastanza freddo da poter riposare. Per questo la maggior parte dei vigneti si trova in fasce di latitudine precise, né troppo fredde né troppo calde.","En plus de la bonne dose de soleil et de chaleur pendant la saison de croissance, la vigne a besoin d'un hiver assez froid pour pouvoir se reposer. C'est pourquoi la plupart des vignobles se trouvent dans des bandes de latitude précises, ni trop froides ni trop chaudes.","Besides the right amount of sunlight and heat during the growing season, a vine needs a winter cold enough to let it rest. This is why most vineyards are found in particular bands of latitude, neither too cold nor too hot."]},{"id":"l10de113c","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi Paesi è un esempio di clima fresco per la vite?","Lequel de ces pays est un exemple de climat frais pour la vigne ?","Which of these is an example of a cool climate wine region?"],"o":[["La Germania","L'Allemagne","Germany"],["Alcune zone dell'Australia","Certaines zones d'Australie","Parts of Australia"],["Alcune zone della California","Certaines zones de Californie","Parts of California"],["Le zone sull'Equatore","Les zones sur l'équateur","Areas on the Equator"]],"e":["La Germania, come il nord della Francia, è vicina ai poli e ha un clima fresco.","L'Allemagne, comme le nord de la France, est proche des pôles et a un climat frais.","Germany, like northern France, lies nearer the poles and has a cool climate."],"d":["Le regioni a clima fresco sono quelle più vicine ai poli, come la Germania e il nord della Francia. Alcune parti dell'Australia e della California sono invece esempi di clima caldo. Vicino all'Equatore fa troppo caldo perché la vite cresca bene e possa riposare in inverno.","Les régions de climat frais sont les plus proches des pôles, comme l'Allemagne et le nord de la France. Certaines parties de l'Australie et de la Californie sont au contraire des exemples de climat chaud. Près de l'équateur, il fait trop chaud pour que la vigne pousse bien et se repose en hiver.","Cool climate regions are those closer to the poles, such as Germany and northern France. Parts of Australia and California are examples of warm climates instead. Right at the Equator it is too hot for vines to grow well and rest in winter."]},{"id":"l1535aca1","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale tipo di uva si coltiva più spesso nelle regioni a clima caldo?","Quel type de raisin cultive-t-on le plus souvent dans les régions chaudes ?","Which type of grape is commonly grown in warm climate regions?"],"o":[["Le uve nere","Les raisins noirs","Black grapes"],["Le uve bianche","Les raisins blancs","White grapes"],["Le uve acerbe","Les raisins verts","Unripe grapes"],["Le uve senza buccia","Les raisins sans peau","Skinless grapes"]],"e":["Nei climi caldi l'uva matura con regolarità ed è comune coltivare uve nere.","En climat chaud, le raisin mûrit régulièrement et on cultive souvent des raisins noirs.","Warm climates ripen grapes reliably, and black grapes are commonly grown."],"d":["Le regioni calde, più vicine all'Equatore, hanno temperature medie alte e un sole più intenso, quindi l'uva matura con regolarità. In queste zone è comune coltivare uve nere. Nelle regioni fresche, dove l'uva a volte fatica a maturare, è invece frequente coltivare uve bianche.","Les régions chaudes, plus proches de l'équateur, ont des températures moyennes élevées et un soleil plus intense ; le raisin y mûrit donc régulièrement. On y cultive souvent des raisins noirs. Dans les régions fraîches, où le raisin peine parfois à mûrir, on cultive plutôt des raisins blancs.","Warm regions, closer to the Equator, have high average temperatures and more intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably. Growing black grapes is common there. In cool regions, closer to the poles, where grapes sometimes struggle to ripen at all, white grapes are more commonly grown."]},{"id":"l1c999a0b","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In un clima fresco, come saranno di solito le uve?","En climat frais, comment seront généralement les raisins ?","In a cool climate, grapes will usually have…"],"o":[["Meno zucchero e più acidità","Moins de sucre et plus d'acidité","Less sugar and more acidity"],["Più zucchero e meno acidità","Plus de sucre et moins d'acidité","More sugar and less acidity"],["Più zucchero e più acidità","Plus de sucre et plus d'acidité","More sugar and more acidity"],["Meno zucchero e meno acidità","Moins de sucre et moins d'acidité","Less sugar and less acidity"]],"e":["Più fa fresco, più l'uva resta acida e meno zucchero accumula.","Plus il fait frais, plus le raisin reste acide et moins il accumule de sucre.","The cooler it is, the more acidic and less sugary the grapes stay."],"d":["Con poco calore e un sole più debole, l'uva matura meno: accumula meno zucchero e conserva più acidità. Il risultato nel bicchiere sono vini tendenzialmente più leggeri e freschi. In un clima caldo succede il contrario: più zucchero, meno acidità e sapori più maturi.","Avec peu de chaleur et un soleil plus faible, le raisin mûrit moins : il accumule moins de sucre et garde plus d'acidité. Dans le verre, cela donne des vins plutôt légers et frais. En climat chaud, c'est l'inverse : plus de sucre, moins d'acidité et des saveurs plus mûres.","With little heat and weaker sunshine, grapes ripen less: they build up less sugar and keep more acidity. In the glass this tends to give lighter, fresher wines. In a warm climate the opposite happens: more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours."]},{"id":"l115b6166","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché un vino da clima caldo tende ad avere sapori di frutta più maturi?","Pourquoi un vin de climat chaud a-t-il en général des saveurs de fruits plus mûres ?","Why does a warm-climate wine tend to show riper fruit flavours?"],"o":[["Il calore fa maturare di più l'uva","La chaleur fait davantage mûrir le raisin","Heat ripens the grapes further"],["Il calore aumenta l'acidità dell'uva","La chaleur augmente l'acidité du raisin","Heat raises the grapes' acidity"],["Il calore toglie colore alle bucce","La chaleur enlève la couleur des peaux","Heat removes colour from the skins"],["Il calore ferma la fioritura","La chaleur arrête la floraison","Heat stops the vine flowering"]],"e":["Con più calore e sole l'uva matura di più: più zucchero, sapori più maturi.","Avec plus de chaleur et de soleil, le raisin mûrit davantage : plus de sucre, saveurs plus mûres.","More heat and sun ripen grapes further: more sugar, riper flavours."],"d":["Nelle regioni calde le temperature medie sono alte e il sole è intenso, quindi l'uva matura con regolarità e a fondo. Questo porta più zucchero, meno acidità e sapori più maturi. Lo Chardonnay, per esempio, passa dai profumi di mela e limone in clima fresco a pesca e ananas in clima caldo.","Dans les régions chaudes, les températures moyennes sont élevées et le soleil est intense ; le raisin mûrit donc régulièrement et pleinement. Cela donne plus de sucre, moins d'acidité et des saveurs plus mûres. Le Chardonnay, par exemple, passe de la pomme et du citron en climat frais à la pêche et à l'ananas en climat chaud.","In warm regions average temperatures are high and the sunshine is intense, so grapes ripen fully and reliably. This brings more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours. Chardonnay, for example, moves from apple and lemon aromas in a cool climate to peach and pineapple in a warm one."]},{"id":"l1025d685","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Uno Chardonnay con profumi di mela e limone viene probabilmente da…","Un Chardonnay aux arômes de pomme et de citron vient probablement…","A Chardonnay with apple and lemon aromas most likely comes from…"],"o":[["Un clima fresco","D'un climat frais","A cool climate"],["Un clima caldo","D'un climat chaud","A warm climate"],["Un clima tropicale","D'un climat tropical","A tropical climate"],["Un clima molto secco","D'un climat très sec","A very dry climate"]],"e":["Frutta verde e agrumi indicano uva meno matura, tipica del clima fresco.","Fruits verts et agrumes signalent un raisin moins mûr, typique du climat frais.","Green fruit and citrus point to less ripe, cool-climate grapes."],"d":["Il clima cambia il tipo di frutta che si sente nel vino. In clima fresco lo Chardonnay dà frutta verde come la mela e agrumi come il limone. In clima caldo, con uva più matura, mostra frutta a nocciolo come la pesca e frutta tropicale come l'ananas.","Le climat change le type de fruits que l'on perçoit dans le vin. En climat frais, le Chardonnay donne des fruits verts comme la pomme et des agrumes comme le citron. En climat chaud, avec un raisin plus mûr, il montre des fruits à noyau comme la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas.","Climate changes the type of fruit you find in a wine. In a cool climate Chardonnay gives green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. In a warm climate, with riper grapes, it shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple."]},{"id":"l19fd4d7a","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché nelle regioni a clima fresco l'uva, in certe annate, fatica a maturare?","Pourquoi, dans les régions fraîches, le raisin a-t-il parfois du mal à mûrir ?","Why can grapes in cool regions struggle to ripen in some years?"],"o":[["Temperature basse e sole più debole","Températures basses et soleil plus faible","Low temperatures and weaker sunlight"],["Temperature alte e sole più intenso","Températures élevées et soleil plus intense","High temperatures and stronger sunlight"],["Inverni troppo miti per riposare","Hivers trop doux pour se reposer","Winters too mild for the vine to rest"],["Viti troppo giovani per fiorire","Vignes trop jeunes pour fleurir","Vines too young to flower"]],"e":["Poco calore e luce più debole rallentano la maturazione dell'uva.","Peu de chaleur et une lumière plus faible ralentissent la maturation du raisin.","Little heat and weaker light slow down ripening."],"d":["Le regioni fresche sono più vicine ai poli: le temperature medie sono basse e la luce del sole può essere meno intensa che vicino all'Equatore. In annate particolarmente fresche l'uva può non maturare del tutto. Per questo in queste zone si coltivano spesso uve bianche.","Les régions fraîches sont plus proches des pôles : les températures moyennes y sont basses et la lumière du soleil peut être moins intense que près de l'équateur. Les années particulièrement fraîches, le raisin peut ne pas mûrir complètement. C'est pourquoi on y cultive souvent des raisins blancs.","Cool regions lie closer to the poles: average temperatures are low and the sunlight can be less intense than near the Equator. In especially cool years the grapes may not ripen fully. This is one reason white grapes are commonly grown there."]},{"id":"l1ecdb47c","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Dopo l'impianto, quanto tempo serve in genere perché una vite dia un raccolto ogni anno?","Après la plantation, combien de temps faut-il en général pour qu'une vigne donne une récolte chaque année ?","After planting, how long does a vine usually take before it gives a crop every year?"],"o":[["Un paio d'anni","Environ deux ans","A couple of years"],["Pochi mesi","Quelques mois","A few months"],["Circa vent'anni","Environ vingt ans","About twenty years"],["Mezzo secolo","Un demi-siècle","Half a century"]],"e":["Una vite diventa adulta un paio d'anni dopo l'impianto, poi produce ogni anno.","Une vigne devient adulte environ deux ans après la plantation, puis produit chaque année.","A vine matures a couple of years after planting, then crops every year."],"d":["La vite è una pianta longeva, che può vivere per diversi decenni. Dopo l'impianto le servono un paio d'anni per diventare adulta; da quel momento produce un raccolto di uva ogni anno, seguendo sempre lo stesso ciclo: fioritura in primavera, maturazione in estate e vendemmia a fine estate.","La vigne est une plante qui vit longtemps, parfois plusieurs dizaines d'années. Après la plantation, il lui faut environ deux ans pour arriver à maturité ; elle donne ensuite une récolte chaque année, en suivant toujours le même cycle : floraison au printemps, maturation en été et vendanges en fin d'été.","The vine is a long-lived plant that can survive for several decades. After planting it needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year, always following the same cycle: flowering in spring, ripening in summer and harvest in late summer."]},{"id":"l128b85be","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Che cosa serve perché avvenga la fermentazione alcolica?","Que faut-il pour que la fermentation alcoolique ait lieu ?","What is needed for alcoholic fermentation to take place?"],"o":[["I lieviti","Des levures","Yeast"],["I tannini","Des tanins","Tannin"],["Il rovere","Du chêne","Oak"],["L'anidride carbonica","Du gaz carbonique","Carbon dioxide"]],"e":["Sono i lieviti a trasformare lo zucchero del succo in alcol.","Ce sont les levures qui transforment le sucre du jus en alcool.","Yeast are what turn the sugar in the juice into alcohol."],"d":["Senza lieviti il succo d'uva resterebbe succo. I lieviti sono organismi microscopici che si nutrono dello zucchero e lo trasformano in alcol e anidride carbonica. Il rovere può servire per fermentare o maturare il vino, ma non è indispensabile; l'anidride carbonica è un prodotto della fermentazione, non un ingrediente.","Sans levures, le jus de raisin resterait du jus. Les levures sont des organismes microscopiques qui se nourrissent du sucre et le transforment en alcool et en gaz carbonique. Le chêne peut servir à fermenter ou élever le vin, mais il n'est pas indispensable ; le gaz carbonique est un produit de la fermentation, pas un ingrédient.","Without yeast, grape juice would stay juice. Yeast are microscopic organisms that feed on sugar and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Oak can be used to ferment or mature wine but is not essential, and carbon dioxide is a product of fermentation, not an ingredient."]},{"id":"l185071c9","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quali sono i due prodotti della fermentazione alcolica?","Quels sont les deux produits de la fermentation alcoolique ?","What are the two products of alcoholic fermentation?"],"o":[["Alcol e anidride carbonica","Alcool et gaz carbonique","Alcohol and carbon dioxide"],["Alcol e zucchero","Alcool et sucre","Alcohol and sugar"],["Zucchero e acido","Sucre et acide","Sugar and acid"],["Acqua e tannini","Eau et tanins","Water and tannin"]],"e":["Zucchero + lieviti → alcol + anidride carbonica.","Sucre + levures → alcool + gaz carbonique.","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide."],"d":["I lieviti mangiano lo zucchero del succo d'uva e lo trasformano in alcol e anidride carbonica. Lo zucchero è quindi il punto di partenza, non un prodotto. L'alcol resta nel vino, mentre l'anidride carbonica, nella maggior parte dei casi, si disperde nell'atmosfera durante la fermentazione.","Les levures mangent le sucre du jus de raisin et le transforment en alcool et en gaz carbonique. Le sucre est donc le point de départ, pas un produit. L'alcool reste dans le vin, tandis que le gaz carbonique, dans la plupart des cas, s'échappe dans l'atmosphère pendant la fermentation.","Yeast eat the sugar in the grape juice and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Sugar is therefore the starting point, not a product. The alcohol stays in the wine, while in most cases the carbon dioxide escapes into the atmosphere during fermentation."]},{"id":"l13bc0d36","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede di solito all'anidride carbonica prodotta durante la fermentazione di un vino fermo?","Que devient en général le gaz carbonique produit pendant la fermentation d'un vin tranquille ?","During the fermentation of a still wine, what usually happens to the carbon dioxide?"],"o":[["Si disperde nell'aria","Il s'échappe dans l'air","It escapes into the air"],["Resta nel vino","Il reste dans le vin","It stays in the wine"],["Si trasforma in zucchero","Il redevient du sucre","It turns back into sugar"],["Viene assorbita dalle bucce","Il est absorbé par les peaux","It is absorbed by the skins"]],"e":["Nella maggior parte dei casi il gas se ne va nell'atmosfera; resta l'alcol.","Dans la plupart des cas, le gaz part dans l'atmosphère ; l'alcool reste.","In most cases the gas escapes to the atmosphere; the alcohol stays."],"d":["Durante la fermentazione i lieviti producono alcol e anidride carbonica. L'alcol rimane nel vino appena fatto, mentre il gas di norma si disperde nell'aria, e così si ottiene un vino fermo, senza bollicine. Negli spumanti, invece, una parte di questo gas viene trattenuta nel vino.","Pendant la fermentation, les levures produisent de l'alcool et du gaz carbonique. L'alcool reste dans le vin nouveau, tandis que le gaz s'échappe normalement dans l'air : on obtient ainsi un vin tranquille, sans bulles. Dans les vins effervescents, au contraire, une partie de ce gaz est retenue dans le vin.","During fermentation yeast produce alcohol and carbon dioxide. The alcohol remains in the new wine, while the gas normally escapes into the air, which gives a still wine with no bubbles. In sparkling wines, by contrast, some of this gas is trapped in the wine."]},{"id":"l1914a957","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Un'etichetta indica 12% vol. Che cosa significa?","Une étiquette indique 12 % vol. Qu'est-ce que cela signifie ?","A label says 12% abv. What does this mean?"],"o":[["Il 12% del liquido è alcol","12 % du liquide est de l'alcool","12% of the liquid is alcohol"],["Il 12% del liquido è zucchero","12 % du liquide est du sucre","12% of the liquid is sugar"],["Il 12% dell'uva era nera","12 % du raisin était noir","12% of the grapes were black"],["Il 12% del vino è maturato in rovere","12 % du vin a été élevé en chêne","12% of the wine was oak-aged"]],"e":["La percentuale in volume indica quanta parte del liquido è alcol.","Le pourcentage en volume indique quelle part du liquide est de l'alcool.","Alcohol by volume tells you what share of the liquid is alcohol."],"d":["Il grado alcolico si esprime come percentuale del volume. Un vino al 10% contiene un decimo di alcol; uno al 12% contiene dodici parti di alcol su cento. L'indicazione non dice nulla sulla dolcezza, sul colore delle uve o sull'uso del rovere: riguarda soltanto l'alcol.","Le degré d'alcool s'exprime en pourcentage du volume. Un vin à 10 % vol. contient un dixième d'alcool ; un vin à 12 % vol. contient douze parts d'alcool sur cent. Cette mention ne dit rien de la douceur, de la couleur des raisins ni de l'usage du chêne : elle ne concerne que l'alcool.","Alcohol is expressed as a percentage of the volume. A wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol; one at 12% abv contains twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. The figure tells you nothing about sweetness, grape colour or the use of oak: it is only about alcohol."]},{"id":"l19026cc1","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Perché la maggior parte dei vini è secca?","Pourquoi la plupart des vins sont-ils secs ?","Why are most wines dry?"],"o":[["I lieviti consumano tutto lo zucchero","Les levures consomment tout le sucre","The yeast eat all the sugar"],["Le bucce assorbono lo zucchero","Les peaux absorbent le sucre","The skins absorb the sugar"],["Il rovere elimina lo zucchero","Le chêne élimine le sucre","Oak removes the sugar"],["L'uva non contiene zucchero","Le raisin ne contient pas de sucre","Grapes contain no sugar"]],"e":["Di solito la fermentazione continua finché non resta più zucchero.","En général, la fermentation continue jusqu'à ce qu'il n'y ait plus de sucre.","Fermentation usually continues until no sugar is left."],"d":["L'uva matura è ricca di zucchero, ma nella maggior parte dei casi i lieviti continuano a lavorare finché non l'hanno trasformato tutto in alcol. Il risultato è un vino secco, cioè senza zucchero o con pochissimo. Per ottenere vini dolci bisogna fare in modo che una parte dello zucchero resti nel vino.","Le raisin mûr est riche en sucre, mais dans la plupart des cas les levures continuent leur travail jusqu'à l'avoir entièrement transformé en alcool. On obtient un vin sec, c'est-à-dire sans sucre ou avec très peu. Pour faire des vins doux, il faut qu'une partie du sucre reste dans le vin.","Ripe grapes are full of sugar, but in most cases the yeast keep working until they have turned all of it into alcohol. The result is a dry wine, meaning one with no sugar or very little. To make sweet wines, some of the sugar has to remain in the wine."]},{"id":"l1fc11d43","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Nella produzione del vino bianco, che cosa avviene subito dopo la pigiatura?","Pour le vin blanc, que se passe-t-il juste après le foulage ?","In white winemaking, what happens straight after crushing?"],"o":[["La pressatura","Le pressurage","Pressing"],["La fermentazione","La fermentation","Fermentation"],["La svinatura","L'écoulage","Draining"],["La maturazione","L'élevage","Maturation"]],"e":["Nel bianco l'uva pigiata si pressa subito, prima di fermentare il succo.","Pour le blanc, le raisin foulé est pressé tout de suite, avant de fermenter le jus.","For white wine, crushed grapes are pressed before the juice ferments."],"d":["Per il bianco l'ordine è: pigiatura, pressatura, fermentazione, maturazione e imbottigliamento. La pressatura serve a recuperare il succo rimasto nell'uva pigiata, così che solo il succo, senza bucce, vada a fermentare. La svinatura è invece una tappa tipica del rosso e del rosato.","Pour le blanc, l'ordre est : foulage, pressurage, fermentation, élevage et mise en bouteille. Le pressurage permet de récupérer le jus resté dans le raisin foulé, pour que seul le jus, sans les peaux, fermente. L'écoulage est en revanche une étape typique du rouge et du rosé.","For white wine the order is: crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation and bottling. Pressing collects the juice left in the crushed grapes, so that only the juice, without the skins, goes on to ferment. Draining, by contrast, is a typical step in making red and rosé wines."]},{"id":"l1a486208","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Dove può fermentare un vino bianco?","Où un vin blanc peut-il fermenter ?","Where can a white wine be fermented?"],"o":[["In vasche di acciaio inox o in botti di rovere","En cuves inox ou en fûts de chêne","Stainless steel tanks or oak barrels"],["Solo in botti di rovere","Uniquement en fûts de chêne","Only in oak barrels"],["Solo in bottiglia","Uniquement en bouteille","Only in the bottle"],["Solo in vasche di acciaio inox","Uniquement en cuves inox","Only in stainless steel tanks"]],"e":["La fermentazione del bianco può avvenire sia in acciaio inox sia in rovere.","La fermentation du blanc peut se faire en inox comme en chêne.","White wine can ferment in either stainless steel or oak."],"d":["Dopo pigiatura e pressatura si aggiungono i lieviti al succo. La fermentazione può svolgersi in vasche di acciaio inossidabile oppure in botti di rovere: è una scelta di chi produce il vino. Anche la maturazione successiva può avvenire in uno di questi due tipi di recipiente.","Après le foulage et le pressurage, on ajoute les levures au jus. La fermentation peut avoir lieu en cuves en acier inoxydable ou en fûts de chêne : c'est un choix de la personne qui fait le vin. L'élevage qui suit peut lui aussi se faire dans l'un de ces deux types de contenants.","After crushing and pressing, yeast are added to the juice. Fermentation can happen in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels; it is the winemaker's choice. The maturation that follows can also take place in either of these two kinds of container."]},{"id":"l1dd38384","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Perché si può fare un vino bianco con uve nere?","Pourquoi peut-on faire un vin blanc avec des raisins noirs ?","Why is it possible to make white wine from black grapes?"],"o":[["Il loro succo è incolore","Leur jus est incolore","Their juice is colourless"],["La loro buccia è dorata","Leur peau est dorée","Their skins are golden"],["Non contengono tannini","Elles n'ont pas de tanins","They contain no tannin"],["Perdono colore in rovere","Elles perdent leur couleur en fût","They lose colour in oak"]],"e":["Il colore è solo nella buccia; il succo delle uve nere è incolore.","La couleur est seulement dans la peau ; le jus des raisins noirs est incolore.","Colour is only in the skin; black grape juice has no colour."],"d":["Le uve nere hanno bucce colorate ma succo incolore, proprio come la polpa delle uve bianche. Se vengono pressate delicatamente prima della fermentazione e il succo viene separato subito dalle bucce, il colore non passa nel succo e si può produrre un vino bianco.","Les raisins noirs ont une peau colorée mais un jus incolore, exactement comme la pulpe des raisins blancs. S'ils sont pressés délicatement avant la fermentation et que le jus est séparé tout de suite des peaux, la couleur ne passe pas dans le jus et l'on peut produire un vin blanc.","Black grapes have coloured skins but colourless juice, just like the pulp of white grapes. If they are pressed gently before fermentation and the juice is separated from the skins straight away, the colour does not pass into the juice and a white wine can be made."]},{"id":"l18858afc","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Nella produzione del vino rosso, che cosa va nel recipiente di fermentazione?","Pour le vin rouge, que met-on dans la cuve de fermentation ?","In red winemaking, what goes into the fermentation vessel?"],"o":[["Il succo insieme alle bucce","Le jus avec les peaux","The juice together with the skins"],["Solo il succo, senza bucce","Le jus seul, sans les peaux","The juice alone, without skins"],["Solo le bucce, senza succo","Les peaux seules, sans jus","The skins alone, without juice"],["Il vino già pressato","Le vin déjà pressé","Wine that is already pressed"]],"e":["Il rosso fermenta con le bucce, che danno colore e tannini.","Le rouge fermente avec les peaux, qui apportent couleur et tanins.","Red wine ferments with the skins, which give colour and tannin."],"d":["Dopo la pigiatura delle uve nere, succo e bucce vanno insieme nel recipiente di fermentazione. È questo contatto prolungato che permette di estrarre colore e tannini dalle bucce. Nel bianco, al contrario, il succo viene separato dalle bucce con la pressatura prima di fermentare.","Après le foulage des raisins noirs, jus et peaux vont ensemble dans la cuve de fermentation. C'est ce contact prolongé qui permet d'extraire la couleur et les tanins des peaux. Pour le blanc, au contraire, le jus est séparé des peaux par le pressurage avant de fermenter.","After black grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This long contact is what draws colour and tannin out of the skins. For white wine, by contrast, the juice is separated from the skins by pressing before it ferments."]},{"id":"l14425607","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Perché durante la fermentazione del rosso succo e bucce vengono mescolati a fondo?","Pourquoi mélange-t-on bien jus et peaux pendant la fermentation du rouge ?","Why are juice and skins mixed thoroughly during red wine fermentation?"],"o":[["Per estrarre colore e tannini","Pour extraire couleur et tanins","To extract colour and tannin"],["Per aggiungere sapore di rovere","Pour ajouter un goût de chêne","To add oak flavours"],["Per togliere zucchero alle bucce","Pour retirer le sucre des peaux","To remove sugar from the skins"],["Per far uscire l'anidride carbonica","Pour faire sortir le gaz carbonique","To release carbon dioxide"]],"e":["Mescolare favorisce il passaggio di colore e tannini dalle bucce al vino.","Mélanger favorise le passage de la couleur et des tanins des peaux au vin.","Mixing helps colour and tannin pass from the skins into the wine."],"d":["Colore e tannini del vino rosso si trovano nelle bucce delle uve nere. Mescolando bene le bucce con il succo durante la fermentazione, queste sostanze passano nel vino. È per questo che un rosso ha colore intenso e una struttura che asciuga la bocca, mentre un bianco no.","La couleur et les tanins du vin rouge se trouvent dans la peau des raisins noirs. En mélangeant bien les peaux avec le jus pendant la fermentation, ces substances passent dans le vin. C'est pourquoi un rouge a une couleur intense et une structure qui assèche la bouche, alors qu'un blanc non.","The colour and tannin of red wine are found in the skins of black grapes. By mixing the skins well with the juice during fermentation, these substances pass into the wine. That is why a red wine has deep colour and a structure that dries the mouth, while a white does not."]},{"id":"l1dbc9141","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Nel vino rosso, quando avviene la svinatura?","Pour le vin rouge, quand a lieu l'écoulage ?","In red winemaking, when is the wine drained off the skins?"],"o":[["Alla fine della fermentazione","À la fin de la fermentation","Once fermentation has finished"],["Subito dopo la pigiatura","Juste après le foulage","Straight after crushing"],["Dopo poche ore di fermentazione","Après quelques heures de fermentation","After a few hours of fermentation"],["Dopo l'imbottigliamento","Après la mise en bouteille","After bottling"]],"e":["Il rosso resta sulle bucce per tutta la fermentazione, poi viene svinato.","Le rouge reste sur les peaux pendant toute la fermentation, puis il est écoulé.","Red wine stays on the skins for the whole fermentation, then is drained."],"d":["Nel rosso le bucce restano a contatto con il succo per tutta la fermentazione, così da cedere molto colore e tannino. Solo quando la fermentazione è terminata il vino nuovo viene scolato via dalle bucce. Svinare dopo poche ore è invece la tecnica tipica del rosato.","Pour le rouge, les peaux restent au contact du jus pendant toute la fermentation, afin de céder beaucoup de couleur et de tanins. Ce n'est qu'une fois la fermentation terminée que le vin nouveau est séparé des peaux. Écouler au bout de quelques heures est en revanche la technique typique du rosé.","For red wine the skins stay in contact with the juice for the whole fermentation, so they give plenty of colour and tannin. Only when fermentation is over is the new wine drained off the skins. Draining after just a few hours is, by contrast, the typical technique for rosé."]},{"id":"l11304c88","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Perché nel vino rosso le bucce vengono pressate dopo la svinatura?","Pourquoi presse-t-on les peaux après l'écoulage du vin rouge ?","Why are the skins pressed after a red wine is drained?"],"o":[["Per recuperare il vino rimasto","Pour récupérer le vin restant","To release the remaining wine"],["Per estrarre altro zucchero","Pour extraire plus de sucre","To extract more sugar"],["Per avviare la fermentazione","Pour lancer la fermentation","To start fermentation"],["Per rendere il vino rosato","Pour rendre le vin rosé","To turn the wine rosé"]],"e":["Le bucce trattengono ancora vino, che si recupera con la pressatura.","Les peaux retiennent encore du vin, que l'on récupère au pressurage.","The skins still hold wine, which pressing recovers."],"d":["Dopo la svinatura le bucce sono ancora impregnate di vino. Pressandole si recupera questo vino, che altrimenti andrebbe perso. Nel rosso, quindi, la pressatura arriva dopo la fermentazione, al contrario del bianco, dove si pressa l'uva prima di fermentare. Seguono maturazione e imbottigliamento.","Après l'écoulage, les peaux sont encore imprégnées de vin. En les pressant, on récupère ce vin, qui serait sinon perdu. Pour le rouge, le pressurage vient donc après la fermentation, à l'inverse du blanc, où l'on presse le raisin avant de fermenter. Viennent ensuite l'élevage et la mise en bouteille.","After draining, the skins are still soaked with wine. Pressing them recovers this wine, which would otherwise be lost. So in red winemaking pressing comes after fermentation, the opposite of white winemaking, where the grapes are pressed before fermenting. Maturation and bottling then follow."]},{"id":"l1700ac16","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'ordine corretto delle fasi per un vino rosso?","Quel est l'ordre correct des étapes pour un vin rouge ?","Which is the correct order of steps for a red wine?"],"o":[["Pigiatura, fermentazione, svinatura, pressatura","Foulage, fermentation, écoulage, pressurage","Crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing"],["Pigiatura, pressatura, fermentazione, svinatura","Foulage, pressurage, fermentation, écoulage","Crushing, pressing, fermentation, draining"],["Pressatura, pigiatura, svinatura, fermentazione","Pressurage, foulage, écoulage, fermentation","Pressing, crushing, draining, fermentation"],["Pigiatura, svinatura, fermentazione, pressatura","Foulage, écoulage, fermentation, pressurage","Crushing, draining, fermentation, pressing"]],"e":["Nel rosso si fermenta con le bucce, poi si svina e si pressa.","Pour le rouge, on fermente avec les peaux, puis on écoule et on presse.","Red ferments on the skins, then is drained and the skins pressed."],"d":["Il rosso segue questa sequenza: pigiatura delle uve nere, fermentazione di succo e bucce, svinatura del vino nuovo, pressatura delle bucce, maturazione e imbottigliamento. Iniziare con pigiatura e poi pressatura descrive invece il bianco, in cui la pressatura avviene prima della fermentazione e solo il succo fermenta.","Le rouge suit cette séquence : foulage des raisins noirs, fermentation du jus avec les peaux, écoulage du vin nouveau, pressurage des peaux, élevage et mise en bouteille. Commencer par le foulage puis le pressurage décrit plutôt le blanc, pour lequel le pressurage a lieu avant la fermentation.","Red wine follows this sequence: crushing the black grapes, fermenting juice and skins together, draining the new wine, pressing the skins, maturation and bottling. Starting with crushing then pressing describes white winemaking instead, where pressing happens before fermentation and only the juice is fermented."]},{"id":"l1541d36b","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Con quale tipo di uva si fa il vino rosato?","Avec quel type de raisin fait-on le vin rosé ?","Which type of grape is used to make rosé wine?"],"o":[["Uve nere","Des raisins noirs","Black grapes"],["Uve bianche","Des raisins blancs","White grapes"],["Uve acerbe","Des raisins verts","Unripe grapes"],["Uve passite","Des raisins secs","Dried grapes"]],"e":["Il rosato nasce da uve nere con un breve contatto con le bucce.","Le rosé naît de raisins noirs avec un court contact avec les peaux.","Rosé comes from black grapes with brief skin contact."],"d":["Il colore rosa viene dalle bucce delle uve nere. Il succo resta a contatto con le bucce solo per poche ore, così ne prende appena un po' di colore, poi viene separato e finisce di fermentare senza bucce. Le uve bianche non hanno bucce abbastanza colorate per farlo.","La couleur rose vient de la peau des raisins noirs. Le jus reste au contact des peaux quelques heures seulement, il n'en prend donc qu'un peu de couleur, puis il est séparé et termine sa fermentation sans les peaux. Les raisins blancs n'ont pas de peau assez colorée pour cela.","The pink colour comes from the skins of black grapes. The juice stays in contact with the skins for only a few hours, so it picks up just a little colour; it is then separated and finishes fermenting without the skins. White grapes do not have skins coloured enough to do this."]},{"id":"l1e55762f","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Per un rosato, quando si separa il succo dalle bucce?","Pour un rosé, quand sépare-t-on le jus des peaux ?","For a rosé, when is the juice drained from the skins?"],"o":[["Dopo poche ore","Après quelques heures","After only a few hours"],["Dopo la fermentazione completa","Après toute la fermentation","After fermentation is complete"],["Dopo la maturazione in rovere","Après l'élevage en chêne","After oak maturation"],["Prima della pigiatura","Avant le foulage","Before crushing"]],"e":["Nel rosato il contatto con le bucce dura solo qualche ora.","Pour le rosé, le contact avec les peaux ne dure que quelques heures.","For rosé, skin contact lasts only a few hours."],"d":["Il rosato comincia come un rosso: uve nere pigiate e fermentazione con le bucce. Dopo appena qualche ora, però, il succo viene separato, quando è ancora solo rosa. La fermentazione si conclude senza bucce. Separare a fermentazione finita darebbe invece un vino rosso.","Le rosé commence comme un rouge : raisins noirs foulés et fermentation avec les peaux. Mais au bout de quelques heures seulement, le jus est séparé, quand il n'est encore que rose. La fermentation se termine sans les peaux. Séparer à la fin de la fermentation donnerait au contraire un vin rouge.","Rosé starts out like a red: black grapes are crushed and fermentation begins with the skins. After only a few hours, though, the juice is drained off while it is still just pink. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. Draining at the end of fermentation would give a red wine instead."]},{"id":"l13b4cb4d","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Che cosa spiega soprattutto la differenza di colore tra un rosato e un rosso?","Qu'est-ce qui explique surtout la différence de couleur entre un rosé et un rouge ?","What mainly explains the colour difference between a rosé and a red?"],"o":[["Il tempo di contatto con le bucce","La durée de contact avec les peaux","How long the juice stays on the skins"],["Il colore della polpa dell'uva","La couleur de la pulpe du raisin","The colour of the grape pulp"],["L'uso di botti di rovere","L'usage de fûts de chêne","The use of oak barrels"],["La quantità di lieviti aggiunti","La quantité de levures ajoutées","The amount of yeast added"]],"e":["Poche ore sulle bucce danno un rosa; tutta la fermentazione dà un rosso.","Quelques heures sur les peaux donnent du rose ; toute la fermentation, du rouge.","A few hours on the skins gives pink; the whole fermentation gives red."],"d":["Rosato e rosso si fanno entrambi con uve nere, la cui polpa ha lo stesso colore di quella delle uve bianche. Il colore viene dalle bucce: nel rosso restano nel succo per tutta la fermentazione, nel rosato solo per poche ore. Per questo il rosato rimane rosa.","Le rosé et le rouge se font tous deux avec des raisins noirs, dont la pulpe a la même couleur que celle des raisins blancs. La couleur vient des peaux : pour le rouge, elles restent dans le jus pendant toute la fermentation ; pour le rosé, quelques heures seulement. C'est pourquoi le rosé reste rose.","Rosé and red are both made from black grapes, whose pulp is the same colour as that of white grapes. The colour comes from the skins: for red they stay in the juice for the whole fermentation, for rosé only for a few hours. That is why rosé stays pink."]},{"id":"l15a04102","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sulla maturazione dei rosati è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur l'élevage des rosés est correcte ?","Which statement about the maturation of rosé wines is correct?"],"o":[["Si usa raramente il rovere","On utilise rarement le chêne","They are rarely matured in oak"],["Maturano sempre in rovere","Ils sont toujours élevés en chêne","They are always matured in oak"],["Maturano sulle bucce","Ils sont élevés sur les peaux","They are matured on their skins"],["Maturano solo in bottiglia","Ils sont élevés uniquement en bouteille","They are matured only in bottle"]],"e":["Il rosato può maturare in acciaio o rovere, ma il rovere è raro.","Le rosé peut être élevé en inox ou en chêne, mais le chêne est rare.","Rosé can mature in steel or oak, but oak is rarely used."],"d":["Dopo la fermentazione, rossi e rosati possono maturare in vasche di acciaio inossidabile o in botti di rovere. Per i rosati, però, il rovere si usa raramente. Le bucce sono già state tolte dopo poche ore, quindi la maturazione non avviene mai sulle bucce. Poi il vino viene imbottigliato.","Après la fermentation, rouges et rosés peuvent être élevés en cuves inox ou en fûts de chêne. Pour les rosés, cependant, le chêne est rarement utilisé. Les peaux ont déjà été retirées au bout de quelques heures, l'élevage ne se fait donc jamais sur les peaux. Le vin est ensuite mis en bouteille.","After fermentation, both reds and rosés can be matured in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels. For rosé, however, oak is rarely used. The skins were already removed after a few hours, so maturation never takes place on the skins. The wine is then bottled."]},{"id":"l19b1c5b4","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quale fase c'è nel vino rosso ma NON nel rosato?","Quelle étape existe pour le rouge mais PAS pour le rosé ?","Which step is part of red winemaking but NOT rosé?"],"o":[["Pressatura delle bucce dopo la fermentazione","Pressurage des peaux après la fermentation","Pressing the skins after fermentation"],["Pigiatura delle uve nere","Foulage des raisins noirs","Crushing the black grapes"],["Aggiunta di lieviti","Ajout de levures","Adding yeast"],["Imbottigliamento","Mise en bouteille","Bottling"]],"e":["Nel rosato le bucce sono tolte presto, quindi non serve pressarle dopo.","Pour le rosé, les peaux sont retirées tôt : inutile de les presser ensuite.","Rosé skins are removed early, so there is nothing to press afterwards."],"d":["Entrambi i vini prevedono pigiatura, lieviti, fermentazione, svinatura, maturazione e imbottigliamento. Nel rosso, però, le bucce restano fino alla fine della fermentazione e poi vengono pressate per recuperare il vino. Nel rosato il succo lascia le bucce dopo poche ore, quindi questa pressatura finale non c'è.","Les deux vins passent par le foulage, les levures, la fermentation, l'écoulage, l'élevage et la mise en bouteille. Pour le rouge, cependant, les peaux restent jusqu'à la fin de la fermentation, puis on les presse pour récupérer le vin. Pour le rosé, le jus quitte les peaux après quelques heures : ce pressurage final n'existe pas.","Both wines go through crushing, adding yeast, fermentation, draining, maturation and bottling. For red, however, the skins stay until fermentation ends and are then pressed to recover the wine. For rosé the juice leaves the skins after a few hours, so this final pressing does not happen."]},{"id":"l124736eb","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["In quale tipo di vino la pressatura avviene PRIMA della fermentazione?","Pour quel type de vin le pressurage a-t-il lieu AVANT la fermentation ?","In which wine is pressing done BEFORE fermentation?"],"o":[["Nel vino bianco","Le vin blanc","White wine"],["Nel vino rosso","Le vin rouge","Red wine"],["Nel vino rosato","Le vin rosé","Rosé wine"],["In nessun tipo di vino","Aucun type de vin","None of them"]],"e":["Nel bianco si pressa subito per fermentare solo il succo.","Pour le blanc, on presse tout de suite pour ne fermenter que le jus.","White grapes are pressed first so only the juice ferments."],"d":["Nel bianco l'uva viene pigiata e poi pressata, così il succo è separato dalle bucce e fermenta da solo. Nel rosso la fermentazione avviene con le bucce, che vengono pressate solo dopo la svinatura. Nel rosato il succo viene scolato dalle bucce dopo poche ore, senza una pressatura finale.","Pour le blanc, le raisin est foulé puis pressé : le jus est ainsi séparé des peaux et fermente seul. Pour le rouge, la fermentation se fait avec les peaux, qui ne sont pressées qu'après l'écoulage. Pour le rosé, le jus est écoulé des peaux après quelques heures, sans pressurage final.","For white wine the grapes are crushed and then pressed, so the juice is separated from the skins and ferments on its own. For red, fermentation happens with the skins, which are only pressed after draining. For rosé the juice is drained off the skins after a few hours, with no final pressing."]},{"id":"l12730150","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Dove possono maturare i vini dopo la fermentazione?","Où les vins peuvent-ils être élevés après la fermentation ?","Where can wines be matured after fermentation?"],"o":[["In vasche di acciaio inox o in botti di rovere","En cuves inox ou en fûts de chêne","In stainless steel tanks or oak barrels"],["Solo nelle bucce pressate","Uniquement dans les peaux pressées","Only among the pressed skins"],["Solo in vigna, sulla pianta","Uniquement sur la vigne","Only on the vine"],["Solo in un secchiello con ghiaccio","Uniquement dans un seau à glace","Only in an ice bucket"]],"e":["La maturazione si fa in acciaio inox o in rovere, per bianchi, rossi e rosati.","L'élevage se fait en inox ou en chêne, pour les blancs, rouges et rosés.","Maturation uses stainless steel or oak, for whites, reds and rosés."],"d":["Terminata la fermentazione, il vino può riposare in vasche di acciaio inossidabile oppure in botti di rovere. Vale per bianchi, rossi e rosati, anche se per i rosati il rovere è raro. Il rovere, come si vedrà più avanti, può dare al vino aromi propri. Dopo la maturazione il vino viene imbottigliato.","Une fois la fermentation terminée, le vin peut reposer en cuves en acier inoxydable ou en fûts de chêne. C'est valable pour les blancs, les rouges et les rosés, même si le chêne est rare pour les rosés. Le chêne, comme on le verra, peut donner au vin ses propres arômes. Après l'élevage vient la mise en bouteille.","Once fermentation is over, the wine can rest in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels. This applies to whites, reds and rosés, although oak is rare for rosé. Oak, as you will see later, can give the wine aromas of its own. After maturation the wine is bottled."]},{"id":"l1a9bcaeb","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale tipo di vino ha ricevuto un'aggiunta di alcol?","Quel type de vin a reçu un ajout d'alcool ?","Which type of wine has had extra alcohol added?"],"o":[["Fortificato","Fortifié","Fortified"],["Spumante","Effervescent","Sparkling"],["Fermo","Tranquille","Still"],["Rosato","Rosé","Rosé"]],"e":["Nei vini fortificati si aggiunge alcol, per questo sono più forti.","On ajoute de l'alcool aux vins fortifiés, d'où leur degré plus élevé.","Fortified wines have alcohol added, which makes them stronger."],"d":["Esistono tre tipi di vino: fermo, spumante e fortificato. Solo il fortificato riceve un'aggiunta di alcol, che porta il grado tra il 15% e il 22% vol. Lo spumante deve le bollicine all'anidride carbonica della fermentazione, mentre il rosato è un colore, non un tipo di vino.","Il existe trois types de vin : tranquille, effervescent et fortifié. Seul le fortifié reçoit un ajout d'alcool, qui porte son degré entre 15 % et 22 % vol. L'effervescent doit ses bulles au dioxyde de carbone de la fermentation, et le rosé est une couleur, pas un type de vin.","There are three types of wine: still, sparkling and fortified. Only fortified wine has extra alcohol added, which lifts it to between 15% and 22% abv. Sparkling wine owes its bubbles to carbon dioxide from fermentation, and rosé is a colour, not a type of wine."]},{"id":"l179538c6","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Qual è la gradazione tipica dei vini fortificati?","Quel est le degré habituel des vins fortifiés ?","What is the usual alcohol range of fortified wines?"],"o":[["15–22% vol.","15–22 % vol.","15–22% abv"],["8–11% vol.","8–11 % vol.","8–11% abv"],["11,5–14% vol.","11,5–14 % vol.","11.5–14% abv"],["4–7% vol.","4–7 % vol.","4–7% abv"]],"e":["L'alcol aggiunto porta i fortificati tra il 15% e il 22% vol.","L'alcool ajouté place les fortifiés entre 15 % et 22 % vol.","The added alcohol puts fortified wines between 15% and 22% abv."],"d":["I vini fermi e spumanti stanno quasi sempre tra l'11,5% e il 14% vol., con estremi tra 8% e 15%. I fortificati, come Sherry e Port, ricevono alcol in più e salgono a una fascia più alta, tra il 15% e il 22% vol.","Les vins tranquilles et effervescents se situent presque toujours entre 11,5 % et 14 % vol., avec des extrêmes de 8 % à 15 %. Les fortifiés, comme le Sherry et le Port, reçoivent de l'alcool en plus et montent dans une fourchette plus haute, de 15 % à 22 % vol.","Still and sparkling wines almost always sit between 11.5% and 14% abv, with extremes from 8% to 15%. Fortified wines such as Sherry and Port have extra alcohol added, so they move up into a higher band of 15% to 22% abv."]},{"id":"l107426b9","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Da dove vengono le bollicine di un vino spumante?","D'où viennent les bulles d'un vin effervescent ?","Where do the bubbles in sparkling wine come from?"],"o":[["Anidride carbonica della fermentazione rimasta nel vino","Dioxyde de carbone de la fermentation resté dans le vin","Carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine"],["Alcol distillato aggiunto dopo la fermentazione","Alcool distillé ajouté après la fermentation","Distilled alcohol added after fermentation"],["Zucchero lasciato nel vino dopo la fermentazione","Sucre laissé dans le vin après la fermentation","Sugar left in the wine after fermentation"],["Aria che entra dalle doghe delle botti","Air qui entre par les douelles des fûts","Air entering through the oak barrel staves"]],"e":["La fermentazione produce anidride carbonica; se resta intrappolata, forma le bollicine.","La fermentation produit du dioxyde de carbone ; piégé, il forme les bulles.","Fermentation makes carbon dioxide; when it is trapped, it becomes the bubbles."],"d":["I lieviti trasformano lo zucchero in alcol e anidride carbonica. Nei vini fermi il gas si disperde nell'aria, mentre negli spumanti viene trattenuto nel vino. Quando si apre la bottiglia, il gas si libera sotto forma di bollicine, come nello Champagne, nel Cava o nel Prosecco.","Les levures transforment le sucre en alcool et en dioxyde de carbone. Dans les vins tranquilles, le gaz s'échappe dans l'air ; dans les effervescents, il est retenu dans le vin. À l'ouverture de la bouteille, il se libère sous forme de bulles, comme dans le Champagne, le Cava ou le Prosecco.","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol and carbon dioxide. In still wines the gas escapes into the air, but in sparkling wines it is kept inside the wine. When the bottle is opened, the gas is released as bubbles, as in Champagne, Cava or Prosecco."]},{"id":"l1971e121","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Tra quali valori si trova la maggior parte dei vini fermi?","Entre quelles valeurs se situent la plupart des vins tranquilles ?","Between which values do most still wines fall?"],"o":[["11,5% e 14% vol.","11,5 % et 14 % vol.","11.5% and 14% abv"],["15% e 22% vol.","15 % et 22 % vol.","15% and 22% abv"],["5% e 8% vol.","5 % et 8 % vol.","5% and 8% abv"],["16% e 20% vol.","16 % et 20 % vol.","16% and 20% abv"]],"e":["I vini fermi vanno da 8% a 15% vol., ma quasi tutti stanno tra 11,5% e 14%.","Les tranquilles vont de 8 % à 15 % vol., mais presque tous entre 11,5 % et 14 %.","Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, but most sit between 11.5% and 14%."],"d":["La fascia completa dei vini fermi va dall'8% al 15% vol., ma la grande maggioranza si colloca tra l'11,5% e il 14%. Valori tra il 15% e il 22% sono tipici dei vini fortificati, a cui si aggiunge alcol. Un vino come il White Zinfandel è un esempio di gradazione bassa.","La fourchette complète des vins tranquilles va de 8 % à 15 % vol., mais la grande majorité se situe entre 11,5 % et 14 %. Les valeurs de 15 % à 22 % sont typiques des vins fortifiés, auxquels on ajoute de l'alcool. Le White Zinfandel est un exemple de vin peu alcoolisé.","The full range for still wines runs from 8% to 15% abv, but the great majority sit between 11.5% and 14%. Figures of 15% to 22% are typical of fortified wines, which have alcohol added. White Zinfandel is an example of a still wine at the low end."]},{"id":"l1e094933","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini prende il nome dal vitigno?","Lequel de ces vins porte le nom de son cépage ?","Which of these wines is named after its grape variety?"],"o":[["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],["Rioja","Rioja","Rioja"],["Chianti","Chianti","Chianti"],["Sancerre","Sancerre","Sancerre"]],"e":["Pinot Grigio è un vitigno; Rioja, Chianti e Sancerre sono zone di produzione.","Pinot Grigio est un cépage ; Rioja, Chianti et Sancerre sont des régions.","Pinot Grigio is a grape; Rioja, Chianti and Sancerre are places."],"d":["Molti vini europei portano il nome della zona in cui sono prodotti: Rioja in Spagna, Chianti in Italia, Sancerre in Francia. Altri vini, invece, indicano in etichetta il vitigno usato. Il Pinot Grigio è proprio un esempio di vino chiamato con il nome dell'uva.","Beaucoup de vins européens portent le nom de leur région de production : Rioja en Espagne, Chianti en Italie, Sancerre en France. D'autres indiquent plutôt le cépage sur l'étiquette. Le Pinot Grigio est justement un exemple de vin désigné par le nom de son raisin.","Many European wines take the name of the area where they are made: Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy, Sancerre in France. Other wines show the grape variety on the label instead. Pinot Grigio is a typical example of a wine named after its grape."]},{"id":"l1fc54261","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi è uno spumante spagnolo?","Lequel de ces vins est un effervescent espagnol ?","Which of these is a Spanish sparkling wine?"],"o":[["Cava","Cava","Cava"],["Prosecco","Prosecco","Prosecco"],["Champagne","Champagne","Champagne"],["Sherry","Sherry","Sherry"]],"e":["Il Cava è lo spumante della Spagna.","Le Cava est l'effervescent espagnol.","Cava is the sparkling wine from Spain."],"d":["Tre spumanti famosi da ricordare: Champagne dalla Francia, Prosecco dall'Italia e Cava dalla Spagna. Anche lo Sherry è spagnolo, ma è un vino fortificato, non uno spumante: ha ricevuto alcol in più e non ha bollicine. Gli spumanti, comunque, si producono oggi in quasi tutti i paesi del vino.","Trois effervescents célèbres à retenir : le Champagne de France, le Prosecco d'Italie et le Cava d'Espagne. Le Sherry est lui aussi espagnol, mais c'est un vin fortifié, pas un effervescent : il a reçu de l'alcool en plus et n'a pas de bulles. On produit d'ailleurs aujourd'hui des effervescents dans presque tous les pays viticoles.","Three famous sparkling wines to remember: Champagne from France, Prosecco from Italy and Cava from Spain. Sherry is also Spanish, but it is a fortified wine, not a sparkling one: it has had alcohol added and has no bubbles. Sparkling wines are, in fact, now made in almost every wine-producing country."]},{"id":"l1822e6c3","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Perché un vino rosso è rosso?","Pourquoi un vin rouge est-il rouge ?","Why is a red wine red?"],"o":[["Le bucce restano nel succo durante la fermentazione","Les peaux restent dans le jus pendant la fermentation","The skins stay in the juice during fermentation"],["La polpa delle uve nere è di colore rosso","La pulpe des raisins noirs est de couleur rouge","The pulp of black grapes is red in colour"],["Le botti di rovere cedono colore al vino","Les fûts de chêne donnent leur couleur au vin","The oak barrels give their colour to the wine"],["Si aggiunge succo d'uva nera non fermentato","On ajoute du jus de raisin noir non fermenté","Unfermented black grape juice is added"]],"e":["Il colore è nelle bucce, che cedono colore durante la fermentazione.","La couleur est dans les peaux, qui la cèdent pendant la fermentation.","The colour is in the skins, which release it during fermentation."],"d":["La polpa delle uve bianche e nere ha lo stesso colore e il succo è incolore. Per fare un rosso si usano uve nere e si lasciano le bucce a contatto con il succo per tutta la fermentazione, mescolando bene: così passano nel vino colore e tannino.","La pulpe des raisins blancs et noirs a la même couleur et le jus est incolore. Pour faire un rouge, on utilise des raisins noirs et on laisse les peaux au contact du jus pendant toute la fermentation, en mélangeant bien : couleur et tanins passent ainsi dans le vin.","The pulp of white and black grapes is the same colour and the juice is colourless. To make a red wine, black grapes are used and the skins are kept in contact with the juice throughout fermentation, mixed in well, so colour and tannin pass into the wine."]},{"id":"l16e9106c","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Si può fare un vino bianco con uve nere?","Peut-on faire un vin blanc avec des raisins noirs ?","Can a white wine be made from black grapes?"],"o":[["Sì, separando le bucce dal succo prima della fermentazione","Oui, en séparant les peaux du jus avant la fermentation","Yes, by separating skins and juice before fermentation"],["Sì, ma solo se il vino viene affinato in rovere","Oui, mais seulement si le vin est élevé en chêne","Yes, but only if the wine is then aged in oak"],["No, le uve nere danno sempre un vino rosso","Non, les raisins noirs donnent toujours du rouge","No, black grapes always give a red wine"],["No, le uve nere danno solo vini rosati","Non, les raisins noirs ne donnent que du rosé","No, black grapes can only make rosé wine"]],"e":["Il succo delle uve nere è incolore: senza bucce, il vino resta bianco.","Le jus des raisins noirs est incolore : sans les peaux, le vin reste blanc.","Black grape juice is colourless, so without the skins the wine stays white."],"d":["Il colore delle uve nere si trova solo nella buccia. Se le uve vengono pressate delicatamente e le bucce separate dal succo prima della fermentazione, il succo resta chiaro e dà un vino bianco. È lo stesso principio che permette di usare il Pinot Noir nello Champagne.","La couleur des raisins noirs se trouve uniquement dans la peau. Si l'on presse les raisins doucement et qu'on sépare les peaux du jus avant la fermentation, le jus reste clair et donne un vin blanc. C'est ce principe qui permet d'utiliser le Pinot Noir dans le Champagne.","All the colour of a black grape is in its skin. If the grapes are pressed gently and the skins are separated from the juice before fermentation, the juice stays pale and makes a white wine. This same idea is what allows Pinot Noir to be used in Champagne."]},{"id":"l18b7549f","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Come si ottiene un vino rosato?","Comment obtient-on un vin rosé ?","How is a rosé wine made?"],"o":[["Uve nere, contatto con le bucce di poche ore","Raisins noirs, contact avec les peaux de quelques heures","Black grapes with only a few hours of skin contact"],["Uve bianche fermentate insieme alle loro bucce","Raisins blancs fermentés avec leurs peaux","White grapes fermented together with their skins"],["Uve nere con bucce fino a fine fermentazione","Raisins noirs avec peaux jusqu'à la fin de la fermentation","Black grapes kept on skins until fermentation ends"],["Uve bianche affinate a lungo in botti di rovere","Raisins blancs élevés longtemps en fût de chêne","White grapes aged for a long time in oak barrels"]],"e":["Il succo resta poche ore con le bucce di uve nere, poi viene separato.","Le jus reste quelques heures avec les peaux de raisins noirs, puis il est écoulé.","The juice sits with black grape skins for a few hours, then is drained off."],"d":["Il rosato nasce da uve nere, come il rosso, ma il contatto con le bucce dura solo qualche ora. Il succo, appena rosa, viene separato e termina la fermentazione senza bucce. Se invece le bucce restassero fino alla fine, si otterrebbe un vino rosso.","Le rosé naît de raisins noirs, comme le rouge, mais le contact avec les peaux ne dure que quelques heures. Le jus, à peine rose, est écoulé et termine sa fermentation sans les peaux. Si les peaux restaient jusqu'à la fin, on obtiendrait un vin rouge.","Rosé comes from black grapes, like red wine, but the skin contact lasts only a few hours. The juice, now just pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins. If the skins stayed in until the end, the result would be a red wine instead."]},{"id":"l11609a42","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini è un rosato?","Lequel de ces vins est un rosé ?","Which of these wines is a rosé?"],"o":[["White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel"],["Chablis","Chablis","Chablis"],["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Sauternes","Sauternes","Sauternes"]],"e":["Nonostante il nome, il White Zinfandel della California è un rosato.","Malgré son nom, le White Zinfandel de Californie est un rosé.","Despite its name, White Zinfandel from California is a rosé."],"d":["Il nome può ingannare: il White Zinfandel è un rosato californiano, di dolcezza media, poco alcolico e con fragola e lampone. Lo Chablis e il Sauternes sono vini bianchi francesi, mentre il Beaujolais è un rosso leggero e poco tannico. Ricorda di non giudicare un vino solo dal nome.","Le nom peut tromper : le White Zinfandel est un rosé californien, demi-doux, peu alcoolisé, aux arômes de fraise et de framboise. Le Chablis et le Sauternes sont des blancs français, tandis que le Beaujolais est un rouge léger et peu tannique. Mieux vaut donc ne jamais juger un vin à son seul nom.","The name can mislead you: White Zinfandel is a Californian rosé, medium-sweet, low in alcohol, with strawberry and raspberry flavours. Chablis and Sauternes are French white wines, while Beaujolais is a light red with low tannin. So never judge a wine by its name alone."]},{"id":"l11970f5b","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede quando si fa un vino secco?","Que se passe-t-il quand on fait un vin sec ?","What happens when a dry wine is made?"],"o":[["I lieviti trasformano in alcol tutto lo zucchero","Les levures transforment tout le sucre en alcool","The yeast turn all of the sugar into alcohol"],["Si aggiunge alcol distillato prima della fine","On ajoute de l'alcool distillé avant la fin","Distilled alcohol is added before fermentation ends"],["Si aggiunge succo d'uva non fermentato","On ajoute du jus de raisin non fermenté","Unfermented grape juice is added to the wine"],["Si tolgono i lieviti prima della fine","On retire les levures avant la fin","The yeast are removed before they finish"]],"e":["Un vino è secco quando i lieviti hanno consumato tutto lo zucchero.","Un vin est sec quand les levures ont consommé tout le sucre.","A wine is dry when the yeast have eaten all the sugar."],"d":["La maggior parte dei vini è secca: i lieviti continuano a lavorare finché non hanno trasformato tutto lo zucchero in alcol. Le altre risposte descrivono come si ottengono vini con zucchero residuo: togliere i lieviti o aggiungere succo per i vini medi, aggiungere alcol per i fortificati dolci.","La plupart des vins sont secs : les levures travaillent jusqu'à avoir transformé tout le sucre en alcool. Les autres réponses décrivent des façons de garder du sucre : retirer les levures ou ajouter du jus pour les demi-doux, ajouter de l'alcool pour les fortifiés doux.","Most wines are dry: the yeast keep working until they have turned all the sugar into alcohol. The other answers describe ways of keeping sugar in the wine: removing yeast or adding juice for medium wines, and adding alcohol for sweet fortified wines."]},{"id":"l137e18b3","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale metodo serve a ottenere un vino di dolcezza media?","Quelle méthode permet d'obtenir un vin demi-doux ?","Which method is used to make a medium-sweet wine?"],"o":[["Aggiungere succo d'uva non fermentato a un vino secco","Ajouter du jus de raisin non fermenté à un vin sec","Adding unfermented grape juice to a dry wine"],["Lasciare le bucce nel succo per più tempo","Laisser les peaux plus longtemps dans le jus","Leaving the skins in the juice for longer"],["Far affinare il vino in botti di rovere","Élever le vin en fût de chêne","Maturing the wine in oak barrels"],["Raccogliere l'uva prima che maturi","Vendanger le raisin avant sa maturité","Picking the grapes before they ripen"]],"e":["Il succo non fermentato aggiunge zucchero a un vino già secco.","Le jus non fermenté apporte du sucre à un vin déjà sec.","Unfermented juice brings sugar back into an already dry wine."],"d":["Per i vini di dolcezza media ci sono due strade: togliere i lieviti prima che abbiano consumato tutto lo zucchero, oppure aggiungere succo d'uva non fermentato a un vino secco. Bucce e rovere influiscono su colore, tannino e aromi, non sulla dolcezza.","Pour les vins demi-doux, il y a deux voies : retirer les levures avant qu'elles aient consommé tout le sucre, ou ajouter du jus de raisin non fermenté à un vin sec. Les peaux et le chêne influencent la couleur, les tanins et les arômes, pas la sucrosité.","There are two routes to a medium-sweet wine: remove the yeast before they have eaten all the sugar, or add unfermented grape juice to a dry wine. Skins and oak affect colour, tannin and aromas, not the level of sweetness."]},{"id":"l13e6e934","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["In un vino fortificato dolce, che cosa ferma la fermentazione?","Dans un vin fortifié doux, qu'est-ce qui arrête la fermentation ?","In a sweet fortified wine, what stops the fermentation?"],"o":[["L'aggiunta di alcol distillato che uccide i lieviti","L'ajout d'alcool distillé qui tue les levures","Adding distilled alcohol, which kills the yeast"],["L'aggiunta di succo d'uva non fermentato","L'ajout de jus de raisin non fermenté","Adding unfermented grape juice to the wine"],["Il passaggio in botti di rovere","Le passage en fût de chêne","Moving the wine into oak barrels"],["La separazione del vino dalle bucce","La séparation du vin et des peaux","Draining the wine off the skins"]],"e":["L'alcol forte aggiunto uccide i lieviti e lascia zucchero nel vino.","L'alcool fort ajouté tue les levures et laisse du sucre dans le vin.","The strong added alcohol kills the yeast, leaving sugar in the wine."],"d":["Nei fortificati dolci si aggiunge alcol distillato ad alta gradazione prima che i lieviti abbiano consumato tutto lo zucchero. I lieviti muoiono, lo zucchero rimasto rende il vino dolce e l'alcol aggiunto lo rende più forte. È il caso del Port e di alcuni Sherry.","Dans les fortifiés doux, on ajoute un alcool distillé très fort avant que les levures aient consommé tout le sucre. Les levures meurent, le sucre restant rend le vin doux et l'alcool ajouté le rend plus fort. C'est le cas du Port et de certains Sherry.","In sweet fortified wines, high-strength distilled alcohol is added before the yeast have eaten all the sugar. The yeast die, the leftover sugar makes the wine sweet and the added alcohol makes it stronger. Port and some Sherries are made this way."]},{"id":"l1b49d626","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale sensazione indica un'acidità alta?","Quelle sensation révèle une acidité élevée ?","Which sensation tells you a wine has high acidity?"],"o":[["Fa venire l'acquolina in bocca","Elle fait saliver","It makes your mouth water"],["Lascia la bocca asciutta","Elle assèche la bouche","It makes your mouth feel dry"],["Dà calore in gola","Elle chauffe la gorge","It warms the back of your throat"],["Sembra densa e sciropposa","Elle paraît épaisse et sirupeuse","It feels thick and syrupy"]],"e":["L'acidità si riconosce perché fa salivare.","On reconnaît l'acidité au fait qu'elle fait saliver.","Acidity is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water."],"d":["Ogni elemento della struttura si riconosce da una sensazione diversa. L'acidità fa salivare e dà freschezza. Il tannino, invece, asciuga la bocca; l'alcol si percepisce come calore; un vino molto dolce può sembrare denso e sciropposo. Troppa acidità, però, rende il vino sgradevolmente aspro.","Chaque élément de la structure se reconnaît à une sensation différente. L'acidité fait saliver et apporte de la fraîcheur. Le tanin, lui, assèche la bouche ; l'alcool se perçoit comme une chaleur ; un vin très doux peut paraître épais et sirupeux. Trop d'acidité rend toutefois le vin désagréablement acide.","Each part of a wine's structure has its own sensation. Acidity makes your mouth water and brings freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth; alcohol is felt as warmth; and a very sweet wine can feel thick and syrupy. Too much acidity, however, makes a wine taste unpleasantly sharp."]},{"id":"l16964d99","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Perché l'acidità è importante nei vini dolci?","Pourquoi l'acidité est-elle importante dans les vins doux ?","Why is acidity important in sweet wines?"],"o":[["Bilancia la dolcezza e evita che il vino stanchi","Elle équilibre la douceur et évite l'écœurement","It balances the sweetness so the wine is not cloying"],["Aumenta il grado alcolico del vino","Elle augmente le degré d'alcool du vin","It raises the alcohol level of the wine"],["Dà al vino un colore più intenso","Elle donne au vin une couleur plus intense","It gives the wine a deeper colour"],["Aggiunge tannino e quindi più corpo","Elle ajoute du tanin et donc du corps","It adds tannin and therefore more body"]],"e":["Senza acidità un vino dolce risulterebbe stucchevole.","Sans acidité, un vin doux serait écœurant.","Without acidity, a sweet wine would taste cloying."],"d":["L'acidità viene dal succo d'uva e rinfresca il vino. Nei vini dolci fa da contrappeso allo zucchero: per questo il Sauternes e i Riesling dolci hanno un'acidità alta. Non influisce su colore, tannino o grado alcolico. Senza di essa il vino sembrerebbe pesante.","L'acidité vient du jus de raisin et rafraîchit le vin. Dans les vins doux, elle fait contrepoids au sucre : c'est pourquoi le Sauternes et les Riesling doux ont une acidité élevée. Elle n'agit ni sur la couleur, ni sur les tanins, ni sur le degré. Sans elle, le vin paraîtrait lourd.","Acidity comes from the grape juice and refreshes the wine. In sweet wines it acts as a counterweight to the sugar, which is why Sauternes and sweet Rieslings have high acidity. It does not change the colour, the tannin or the alcohol level. Without it, the wine would feel heavy."]},{"id":"l14d484db","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Da dove proviene il tannino del vino?","D'où vient le tanin du vin ?","Where does tannin in wine come from?"],"o":[["Dalle bucce delle uve nere","De la peau des raisins noirs","The skins of black grapes"],["Dalla polpa delle uve bianche","De la pulpe des raisins blancs","The pulp of white grapes"],["Dallo zucchero del succo","Du sucre du jus","The sugar in the juice"],["Dai lieviti della fermentazione","Des levures de fermentation","The yeast used in fermentation"]],"e":["Il tannino si trova nelle bucce delle uve nere ed è tipico dei rossi.","Le tanin se trouve dans la peau des raisins noirs ; il est typique des rouges.","Tannin sits in black grape skins, which is why it is a red-wine feature."],"d":["Le uve nere hanno bucce colorate che contengono tannini. Durante la fermentazione dei rossi le bucce restano nel succo e cedono colore e tannino. Quanto tannino avrà il vino dipende dal vitigno e dalla vinificazione: ne ha molto il Bordeaux rosso, poco il Beaujolais.","Les raisins noirs ont une peau colorée qui contient des tanins. Pendant la fermentation des rouges, les peaux restent dans le jus et cèdent couleur et tanins. La quantité finale dépend du cépage et de la vinification : beaucoup dans le Bordeaux rouge, peu dans le Beaujolais.","Black grapes have coloured skins that contain tannins. When red wine ferments, the skins stay in the juice and release colour and tannin. How much tannin the wine ends up with depends on the grape and the winemaking: red Bordeaux has a lot, Beaujolais very little."]},{"id":"l18f8a4b7","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi rossi ha poco tannino?","Lequel de ces rouges a peu de tanins ?","Which of these reds is low in tannin?"],"o":[["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Bordeaux rosso","Bordeaux rouge","Red Bordeaux"],["Chianti","Chianti","Chianti"],["Port","Port","Port"]],"e":["Il Beaujolais è un rosso leggero, fresco e poco tannico.","Le Beaujolais est un rouge léger, frais et peu tannique.","Beaujolais is a light, fresh red with low tannin."],"d":["Il Beaujolais è un esempio classico di rosso poco tannico, insieme ad alcuni Pinot Noir. Il Bordeaux rosso e il Chianti, invece, sono citati come rossi molto tannici, e anche il Port, vino fortificato rosso e dolce, ha tannini alti. Ricorda che il tannino lascia la bocca asciutta.","Le Beaujolais est un exemple classique de rouge peu tannique, comme certains Pinot Noir. Le Bordeaux rouge et le Chianti sont au contraire cités comme des rouges très tanniques, et le Port, vin fortifié rouge et doux, a lui aussi des tanins élevés. Rappel : le tanin assèche la bouche.","Beaujolais is a classic example of a low-tannin red, along with some Pinot Noir wines. Red Bordeaux and Chianti, by contrast, are standard examples of high-tannin reds, and Port, a sweet red fortified wine, also has high tannins. Remember that tannin leaves the mouth feeling dry."]},{"id":"l1076240a","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini è un esempio di vino molto alcolico?","Lequel de ces vins est un exemple de vin riche en alcool ?","Which of these is an example of a high-alcohol wine?"],"o":[["Châteauneuf-du-Pape","Châteauneuf-du-Pape","Châteauneuf-du-Pape"],["White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel"],["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"]],"e":["Lo Châteauneuf-du-Pape è un rosso francese pieno e ricco di alcol.","Le Châteauneuf-du-Pape est un rouge français corsé et riche en alcool.","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is a full-bodied French red with high alcohol."],"d":["Lo Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rosso del Rodano, è il classico esempio di vino ad alta gradazione: secco, di corpo pieno, con fragola e chiodi di garofano. All'opposto il White Zinfandel è citato come vino poco alcolico; Beaujolais e Pinot Grigio sono vini leggeri.","Le Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rouge de la vallée du Rhône, est l'exemple type du vin riche en alcool : sec, corsé, avec fraise et clou de girofle. À l'opposé, le White Zinfandel est cité comme vin peu alcoolisé ; Beaujolais et Pinot Grigio sont des vins légers.","Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a red from the Rhône, is the textbook example of a high-alcohol wine: dry and full-bodied, with strawberry and clove. At the other end, White Zinfandel is the standard low-alcohol example, while Beaujolais and Pinot Grigio are light-bodied wines."]},{"id":"l157bd02d","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa «12% vol.» in etichetta?","Que signifie « 12 % vol. » sur l'étiquette ?","What does «12% abv» on a label mean?"],"o":[["Il 12% del liquido è alcol","12 % du liquide est de l'alcool","12% of the liquid is alcohol"],["Il vino contiene il 12% di zucchero","Le vin contient 12 % de sucre","The wine contains 12% sugar"],["Il 12% delle uve era nero","12 % des raisins étaient noirs","12% of the grapes were black"],["Il vino ha passato 12 mesi in botte","Le vin a passé 12 mois en fût","The wine spent 12 months in oak"]],"e":["La percentuale in volume indica quanta parte del vino è alcol.","Le pourcentage en volume indique la part d'alcool dans le vin.","Alcohol by volume shows what share of the wine is alcohol."],"d":["Il grado alcolico si misura come percentuale in volume (abv in inglese). Un vino a 12% vol. contiene dodici parti di alcol su cento. È un valore tipico di un vino fermo: la maggior parte si colloca tra l'11,5% e il 14%.","Le degré d'alcool se mesure en pourcentage du volume (abv en anglais). Un vin à 12 % vol. contient douze parts d'alcool sur cent. C'est une valeur typique d'un vin tranquille : la plupart se situent entre 11,5 % et 14 %.","Alcohol is measured as a percentage of the total volume, called alcohol by volume or abv. A wine at 12% abv has twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. That is a typical figure for a still wine, as most sit between 11.5% and 14%."]},{"id":"l129fb223","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa descrive il corpo di un vino?","Que décrit le corps d'un vin ?","What does the body of a wine describe?"],"o":[["Quanto il vino riempie la bocca","À quel point le vin remplit la bouche","How mouth-filling the wine feels"],["Quanta acidità contiene il vino","Combien d'acidité contient le vin","How much acidity the wine contains"],["Quanto è intenso il colore del vino","L'intensité de la couleur du vin","How deep the colour of the wine is"],["Quanto tempo è rimasto in botte","Combien de temps il est resté en fût","How long the wine stayed in oak"]],"e":["Il corpo è la sensazione generale in bocca: leggero, medio o pieno.","Le corps est la sensation globale en bouche : léger, moyen ou corsé.","Body is the overall feel in the mouth: light, medium or full."],"d":["Il corpo dipende da molti fattori, quindi la domanda pratica è: quanto riempie la bocca questo vino? I vini pieni, come Sauternes o un Cabernet Sauvignon californiano, sembrano densi e avvolgenti; quelli leggeri, come Pinot Grigio e Beaujolais, più delicati.","Le corps dépend de nombreux facteurs, d'où la question pratique : à quel point ce vin remplit-il la bouche ? Les vins corsés, comme le Sauternes ou un Cabernet Sauvignon de Californie, paraissent denses ; les vins légers, comme le Pinot Grigio et le Beaujolais, plus délicats.","Many factors shape body, so the practical question is: how much does this wine fill my mouth? Full-bodied wines such as Sauternes or a Californian Cabernet Sauvignon feel dense and rich, while light ones such as Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais feel more delicate."]},{"id":"l14c942e8","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini ha corpo pieno?","Lequel de ces vins est corsé ?","Which of these wines is full-bodied?"],"o":[["Sauternes","Sauternes","Sauternes"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Sancerre","Sancerre","Sancerre"]],"e":["Il Sauternes, bianco dolce di Bordeaux, ha corpo pieno.","Le Sauternes, blanc doux de Bordeaux, est corsé.","Sauternes, the sweet white from Bordeaux, is full-bodied."],"d":["Il Sauternes è dolce e di corpo pieno, con albicocca, miele e vaniglia. Il Pinot Grigio e il Beaujolais sono esempi di vini di corpo leggero, mentre il Sancerre è un bianco secco di corpo medio. Anche un Cabernet Sauvignon californiano sarebbe un buon esempio di vino pieno.","Le Sauternes est doux et corsé, avec abricot, miel et vanille. Le Pinot Grigio et le Beaujolais sont des exemples de vins légers, tandis que le Sancerre est un blanc sec de corps moyen. Un Cabernet Sauvignon de Californie serait lui aussi un bon exemple de vin corsé.","Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla. Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais are examples of light-bodied wines, and Sancerre is a dry white with medium body. A Californian Cabernet Sauvignon would also be a good example of a full-bodied wine."]},{"id":"l10adad8b","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale gruppo di aromi deriva tipicamente dal rovere?","Quel groupe d'arômes vient en général du chêne ?","Which group of aromas typically comes from oak?"],"o":[["Vaniglia, cedro, affumicato","Vanille, cèdre, fumé","Vanilla, cedar, smoke"],["Mela, limone, pera","Pomme, citron, poire","Apple, lemon, pear"],["Erba, asparago, peperone","Herbe, asperge, poivron","Grass, asparagus, bell pepper"],["Fragola, lampone, ciliegia","Fraise, framboise, cerise","Strawberry, raspberry, cherry"]],"e":["Il rovere dà vaniglia, cedro, affumicato, cocco e chiodi di garofano.","Le chêne apporte vanille, cèdre, fumé, noix de coco et clou de girofle.","Oak gives vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves."],"d":["Quando un vino fermenta o si affina in botti di rovere, il legno aggiunge note di vaniglia, cedro, affumicato, cocco e chiodi di garofano. Mela, limone e pera sono aromi di frutta; erba, asparago e peperone sono note erbacee tipiche, per esempio, del Sauvignon Blanc.","Quand un vin fermente ou s'élève en fût de chêne, le bois apporte des notes de vanille, de cèdre, de fumé, de noix de coco et de clou de girofle. Pomme, citron et poire sont des arômes de fruit ; herbe, asperge et poivron sont des notes herbacées typiques du Sauvignon Blanc.","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, the wood adds notes of vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves. Apple, lemon and pear are fruit aromas, while grass, asparagus and bell pepper are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc, for example."]},{"id":"l14ebd294","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi ha di solito uno Chardonnay di clima fresco?","Quels arômes a en général un Chardonnay de climat frais ?","Which aromas does a cool-climate Chardonnay usually show?"],"o":[["Mela verde e limone","Pomme verte et citron","Green apple and lemon"],["Pesca e ananas","Pêche et ananas","Peach and pineapple"],["Ribes nero e menta","Cassis et menthe","Blackcurrant and mint"],["Fragola e ciliegia","Fraise et cerise","Strawberry and cherry"]],"e":["Nel clima fresco le uve maturano meno: frutta verde e agrumi.","En climat frais, le raisin mûrit moins : fruits verts et agrumes.","In a cool climate grapes ripen less, giving green fruit and citrus."],"d":["La maturità delle uve cambia il tipo di frutta che si sente. Uno Chardonnay di clima fresco profuma di mela verde e limone; uno di clima caldo di pesca e frutta tropicale come l'ananas. Ribes nero e menta sono tipici del Cabernet Sauvignon, fragola e ciliegia del Pinot Noir.","La maturité du raisin change le type de fruit perçu. Un Chardonnay de climat frais sent la pomme verte et le citron ; un Chardonnay de climat chaud, la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas. Cassis et menthe sont typiques du Cabernet Sauvignon, fraise et cerise du Pinot Noir.","How ripe the grapes are changes the fruit you notice. A cool-climate Chardonnay smells of green apple and lemon; a warm-climate one of peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple. Blackcurrant and mint are typical of Cabernet Sauvignon, and strawberry and cherry of Pinot Noir."]},{"id":"l17f42e55","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi è un aroma della famiglia «altro»?","Lequel de ces arômes appartient à la famille « autres » ?","Which of these aromas belongs to the «other» family?"],"o":[["Funghi","Champignon","Mushroom"],["Ananas","Ananas","Pineapple"],["Vaniglia","Vanille","Vanilla"],["Ribes nero","Cassis","Blackcurrant"]],"e":["Funghi, terra, cuoio, erba e fiori rientrano negli «altri» aromi.","Champignon, terre, cuir, herbe et fleurs font partie des « autres » arômes.","Mushroom, earth, leather, grass and flowers are «other» aromas."],"d":["Gli aromi si dividono in tre famiglie: frutta, rovere e altro. Ananas e ribes nero sono frutta, la vaniglia viene dal rovere. Nella famiglia «altro» rientrano invece erba, fiori, erbe aromatiche, ortaggi, terra, funghi e cuoio. Sono proprio questi aromi a rendere il vino così vario e interessante.","Les arômes se répartissent en trois familles : fruit, chêne et autres. L'ananas et le cassis sont des fruits, la vanille vient du chêne. La famille « autres » regroupe l'herbe, les fleurs, les herbes aromatiques, les légumes, la terre, le champignon et le cuir. Ce sont justement ces arômes qui rendent le vin si varié et passionnant.","Aromas fall into three families: fruit, oak and other. Pineapple and blackcurrant are fruit, and vanilla comes from oak. The «other» family covers grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. These are the aromas that make wine so varied and interesting to explore."]},{"id":"l1508807c","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è lo stile di un vino?","Qu'est-ce que le style d'un vin ?","What is the style of a wine?"],"o":[["L'insieme di colore, struttura e aromi","L'ensemble couleur, structure et arômes","Its colour, structure and aromas combined"],["Solo il vitigno con cui è fatto","Uniquement le cépage utilisé","Only the grape variety it is made from"],["Solo la zona in cui è prodotto","Uniquement la région de production","Only the region where it is produced"],["Solo il suo grado alcolico","Uniquement son degré d'alcool","Only its level of alcohol"]],"e":["Lo stile combina colore, struttura e aromi e sapori.","Le style combine couleur, structure, arômes et saveurs.","Style combines colour, structure, and aromas and flavours."],"d":["Vitigno, zona e alcol influenzano lo stile, ma da soli non lo descrivono. Lo stile è la somma di colore, struttura (dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol, corpo) e aromi e sapori. Per questo due bianchi francesi come Chablis e Sauternes possono avere stili opposti.","Le cépage, la région et l'alcool influencent le style, mais ne le décrivent pas à eux seuls. Le style est la somme de la couleur, de la structure (sucrosité, acidité, tanins, alcool, corps) et des arômes et saveurs. Deux blancs français comme le Chablis et le Sauternes peuvent donc s'opposer.","Grape, region and alcohol all influence style, but none of them describes it alone. Style is the sum of colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. That is how two French whites such as Chablis and Sauternes can be complete opposites."]},{"id":"l180fa384","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che effetto ha un clima fresco sulle uve?","Quel effet a un climat frais sur le raisin ?","What effect does a cool climate have on the grapes?"],"o":[["Meno zucchero e più acidità","Moins de sucre et plus d'acidité","Less sugar and more acidity"],["Più zucchero e meno acidità","Plus de sucre et moins d'acidité","More sugar and less acidity"],["Più tannino e più colore","Plus de tanin et plus de couleur","More tannin and more colour"],["Sapori più maturi e tropicali","Des saveurs plus mûres et tropicales","Riper, more tropical flavours"]],"e":["Più fa fresco, meno zucchero e più acidità hanno le uve.","Plus il fait frais, moins le raisin a de sucre et plus il a d'acidité.","The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acid the grapes have."],"d":["In generale, più il clima è fresco, più le uve restano acide e meno zuccherine; più è caldo, più zucchero e meno acidità, con sapori più maturi. Per questo i vini di clima fresco tendono a essere più freschi e leggeri, con frutta verde e agrumi.","En général, plus le climat est frais, plus le raisin reste acide et peu sucré ; plus il est chaud, plus il a de sucre et moins d'acidité, avec des saveurs plus mûres. C'est pourquoi les vins de climat frais sont souvent plus frais et légers, aux fruits verts et agrumes.","As a rule, the cooler the climate, the more acidic and the less sugary the grapes stay; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, with riper flavours. That is why cool-climate wines tend to be fresher and lighter, with green fruit and citrus."]},{"id":"l183b7062","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Come si presenta di solito uno Chardonnay di clima fresco?","Comment se présente en général un Chardonnay de climat frais ?","What is a cool-climate Chardonnay usually like?"],"o":[["Acidità alta, corpo leggero-medio, mela e limone","Acidité élevée, corps léger à moyen, pomme et citron","High acidity, light to medium body, apple and lemon"],["Acidità media, corpo pieno, ananas e banana","Acidité moyenne, corps ample, ananas et banane","Medium acidity, full body, pineapple and banana"],["Acidità bassa, corpo pieno, miele e albicocca","Acidité faible, corps ample, miel et abricot","Low acidity, full body, honey and apricot"],["Acidità media, corpo leggero, pera e fiori","Acidité moyenne, corps léger, poire et fleurs","Medium acidity, light body, pear and flowers"]],"e":["Il clima fresco mantiene alta l'acidità e dà frutta verde e agrumi.","Le climat frais garde l'acidité élevée et donne fruits verts et agrumes.","A cool climate keeps acidity high and gives green fruit and citrus."],"d":["Nei climi freschi le uve maturano meno, quindi hanno più acidità e meno zucchero. Lo Chardonnay che ne nasce ha acidità alta, corpo da leggero a medio e aromi di mela e limone. Lo Chablis, dalla parte più fresca di Burgundy, ne è l'esempio classico.","En climat frais, le raisin mûrit moins : il a plus d'acidité et moins de sucre. Le Chardonnay obtenu a une acidité élevée, un corps léger à moyen et des arômes de pomme et de citron. Le Chablis, issu de la partie la plus fraîche de la Bourgogne, en est l'exemple classique.","In cool climates the grapes ripen less, so they keep more acidity and less sugar. The resulting Chardonnay has high acidity, a light to medium body and aromas of apple and lemon. Chablis, from the coolest part of Burgundy, is the classic example of this style."]},{"id":"l1c0cbf68","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quali sapori ricorda uno Chardonnay di clima caldo?","Quelles saveurs évoque un Chardonnay de climat chaud ?","Which flavours does a warm-climate Chardonnay show?"],"o":[["Pesca, ananas e banana","Pêche, ananas et banane","Peach, pineapple and banana"],["Mela verde e limone","Pomme verte et citron","Green apple and lemon"],["Pompelmo, asparago ed erba","Pamplemousse, asperge et herbe","Grapefruit, asparagus and grass"],["Ribes nero, menta e cedro","Cassis, menthe et cèdre","Blackcurrant, mint and cedar"]],"e":["Con il caldo le uve maturano di più: frutta a nocciolo e tropicale.","Avec la chaleur, le raisin mûrit davantage : fruits à noyau et tropicaux.","Warmth ripens the grapes further, giving stone and tropical fruit."],"d":["Lo Chardonnay di clima caldo ha uve più mature: acidità media, corpo da medio a pieno e sapori di pesca, ananas e banana. Mela verde e limone indicano invece un clima fresco. Pompelmo e asparago fanno pensare al Sauvignon Blanc, ribes nero e menta al Cabernet Sauvignon.","Le Chardonnay de climat chaud provient de raisins plus mûrs : acidité moyenne, corps moyen à ample, saveurs de pêche, d'ananas et de banane. La pomme verte et le citron signalent au contraire un climat frais. Pamplemousse et asperge évoquent le Sauvignon Blanc, cassis et menthe le Cabernet Sauvignon.","Warm-climate Chardonnay comes from riper grapes: medium acidity, medium to full body, and flavours of peach, pineapple and banana. Green apple and lemon point instead to a cool climate. Grapefruit and asparagus suggest Sauvignon Blanc, while blackcurrant and mint suggest Cabernet Sauvignon."]},{"id":"l19f2c652","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Con quale vitigno si fanno i bianchi di Burgundy?","Avec quel cépage fait-on les blancs de Bourgogne ?","Which grape is used for white Burgundy?"],"o":[["Chardonnay","Chardonnay","Chardonnay"],["Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc"],["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"]],"e":["I bianchi di Burgundy, Chablis compreso, sono fatti con Chardonnay.","Les blancs de Bourgogne, Chablis compris, sont faits de Chardonnay.","White Burgundy, including Chablis, is made from Chardonnay."],"d":["Burgundy (Bourgogne) è la regione francese di riferimento per lo Chardonnay. I suoi bianchi sono di corpo medio, con acidità alta, limone e pesca e a volte vaniglia del rovere. Anche lo Chablis, dalla parte più fresca della regione, è Chardonnay. Il Sauvignon Blanc è invece l'uva del Sancerre.","La Bourgogne (Burgundy) est la région française de référence pour le Chardonnay. Ses blancs ont un corps moyen, une acidité élevée, des notes de citron et de pêche et parfois de vanille du chêne. Le Chablis, issu de la partie la plus fraîche, est aussi du Chardonnay. Le Sauvignon Blanc est le cépage du Sancerre.","Burgundy (Bourgogne) is France's benchmark region for Chardonnay. Its whites are medium-bodied with high acidity, lemon and peach, and sometimes vanilla from oak. Chablis, from the coolest part of the region, is also Chardonnay. Sauvignon Blanc, by contrast, is the grape of Sancerre."]},{"id":"l1ce6cc49","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Perché lo Chablis ha un'acidità alta?","Pourquoi le Chablis a-t-il une acidité élevée ?","Why does Chablis have high acidity?"],"o":[["Viene dalla parte più fresca di Burgundy","Il vient de la partie la plus fraîche de la Bourgogne","It comes from the coolest part of Burgundy"],["Viene affinato a lungo in rovere nuovo","Il est longuement élevé en chêne neuf","It is aged for a long time in new oak"],["È fatto con uve nere pressate","Il est fait de raisins noirs pressés","It is made from pressed black grapes"],["Le uve vengono raccolte molto mature","Le raisin est vendangé très mûr","The grapes are picked very ripe"]],"e":["Il clima fresco fa maturare meno le uve, che restano più acide.","Le climat frais limite la maturité : le raisin reste plus acide.","A cool climate limits ripening, so the grapes stay more acidic."],"d":["Lo Chablis nasce dalla zona più fresca di Burgundy. Lì le uve maturano meno: restano più acide e danno sapori di mela verde e limone. Ne risulta un bianco secco, di corpo leggero o medio, di solito senza rovere. Uve molto mature darebbero, al contrario, meno acidità.","Le Chablis vient de la zone la plus fraîche de la Bourgogne. Le raisin y mûrit moins : il reste plus acide et donne des saveurs de pomme verte et de citron. On obtient un blanc sec, léger à moyen en corps, en général sans chêne. Un raisin très mûr donnerait, au contraire, moins d'acidité.","Chablis comes from the coolest area of Burgundy. There the grapes ripen less, so they stay more acidic and give green apple and lemon flavours. The result is a dry white, light to medium in body, usually with no oak. Very ripe grapes would do the opposite and give lower acidity."]},{"id":"l12156d84","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Da dove vengono le note di vaniglia in alcuni bianchi di Burgundy?","D'où viennent les notes de vanille de certains Bourgogne blancs ?","Where do vanilla notes in some white Burgundies come from?"],"o":[["Dall'affinamento in rovere","De l'élevage en fût de chêne","Maturation in oak"],["Dal clima fresco della regione","Du climat frais de la région","The region's cool climate"],["Dalle bucce delle uve","De la peau des raisins","The grape skins"],["Dall'acciaio inox","De la cuve inox","Stainless steel tanks"]],"e":["La vaniglia è un aroma tipico del passaggio in rovere.","La vanille est un arôme typique du passage en chêne.","Vanilla is a typical aroma from time in oak."],"d":["I bianchi di Burgundy possono essere affinati in rovere oppure no. Quando passano in botte, il legno aggiunge note di vaniglia ai profumi di limone e pesca. L'acciaio inox, al contrario, non cede aromi, e il clima fresco influisce su acidità e tipo di frutta, non sulla vaniglia.","Les Bourgogne blancs peuvent être élevés en chêne ou non. Quand ils passent en fût, le bois ajoute des notes de vanille aux arômes de citron et de pêche. La cuve inox, elle, n'apporte pas d'arôme, et le climat frais agit sur l'acidité et le type de fruit, pas sur la vanille.","White Burgundy can be matured in oak or not. When it spends time in barrel, the wood adds vanilla notes to the lemon and peach aromas. Stainless steel, by contrast, adds no aromas, and the cool climate affects acidity and the type of fruit rather than vanilla."]},{"id":"l105445c9","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Nello Champagne, lo Chardonnay è spesso unito a quale vitigno?","Dans le Champagne, à quel cépage le Chardonnay est-il souvent assemblé ?","In Champagne, Chardonnay is often blended with which grape?"],"o":[["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"],["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"],["Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc"]],"e":["Lo Champagne si fa con Chardonnay e Pinot Noir.","Le Champagne est fait de Chardonnay et de Pinot Noir.","Champagne is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir."],"d":["Lo Champagne, il celebre spumante francese, nasce da Chardonnay e Pinot Noir, spesso uniti. Il Pinot Noir è un'uva nera, ma il suo succo è incolore: separando subito le bucce si ottiene un vino bianco. Merlot e Riesling non sono vitigni dello Champagne.","Le Champagne, célèbre effervescent français, est fait de Chardonnay et de Pinot Noir, souvent assemblés. Le Pinot Noir est un raisin noir, mais son jus est incolore : en séparant tout de suite les peaux, on obtient un vin blanc. Le Merlot et le Riesling ne sont pas des cépages du Champagne.","Champagne, the famous French sparkling wine, is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, often blended together. Pinot Noir is a black grape, but its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a white wine. Merlot and Riesling are not Champagne grapes."]},{"id":"l1a851ac9","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Oltre a Burgundy, quali zone sono famose per lo Chardonnay?","Outre la Bourgogne, quelles régions sont réputées pour le Chardonnay ?","Besides Burgundy, which places are well known for Chardonnay?"],"o":[["Australia e California","Australie et Californie","Australia and California"],["Germania e Alsazia","Allemagne et Alsace","Germany and Alsace"],["Spagna e Portogallo","Espagne et Portugal","Spain and Portugal"],["Nuova Zelanda e Loira","Nouvelle-Zélande et Loire","New Zealand and the Loire"]],"e":["Australia e California sono note per i loro Chardonnay.","L'Australie et la Californie sont réputées pour leurs Chardonnay.","Australia and California are well known for their Chardonnay."],"d":["Lo Chardonnay si coltiva in molti paesi, ma oltre a Burgundy sono particolarmente note Australia e California, spesso con stili più caldi e fruttati. Germania e Alsazia sono famose per il Riesling, Nuova Zelanda e Loira (Sancerre) per il Sauvignon Blanc.","Le Chardonnay est cultivé dans de nombreux pays, mais outre la Bourgogne, l'Australie et la Californie sont particulièrement réputées, souvent pour des styles plus chauds et fruités. L'Allemagne et l'Alsace sont connues pour le Riesling, la Nouvelle-Zélande et la Loire (Sancerre) pour le Sauvignon Blanc.","Chardonnay is grown in many countries, but besides Burgundy, Australia and California are especially well known, often for warmer, fruitier styles. Germany and Alsace are famous for Riesling, while New Zealand and the Loire (Sancerre) are famous for Sauvignon Blanc."]},{"id":"l118cf491","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quali note erbacee sono tipiche del Sauvignon Blanc?","Quelles notes herbacées sont typiques du Sauvignon Blanc ?","Which herbaceous notes are typical of Sauvignon Blanc?"],"o":[["Asparago, peperone verde, erba","Asperge, poivron vert, herbe","Asparagus, green bell pepper, grass"],["Vaniglia, cocco, affumicato","Vanille, noix de coco, fumé","Vanilla, coconut, smoke"],["Miele, albicocca, pesca","Miel, abricot, pêche","Honey, apricot, peach"],["Pepe nero, liquirizia, mora","Poivre noir, réglisse, mûre","Black pepper, liquorice, blackberry"]],"e":["Il Sauvignon Blanc unisce frutta fresca a note di asparago, peperone ed erba.","Le Sauvignon Blanc associe fruit frais et notes d'asperge, de poivron et d'herbe.","Sauvignon Blanc pairs fresh fruit with asparagus, green pepper and grass."],"d":["Oltre alla frutta (mela, pompelmo, frutto della passione), il Sauvignon Blanc mostra spesso note erbacee: asparago, peperone verde ed erba tagliata. Vaniglia, cocco e affumicato vengono dal rovere; pepe nero e liquirizia sono tipici di Syrah/Shiraz; miele e albicocca del Sauternes.","En plus du fruit (pomme, pamplemousse, fruit de la passion), le Sauvignon Blanc montre souvent des notes herbacées : asperge, poivron vert, herbe coupée. Vanille, noix de coco et fumé viennent du chêne ; poivre noir et réglisse sont typiques de la Syrah/Shiraz ; miel et abricot du Sauternes.","Besides fruit (apple, grapefruit, passion fruit), Sauvignon Blanc often shows herbaceous notes: asparagus, green bell pepper and cut grass. Vanilla, coconut and smoke come from oak; black pepper and liquorice are typical of Syrah/Shiraz; and honey and apricot belong to Sauternes."]},{"id":"l197f07be","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Perché il Sauvignon Blanc di solito non passa in rovere?","Pourquoi le Sauvignon Blanc n'est-il en général pas élevé en chêne ?","Why is Sauvignon Blanc usually not matured in oak?"],"o":[["Per conservare i suoi aromi tipici","Pour garder ses arômes typiques","To keep its characteristic aromas"],["Per aumentare il tannino del vino","Pour augmenter les tanins du vin","To increase the wine's tannin"],["Per renderlo più dolce","Pour le rendre plus doux","To make the wine sweeter"],["Per dargli un colore più scuro","Pour lui donner une couleur plus foncée","To give it a darker colour"]],"e":["Senza legno restano in primo piano gli aromi intensi del vitigno.","Sans bois, les arômes intenses du cépage restent au premier plan.","Without oak, the grape's intense aromas stay in the spotlight."],"d":["Il Sauvignon Blanc è apprezzato proprio per i suoi profumi intensi di frutta ed erbe. Per proteggerli fermenta spesso in acciaio inox e di solito non viene affinato in rovere, che aggiungerebbe vaniglia e note tostate. Il legno non serve a renderlo più dolce né più scuro.","Le Sauvignon Blanc est apprécié justement pour ses arômes intenses de fruit et d'herbe. Pour les protéger, il fermente souvent en cuve inox et n'est en général pas élevé en chêne, qui ajouterait vanille et notes grillées. Le bois ne sert ni à l'adoucir ni à le foncer.","Sauvignon Blanc is loved precisely for its intense fruity and herbaceous aromas. To protect them, it is often fermented in stainless steel and usually not matured in oak, which would add vanilla and toasty notes. Oak is not used to make it sweeter or darker."]},{"id":"l174d30fd","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quale vino francese è fatto con Sauvignon Blanc?","Quel vin français est fait de Sauvignon Blanc ?","Which French wine is made from Sauvignon Blanc?"],"o":[["Sancerre","Sancerre","Sancerre"],["Chablis","Chablis","Chablis"],["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Côtes du Rhône","Côtes du Rhône","Côtes du Rhône"]],"e":["Il Sancerre, bianco della Loira, è fatto con Sauvignon Blanc.","Le Sancerre, blanc de la Loire, est fait de Sauvignon Blanc.","Sancerre, a white from the Loire, is made from Sauvignon Blanc."],"d":["Il Sancerre è un bianco secco della Valle della Loira, di corpo medio, con mela verde ed erba e acidità alta: è Sauvignon Blanc, anche se l'etichetta di solito non lo dice. Lo Chablis è Chardonnay, mentre Beaujolais e Côtes du Rhône sono vini rossi.","Le Sancerre est un blanc sec de la vallée de la Loire, de corps moyen, avec pomme verte, herbe et acidité élevée : c'est du Sauvignon Blanc, même si l'étiquette ne le dit pas en général. Le Chablis est du Chardonnay, tandis que le Beaujolais et le Côtes du Rhône sont des rouges.","Sancerre is a dry, medium-bodied white from the Loire Valley with green apple, grass and high acidity. It is Sauvignon Blanc, even though the label usually does not say so. Chablis is made from Chardonnay, while Beaujolais and Côtes du Rhône are red wines."]},{"id":"l1586d332","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quale coppia di vini è un classico del Sauvignon Blanc?","Quelle paire de vins est un classique du Sauvignon Blanc ?","Which pair of wines are classic Sauvignon Blanc wines?"],"o":[["Nuova Zelanda Sauvignon Blanc e Sancerre","Sauvignon Blanc de Nouvelle-Zélande et Sancerre","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre"],["Chablis e Burgundy bianco","Chablis et Bourgogne blanc","Chablis and white Burgundy"],["Riesling d'Alsazia e della Mosella","Riesling d'Alsace et de Moselle","Alsace and Mosel Riesling"],["Prosecco e Cava","Prosecco et Cava","Prosecco and Cava"]],"e":["Sono i due vini più popolari citati per il Sauvignon Blanc.","Ce sont les deux vins de Sauvignon Blanc les plus populaires.","They are the two most popular Sauvignon Blanc wines to know."],"d":["Il Sauvignon Blanc della Nuova Zelanda, per esempio di Marlborough, e il Sancerre della Loira sono i due esempi più popolari di questo vitigno: secchi, aromatici, con acidità alta. Chablis e Burgundy bianco sono Chardonnay; Prosecco e Cava sono spumanti fatti con altri vitigni.","Le Sauvignon Blanc de Nouvelle-Zélande, par exemple de Marlborough, et le Sancerre de la Loire sont les deux exemples les plus populaires de ce cépage : secs, aromatiques, à l'acidité élevée. Chablis et Bourgogne blanc sont du Chardonnay ; Prosecco et Cava sont des effervescents d'autres cépages.","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc, from Marlborough for example, and Sancerre from the Loire are the two most popular examples of the grape: dry, aromatic and high in acidity. Chablis and white Burgundy are Chardonnay, while Prosecco and Cava are sparkling wines made from other grapes."]},{"id":"l1df10096","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quali sono acidità e corpo tipici del Sauvignon Blanc?","Quels sont l'acidité et le corps typiques du Sauvignon Blanc ?","What acidity and body are typical of Sauvignon Blanc?"],"o":[["Acidità alta, corpo leggero-medio","Acidité élevée, corps léger à moyen","High acidity, light to medium body"],["Acidità bassa, corpo pieno","Acidité faible, corps ample","Low acidity, full body"],["Acidità media, corpo pieno","Acidité moyenne, corps ample","Medium acidity, full body"],["Acidità bassa, corpo leggero","Acidité faible, corps léger","Low acidity, light body"]],"e":["Il Sauvignon Blanc è fresco e vivace: acidità alta, corpo leggero-medio.","Le Sauvignon Blanc est vif : acidité élevée, corps léger à moyen.","Sauvignon Blanc is crisp: high acidity with a light to medium body."],"d":["Il Sauvignon Blanc dà vini secchi con un'acidità alta e rinfrescante e un corpo da leggero a medio. Insieme ai profumi intensi di frutta ed erba, questa freschezza ne definisce lo stile. Un corpo pieno con acidità media fa pensare piuttosto a uno Chardonnay di clima caldo.","Le Sauvignon Blanc donne des vins secs, à l'acidité élevée et rafraîchissante, au corps léger à moyen. Avec ses arômes intenses de fruit et d'herbe, cette fraîcheur définit son style. Un corps ample avec une acidité moyenne évoquerait plutôt un Chardonnay de climat chaud.","Sauvignon Blanc makes dry wines with refreshingly high acidity and a light to medium body. Together with its intense fruity and herbaceous aromas, that freshness defines its style. A full body with medium acidity would point more towards a warm-climate Chardonnay."]},{"id":"l1d90bad1","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quale gamma di frutta si trova nel Sauvignon Blanc?","Quelle gamme de fruits trouve-t-on dans le Sauvignon Blanc ?","Which range of fruit is found in Sauvignon Blanc?"],"o":[["Mela, pompelmo, frutto della passione","Pomme, pamplemousse, fruit de la passion","Apple, grapefruit, passion fruit"],["Ribes nero, ciliegia nera, mora","Cassis, cerise noire, mûre","Blackcurrant, black cherry, blackberry"],["Fragola, lampone, ciliegia rossa","Fraise, framboise, cerise rouge","Strawberry, raspberry, red cherry"],["Albicocca, miele, pesca matura","Abricot, miel, pêche mûre","Apricot, honey, ripe peach"]],"e":["Il Sauvignon Blanc va dalla frutta verde agli agrumi ai tropicali.","Le Sauvignon Blanc va du fruit vert aux agrumes et aux fruits tropicaux.","Sauvignon Blanc ranges from green fruit to citrus to tropical fruit."],"d":["Gli aromi di frutta del Sauvignon Blanc vanno dalla mela verde al pompelmo fino al frutto della passione, spesso con note erbacee. La frutta nera è tipica dei rossi come il Cabernet Sauvignon, quella rossa del Pinot Noir, mentre albicocca e miele ricordano il Sauternes. Riconoscere la famiglia di frutta è il primo passo per indovinare il vitigno.","Les arômes fruités du Sauvignon Blanc vont de la pomme verte au pamplemousse jusqu'au fruit de la passion, souvent avec des notes herbacées. Les fruits noirs sont typiques de rouges comme le Cabernet Sauvignon, les fruits rouges du Pinot Noir, et l'abricot et le miel évoquent le Sauternes. Reconnaître la famille de fruits est le premier pas pour deviner le cépage.","Sauvignon Blanc's fruit aromas run from green apple through grapefruit to passion fruit, often with herbaceous notes. Black fruit is typical of reds like Cabernet Sauvignon, red fruit of Pinot Noir, while apricot and honey bring Sauternes to mind. Recognising the family of fruit is the first step towards naming the grape."]},{"id":"l108306c7","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde a un Pinot Grigio?","Quelle description correspond à un Pinot Grigio ?","Which description matches a Pinot Grigio?"],"o":[["Secco, leggero, pera e limone","Sec, léger, poire et citron","Dry, light-bodied, pear and lemon"],["Dolce, pieno, albicocca e miele","Doux, ample, abricot et miel","Sweet, full-bodied, apricot and honey"],["Secco, pieno, ananas e vaniglia","Sec, ample, ananas et vanille","Dry, full-bodied, pineapple and vanilla"],["Medio, leggero, fragola e lampone","Demi-doux, léger, fraise et framboise","Medium, light, strawberry and raspberry"]],"e":["Il Pinot Grigio è di solito secco, leggero, con pera e limone.","Le Pinot Grigio est en général sec, léger, sur la poire et le citron.","Pinot Grigio is usually dry and light, with pear and lemon."],"d":["Il Pinot Grigio dà vini di solito secchi, di corpo leggero, con acidità da media ad alta e sapori semplici di pera e limone. Le altre descrizioni corrispondono ad altri vini: il Sauternes (dolce, albicocca e miele), uno Chardonnay caldo e passato in legno, e il White Zinfandel. Pensa a un bianco semplice e fresco.","Le Pinot Grigio donne des vins en général secs, légers, à l'acidité moyenne à élevée, aux saveurs simples de poire et de citron. Les autres descriptions correspondent à d'autres vins : le Sauternes (doux, abricot et miel), un Chardonnay de climat chaud boisé et le White Zinfandel. Pensez à un blanc simple et frais.","Pinot Grigio usually makes dry, light-bodied wines with medium to high acidity and simple pear and lemon flavours. The other descriptions fit other wines: Sauternes (sweet, apricot and honey), an oaked warm-climate Chardonnay, and White Zinfandel. Think of it as a simple, fresh and easy white."]},{"id":"l1067a05d","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["A quale paese è legato soprattutto il Pinot Grigio?","À quel pays le Pinot Grigio est-il surtout associé ?","Which country is Pinot Grigio mainly associated with?"],"o":[["Italia","Italie","Italy"],["Germania","Allemagne","Germany"],["Spagna","Espagne","Spain"],["Nuova Zelanda","Nouvelle-Zélande","New Zealand"]],"e":["Il Pinot Grigio è legato soprattutto all'Italia, ma si coltiva anche altrove.","Le Pinot Grigio est surtout associé à l'Italie, mais il est cultivé ailleurs aussi.","Pinot Grigio is mainly linked with Italy, though grown elsewhere too."],"d":["Il Pinot Grigio è un vitigno molto popolare associato soprattutto all'Italia, con zone come il Veneto o il Trentino, anche se si coltiva in diversi altri paesi. La Germania è la patria classica del Riesling, la Nuova Zelanda è nota per il Sauvignon Blanc e il Pinot Noir.","Le Pinot Grigio est un cépage très populaire, surtout associé à l'Italie, avec des zones comme la Vénétie ou le Trentin, même s'il est cultivé dans plusieurs autres pays. L'Allemagne est la patrie classique du Riesling, et la Nouvelle-Zélande est connue pour le Sauvignon Blanc et le Pinot Noir.","Pinot Grigio is a hugely popular grape mainly associated with Italy, in areas such as Veneto or Trentino, although it is grown in several other countries too. Germany is the classic home of Riesling, and New Zealand is known for Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Noir."]},{"id":"l1643c9fc","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Perché il Pinot Grigio fermenta di solito in acciaio senza rovere?","Pourquoi le Pinot Grigio fermente-t-il en général en inox, sans chêne ?","Why is Pinot Grigio usually made in stainless steel without oak?"],"o":[["Per conservarne i sapori fruttati","Pour préserver ses saveurs fruitées","To keep its fruity flavours"],["Per aggiungere note di vaniglia","Pour ajouter des notes de vanille","To add notes of vanilla"],["Per aumentarne il tannino","Pour augmenter ses tanins","To increase its tannin"],["Per renderlo più alcolico","Pour le rendre plus alcoolisé","To make it higher in alcohol"]],"e":["L'acciaio non aggiunge aromi e lascia intatta la frutta delicata.","L'inox n'ajoute pas d'arômes et laisse intact un fruit délicat.","Steel adds no aromas, so the delicate fruit stays intact."],"d":["Il Pinot Grigio ha sapori delicati di pera e limone. Fermentandolo in acciaio inox e senza affinamento in rovere, la cantina ne protegge la frutta e la leggerezza. Il rovere aggiungerebbe proprio la vaniglia, mentre tannino e alcol non dipendono dal recipiente usato.","Le Pinot Grigio a des saveurs délicates de poire et de citron. En le faisant fermenter en cuve inox, sans élevage en chêne, on protège son fruit et sa légèreté. Le chêne ajouterait justement de la vanille, tandis que les tanins et l'alcool ne dépendent pas du contenant.","Pinot Grigio has delicate pear and lemon flavours. Fermenting it in stainless steel and skipping oak maturation protects that fruit and lightness. Oak would add exactly the vanilla notes the style avoids, while tannin and alcohol do not depend on the vessel used."]},{"id":"l1f46269d","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quale gamma di dolcezza può avere il Riesling?","Quelle gamme de sucrosité le Riesling peut-il avoir ?","What range of sweetness can Riesling have?"],"o":[["Da secco a dolce, sempre molto acido","Du sec au doux, toujours très acide","Dry to sweet, always with high acidity"],["Sempre dolce, con acidità bassa","Toujours doux, avec une acidité faible","Always sweet, with low acidity"],["Sempre secco, con acidità bassa","Toujours sec, avec une acidité faible","Always dry, with low acidity"],["Solo medio, con acidità media","Uniquement demi-doux, acidité moyenne","Only medium, with medium acidity"]],"e":["Il Riesling può essere secco, medio o dolce, ma è sempre molto acido.","Le Riesling peut être sec, demi-doux ou doux, mais toujours très acide.","Riesling can be dry, medium or sweet, but always has high acidity."],"d":["Il Riesling è versatile: dà vini secchi, di dolcezza media o dolci. Ciò che non cambia è l'acidità alta, che bilancia lo zucchero e mantiene il vino fresco. Per questo, leggendo «Riesling» in etichetta, conviene guardare l'origine o la descrizione per capire quanto sarà dolce.","Le Riesling est polyvalent : il donne des vins secs, demi-doux ou doux. Ce qui ne change pas, c'est l'acidité élevée, qui équilibre le sucre et garde le vin frais. Face à « Riesling » sur une étiquette, mieux vaut donc regarder l'origine ou la description pour deviner la sucrosité.","Riesling is versatile: it makes dry, medium and sweet wines. What does not change is its high acidity, which balances the sugar and keeps the wine fresh. So when you see «Riesling» on a label, check the origin or the description to work out how sweet it will be."]},{"id":"l11947379","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Qual è il paese classico del Riesling?","Quel est le pays classique du Riesling ?","Which country is the classic home of Riesling?"],"o":[["Germania","Allemagne","Germany"],["Italia","Italie","Italy"],["Spagna","Espagne","Spain"],["Cile","Chili","Chile"]],"e":["La Germania è la patria classica del Riesling, dal secco al dolce.","L'Allemagne est la patrie classique du Riesling, du sec au doux.","Germany is Riesling's classic home, making it from dry to sweet."],"d":["Il Riesling è il vitigno classico della Germania, dove si producono vini in tutta la gamma di dolcezza, dal secco al dolce. Ottimi Riesling secchi arrivano anche dall'Alsazia, in Francia, e dall'Australia. L'Italia è invece associata soprattutto al Pinot Grigio tra i bianchi principali.","Le Riesling est le cépage classique de l'Allemagne, où l'on produit toute la gamme de sucrosité, du sec au doux. De très bons Riesling secs viennent aussi d'Alsace, en France, et d'Australie. L'Italie est surtout associée au Pinot Grigio parmi les grands blancs.","Riesling is the classic grape of Germany, where it is made across the full sweetness range, from dry to sweet. Fine dry Rieslings also come from Alsace in France and from Australia. Among the key white grapes, Italy is linked mainly with Pinot Grigio."]},{"id":"l16a751da","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["In quale stile si producono i Riesling di Alsazia e Australia?","Dans quel style l'Alsace et l'Australie produisent-elles leurs Riesling ?","In which style do Alsace and Australia make Riesling?"],"o":[["Secco","Sec","Dry"],["Dolce","Doux","Sweet"],["Spumante","Effervescent","Sparkling"],["Fortificato","Fortifié","Fortified"]],"e":["Alsazia e Australia sono note per Riesling in stile secco.","L'Alsace et l'Australie sont connues pour des Riesling secs.","Alsace and Australia are known for dry Riesling."],"d":["Mentre la Germania produce Riesling dal secco al dolce, l'Alsazia in Francia e l'Australia lo fanno in stile secco. Sono vini molto freschi, con agrumi come lime e limone, note floreali e talvolta pesca. Riconoscere l'origine aiuta quindi a prevedere la dolcezza.","Alors que l'Allemagne produit des Riesling du sec au doux, l'Alsace et l'Australie le font en style sec. Ce sont des vins très frais, aux notes d'agrumes comme le citron vert et le citron, de fleurs et parfois de pêche. Connaître l'origine aide donc à prévoir la sucrosité.","While Germany makes Riesling from dry to sweet, Alsace in France and Australia make it in a dry style. These are very fresh wines with citrus such as lime and lemon, floral notes and sometimes peach. Knowing the origin therefore helps you predict the sweetness."]},{"id":"l1e4f3176","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Perché un Riesling dolce non risulta stucchevole?","Pourquoi un Riesling doux n'est-il pas écœurant ?","Why does a sweet Riesling not taste cloying?"],"o":[["L'acidità alta bilancia la dolcezza","L'acidité élevée équilibre la douceur","Its high acidity balances the sweetness"],["Il rovere copre lo zucchero","Le chêne masque le sucre","Oak flavours mask the sugar"],["Il tannino asciuga la bocca","Le tanin assèche la bouche","Tannin dries out the mouth"],["L'alcol alto nasconde lo zucchero","L'alcool élevé cache le sucre","High alcohol hides the sugar"]],"e":["Tutti i Riesling sono molto acidi e l'acidità fa da contrappeso allo zucchero.","Tous les Riesling sont très acides, et l'acidité fait contrepoids au sucre.","All Rieslings are high in acid, which counterbalances the sugar."],"d":["Il Riesling ha sempre un'acidità alta. Nei vini dolci o medi questa acidità bilancia lo zucchero e mantiene il sorso fresco. Il Riesling di solito non passa in rovere, è un vino bianco quindi quasi privo di tannino, e i Riesling dolci tedeschi sono spesso poco alcolici.","Le Riesling a toujours une acidité élevée. Dans les vins doux ou demi-doux, elle équilibre le sucre et garde la gorgée fraîche. Le Riesling n'est en général pas élevé en chêne, c'est un blanc donc pratiquement sans tanin, et les Riesling doux allemands sont souvent peu alcoolisés.","Riesling always has high acidity. In sweet or medium wines, that acidity balances the sugar and keeps each sip fresh. Riesling is usually not oaked, as a white wine it has almost no tannin, and sweet German Rieslings are often low in alcohol, so the other options do not apply."]},{"id":"l151dbc30","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi può mostrare un Riesling?","Quels arômes un Riesling peut-il montrer ?","Which aromas can a Riesling show?"],"o":[["Fiori, lime, pesca","Fleurs, citron vert, pêche","Floral, lime, peach"],["Vaniglia, cedro, affumicato","Vanille, cèdre, fumé","Vanilla, cedar, smoke"],["Pepe nero, liquirizia, mora","Poivre noir, réglisse, mûre","Black pepper, liquorice, blackberry"],["Ribes nero, menta, peperone","Cassis, menthe, poivron","Blackcurrant, mint, bell pepper"]],"e":["Il Riesling va dai fiori e dagli agrumi fino alla frutta a nocciolo.","Le Riesling va des fleurs et des agrumes jusqu'aux fruits à noyau.","Riesling ranges from floral and citrus aromas to stone fruit."],"d":["Il Riesling ha profumi intensi che possono andare da fiori e mela verde ad agrumi come lime e limone, fino a pesca e albicocca. Non passa di solito in rovere, quindi vaniglia, cedro e affumicato non sono tipici. Pepe nero e ribes nero appartengono a vitigni rossi.","Le Riesling a des arômes intenses qui vont des fleurs et de la pomme verte aux agrumes comme le citron vert et le citron, jusqu'à la pêche et l'abricot. Il n'est en général pas boisé : vanille, cèdre et fumé ne sont pas typiques. Poivre noir et cassis appartiennent à des cépages rouges.","Riesling has pronounced aromas that can range from flowers and green apple to citrus such as lime and lemon, and on to peach and apricot. It is usually unoaked, so vanilla, cedar and smoke are not typical. Black pepper and blackcurrant belong to black grape varieties."]},{"id":"l1a0f4cf0","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quale dei quattro bianchi principali è più spesso affinato in rovere?","Lequel des quatre grands blancs est le plus souvent élevé en chêne ?","Which of the four key white grapes is most often matured in oak?"],"o":[["Chardonnay","Chardonnay","Chardonnay"],["Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"]],"e":["Lo Chardonnay può passare in rovere; gli altri tre di solito no.","Le Chardonnay peut être boisé ; les trois autres en général non.","Chardonnay can be oaked; the other three usually are not."],"d":["Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio e Riesling fermentano spesso in acciaio inox e di solito non passano in rovere, per proteggere i loro aromi fruttati. Lo Chardonnay, invece, viene spesso affinato in legno, che aggiunge vaniglia: pensiamo a molti bianchi di Burgundy o agli Chardonnay californiani.","Le Sauvignon Blanc, le Pinot Grigio et le Riesling fermentent souvent en cuve inox et ne sont en général pas élevés en chêne, pour protéger leur fruit. Le Chardonnay, lui, est souvent élevé en fût, ce qui apporte de la vanille : pensons à de nombreux Bourgogne blancs ou aux Chardonnay californiens.","Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling are often fermented in stainless steel and usually not matured in oak, to protect their fruity aromas. Chardonnay, on the other hand, is often aged in oak, which adds vanilla: think of many white Burgundies or Californian Chardonnays."]},{"id":"l14c9b7eb","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["In carta: «corpo pieno, frutta tropicale matura e vaniglia». Quale vino è?","Sur une carte : « corsé, fruit tropical mûr et vanille ». Quel vin est-ce ?","A wine list says «full-bodied, ripe tropical fruit and vanilla». Which wine is it?"],"o":[["Uno Chardonnay della California","Un Chardonnay de Californie","A Californian Chardonnay"],["Uno Chablis","Un Chablis","A Chablis"],["Un Pinot Grigio italiano","Un Pinot Grigio italien","An Italian Pinot Grigio"],["Un Riesling dell'Alsazia","Un Riesling d'Alsace","An Alsace Riesling"]],"e":["Clima caldo e rovere danno corpo, frutta tropicale e vaniglia.","Climat chaud et chêne donnent corps, fruit tropical et vanille.","Warm climate plus oak gives body, tropical fruit and vanilla."],"d":["La frutta tropicale matura indica un clima caldo, la vaniglia indica il rovere e il corpo pieno completa il quadro: è lo stile di uno Chardonnay californiano. Lo Chablis è leggero e senza legno, il Pinot Grigio è leggero con pera e limone, il Riesling d'Alsazia è secco, floreale e senza rovere.","Le fruit tropical mûr signale un climat chaud, la vanille indique le chêne, et le corps ample complète le tableau : c'est le style d'un Chardonnay californien. Le Chablis est léger et sans bois, le Pinot Grigio léger sur la poire et le citron, et le Riesling d'Alsace sec, floral et sans chêne.","Ripe tropical fruit points to a warm climate, vanilla points to oak, and a full body completes the picture: this is the style of a Californian Chardonnay. Chablis is light and unoaked, Pinot Grigio is light with pear and lemon, and Alsace Riesling is dry, floral and unoaked."]},{"id":"l149961dc","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["Quale vitigno bianco si usa per lo Champagne?","Quel cépage blanc entre dans le Champagne ?","Which white grape is used to make Champagne?"],"o":[["Chardonnay","Chardonnay","Chardonnay"],["Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"]],"e":["Lo Chardonnay è il vitigno bianco dello Champagne, spesso con il Pinot Noir.","Le Chardonnay est le cépage blanc du Champagne, souvent avec le Pinot Noir.","Chardonnay is Champagne's white grape, often blended with Pinot Noir."],"d":["Tra i quattro bianchi principali, solo lo Chardonnay entra nello Champagne, dove viene spesso unito al Pinot Noir, un'uva nera. Il risultato è uno spumante di solito secco, con acidità alta, mela verde, limone e note di pane tostato. Gli altri tre vitigni non sono uve dello Champagne.","Parmi les quatre grands blancs, seul le Chardonnay entre dans le Champagne, où il est souvent assemblé au Pinot Noir, un raisin noir. On obtient un effervescent en général sec, à l'acidité élevée, aux notes de pomme verte, de citron et de pain grillé. Les trois autres cépages ne sont pas des raisins du Champagne.","Of the four key white grapes, only Chardonnay goes into Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir, a black grape. The result is a sparkling wine that is usually dry, with high acidity, green apple, lemon and notes of toasted bread. The other three grapes are not used for Champagne."]},{"id":"l1429d652","c":"w2","p":0,"q":["In carta: «Australia, secco, profumi di lime e fiori». Quale vitigno è?","Sur une carte : « Australie, sec, arômes de citron vert et de fleurs ». Quel cépage ?","A list says «Australia, dry, aromas of lime and blossom». Which grape is it?"],"o":[["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"],["Chardonnay","Chardonnay","Chardonnay"],["Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"]],"e":["Lime e fiori in un bianco secco australiano indicano il Riesling.","Citron vert et fleurs dans un blanc sec australien désignent le Riesling.","Lime and blossom in a dry Australian white point to Riesling."],"d":["L'Australia produce Riesling in stile secco, con agrumi come il lime e note floreali, sostenuti da un'acidità alta. Lo Chardonnay australiano tende a frutta più matura e spesso vaniglia; il Sauvignon Blanc unisce agrumi a note erbacee; il Pinot Grigio ha pera e limone, senza profumi floreali marcati.","L'Australie produit des Riesling secs, aux agrumes comme le citron vert et aux notes florales, portés par une acidité élevée. Le Chardonnay australien tend vers un fruit plus mûr, souvent vanillé ; le Sauvignon Blanc associe agrumes et notes herbacées ; le Pinot Grigio a poire et citron, sans arômes floraux marqués.","Australia makes Riesling in a dry style, with citrus such as lime and floral notes, carried by high acidity. Australian Chardonnay leans towards riper fruit and often vanilla; Sauvignon Blanc pairs citrus with herbaceous notes; and Pinot Grigio shows pear and lemon without marked floral aromas."]},{"id":"l1dfef3f4","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quale struttura è tipica del Cabernet Sauvignon?","Quelle structure est typique du Cabernet Sauvignon ?","Which structure is typical of Cabernet Sauvignon?"],"o":[["Tannino alto e acidità alta","Tanins élevés et acidité élevée","High tannin and high acidity"],["Tannino basso e acidità alta","Tanins faibles et acidité élevée","Low tannin and high acidity"],["Tannino medio e acidità media","Tanins moyens et acidité moyenne","Medium tannin and medium acidity"],["Tannino basso e acidità bassa","Tanins faibles et acidité faible","Low tannin and low acidity"]],"e":["Il Cabernet Sauvignon è ricco sia di tannino sia di acidità.","Le Cabernet Sauvignon est riche à la fois en tanins et en acidité.","Cabernet Sauvignon is high in both tannin and acidity."],"d":["Il Cabernet Sauvignon dà rossi secchi con tannino alto e acidità alta, di corpo medio o pieno. Il Merlot ha invece tannino e acidità medi, mentre il Pinot Noir ha acidità alta ma tannino da basso a medio. Proprio il tannino alto spiega perché il Cabernet viene spesso unito al Merlot.","Le Cabernet Sauvignon donne des rouges secs aux tanins élevés et à l'acidité élevée, de corps moyen à ample. Le Merlot a des tanins et une acidité moyens, et le Pinot Noir une acidité élevée mais des tanins faibles à moyens. Ce sont ces tanins élevés qui expliquent l'assemblage fréquent avec le Merlot.","Cabernet Sauvignon makes dry reds with high tannin and high acidity, and a medium to full body. Merlot has medium tannin and acidity, while Pinot Noir has high acidity but low to medium tannin. That high tannin is exactly why Cabernet is so often blended with Merlot."]},{"id":"l1592df17","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quale frutto è l'aroma tipico del Cabernet Sauvignon?","Quel fruit est l'arôme typique du Cabernet Sauvignon ?","Which fruit is the signature aroma of Cabernet Sauvignon?"],"o":[["Ribes nero","Cassis","Blackcurrant"],["Fragola","Fraise","Strawberry"],["Pera","Poire","Pear"],["Lampone","Framboise","Raspberry"]],"e":["Il ribes nero è l'aroma simbolo del Cabernet Sauvignon.","Le cassis est l'arôme emblématique du Cabernet Sauvignon.","Blackcurrant is Cabernet Sauvignon's hallmark aroma."],"d":["Il Cabernet Sauvignon profuma di frutti neri, soprattutto ribes nero e ciliegia nera, spesso con note di peperone verde e menta. Fragola e lampone sono frutti rossi tipici del Pinot Noir o del Beaujolais, mentre la pera è legata a bianchi come il Pinot Grigio.","Le Cabernet Sauvignon sent les fruits noirs, surtout le cassis et la cerise noire, souvent avec des notes de poivron vert et de menthe. La fraise et la framboise sont des fruits rouges typiques du Pinot Noir ou du Beaujolais, tandis que la poire est liée à des blancs comme le Pinot Grigio.","Cabernet Sauvignon smells of black fruit, above all blackcurrant and black cherry, often with notes of green bell pepper and mint. Strawberry and raspberry are red fruits typical of Pinot Noir or Beaujolais, while pear belongs to whites such as Pinot Grigio."]},{"id":"l141a4674","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quali note erbacee può avere il Cabernet Sauvignon?","Quelles notes herbacées le Cabernet Sauvignon peut-il avoir ?","Which herbaceous notes can Cabernet Sauvignon show?"],"o":[["Peperone verde e menta","Poivron vert et menthe","Green bell pepper and mint"],["Pepe nero e liquirizia","Poivre noir et réglisse","Black pepper and liquorice"],["Erbe secche e chiodi di garofano","Herbes séchées et clou de girofle","Dried herbs and cloves"],["Fiori e miele","Fleurs et miel","Flowers and honey"]],"e":["Peperone verde e menta accompagnano spesso il ribes nero del Cabernet.","Poivron vert et menthe accompagnent souvent le cassis du Cabernet.","Green pepper and mint often sit alongside Cabernet's blackcurrant."],"d":["Oltre al ribes nero e alla ciliegia nera, il Cabernet Sauvignon ha spesso note erbacee di peperone verde e di menta. Pepe nero e liquirizia sono spezie tipiche di Syrah/Shiraz; le erbe secche si trovano nel Chianti; i chiodi di garofano vengono dal rovere. Le note «verdi» sono quindi un buon indizio per riconoscerlo.","En plus du cassis et de la cerise noire, le Cabernet Sauvignon montre souvent des notes herbacées de poivron vert et de menthe. Poivre noir et réglisse sont des épices typiques de la Syrah/Shiraz ; les herbes séchées se trouvent dans le Chianti ; le clou de girofle vient du chêne. Ces notes « vertes » sont donc un bon indice pour le reconnaître.","Besides blackcurrant and black cherry, Cabernet Sauvignon often shows herbaceous notes of green bell pepper and mint. Black pepper and liquorice are spices typical of Syrah/Shiraz, dried herbs are found in Chianti, and cloves come from oak. Those «green» notes are therefore a useful clue for recognising it."]},{"id":"l1dd31179","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi aggiunge il rovere a un Cabernet Sauvignon?","Quels arômes le chêne ajoute-t-il à un Cabernet Sauvignon ?","Which aromas does oak add to a Cabernet Sauvignon?"],"o":[["Cedro e vaniglia","Cèdre et vanille","Cedar and vanilla"],["Menta e peperone verde","Menthe et poivron vert","Mint and green bell pepper"],["Ribes nero e ciliegia nera","Cassis et cerise noire","Blackcurrant and black cherry"],["Limone e mela verde","Citron et pomme verte","Lemon and green apple"]],"e":["Il rovere porta cedro e vaniglia; frutta e note erbacee vengono dall'uva.","Le chêne apporte cèdre et vanille ; fruit et notes herbacées viennent du raisin.","Oak brings cedar and vanilla; fruit and herbaceous notes come from the grape."],"d":["Il Cabernet Sauvignon viene spesso affinato in rovere, che aggiunge note di cedro e vaniglia. Ribes nero, ciliegia nera, menta e peperone verde, invece, arrivano dall'uva stessa. Saper separare gli aromi dell'uva da quelli del legno aiuta a capire come è stato fatto il vino.","Le Cabernet Sauvignon est souvent élevé en chêne, qui ajoute des notes de cèdre et de vanille. Le cassis, la cerise noire, la menthe et le poivron vert viennent en revanche du raisin lui-même. Distinguer les arômes du raisin de ceux du bois aide à comprendre comment le vin a été fait.","Cabernet Sauvignon is often matured in oak, which adds cedar and vanilla notes. Blackcurrant, black cherry, mint and green bell pepper, on the other hand, come from the grape itself. Separating grape aromas from oak aromas helps you understand how the wine was made."]},{"id":"l15960292","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Perché il Cabernet Sauvignon viene spesso unito al Merlot?","Pourquoi le Cabernet Sauvignon est-il souvent assemblé au Merlot ?","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon often blended with Merlot?"],"o":[["Il Merlot ammorbidisce il tannino e dà corpo","Le Merlot assouplit les tanins et donne du corps","Merlot softens the tannin and adds body"],["Il Merlot aumenta acidità e tannino","Le Merlot augmente acidité et tanins","Merlot raises acidity and tannin"],["Il Merlot rende il vino dolce","Le Merlot rend le vin doux","Merlot makes the wine sweet"],["Il Merlot schiarisce il colore","Le Merlot éclaircit la couleur","Merlot makes the colour lighter"]],"e":["Il tannino alto del Cabernet viene ammorbidito dal Merlot, che aggiunge corpo.","Les tanins élevés du Cabernet sont assouplis par le Merlot, qui ajoute du corps.","Merlot softens Cabernet's high tannin and adds body."],"d":["Il Cabernet Sauvignon ha molto tannino. Unendolo al Merlot, che ha tannino e acidità medi, si ottiene un vino più morbido e con più corpo. Il rapporto funziona anche al contrario: il Cabernet porta al Merlot tannino e acidità. Bordeaux è la regione più famosa per questo taglio.","Le Cabernet Sauvignon a beaucoup de tanins. En l'assemblant au Merlot, aux tanins et à l'acidité moyens, on obtient un vin plus souple et plus ample. Cela fonctionne aussi dans l'autre sens : le Cabernet apporte au Merlot tanins et acidité. Bordeaux est la région la plus célèbre pour cet assemblage.","Cabernet Sauvignon has a lot of tannin. Blending it with Merlot, which has medium tannin and acidity, gives a softer wine with more body. It works the other way round too: Cabernet gives Merlot extra tannin and acidity. Bordeaux is the most famous region for this blend."]},{"id":"l1242ffe1","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["In Australia, con quale vitigno si unisce a volte il Cabernet Sauvignon?","En Australie, avec quel cépage le Cabernet Sauvignon est-il parfois assemblé ?","In Australia, Cabernet Sauvignon is sometimes blended with which grape?"],"o":[["Shiraz","Shiraz","Shiraz"],["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"],["Chardonnay","Chardonnay","Chardonnay"]],"e":["In Australia lo Shiraz porta aromi speziati al Cabernet Sauvignon.","En Australie, la Shiraz apporte des arômes épicés au Cabernet Sauvignon.","In Australia, Shiraz adds spicy aromas to Cabernet Sauvignon."],"d":["Il Cabernet Sauvignon si coltiva molto in Australia, dove talvolta viene unito allo Shiraz, che aggiunge aromi di spezie. Il Pinot Noir, per i vini rossi, di solito non si usa in taglio, mentre Riesling e Chardonnay sono uve bianche e non entrano nei rossi.","Le Cabernet Sauvignon est très cultivé en Australie, où il est parfois assemblé à la Shiraz, qui ajoute des arômes d'épices. Le Pinot Noir n'est en général pas assemblé pour les rouges, et le Riesling et le Chardonnay sont des raisins blancs qui n'entrent pas dans les rouges.","Cabernet Sauvignon is widely grown in Australia, where it is sometimes blended with Shiraz, which adds spicy aromas. Pinot Noir is not usually blended when making red wine, and Riesling and Chardonnay are white grapes that do not go into red blends."]},{"id":"l1762d24b","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quale struttura ha di solito il Merlot?","Quelle structure a en général le Merlot ?","What structure does Merlot usually have?"],"o":[["Acidità e tannino medi, corpo medio-pieno","Acidité et tanins moyens, corps moyen à ample","Medium acidity and tannin, medium to full body"],["Acidità e tannino alti, corpo pieno","Acidité et tanins élevés, corps ample","High acidity and tannin, full body"],["Acidità alta, tannino basso, corpo leggero","Acidité élevée, tanins faibles, corps léger","High acidity, low tannin, light body"],["Acidità bassa, tannino alto, corpo leggero","Acidité faible, tanins élevés, corps léger","Low acidity, high tannin, light body"]],"e":["Il Merlot è morbido: acidità e tannino medi, corpo medio-pieno.","Le Merlot est souple : acidité et tanins moyens, corps moyen à ample.","Merlot is soft: medium acidity and tannin, medium to full body."],"d":["Il Merlot dà vini generalmente secchi, di corpo da medio a pieno, con acidità e tannino medi. Il Cabernet Sauvignon ha invece tannino e acidità alti, mentre il Pinot Noir ha acidità alta, tannino basso o medio e corpo leggero-medio. Per questo il Merlot appare più morbido.","Le Merlot donne des vins généralement secs, au corps moyen à ample, avec une acidité et des tanins moyens. Le Cabernet Sauvignon a des tanins et une acidité élevés, tandis que le Pinot Noir a une acidité élevée, des tanins faibles à moyens et un corps léger à moyen. Le Merlot paraît donc plus souple.","Merlot makes wines that are generally dry, with a medium to full body and medium acidity and tannin. Cabernet Sauvignon has high tannin and acidity, while Pinot Noir has high acidity, low to medium tannin and a light to medium body. That is why Merlot feels softer."]},{"id":"l18cd5ac0","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quali frutti si trovano tipicamente nel Merlot?","Quels fruits trouve-t-on typiquement dans le Merlot ?","Which fruits are typically found in Merlot?"],"o":[["Da fragola e prugna rossa a mora e prugna nera","De la fraise et prune rouge à la mûre et prune noire","Strawberry and red plum through to blackberry and black plum"],["Mela verde, limone e pompelmo","Pomme verte, citron et pamplemousse","Green apple, lemon and grapefruit"],["Albicocca, pesca e miele","Abricot, pêche et miel","Apricot, peach and honey"],["Pera, fiori e lime","Poire, fleurs et citron vert","Pear, flowers and lime"]],"e":["Il Merlot va dai frutti rossi ai frutti neri.","Le Merlot va des fruits rouges aux fruits noirs.","Merlot ranges from red fruit to black fruit."],"d":["Il Merlot può avere sapori di frutti rossi, come fragola e prugna rossa, oppure di frutti neri, come mora e prugna nera. Spesso passa in rovere, che aggiunge vaniglia. Le altre opzioni descrivono aromi di vini bianchi come Sauvignon Blanc, Sauternes o Riesling.","Le Merlot peut avoir des saveurs de fruits rouges, comme la fraise et la prune rouge, ou de fruits noirs, comme la mûre et la prune noire. Il passe souvent en chêne, qui ajoute de la vanille. Les autres réponses décrivent des arômes de blancs comme le Sauvignon Blanc, le Sauternes ou le Riesling.","Merlot can show red fruit such as strawberry and red plum, or black fruit such as blackberry and black plum. It is often matured in oak, which adds vanilla. The other options describe aromas of white wines such as Sauvignon Blanc, Sauternes or Riesling."]},{"id":"l13affb4a","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Che cosa aggiunge il Cabernet Sauvignon a un taglio con il Merlot?","Qu'apporte le Cabernet Sauvignon dans un assemblage avec le Merlot ?","What does Cabernet Sauvignon add to a blend with Merlot?"],"o":[["Tannino e acidità","Tanins et acidité","Tannin and acidity"],["Dolcezza e morbidezza","Sucrosité et souplesse","Sweetness and softness"],["Bollicine e freschezza","Bulles et fraîcheur","Bubbles and freshness"],["Colore chiaro e leggerezza","Couleur claire et légèreté","Pale colour and lightness"]],"e":["Il Cabernet porta tannino e acidità; il Merlot morbidezza e corpo.","Le Cabernet apporte tanins et acidité ; le Merlot souplesse et corps.","Cabernet brings tannin and acidity; Merlot brings softness and body."],"d":["Nel taglio di Bordeaux i due vitigni si completano. Il Merlot, con tannino e acidità medi, porta morbidezza e corpo. Il Cabernet Sauvignon, con tannino e acidità alti, dà al vino struttura e freschezza. Il risultato è un rosso secco, di corpo medio-pieno, con frutti neri e spesso cedro del rovere.","Dans l'assemblage bordelais, les deux cépages se complètent. Le Merlot, aux tanins et à l'acidité moyens, apporte souplesse et corps. Le Cabernet Sauvignon, aux tanins et à l'acidité élevés, donne structure et fraîcheur. On obtient un rouge sec, de corps moyen à ample, aux fruits noirs, souvent avec du cèdre.","In the Bordeaux blend the two grapes complete each other. Merlot, with medium tannin and acidity, brings softness and body. Cabernet Sauvignon, with high tannin and acidity, gives the wine structure and freshness. The result is a dry, medium- to full-bodied red with black fruit, often with cedar from oak."]},{"id":"l19591fec","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quali paesi producono Merlot morbidi e fruttati?","Quels pays produisent des Merlot souples et fruités ?","Which countries make soft, fruity Merlot?"],"o":[["Cile e California","Chili et Californie","Chile and California"],["Germania e Alsazia","Allemagne et Alsace","Germany and Alsace"],["Nuova Zelanda e Loira","Nouvelle-Zélande et Loire","New Zealand and the Loire"],["Portogallo e Spagna","Portugal et Espagne","Portugal and Spain"]],"e":["Cile e California sono citati per i loro Merlot morbidi e fruttati.","Le Chili et la Californie sont connus pour leurs Merlot souples et fruités.","Chile and California are known for soft, fruity Merlot."],"d":["Il Merlot si coltiva in molti luoghi; in Cile e in California se ne fanno vini morbidi, fruttati e facili da bere, spesso con prugna nera e mora. Germania e Alsazia sono legate al Riesling, Nuova Zelanda e Loira al Sauvignon Blanc, il Portogallo al Port.","Le Merlot est cultivé dans de nombreux endroits ; au Chili et en Californie, on en fait des vins souples, fruités et faciles à boire, souvent sur la prune noire et la mûre. L'Allemagne et l'Alsace sont liées au Riesling, la Nouvelle-Zélande et la Loire au Sauvignon Blanc, le Portugal au Port.","Merlot is grown in many places; Chile and California use it for soft, fruity, easy-drinking wines, often with black plum and blackberry. Germany and Alsace are linked with Riesling, New Zealand and the Loire with Sauvignon Blanc, and Portugal with Port."]},{"id":"l16c7cdda","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quale regione è la più famosa per il taglio Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon?","Quelle région est la plus célèbre pour l'assemblage Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon ?","Which region is most famous for Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon blends?"],"o":[["Bordeaux","Bordeaux","Bordeaux"],["Burgundy","Bourgogne","Burgundy"],["Rioja","Rioja","Rioja"],["Champagne","Champagne","Champagne"]],"e":["Bordeaux è la patria del taglio tra Merlot e Cabernet Sauvignon.","Bordeaux est la patrie de l'assemblage Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon.","Bordeaux is the home of the Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon blend."],"d":["Bordeaux, in Francia, è la regione più famosa per il taglio di Merlot e Cabernet Sauvignon, oggi diffuso anche in molti altri paesi. Burgundy usa invece Pinot Noir per i rossi e Chardonnay per i bianchi, mentre lo Champagne nasce da Chardonnay e Pinot Noir.","Bordeaux, en France, est la région la plus célèbre pour l'assemblage de Merlot et de Cabernet Sauvignon, aujourd'hui répandu dans bien d'autres pays. La Bourgogne utilise le Pinot Noir pour ses rouges et le Chardonnay pour ses blancs, et le Champagne naît du Chardonnay et du Pinot Noir.","Bordeaux in France is the most famous region for blending Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon, a blend now common in many other countries too. Burgundy uses Pinot Noir for its reds and Chardonnay for its whites, while Champagne is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir."]},{"id":"l11734dff","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde al Pinot Noir?","Quelle description correspond au Pinot Noir ?","Which description fits Pinot Noir?"],"o":[["Corpo leggero-medio, acidità alta, tannino basso-medio","Corps léger à moyen, acidité élevée, tanins faibles à moyens","Light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin"],["Corpo pieno, acidità media, tannino alto","Corps ample, acidité moyenne, tanins élevés","Full body, medium acidity, high tannin"],["Corpo pieno, acidità alta, tannino alto","Corps ample, acidité élevée, tanins élevés","Full body, high acidity, high tannin"],["Corpo medio, acidità bassa, tannino medio","Corps moyen, acidité faible, tanins moyens","Medium body, low acidity, medium tannin"]],"e":["Il Pinot Noir è un rosso fresco e delicato, poco tannico.","Le Pinot Noir est un rouge frais et délicat, peu tannique.","Pinot Noir is a fresh, delicate red with modest tannin."],"d":["Il Pinot Noir dà rossi di solito secchi, di corpo da leggero a medio, con acidità alta e tannino basso o medio. Ha aromi di frutti rossi come fragola, ciliegia rossa e lampone. Corpo pieno e tannino alto descrivono piuttosto Cabernet Sauvignon o Shiraz.","Le Pinot Noir donne des rouges en général secs, au corps léger à moyen, à l'acidité élevée et aux tanins faibles à moyens. Il a des arômes de fruits rouges comme la fraise, la cerise rouge et la framboise. Un corps ample et des tanins élevés décrivent plutôt le Cabernet Sauvignon ou la Shiraz.","Pinot Noir makes reds that are usually dry, light to medium in body, with high acidity and low to medium tannin. It has red fruit aromas such as strawberry, red cherry and raspberry. A full body with high tannin describes Cabernet Sauvignon or Shiraz instead."]},{"id":"l1ffbf5c5","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi di frutta sono tipici del Pinot Noir?","Quels arômes de fruits sont typiques du Pinot Noir ?","Which fruit aromas are typical of Pinot Noir?"],"o":[["Fragola, ciliegia rossa, lampone","Fraise, cerise rouge, framboise","Strawberry, red cherry, raspberry"],["Ribes nero, ciliegia nera, menta","Cassis, cerise noire, menthe","Blackcurrant, black cherry, mint"],["Mora, pepe nero, liquirizia","Mûre, poivre noir, réglisse","Blackberry, black pepper, liquorice"],["Pera, limone, mela","Poire, citron, pomme","Pear, lemon, apple"]],"e":["Il Pinot Noir profuma di frutti rossi.","Le Pinot Noir sent les fruits rouges.","Pinot Noir smells of red fruit."],"d":["Il Pinot Noir è il vitigno dei frutti rossi: fragola, ciliegia rossa e lampone, spesso con vaniglia e affumicato se passa in rovere. Ribes nero e menta indicano il Cabernet Sauvignon; mora, pepe nero e liquirizia indicano Syrah/Shiraz; pera e limone sono aromi di vini bianchi.","Le Pinot Noir est le cépage des fruits rouges : fraise, cerise rouge et framboise, souvent avec vanille et fumé s'il passe en chêne. Cassis et menthe signalent le Cabernet Sauvignon ; mûre, poivre noir et réglisse, la Syrah/Shiraz ; poire et citron sont des arômes de vins blancs.","Pinot Noir is the red-fruit grape: strawberry, red cherry and raspberry, often with vanilla and smoke when oaked. Blackcurrant and mint point to Cabernet Sauvignon; blackberry, black pepper and liquorice point to Syrah/Shiraz; and pear and lemon are white-wine aromas."]},{"id":"l1ba4271a","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Con quale vitigno si fanno i rossi di Burgundy?","Avec quel cépage fait-on les Bourgogne rouges ?","Which grape is used for red Burgundy?"],"o":[["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"],["Syrah","Syrah","Syrah"],["Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon"]],"e":["I rossi di Burgundy sono fatti con Pinot Noir.","Les Bourgogne rouges sont faits de Pinot Noir.","Red Burgundy is made from Pinot Noir."],"d":["Burgundy (Bourgogne) usa il Pinot Noir per i rossi e lo Chardonnay per i bianchi. I rossi sono secchi, leggeri o medi, con acidità alta, tannino basso o medio e frutti rossi. Merlot e Cabernet Sauvignon sono i vitigni di Bordeaux, il Syrah è tipico del Rodano settentrionale.","La Bourgogne utilise le Pinot Noir pour les rouges et le Chardonnay pour les blancs. Les rouges sont secs, légers à moyens, à l'acidité élevée, aux tanins faibles à moyens et aux fruits rouges. Merlot et Cabernet Sauvignon sont les cépages de Bordeaux, la Syrah est typique du nord du Rhône.","Burgundy (Bourgogne) uses Pinot Noir for its reds and Chardonnay for its whites. The reds are dry, light to medium-bodied, with high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit. Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon are the grapes of Bordeaux, and Syrah is typical of the Northern Rhône."]},{"id":"l18e76f93","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["In quale paese il Pinot Noir è il principale vitigno nero?","Dans quel pays le Pinot Noir est-il le principal cépage noir ?","In which country is Pinot Noir the main black grape?"],"o":[["Nuova Zelanda","Nouvelle-Zélande","New Zealand"],["Australia","Australie","Australia"],["Cile","Chili","Chile"],["Sudafrica","Afrique du Sud","South Africa"]],"e":["In Nuova Zelanda il Pinot Noir è l'uva nera principale.","En Nouvelle-Zélande, le Pinot Noir est le premier cépage noir.","In New Zealand, Pinot Noir is the leading black grape."],"d":["Oltre a Burgundy, il Pinot Noir è il principale vitigno nero della Nuova Zelanda, con zone come Central Otago. Australia, Cile e Sudafrica sono invece citati soprattutto per il Cabernet Sauvignon, e l'Australia anche per lo Shiraz. La Nuova Zelanda è famosa anche per il Sauvignon Blanc.","Outre la Bourgogne, le Pinot Noir est le principal cépage noir de Nouvelle-Zélande, avec des régions comme Central Otago. L'Australie, le Chili et l'Afrique du Sud sont surtout cités pour le Cabernet Sauvignon, et l'Australie aussi pour la Shiraz. La Nouvelle-Zélande est aussi célèbre pour son Sauvignon Blanc.","Besides Burgundy, Pinot Noir is the main black grape of New Zealand, in regions such as Central Otago. Australia, Chile and South Africa are mentioned mainly for Cabernet Sauvignon, and Australia also for Shiraz. New Zealand is also famous for its Sauvignon Blanc."]},{"id":"l1e70d050","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Per i vini rossi, il Pinot Noir di solito viene...","Pour les vins rouges, le Pinot Noir est en général...","When making red wine, Pinot Noir is usually..."],"o":[["vinificato da solo, senza altri vitigni","vinifié seul, sans autre cépage","made on its own, without other grapes"],["unito al Cabernet Sauvignon","assemblé au Cabernet Sauvignon","blended with Cabernet Sauvignon"],["unito allo Shiraz","assemblé à la Shiraz","blended with Shiraz"],["unito al Merlot","assemblé au Merlot","blended with Merlot"]],"e":["Per i rossi il Pinot Noir di solito non si usa in taglio.","Pour les rouges, le Pinot Noir n'est en général pas assemblé.","For red wines, Pinot Noir is not usually blended."],"d":["A differenza di Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot e Shiraz, che spesso vengono uniti tra loro, il Pinot Noir per i rossi viene di solito vinificato in purezza. L'unico taglio importante da ricordare è nello Champagne, dove il Pinot Noir si unisce allo Chardonnay per fare uno spumante.","Contrairement au Cabernet Sauvignon, au Merlot et à la Shiraz, souvent assemblés entre eux, le Pinot Noir est en général vinifié seul pour les rouges. Le seul assemblage important à retenir est celui du Champagne, où le Pinot Noir s'allie au Chardonnay pour faire un effervescent.","Unlike Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot and Shiraz, which are often blended with each other, Pinot Noir is usually made on its own when producing red wine. The one important blend to remember is Champagne, where Pinot Noir is combined with Chardonnay to make a sparkling wine."]},{"id":"l11d03897","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Come si chiama il Syrah in Australia?","Comment appelle-t-on la Syrah en Australie ?","What is Syrah called in Australia?"],"o":[["Shiraz","Shiraz","Shiraz"],["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"],["Zinfandel","Zinfandel","Zinfandel"],["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"]],"e":["Syrah in Francia e Shiraz in Australia sono lo stesso vitigno.","Syrah en France et Shiraz en Australie désignent le même cépage.","Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia are the same grape."],"d":["Lo stesso vitigno ha due nomi: Syrah in Francia e Shiraz in Australia. Il nome in etichetta dà quindi un indizio sull'origine e spesso sullo stile, più fresco e pepato in Francia, più pieno e maturo nelle zone calde dell'Australia. Merlot e Pinot Noir sono vitigni diversi.","Le même cépage porte deux noms : Syrah en France et Shiraz en Australie. Le nom sur l'étiquette donne donc un indice sur l'origine et souvent sur le style, plus frais et poivré en France, plus ample et mûr dans les régions chaudes d'Australie. Merlot et Pinot Noir sont d'autres cépages.","The same grape has two names: Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia. The name on the label therefore hints at the origin and often the style, fresher and more peppery in France, fuller and riper in Australia's warm regions. Merlot and Pinot Noir are different grapes."]},{"id":"l172cb2dd","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quali spezie sono tipiche di Syrah/Shiraz?","Quelles épices sont typiques de la Syrah/Shiraz ?","Which spices are typical of Syrah/Shiraz?"],"o":[["Pepe nero e liquirizia","Poivre noir et réglisse","Black pepper and liquorice"],["Vaniglia e cocco","Vanille et noix de coco","Vanilla and coconut"],["Menta e peperone verde","Menthe et poivron vert","Mint and green bell pepper"],["Pepe bianco ed erbe secche","Poivre blanc et herbes séchées","White pepper and dried herbs"]],"e":["Syrah/Shiraz unisce frutta nera a pepe nero e liquirizia.","La Syrah/Shiraz associe fruit noir, poivre noir et réglisse.","Syrah/Shiraz pairs black fruit with black pepper and liquorice."],"d":["I sapori tipici di Syrah/Shiraz sono frutti neri come mora e ciliegia nera, con spezie come pepe nero e liquirizia. Vaniglia e cocco arrivano dal rovere, non dall'uva. Menta e peperone verde sono note del Cabernet Sauvignon; il pepe bianco è citato per il Côtes du Rhône.","Les saveurs typiques de la Syrah/Shiraz sont les fruits noirs comme la mûre et la cerise noire, avec des épices comme le poivre noir et la réglisse. Vanille et noix de coco viennent du chêne, pas du raisin. Menthe et poivron vert sont des notes du Cabernet Sauvignon ; le poivre blanc est cité pour le Côtes du Rhône.","Syrah/Shiraz typically shows black fruit such as blackberry and black cherry, with spices such as black pepper and liquorice. Vanilla and coconut come from oak rather than the grape. Mint and green bell pepper are Cabernet Sauvignon notes, and white pepper is mentioned for Côtes du Rhône."]},{"id":"l1a82f11e","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Che stile ha spesso il Syrah del Rodano settentrionale?","Quel style a souvent la Syrah du nord du Rhône ?","What style does Northern Rhône Syrah often have?"],"o":[["Corpo medio, mora fresca e pepe nero","Corps moyen, mûre fraîche et poivre noir","Medium body, fresh blackberry and black pepper"],["Corpo pieno, ciliegia nera in confettura","Corps ample, cerise noire confiturée","Full body, jammy black cherry"],["Corpo leggero, fragola e lampone","Corps léger, fraise et framboise","Light body, strawberry and raspberry"],["Dolce, prugna nera e miele","Doux, prune noire et miel","Sweet, black plum and honey"]],"e":["Nel Rodano settentrionale il Syrah è più fresco: corpo medio, mora e pepe.","Dans le nord du Rhône, la Syrah est plus fraîche : corps moyen, mûre et poivre.","Northern Rhône Syrah is fresher: medium body, blackberry and pepper."],"d":["Il Rodano settentrionale, in Francia, può dare Syrah di corpo medio, con mora fresca e pepe nero. Nelle zone calde dell'Australia, invece, le uve maturano di più e lo Shiraz diventa pieno, con ciliegia nera dal gusto di confettura e liquirizia. Stesso vitigno, climi diversi, stili diversi. Il clima spiega la differenza.","Le nord de la vallée du Rhône peut donner des Syrah de corps moyen, avec mûre fraîche et poivre noir. Dans les régions chaudes d'Australie, le raisin mûrit davantage et la Shiraz devient corsée, avec une cerise noire confiturée et de la réglisse. Même cépage, climats différents, styles différents. Le climat explique la différence.","France's Northern Rhône can produce medium-bodied Syrah with fresh blackberry and black pepper. In warm parts of Australia the grapes ripen further and Shiraz becomes full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice. Same grape, different climates, different styles. Climate explains the difference."]},{"id":"l15145366","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Perché lo Shiraz delle zone calde dell'Australia è spesso di corpo pieno?","Pourquoi la Shiraz des régions chaudes d'Australie est-elle souvent corsée ?","Why is Shiraz from warm parts of Australia often full-bodied?"],"o":[["Il caldo fa maturare di più le uve","La chaleur fait davantage mûrir le raisin","The heat makes the grapes riper"],["Le uve vengono raccolte acerbe","Le raisin est vendangé avant maturité","The grapes are picked unripe"],["Il vino è fatto senza bucce","Le vin est fait sans les peaux","The wine is made without skins"],["Si aggiunge succo non fermentato","On ajoute du jus non fermenté","Unfermented juice is added"]],"e":["Più calore = uve più mature e zuccherine = vino più pieno e maturo.","Plus de chaleur = raisin plus mûr et sucré = vin plus ample et mûr.","More heat means riper, sweeter grapes and a fuller, riper wine."],"d":["Nei climi caldi le uve maturano con regolarità e accumulano più zucchero. Ne nascono vini più maturi e corposi: lo Shiraz australiano delle zone calde, come la Barossa Valley, è pieno, con ciliegia nera dal gusto di confettura e liquirizia. Nel Rodano settentrionale, più fresco, lo stile è di corpo medio.","En climat chaud, le raisin mûrit régulièrement et accumule plus de sucre. On obtient des vins plus mûrs et plus amples : la Shiraz des régions chaudes d'Australie, comme la Barossa Valley, est corsée, avec une cerise noire confiturée et de la réglisse. Dans le nord du Rhône, plus frais, le style est de corps moyen.","In warm climates grapes ripen reliably and build up more sugar. That gives riper, fuller wines: Shiraz from warm Australian regions such as the Barossa Valley is full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice. In the cooler Northern Rhône, the style is medium-bodied instead."]},{"id":"l1b4fcb91","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quali note aggiunge il rovere a molti Syrah/Shiraz?","Quelles notes le chêne ajoute-t-il à beaucoup de Syrah/Shiraz ?","Which notes does oak add to many Syrah/Shiraz wines?"],"o":[["Vaniglia o cocco","Vanille ou noix de coco","Vanilla or coconut"],["Pepe nero o liquirizia","Poivre noir ou réglisse","Black pepper or liquorice"],["Mora o ciliegia nera","Mûre ou cerise noire","Blackberry or black cherry"],["Erba o asparago","Herbe ou asperge","Grass or asparagus"]],"e":["Il rovere dà vaniglia o cocco; frutta nera e spezie vengono dall'uva.","Le chêne donne vanille ou coco ; fruit noir et épices viennent du raisin.","Oak gives vanilla or coconut; black fruit and spice come from the grape."],"d":["Molti Syrah e Shiraz vengono affinati in rovere, che aggiunge note di vaniglia o di cocco. La frutta nera (mora, ciliegia nera) e le spezie (pepe nero, liquirizia) sono invece aromi propri del vitigno. Erba e asparago sono note erbacee tipiche del Sauvignon Blanc.","Beaucoup de Syrah et de Shiraz sont élevées en chêne, qui ajoute des notes de vanille ou de noix de coco. Les fruits noirs (mûre, cerise noire) et les épices (poivre noir, réglisse) sont en revanche des arômes propres au cépage. Herbe et asperge sont des notes herbacées typiques du Sauvignon Blanc.","Many Syrahs and Shirazes are matured in oak, which adds vanilla or coconut notes. Black fruit (blackberry, black cherry) and spice (black pepper, liquorice), on the other hand, are the grape's own aromas. Grass and asparagus are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc."]},{"id":"l15adbdbc","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["In carta: «leggero, acidità alta, fragola e ciliegia rossa». Quale vitigno?","Sur une carte : « léger, acidité élevée, fraise et cerise rouge ». Quel cépage ?","A list says «light-bodied, high acidity, strawberry and red cherry». Which grape?"],"o":[["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],["Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon"],["Shiraz","Shiraz","Shiraz"],["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"]],"e":["Corpo leggero, acidità alta e frutti rossi indicano il Pinot Noir.","Corps léger, acidité élevée et fruits rouges désignent le Pinot Noir.","Light body, high acidity and red fruit point to Pinot Noir."],"d":["Tra i quattro rossi principali, il Pinot Noir è quello più leggero e fresco: corpo leggero o medio, acidità alta, tannino basso o medio e frutti rossi. Cabernet Sauvignon e Shiraz sono più pieni e con frutta nera; il Merlot ha acidità media e corpo da medio a pieno.","Parmi les quatre grands rouges, le Pinot Noir est le plus léger et le plus frais : corps léger à moyen, acidité élevée, tanins faibles à moyens et fruits rouges. Le Cabernet Sauvignon et la Shiraz sont plus amples, aux fruits noirs ; le Merlot a une acidité moyenne et un corps moyen à ample.","Of the four key black grapes, Pinot Noir is the lightest and freshest: light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit. Cabernet Sauvignon and Shiraz are fuller, with black fruit, while Merlot has medium acidity and a medium to full body."]},{"id":"l1a83e705","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["In carta: «Australia, corpo pieno, ciliegia nera intensa e liquirizia». Quale vitigno?","Sur une carte : « Australie, corsé, cerise noire intense et réglisse ». Quel cépage ?","A list says «Australia, full-bodied, intense black cherry and liquorice». Which grape?"],"o":[["Shiraz","Shiraz","Shiraz"],["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"],["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"]],"e":["Ciliegia nera e liquirizia in un rosso pieno australiano indicano lo Shiraz.","Cerise noire et réglisse dans un rouge corsé australien : c'est la Shiraz.","Black cherry and liquorice in a full Australian red point to Shiraz."],"d":["Le zone calde dell'Australia, come la Barossa Valley, producono Shiraz di corpo pieno, con ciliegia nera matura e liquirizia. Il Pinot Noir è leggero e con frutti rossi, il Merlot è morbido con prugna e mora, e il Riesling è un'uva bianca.","Les régions chaudes d'Australie, comme la Barossa Valley, produisent des Shiraz corsées, à la cerise noire mûre et à la réglisse. Le Pinot Noir est léger et sur les fruits rouges, le Merlot souple sur la prune et la mûre, et le Riesling est un raisin blanc.","Warm Australian regions such as the Barossa Valley make full-bodied Shiraz with ripe black cherry and liquorice. Pinot Noir is light with red fruit, Merlot is soft with plum and blackberry, and Riesling is a white grape, so none of them fits this description."]},{"id":"l14302cdf","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["Quale uva nera si usa per lo Champagne?","Quel raisin noir entre dans le Champagne ?","Which black grape is used to make Champagne?"],"o":[["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"],["Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon"],["Syrah","Syrah","Syrah"]],"e":["Lo Champagne unisce spesso Pinot Noir e Chardonnay.","Le Champagne assemble souvent Pinot Noir et Chardonnay.","Champagne often blends Pinot Noir with Chardonnay."],"d":["Tra i quattro rossi principali, solo il Pinot Noir entra nello Champagne, dove viene spesso unito allo Chardonnay. Anche se è un'uva nera, il suo succo è incolore: separando subito le bucce si ottiene una base chiara. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon e Syrah non sono vitigni dello Champagne.","Parmi les quatre grands rouges, seul le Pinot Noir entre dans le Champagne, où il est souvent assemblé au Chardonnay. Bien que ce soit un raisin noir, son jus est incolore : en séparant tout de suite les peaux, on obtient une base claire. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon et Syrah ne sont pas des cépages du Champagne.","Of the four key black grapes, only Pinot Noir goes into Champagne, where it is often blended with Chardonnay. Although it is a black grape, its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a pale base wine. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon and Syrah are not Champagne grapes."]},{"id":"l171db47b","c":"w3","p":0,"q":["In quali regioni è comune coltivare uve nere come il Cabernet Sauvignon?","Dans quelles régions cultive-t-on couramment des raisins noirs comme le Cabernet Sauvignon ?","In which regions is it common to grow black grapes like Cabernet Sauvignon?"],"o":[["Regioni calde, dove le uve maturano con regolarità","Régions chaudes, où le raisin mûrit régulièrement","Warm regions, where grapes ripen reliably"],["Regioni fresche, dove le uve faticano a maturare","Régions fraîches, où le raisin peine à mûrir","Cool regions, where grapes struggle to ripen"],["Regioni senza inverno, dove la vite non riposa","Régions sans hiver, où la vigne ne se repose pas","Regions with no winter, where vines never rest"],["Regioni vicino ai poli, con luce debole","Régions proches des pôles, à la lumière faible","Regions near the poles, with weak sunlight"]],"e":["Nei climi caldi le uve maturano bene: lì è comune coltivare uve nere.","En climat chaud, le raisin mûrit bien : on y cultive souvent des raisins noirs.","Warm climates ripen grapes well, so black grapes are commonly grown there."],"d":["Le regioni calde, più vicine all'Equatore, come parti dell'Australia e della California, hanno temperature alte e sole intenso: le uve maturano con regolarità ed è comune coltivare uve nere. Nelle regioni fresche, come Germania e nord della Francia, si coltivano più spesso uve bianche.","Les régions chaudes, plus proches de l'équateur, comme certaines parties de l'Australie et de la Californie, ont des températures élevées et un soleil intense : le raisin mûrit régulièrement et l'on y cultive souvent des raisins noirs. Dans les régions fraîches, comme l'Allemagne et le nord de la France, on cultive plutôt des raisins blancs.","Warm regions closer to the Equator, such as parts of Australia and California, have high temperatures and intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably and black grapes are commonly grown. In cool regions such as Germany and northern France, white grapes are grown more often."]},{"id":"l1e56aa9e","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Come va conservato un vino per un lungo periodo?","Comment conserver un vin sur une longue période ?","How should wine be kept for long-term storage?"],"o":[["Al fresco, a temperatura costante","Au frais, à température constante","Cool, at a constant temperature"],["Al caldo, a temperatura costante","Au chaud, à température constante","Warm, at a constant temperature"],["Al fresco di notte, al caldo di giorno","Au frais la nuit, au chaud le jour","Cool at night, warm by day"],["Vicino a una finestra luminosa","Près d'une fenêtre lumineuse","Next to a bright window"]],"e":["Fresco e costante: estremi e sbalzi di temperatura danneggiano il vino.","Frais et constant : extrêmes et variations de température abîment le vin.","Cool and steady: extremes and swings in temperature damage wine."],"d":["Per una conservazione lunga il vino ha bisogno di un luogo fresco e con temperatura stabile. Sia il caldo o il freddo estremi sia le forti variazioni possono rovinarlo, facendogli perdere carattere e, alla lunga, causando difetti. Anche la luce intensa va evitata, perché fa perdere al vino il suo frutto.","Pour une conservation longue, le vin a besoin d'un endroit frais et à température stable. La chaleur ou le froid extrêmes, comme les fortes variations, peuvent l'abîmer, lui faire perdre son caractère et, à terme, provoquer des défauts. Il faut aussi éviter la lumière vive, qui lui fait perdre son fruit.","For long-term storage, wine needs a cool place with a stable temperature. Extreme heat or cold, as well as big swings, can damage it, making it lose character and eventually causing faults. Bright light should also be avoided, because it makes the wine lose its fruitiness."]},{"id":"l1cfd4b77","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Che effetto possono avere sul vino il sole forte e le luci artificiali intense?","Quel effet le soleil fort et les lumières vives peuvent-ils avoir sur le vin ?","What can strong sunshine and bright artificial light do to wine?"],"o":[["Fargli perdere il carattere fruttato","Lui faire perdre son caractère fruité","Make it lose its fruity character"],["Aumentarne il grado alcolico","Augmenter son degré d'alcool","Raise its alcohol level"],["Renderlo più dolce","Le rendre plus sucré","Make it sweeter"],["Aumentarne i tannini","Augmenter ses tanins","Increase its tannins"]],"e":["La luce e il calore che genera tolgono al vino il suo frutto.","La lumière et la chaleur qu'elle génère font perdre au vin son fruit.","Light, and the heat it brings, strip wine of its fruitiness."],"d":["Le bottiglie vanno tenute lontano dal sole forte e dalle luci artificiali intense. Sia la luce sia il calore che queste producono possono far perdere al vino il suo carattere fruttato. Non cambiano invece l'alcol, lo zucchero o i tannini: il danno riguarda soprattutto profumi e sapori di frutta.","Les bouteilles doivent être tenues à l'écart du soleil fort et des lumières artificielles vives. La lumière, comme la chaleur qu'elle produit, peut faire perdre au vin son caractère fruité. Elles ne changent pas l'alcool, le sucre ou les tanins : le dommage touche surtout les arômes et saveurs de fruits.","Bottles should be kept away from strong sunshine and bright artificial light. Both the light and the heat it gives off can make a wine lose its fruity character. They do not change the alcohol, sugar or tannin: the damage is mainly to the fruit aromas and flavours."]},{"id":"l190f9c55","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Perché una bottiglia con tappo di sughero va conservata coricata?","Pourquoi une bouteille bouchée au liège se conserve-t-elle couchée ?","Why should a bottle sealed with a cork be stored on its side?"],"o":[["Il sughero resta umido e non fa entrare aria","Le liège reste humide et ne laisse pas entrer l'air","The cork stays moist and keeps air out"],["Il vino matura più in fretta","Le vin vieillit plus vite","The wine matures faster"],["Il vino diventa più dolce","Le vin devient plus doux","The wine becomes sweeter"],["Si risparmia spazio in cantina","On gagne de la place en cave","It saves space in the cellar"]],"e":["Coricata, il sughero tocca il vino e non si secca.","Couchée, le liège touche le vin et ne se dessèche pas.","Lying down, the cork touches the wine and does not dry out."],"d":["Tenendo la bottiglia coricata, il tappo di sughero resta a contatto con il vino e rimane umido. Un sughero secco può lasciar entrare aria nella bottiglia, e l'aria fa perdere al vino il suo carattere fruttato. Le bottiglie con tappo a vite non corrono questo rischio e possono stare in piedi.","Quand la bouteille est couchée, le bouchon en liège reste au contact du vin et demeure humide. Un liège sec peut laisser entrer de l'air dans la bouteille, et l'air fait perdre au vin son caractère fruité. Les bouteilles à capsule à vis ne courent pas ce risque et peuvent rester debout.","With the bottle on its side, the cork stays in contact with the wine and remains moist. A dried-out cork can let air into the bottle, and air makes the wine lose its fruity character. Screwcap bottles do not run this risk and can be stored upright."]},{"id":"l13c9d9cf","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Come si possono conservare le bottiglie con tappo a vite?","Comment peut-on conserver les bouteilles à capsule à vis ?","How can screwcap bottles be stored?"],"o":[["Anche in piedi","Debout, sans problème","Standing up"],["Solo coricate","Uniquement couchées","Only on their side"],["Solo capovolte","Uniquement à l'envers","Only upside down"],["Solo vicino a una fonte di calore","Uniquement près d'une source de chaleur","Only near a heat source"]],"e":["Senza sughero da tenere umido, la bottiglia può stare in piedi.","Sans liège à garder humide, la bouteille peut rester debout.","With no cork to keep moist, the bottle can stand up."],"d":["La posizione coricata serve solo a mantenere umido il tappo di sughero, così che non si secchi e non lasci entrare aria. Il tappo a vite non ha questo problema, quindi la bottiglia può essere conservata in piedi. Le altre regole, cioè fresco, temperatura costante e niente luce forte, restano valide.","La position couchée sert seulement à garder le bouchon en liège humide, pour qu'il ne se dessèche pas et ne laisse pas entrer l'air. La capsule à vis n'a pas ce problème, la bouteille peut donc être conservée debout. Les autres règles, fraîcheur, température constante et pas de lumière vive, restent valables.","Lying a bottle down only serves to keep a cork moist, so it does not dry out and let air in. A screwcap has no such problem, so the bottle can be stored standing up. The other rules, a cool and constant temperature and no bright light, still apply."]},{"id":"l1bf21199","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Come funziona un sistema sottovuoto per il vino aperto?","Comment fonctionne un système sous vide pour le vin ouvert ?","How does a vacuum system keep opened wine fresh?"],"o":[["Una pompa toglie l'aria dalla bottiglia","Une pompe retire l'air de la bouteille","A pump removes air from the bottle"],["Un gas spinge fuori l'aria","Un gaz chasse l'air","A gas pushes the air out"],["Il ghiaccio raffredda il collo","La glace refroidit le col","Ice chills the bottle neck"],["Il tappo viene sigillato con la cera","Le bouchon est scellé à la cire","The cork is sealed with wax"]],"e":["Il sottovuoto aspira l'aria; il sistema a gas, invece, la spinge fuori.","Le système sous vide aspire l'air ; le système à gaz, lui, le chasse.","A vacuum pumps air out; a blanket system pushes it out with gas."],"d":["Il vino aperto diventa stantio perché reagisce con l'aria. I sistemi sottovuoto usano una pompa per estrarre l'aria dalla bottiglia, riducendo questo contatto. Non vanno confusi con i sistemi a coperta di gas, che invece introducono un gas innocuo per spingere fuori l'aria.","Le vin ouvert s'évente parce qu'il réagit avec l'air. Les systèmes sous vide utilisent une pompe pour extraire l'air de la bouteille et réduire ce contact. Il ne faut pas les confondre avec les systèmes à couverture de gaz, qui injectent au contraire un gaz inoffensif pour chasser l'air.","Opened wine goes stale because it reacts with air. Vacuum systems use a pump to draw the air out of the bottle, reducing this contact. They should not be confused with blanket systems, which instead pump in a harmless gas to push the air out."]},{"id":"l198ffd6c","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Come funziona un sistema a «coperta» di gas?","Comment fonctionne un système à « couverture » de gaz ?","How does a blanket system work?"],"o":[["Un gas innocuo spinge fuori l'aria","Un gaz inoffensif chasse l'air","A harmless gas pushes the air out"],["Una pompa aspira il vino","Une pompe aspire le vin","A pump draws out the wine"],["Un panno copre la bottiglia","Un linge couvre la bouteille","A cloth covers the bottle"],["Si aggiunge vino nuovo ogni giorno","On ajoute du vin neuf chaque jour","Fresh wine is added daily"]],"e":["Il gas prende il posto dell'aria e non danneggia il vino.","Le gaz prend la place de l'air et n'abîme pas le vin.","The gas takes the air's place and does not harm the wine."],"d":["Nei sistemi a coperta si pompa nella bottiglia un gas che spinge fuori l'aria. Il gas non danneggia il vino e lo protegge dal contatto con l'aria, che altrimenti lo renderebbe stantio. È un'alternativa al sottovuoto, che invece toglie l'aria con una pompa.","Dans les systèmes à couverture, on injecte dans la bouteille un gaz qui chasse l'air. Ce gaz n'abîme pas le vin et le protège du contact avec l'air, qui sinon l'éventerait. C'est une alternative au système sous vide, qui retire l'air à l'aide d'une pompe.","In blanket systems a gas is pumped into the bottle, pushing the air out. The gas does not harm the wine and shields it from contact with air, which would otherwise make it stale. It is an alternative to a vacuum system, which removes the air with a pump."]},{"id":"l11af3a5a","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Qual è il modo più semplice per mantenere fresco un vino aperto?","Quelle est la façon la plus simple de garder frais un vin ouvert ?","What is the simplest way to keep an opened wine fresher?"],"o":[["Rimettere il tappo e metterlo in frigo","Le reboucher et le mettre au réfrigérateur","Recork it and keep it in the fridge"],["Lasciarlo aperto sul tavolo","Le laisser ouvert sur la table","Leave it open on the table"],["Scaldarlo vicino a un termosifone","Le chauffer près d'un radiateur","Warm it near a radiator"],["Metterlo alla luce del sole","Le mettre au soleil","Put it in sunlight"]],"e":["Tappo e frigorifero rallentano il passaggio a stantio.","Bouchon et réfrigérateur ralentissent l'évent.","Cork and fridge slow down the wine going stale."],"d":["Dopo l'apertura il vino reagisce con l'aria e lentamente perde freschezza. Rimettere il tappo e tenerlo in frigorifero aiuta a conservarlo più a lungo. Per tempi ancora più lunghi si possono usare sistemi sottovuoto o a coperta di gas. Calore e luce, invece, peggiorano le cose.","Après l'ouverture, le vin réagit avec l'air et perd lentement sa fraîcheur. Le reboucher et le garder au réfrigérateur aide à le conserver plus longtemps. Pour des durées encore plus longues, on peut utiliser des systèmes sous vide ou à couverture de gaz. La chaleur et la lumière, elles, aggravent les choses.","After opening, wine reacts with air and slowly loses its freshness. Putting the cork back and keeping it in the fridge helps it last longer. For even longer, vacuum or blanket systems can be used. Heat and light, on the other hand, only make things worse."]},{"id":"l116d9ab7","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["A quale temperatura si serve un vino dolce come il Sauternes?","À quelle température sert-on un vin doux comme le Sauternes ?","At what temperature should a sweet wine such as Sauternes be served?"],"o":[["Molto fresco, 6–8 °C","Bien frais, 6–8 °C","Well chilled, 6–8°C (43–45°F)"],["Appena fresco, 10–13 °C","Légèrement frais, 10–13 °C","Lightly chilled, 10–13°C (50–55°F)"],["Appena fresco, circa 13 °C","Légèrement frais, environ 13 °C","Lightly chilled, about 13°C (55°F)"],["Temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C","Température ambiante, 15–18 °C","Room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F)"]],"e":["I vini dolci, come il Sauternes, si servono molto freschi, a 6–8 °C.","Les vins doux, comme le Sauternes, se servent bien frais, à 6–8 °C.","Sweet wines such as Sauternes are served well chilled, at 6–8°C."],"d":["I vini dolci sono tra quelli da servire più freddi, insieme agli spumanti. L'intervallo consigliato per un dolce come il Sauternes è 6–8 °C. 10–13 °C è invece la temperatura dei bianchi corposi, circa 13 °C quella dei rossi leggeri e 15–18 °C quella dei rossi medi o corposi.","Les vins doux font partie des vins servis le plus froid, avec les effervescents. La fourchette conseillée pour un doux comme le Sauternes est de 6 à 8 °C. 10–13 °C correspond plutôt aux blancs corsés, environ 13 °C aux rouges légers et 15–18 °C aux rouges moyens ou corsés.","Sweet wines are among the coldest-served wines, together with sparkling wines. The recommended range for a sweet wine such as Sauternes is 6–8°C. By contrast, 10–13°C suits full-bodied whites, around 13°C suits light reds, and 15–18°C suits medium- and full-bodied reds."]},{"id":"l17fe3b27","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Come si serve uno spumante come lo Champagne?","Comment sert-on un effervescent comme le Champagne ?","How should a sparkling wine such as Champagne be served?"],"o":[["Molto fresco, 6–10 °C","Bien frais, 6–10 °C","Well chilled, 6–10°C (43–50°F)"],["Appena fresco, 10–13 °C","Légèrement frais, 10–13 °C","Lightly chilled, 10–13°C (50–55°F)"],["Temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C","Température ambiante, 15–18 °C","Room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F)"],["Leggermente scaldato","Légèrement réchauffé","Slightly warmed"]],"e":["Gli spumanti si servono molto freschi, tra 6 e 10 °C.","Les effervescents se servent bien frais, entre 6 et 10 °C.","Sparkling wines are served well chilled, between 6 and 10°C."],"d":["Lo Champagne e gli altri spumanti vanno serviti molto freschi, nell'intervallo 6–10 °C. Il freddo ha anche un vantaggio pratico: riduce la pressione nella bottiglia e rende l'apertura più sicura. Per mantenerlo fresco si può usare un secchiello con ghiaccio e acqua fredda o un contenitore isolante.","Le Champagne et les autres effervescents se servent bien frais, entre 6 et 10 °C. Le froid a aussi un avantage pratique : il réduit la pression dans la bouteille et rend l'ouverture plus sûre. Pour le garder frais, on peut utiliser un seau avec de la glace et de l'eau froide ou un contenant isotherme.","Champagne and other sparkling wines should be served well chilled, in the 6–10°C range. Cold also has a practical benefit: it reduces the pressure in the bottle and makes opening safer. To keep it cool, use an ice bucket with ice and cold water or an insulated container."]},{"id":"l1a80bb8a","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["A quale temperatura si serve un bianco leggero come il Pinot Grigio?","À quelle température sert-on un blanc léger comme le Pinot Grigio ?","At what temperature should a light white such as Pinot Grigio be served?"],"o":[["Fresco, 7–10 °C","Frais, 7–10 °C","Chilled, 7–10°C (45–50°F)"],["Appena fresco, 10–13 °C","Légèrement frais, 10–13 °C","Lightly chilled, 10–13°C (50–55°F)"],["Temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C","Température ambiante, 15–18 °C","Room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F)"],["Appena fresco, circa 13 °C","Légèrement frais, environ 13 °C","Lightly chilled, about 13°C (55°F)"]],"e":["Bianchi leggeri o medi e rosati: freschi, a 7–10 °C.","Blancs légers ou moyens et rosés : frais, à 7–10 °C.","Light and medium whites and rosés: chilled, at 7–10°C."],"d":["I bianchi di corpo leggero o medio, come il Pinot Grigio, e i rosati si servono freschi, tra 7 e 10 °C. Solo i bianchi più corposi, come uno Chardonnay maturato in rovere, si servono un po' meno freddi, a 10–13 °C. Gli altri valori riguardano i vini rossi.","Les blancs légers ou de corps moyen, comme le Pinot Grigio, et les rosés se servent frais, entre 7 et 10 °C. Seuls les blancs plus corsés, comme un Chardonnay élevé en chêne, se servent un peu moins froids, à 10–13 °C. Les autres valeurs concernent les vins rouges.","Light- and medium-bodied whites such as Pinot Grigio, and rosés, are served chilled at 7–10°C. Only fuller whites, such as an oaked Chardonnay, are served a little warmer, at 10–13°C. The remaining ranges, from lightly chilled to room temperature, apply to red wines."]},{"id":"l1d65b210","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Quale vino si serve «appena fresco» a 10–13 °C?","Quel vin se sert « légèrement frais » à 10–13 °C ?","Which wine is served lightly chilled at 10–13°C (50–55°F)?"],"o":[["Uno Chardonnay maturato in rovere","Un Chardonnay élevé en chêne","An oaked Chardonnay"],["Uno Champagne","Un Champagne","A Champagne"],["Un Sauternes","Un Sauternes","A Sauternes"],["Uno Shiraz","Un Shiraz","A Shiraz"]],"e":["I bianchi corposi, come lo Chardonnay in rovere, si servono appena freschi.","Les blancs corsés, comme le Chardonnay boisé, se servent légèrement frais.","Full-bodied whites, like oaked Chardonnay, are served lightly chilled."],"d":["Un bianco di corpo pieno, come uno Chardonnay maturato in rovere, si serve un po' meno freddo degli altri bianchi, a 10–13 °C. Champagne e Sauternes vanno serviti molto freschi, mentre uno Shiraz, rosso di corpo medio o pieno, si serve a temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C.","Un blanc corsé, comme un Chardonnay élevé en chêne, se sert un peu moins froid que les autres blancs, à 10–13 °C. Le Champagne et le Sauternes se servent bien frais, tandis qu'un Shiraz, rouge de corps moyen à corsé, se sert à température ambiante, 15–18 °C.","A full-bodied white, such as an oaked Chardonnay, is served a little less cold than other whites, at 10–13°C. Champagne and Sauternes are served well chilled, while a Shiraz, a medium- to full-bodied red, is served at room temperature, 15–18°C."]},{"id":"l1ae0198c","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Come si serve un rosso leggero come il Beaujolais?","Comment sert-on un rouge léger comme le Beaujolais ?","How should a light-bodied red such as Beaujolais be served?"],"o":[["Appena fresco, circa 13 °C","Légèrement frais, environ 13 °C","Lightly chilled, about 13°C (55°F)"],["Molto fresco, 6–8 °C","Bien frais, 6–8 °C","Well chilled, 6–8°C (43–45°F)"],["Temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C","Température ambiante, 15–18 °C","Room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F)"],["Scaldato sopra i 20 °C","Réchauffé au-delà de 20 °C","Warmed above 20°C (68°F)"]],"e":["I rossi leggeri si servono appena freschi, intorno ai 13 °C.","Les rouges légers se servent légèrement frais, vers 13 °C.","Light reds are served lightly chilled, at around 13°C."],"d":["Non tutti i rossi si servono a temperatura ambiente. Quelli di corpo leggero, come il Beaujolais, sono più piacevoli appena freschi, intorno ai 13 °C. I rossi di corpo medio o pieno, come lo Shiraz, si servono invece a temperatura ambiente, tra 15 e 18 °C.","Tous les rouges ne se servent pas à température ambiante. Les rouges légers, comme le Beaujolais, sont plus agréables légèrement rafraîchis, vers 13 °C. Les rouges de corps moyen ou corsés, comme le Shiraz, se servent en revanche à température ambiante, entre 15 et 18 °C.","Not all reds are served at room temperature. Light-bodied ones such as Beaujolais are more enjoyable lightly chilled, at around 13°C. Medium- and full-bodied reds such as Shiraz, on the other hand, are served at room temperature, between 15 and 18°C."]},{"id":"l1b71b148","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Quale intervallo è consigliato per un rosso corposo come lo Shiraz?","Quelle fourchette conseille-t-on pour un rouge corsé comme le Shiraz ?","Which range is recommended for a full-bodied red such as Shiraz?"],"o":[["15–18 °C","15–18 °C","15–18°C (59–64°F)"],["6–8 °C","6–8 °C","6–8°C (43–45°F)"],["7–10 °C","7–10 °C","7–10°C (45–50°F)"],["10–13 °C","10–13 °C","10–13°C (50–55°F)"]],"e":["I rossi medi e corposi si servono a temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C.","Les rouges moyens et corsés se servent à température ambiante, 15–18 °C.","Medium and full reds are served at room temperature, 15–18°C."],"d":["Per i rossi di corpo medio o pieno la «temperatura ambiente» corrisponde a 15–18 °C. Poiché riscaldamento e aria condizionata fanno variare molto la temperatura delle stanze, è più sicuro riferirsi a questo intervallo. Gli intervalli più freddi riguardano bianchi, rosati, spumanti e vini dolci.","Pour les rouges de corps moyen ou corsés, la « température ambiante » correspond à 15–18 °C. Comme le chauffage et la climatisation font beaucoup varier la température des pièces, il est plus sûr de se référer à cette fourchette. Les fourchettes plus froides concernent les blancs, rosés, effervescents et vins doux.","For medium- and full-bodied reds, 'room temperature' means 15–18°C. Because heating and air conditioning make room temperatures vary a lot, it is safer to rely on this range. The colder ranges are for whites, rosés, sparkling wines and sweet wines."]},{"id":"l11bd4d3b","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Come va riempito un secchiello per tenere fresco il vino?","Comment remplir un seau pour garder le vin au frais ?","How should an ice bucket be filled to keep wine cool?"],"o":[["Con ghiaccio e acqua fredda","Avec de la glace et de l'eau froide","With ice and cold water"],["Solo con ghiaccio","Uniquement avec de la glace","With ice only"],["Solo con acqua a temperatura ambiente","Uniquement avec de l'eau à température ambiante","With room-temperature water only"],["Con sale e ghiaccio secco","Avec du sel et de la glace carbonique","With salt and dry ice"]],"e":["Con il solo ghiaccio il secchiello raffredda molto meno bene.","Avec de la glace seule, le seau refroidit beaucoup moins bien.","Ice alone cools much less efficiently."],"d":["Per mantenere fresco un vino fino alla fine della bottiglia si può usare un contenitore isolante oppure un secchiello. Se si sceglie il secchiello, va riempito con ghiaccio e acqua fredda insieme: l'acqua avvolge la bottiglia e la raffredda in modo molto più efficace del solo ghiaccio.","Pour garder un vin frais jusqu'à la fin de la bouteille, on peut utiliser un contenant isotherme ou un seau. Si l'on choisit le seau, il faut le remplir de glace et d'eau froide ensemble : l'eau enveloppe la bouteille et la refroidit bien plus efficacement que la glace seule.","To keep a wine cool until the bottle is finished, you can use an insulated container or an ice bucket. If you choose a bucket, fill it with ice and cold water together: the water surrounds the bottle and chills it far more effectively than ice on its own."]},{"id":"l15928458","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Un rosso è troppo freddo. Che cosa conviene fare?","Un rouge est trop froid. Que faut-il faire ?","A red wine is too cold. What should you do?"],"o":[["Lasciarlo scaldare da solo nella stanza","Le laisser se réchauffer seul dans la pièce","Let it warm up naturally in the room"],["Metterlo vicino a un termosifone","Le poser près d'un radiateur","Place it next to a radiator"],["Immergerlo in acqua bollente","Le plonger dans de l'eau bouillante","Stand it in boiling water"],["Scaldarlo al microonde","Le chauffer au micro-ondes","Heat it in a microwave"]],"e":["Scaldare il vino ne rovina i sapori; meglio lasciarlo intiepidire da solo.","Chauffer le vin abîme ses saveurs ; mieux vaut le laisser se réchauffer seul.","Heating damages the flavours; let the wine warm up by itself."],"d":["Avvicinare il vino a una fonte di calore, come un termosifone, può danneggiarne i sapori. La soluzione corretta è portare la bottiglia nella stanza in cui sarà servita e lasciare che la temperatura salga naturalmente. Con un po' di anticipo, il vino arriverà al punto giusto.","Approcher le vin d'une source de chaleur, comme un radiateur, peut abîmer ses saveurs. La bonne solution est d'apporter la bouteille dans la pièce où elle sera servie et de laisser la température monter naturellement. En s'y prenant un peu à l'avance, le vin arrivera à la bonne température.","Putting wine near a heat source such as a radiator can damage its flavours. The right approach is to take the bottle into the room where it will be served and let its temperature rise naturally. With a little advance planning, the wine will reach the right temperature."]},{"id":"l1f0cb4ed","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Quando si apre uno spumante, da quale momento bisogna tenere sempre la mano sul tappo?","En ouvrant un effervescent, à partir de quand faut-il garder la main sur le bouchon ?","When opening sparkling wine, from when must your hand stay on the cork?"],"o":[["Da quando si allenta la gabbietta","Dès que l'on desserre le muselet","From loosening the wire cage"],["Solo quando il tappo è uscito","Seulement quand le bouchon est sorti","Only once the cork is out"],["Solo quando si versa il vino","Seulement au moment de servir","Only when pouring the wine"],["Da quando la bottiglia è in frigo","Dès que la bouteille est au frais","From when it goes in the fridge"]],"e":["Allentata la gabbietta, la pressione può far schizzare via il tappo.","Une fois le muselet desserré, la pression peut faire sauter le bouchon.","Once the cage is loose, pressure can shoot the cork out."],"d":["In una bottiglia di spumante c'è molta pressione, e anche da freddo il tappo può volar via e ferire qualcuno. Per questo, appena si allenta la gabbietta, il tappo va coperto con la mano e tenuto sotto controllo finché non è completamente fuori dalla bottiglia.","Une bouteille d'effervescent est sous forte pression, et même froid, le bouchon peut s'envoler et blesser quelqu'un. C'est pourquoi, dès que l'on desserre le muselet, il faut couvrir le bouchon avec la main et le garder sous contrôle jusqu'à ce qu'il soit complètement sorti de la bouteille.","A bottle of sparkling wine holds a lot of pressure, and even when chilled the cork can fly out and hurt someone. That is why, as soon as the wire cage is loosened, the cork must be covered by your hand and kept under control until it is fully out of the bottle."]},{"id":"l1affbe41","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Qual è la tecnica corretta per aprire uno spumante?","Quelle est la bonne technique pour ouvrir un effervescent ?","What is the correct technique for opening sparkling wine?"],"o":[["Bottiglia inclinata, si gira la bottiglia","Bouteille inclinée, on tourne la bouteille","Hold the bottle at an angle and turn the bottle"],["Bottiglia dritta, si gira il tappo","Bouteille droite, on tourne le bouchon","Hold the bottle upright and twist the cork"],["Si scuote la bottiglia e si spinge il tappo","On secoue la bouteille et on pousse le bouchon","Shake the bottle and push the cork"],["Si usa un cavatappi a vite","On utilise un tire-bouchon à mèche","Use a screw corkscrew"]],"e":["Si tiene il tappo fermo e si fa ruotare la bottiglia inclinata.","On tient le bouchon et on fait tourner la bouteille inclinée.","Hold the cork still and turn the tilted bottle."],"d":["Dopo aver tolto la stagnola e allentato la gabbietta, si inclina la bottiglia, si tiene il tappo con una mano e la base con l'altra, e si fa ruotare la bottiglia. Tenendo il tappo ben stretto, la pressione esce piano, con un leggero sospiro e senza perdere vino.","Après avoir retiré la feuille et desserré le muselet, on incline la bouteille, on tient le bouchon d'une main et le fond de l'autre, puis on fait tourner la bouteille. En tenant fermement le bouchon, la pression s'échappe doucement, avec un léger soupir et sans perte de vin.","After removing the foil and loosening the cage, tilt the bottle, hold the cork in one hand and the base in the other, and turn the bottle. Holding the cork firmly lets the pressure escape gently, with a quiet sigh and without losing any wine."]},{"id":"l13777c47","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si fa subito dopo aver estratto il tappo di un vino fermo?","Que fait-on juste après avoir retiré le bouchon d'un vin tranquille ?","What should you do right after pulling the cork from a still wine?"],"o":[["Pulire il collo dentro e fuori con un panno","Essuyer le col dedans et dehors avec un linge","Wipe the neck inside and out with a cloth"],["Rimettere subito la capsula","Remettre tout de suite la capsule","Put the capsule back on at once"],["Scuotere la bottiglia","Secouer la bouteille","Shake the bottle"],["Scaldare il collo della bottiglia","Chauffer le col de la bouteille","Warm the bottle neck"]],"e":["Dopo l'estrazione si ripulisce il collo, dentro e fuori, con un panno.","Après l'extraction, on essuie le col, dedans et dehors, avec un linge.","Once the cork is out, wipe the neck inside and out."],"d":["Per aprire un vino fermo con tappo di sughero si toglie la parte alta della capsula e si pulisce il collo; poi si centra il cavatappi, lo si avvita e si estrae il tappo con delicatezza. Infine si passa un panno intorno al collo, sia all'interno sia all'esterno, prima di servire.","Pour ouvrir un vin tranquille bouché au liège, on retire le haut de la capsule et on essuie le col ; on centre ensuite le tire-bouchon, on le visse et on tire doucement le bouchon. Enfin, on passe un linge autour du col, à l'intérieur comme à l'extérieur, avant de servir.","To open a still wine with a cork, remove the top of the capsule and wipe the neck; then centre the corkscrew, screw it in and draw the cork out gently. Finally, run a cloth round the neck, both inside and outside, before serving."]},{"id":"l16c77962","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Perché i bicchieri migliori si restringono verso il bordo?","Pourquoi les meilleurs verres se resserrent-ils vers le bord ?","Why do the best wine glasses narrow at the rim?"],"o":[["Per concentrare i profumi del vino","Pour concentrer les arômes du vin","To concentrate the wine's aromas"],["Per tenere il vino più caldo","Pour garder le vin plus chaud","To keep the wine warmer"],["Per ridurre la quantità servita","Pour réduire la quantité servie","To reduce the amount poured"],["Per far durare di più le bollicine","Pour faire durer les bulles","To make bubbles last longer"]],"e":["La forma trattiene i profumi nel bicchiere, così si apprezzano meglio.","Cette forme retient les arômes dans le verre, pour mieux les apprécier.","The shape keeps aromas in the glass so they are easier to appreciate."],"d":["Esistono moltissime forme di bicchieri, ma i migliori hanno la coppa che si stringe verso l'alto. Così i profumi restano concentrati all'interno e si possono apprezzare meglio. È lo stesso motivo per cui, in una degustazione, si sceglie un bicchiere ampio che si restringe in cima.","Il existe de très nombreuses formes de verres, mais les meilleurs ont un calice qui se resserre vers le haut. Ainsi, les arômes restent concentrés à l'intérieur et s'apprécient mieux. C'est pour la même raison qu'en dégustation, on choisit un verre large qui se resserre en haut.","There are many glass shapes, but the best have a bowl that narrows towards the top. This keeps the aromas concentrated inside so they can be appreciated better. It is the same reason a wide glass narrowing at the top is chosen for tasting."]},{"id":"l11f6b8eb","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["In quale bicchiere si serve di solito uno spumante?","Dans quel verre sert-on généralement un effervescent ?","In which glass is sparkling wine usually served?"],"o":[["Nel flûte","Dans une flûte","A flute"],["Nel bicchiere da rosso","Dans un verre à rouge","A red wine glass"],["Nel bicchiere da bianco","Dans un verre à blanc","A white wine glass"],["In un bicchiere senza stelo","Dans un gobelet","A tumbler"]],"e":["Gli spumanti si servono nei flûte; i rossi in bicchieri un po' più grandi dei bianchi.","Les effervescents se servent en flûte ; les rouges en verres un peu plus grands que les blancs.","Sparkling wines go in flutes; reds in glasses slightly larger than whites."],"d":["Di solito gli spumanti si servono nei flûte, mentre i bicchieri da vino rosso sono leggermente più grandi di quelli da bianco. Qualunque sia la forma, il bicchiere deve essere pulito e lucidato, perché sporco e residui di detersivo possono rovinare il vino.","En général, les effervescents se servent en flûte, tandis que les verres à vin rouge sont légèrement plus grands que les verres à vin blanc. Quelle que soit la forme, le verre doit être propre et lustré, car la saleté et les restes de détergent peuvent gâcher le vin.","Sparkling wines are usually served in flutes, while red wine glasses are slightly larger than white wine glasses. Whatever the shape, the glass must be completely clean and polished before use, because dirt and traces of detergent can spoil the wine."]},{"id":"l141c0b29","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Prima di servire, quale segnale nel profumo indica un possibile difetto?","Avant de servir, quel signe au nez peut indiquer un défaut ?","Before serving, which smell suggests a wine may be faulty?"],"o":[["Odore di cartone bagnato","Une odeur de carton mouillé","A wet cardboard smell"],["Profumo di frutta fresca","Une odeur de fruits frais","A fresh fruit aroma"],["Note di vaniglia del rovere","Des notes de vanille du chêne","Vanilla notes from oak"],["Profumi floreali delicati","Des arômes floraux délicats","Delicate floral aromas"]],"e":["Odori di stantio, cartone bagnato o aceto possono segnalare un difetto.","Des odeurs d'éventé, de carton mouillé ou de vinaigre peuvent signaler un défaut.","Stale, wet cardboard or vinegar smells can signal a fault."],"d":["Prima di servire si controlla l'aspetto, cercando velature o pezzetti, e poi il naso. Un vino in buono stato non deve sapere di stantio né avere odori di cartone bagnato o di aceto. Frutta, fiori e vaniglia del rovere sono invece profumi normali e piacevoli.","Avant de servir, on vérifie l'aspect, en cherchant un voile ou des morceaux, puis le nez. Un vin en bon état ne doit pas sentir l'éventé, ni avoir d'odeur de carton mouillé ou de vinaigre. Les fruits, les fleurs et la vanille du chêne sont au contraire des arômes normaux et agréables.","Before serving, check the appearance for haziness or floating bits, then the nose. A sound wine should not smell stale or of wet cardboard or vinegar. Fruit, flowers and vanilla from oak, on the other hand, are normal and pleasant aromas."]},{"id":"l13345f8a","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Osservando il vino prima di servirlo, che cosa può indicare un difetto?","En regardant le vin avant de le servir, qu'est-ce qui peut signaler un défaut ?","When checking a wine's appearance before serving, what may indicate a fault?"],"o":[["Un aspetto velato, torbido","Un aspect voilé, trouble","Haziness"],["Un colore rosa","Une couleur rose","A pink colour"],["Un colore dorato","Une couleur dorée","A golden colour"],["Un colore rosso intenso","Une couleur rouge intense","A deep red colour"]],"e":["Un vino velato può essere difettoso; anche pezzetti galleggianti sono da evitare.","Un vin voilé peut être défectueux ; les morceaux flottants sont aussi à éviter.","A hazy wine may be faulty; floating bits should also be avoided."],"d":["Rosa, dorato o rosso intenso sono semplicemente i colori di diversi tipi di vino. Un vino velato, invece, può segnalare un difetto. Prima di servire si controlla anche che non ci siano pezzetti che galleggiano e che il profumo non sia stantio o di aceto.","Rose, doré ou rouge intense sont simplement les couleurs de différents types de vins. Un vin voilé, en revanche, peut signaler un défaut. Avant de servir, on vérifie aussi qu'aucun morceau ne flotte et que le nez ne sent ni l'éventé ni le vinaigre.","Pink, golden or deep red are simply the colours of different types of wine. A hazy wine, however, may point to a fault. Before serving you should also check that nothing is floating in the wine and that it does not smell stale or of vinegar."]},{"id":"l1e1f40ca","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quando si consiglia un vino da abbinare a un piatto, che cosa conta di più?","Quand on conseille un vin pour un plat, qu'est-ce qui compte le plus ?","When recommending a wine with food, what matters most?"],"o":[["I gusti della persona","Les goûts de la personne","The person's own preferences"],["Il prezzo della bottiglia","Le prix de la bouteille","The price of the bottle"],["L'annata del vino","Le millésime du vin","The vintage of the wine"],["Il colore del piatto","La couleur du plat","The colour of the dish"]],"e":["Se una persona non ama quello stile di vino, non ha senso consigliarlo.","Si une personne n'aime pas ce style de vin, inutile de le conseiller.","If someone dislikes that style of wine, there is no point suggesting it."],"d":["Un abbinamento può sembrare eccezionale a chi lo propone, ma il primo criterio è sempre ciò che piace o non piace a chi berrà il vino. Solo dopo entrano in gioco le reazioni tra cibo e vino, che aiutano a evitare gli abbinamenti che la maggior parte delle persone trova sgradevoli.","Un accord peut sembler exceptionnel à la personne qui le propose, mais le premier critère reste toujours ce qu'aime ou n'aime pas la personne qui boira le vin. Ce n'est qu'ensuite qu'interviennent les réactions entre plat et vin, qui aident à éviter les accords que la plupart des gens trouvent déplaisants.","A pairing may seem exceptional to the person suggesting it, but the first criterion is always what the person drinking the wine likes or dislikes. Only after that do the food and wine interactions come in, helping you avoid the combinations that most people find unpleasant."]},{"id":"l108c6bde","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Un cibo dolce fa sembrare il vino…","Un plat sucré fait paraître le vin…","Sweet food makes a wine seem…"],"o":[["Più acido e meno fruttato","Plus acide et moins fruité","More acidic and less fruity"],["Meno acido e più fruttato","Moins acide et plus fruité","Less acidic and more fruity"],["Più dolce e più corposo","Plus doux et plus corsé","Sweeter and fuller-bodied"],["Meno amaro e più dolce","Moins amer et plus doux","Less bitter and sweeter"]],"e":["La dolcezza del cibo rende il vino più acido, amaro e meno fruttato.","Le sucré du plat rend le vin plus acide, amer et moins fruité.","Sweetness in food makes wine more acidic, bitter and less fruity."],"d":["Il dolce è uno degli elementi più difficili da abbinare. Fa sembrare il vino più secco e amaro, più acido, meno dolce e meno fruttato. Per questo un vino secco servito con un dessert può risultare aspro e spento. Con i piatti dolci funziona meglio un vino che abbia almeno altrettanta dolcezza.","Le sucré est l'un des éléments les plus difficiles à accorder. Il fait paraître le vin plus asséchant et amer, plus acide, moins doux et moins fruité. C'est pourquoi un vin sec servi avec un dessert peut sembler acide et terne. Avec un plat sucré, mieux vaut un vin au moins aussi doux.","Sweetness is one of the hardest elements to pair. It makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. That is why a dry wine served with a dessert can taste sour and dull. With sweet dishes, a wine with at least as much sweetness works better."]},{"id":"l1b8e51b8","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quale elemento del cibo ha sul vino lo stesso effetto della dolcezza?","Quel élément du plat a sur le vin le même effet que le sucré ?","Which food component has the same effect on wine as sweetness?"],"o":[["L'umami","L'umami","Umami"],["Il sale","Le sel","Salt"],["L'acidità","L'acidité","Acidity"],["Il grasso","Le gras","Fat"]],"e":["Umami e dolce rendono entrambi il vino più amaro, acido e meno fruttato.","L'umami et le sucré rendent tous deux le vin plus amer, acide et moins fruité.","Umami and sweetness both make wine more bitter, acidic and less fruity."],"d":["Umami e dolcezza agiscono sul vino nello stesso modo: lo fanno sembrare più secco e amaro, più acido, meno dolce e meno fruttato. Sale e acidità hanno invece l'effetto opposto, mentre il grasso agisce soltanto sulla percezione dell'acidità, che diminuisce.","L'umami et le sucré agissent sur le vin de la même façon : ils le font paraître plus asséchant et amer, plus acide, moins doux et moins fruité. Le sel et l'acidité ont au contraire l'effet inverse, tandis que le gras agit seulement sur la perception de l'acidité, qui diminue.","Umami and sweetness act on wine in the same way: they make it seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. Salt and acidity have the opposite effect, while fat only changes how acidic the wine seems, making it taste less acidic."]},{"id":"l1bd1f2bd","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Un piatto ricco di umami può rendere sgradevole soprattutto quale vino?","Avec un plat riche en umami, quel vin risque le plus de devenir désagréable ?","With an umami-rich dish, which wine is most likely to taste harsh?"],"o":[["Un rosso molto tannico","Un rouge très tannique","A very tannic red"],["Un rosato fruttato","Un rosé fruité","A fruity rosé"],["Un bianco dolce","Un blanc doux","A sweet white"],["Un rosso leggero poco tannico","Un rouge léger peu tannique","A light, low-tannin red"]],"e":["L'umami aumenta amaro e secchezza, già forti in un rosso tannico.","L'umami renforce l'amertume et l'assèchement, déjà forts dans un rouge tannique.","Umami boosts bitterness and dryness, already strong in a tannic red."],"d":["L'umami fa sembrare il vino più secco e amaro, più acido e meno fruttato. In un rosso molto tannico, che già asciuga la bocca e può avere note amare, questo effetto si somma e il vino può diventare duro. Un rosso leggero e poco tannico ne soffre molto meno.","L'umami fait paraître le vin plus asséchant et amer, plus acide et moins fruité. Dans un rouge très tannique, qui assèche déjà la bouche et peut avoir de l'amertume, cet effet s'ajoute et le vin peut devenir dur. Un rouge léger et peu tannique en souffre beaucoup moins.","Umami makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic and less fruity. In a very tannic red, which already dries the mouth and can taste bitter, this effect adds up and the wine can turn harsh. A light, low-tannin red suffers much less."]},{"id":"l142189a5","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Che effetto ha un cibo salato sul vino?","Quel effet un plat salé a-t-il sur le vin ?","What effect does salty food have on wine?"],"o":[["Lo fa sembrare più fruttato e corposo","Il le rend plus fruité et corsé","It seems fruitier and fuller-bodied"],["Lo fa sembrare più amaro e acido","Il le rend plus amer et acide","It seems more bitter and acidic"],["Lo fa sembrare meno fruttato","Il le rend moins fruité","It seems less fruity"],["Ne fa risaltare l'alcol","Il fait ressortir l'alcool","It makes the alcohol stand out"]],"e":["Il sale rende il vino meno amaro e acido, più fruttato e corposo.","Le sel rend le vin moins amer et acide, plus fruité et corsé.","Salt makes wine less bitter and acidic, fruitier and fuller."],"d":["Il sale è un elemento amico del vino. Un cibo salato lo fa sembrare meno secco e amaro, meno acido, più fruttato e con più corpo. Per questo i piatti salati sono in genere facili da abbinare. L'aumento della percezione dell'alcol è invece legato al piccante del peperoncino.","Le sel est un allié du vin. Un plat salé le fait paraître moins asséchant et amer, moins acide, plus fruité et avec plus de corps. C'est pourquoi les plats salés sont en général faciles à accorder. Le renforcement de la sensation d'alcool est en revanche lié au piquant du piment.","Salt is wine-friendly. Salty food makes a wine seem less drying and bitter, less acidic, fruitier and fuller-bodied. That is why salty dishes are generally easy to pair. Making the alcohol more noticeable, on the other hand, is the effect of chilli heat."]},{"id":"l16736dd9","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Un cibo acido fa sembrare il vino…","Un plat acide fait paraître le vin…","Acidic food makes a wine seem…"],"o":[["Più dolce e fruttato","Plus doux et fruité","Sweeter and fruitier"],["Più acido e amaro","Plus acide et amer","More acidic and bitter"],["Meno dolce e fruttato","Moins doux et fruité","Less sweet and fruity"],["Più alcolico e caldo","Plus alcoolisé et chaud","More alcoholic and hot"]],"e":["L'acidità del cibo rende il vino meno acido, più dolce e fruttato.","L'acidité du plat rend le vin moins acide, plus doux et fruité.","Acid in food makes wine less acidic, sweeter and fruitier."],"d":["Può sembrare strano, ma un cibo acido fa percepire il vino come meno acido. Inoltre lo fa sembrare meno secco e amaro, più dolce e più fruttato. Per questo un piatto con una nota acida può ammorbidire un vino molto vivace, che da solo sembrerebbe pungente.","Cela peut surprendre, mais un plat acide fait percevoir le vin comme moins acide. Il le rend aussi moins asséchant et amer, plus doux et plus fruité. C'est pourquoi un plat avec une touche acide peut adoucir un vin très vif, qui seul semblerait tranchant.","It may sound surprising, but acidic food makes a wine taste less acidic. It also makes it seem less drying and bitter, sweeter and fruitier. That is why a dish with a sharp, acidic note can soften a very crisp wine that might seem sharp on its own."]},{"id":"l12766e3e","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede a un vino delicato servito con un piatto dai sapori molto intensi?","Que devient un vin délicat servi avec un plat aux saveurs très intenses ?","What happens to a delicate wine served with a very highly flavoured dish?"],"o":[["Viene sovrastato dal cibo","Il est écrasé par le plat","It is overwhelmed by the food"],["Sembra più corposo","Il paraît plus corsé","It seems fuller-bodied"],["Sembra più dolce","Il paraît plus doux","It seems sweeter"],["Sembra più tannico","Il paraît plus tannique","It seems more tannic"]],"e":["Sapori molto intensi coprono il vino, che sembra sparire.","Des saveurs très intenses couvrent le vin, qui semble disparaître.","Very intense flavours cover the wine, which seems to vanish."],"d":["Quando il cibo ha sapori molto intensi, il vino può esserne sovrastato: i suoi profumi e sapori quasi non si sentono più. È soprattutto un rischio per i vini delicati o leggeri. Con piatti molto saporiti conviene quindi un vino con abbastanza intensità di sapore da reggere il confronto.","Quand le plat a des saveurs très intenses, le vin peut être écrasé : ses arômes et saveurs se perçoivent à peine. C'est surtout un risque pour les vins délicats ou légers. Avec des plats très relevés, mieux vaut donc un vin assez intense en saveurs pour tenir la comparaison.","When food is very highly flavoured, the wine can be overwhelmed: its aromas and flavours can hardly be noticed. This is mainly a risk for delicate or light wines. With strongly flavoured dishes, it is better to choose a wine with enough flavour intensity to hold its own."]},{"id":"l1ebcc2a4","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Che effetto ha un cibo grasso o oleoso sul vino?","Quel effet un plat gras ou huileux a-t-il sur le vin ?","What effect does fatty or oily food have on wine?"],"o":[["Lo fa sembrare meno acido","Il le rend moins acide","It makes it seem less acidic"],["Lo fa sembrare più acido","Il le rend plus acide","It makes it seem more acidic"],["Lo fa sembrare più alcolico","Il le rend plus alcoolisé","It makes it seem more alcoholic"],["Lo fa sembrare più amaro","Il le rend plus amer","It makes it seem more bitter"]],"e":["Il grasso attenua la percezione dell'acidità del vino.","Le gras atténue la perception de l'acidité du vin.","Fat softens how acidic the wine seems."],"d":["Un cibo grasso o oleoso fa sembrare il vino meno acido. È un effetto utile da ricordare: un vino con acidità alta può risultare piacevole accanto a un piatto ricco di grassi. L'aumento dell'alcol percepito dipende invece dal peperoncino, l'aumento dell'amaro da dolce e umami.","Un plat gras ou huileux fait paraître le vin moins acide. C'est un effet utile à retenir : un vin à l'acidité élevée peut être agréable à côté d'un plat riche en gras. L'alcool plus marqué dépend plutôt du piment, et l'amertume accrue du sucré et de l'umami.","Fatty or oily food makes a wine seem less acidic. This is a useful effect to remember: a wine with high acidity can be pleasant alongside a rich, fatty dish. A stronger feel of alcohol comes from chilli instead, while extra bitterness comes from sweetness and umami."]},{"id":"l1db1f34e","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede quando si beve un vino molto alcolico con un piatto piccante?","Que se passe-t-il quand on boit un vin très alcoolisé avec un plat pimenté ?","What happens when a high-alcohol wine is drunk with a chilli-hot dish?"],"o":[["Il bruciore del peperoncino aumenta","La brûlure du piment augmente","The chilli burn increases"],["Il bruciore del peperoncino sparisce","La brûlure du piment disparaît","The chilli burn disappears"],["Il vino sembra più dolce","Le vin paraît plus doux","The wine seems sweeter"],["Il vino sembra meno alcolico","Le vin paraît moins alcoolisé","The wine seems less alcoholic"]],"e":["L'alcol amplifica il piccante e il piccante fa risaltare l'alcol.","L'alcool amplifie le piquant, et le piquant fait ressortir l'alcool.","Alcohol boosts chilli heat, and chilli makes alcohol more noticeable."],"d":["Con il piccante del peperoncino l'alcol del vino diventa più evidente, e l'alcol a sua volta aumenta la sensazione di bruciore. Il risultato è un abbinamento che molte persone trovano scomodo. Con i piatti piccanti, quindi, conviene scegliere un vino non troppo alcolico.","Avec le piquant du piment, l'alcool du vin devient plus perceptible, et l'alcool, à son tour, augmente la sensation de brûlure. Le résultat est un accord que beaucoup de personnes trouvent inconfortable. Avec les plats pimentés, mieux vaut donc choisir un vin pas trop alcoolisé.","With chilli heat, the alcohol in the wine becomes more noticeable, and the alcohol in turn increases the burning sensation. The result is a pairing many people find uncomfortable. With chilli-hot dishes, it is therefore better to choose a wine that is not too high in alcohol."]},{"id":"l13d1192e","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Da dove può venire l'amaro in un vino?","D'où peut venir l'amertume d'un vin ?","Where can bitterness in a wine come from?"],"o":[["Dai tannini o dal rovere","Des tanins ou du chêne","Tannin or oak"],["Dallo zucchero residuo","Du sucre résiduel","Leftover sugar"],["Dall'anidride carbonica","Du gaz carbonique","Carbon dioxide"],["Dalla polpa dell'uva","De la pulpe du raisin","The grape pulp"]],"e":["L'amaro nel vino viene dai tannini delle bucce oppure dal rovere.","L'amertume vient des tanins des peaux ou du chêne.","Bitterness comes from skin tannins or from oak."],"d":["Nelle interazioni con il cibo si parla spesso di vino che diventa «più amaro». Questo amaro può venire dai tannini, presenti soprattutto nei rossi perché arrivano dalle bucce delle uve nere, oppure dal rovere usato per fermentare o maturare il vino. Dolce e umami lo accentuano.","Dans les accords, on dit souvent que le vin devient « plus amer ». Cette amertume peut venir des tanins, présents surtout dans les rouges car ils viennent de la peau des raisins noirs, ou du chêne utilisé pour la fermentation ou l'élevage. Le sucré et l'umami l'accentuent.","In food pairing you often hear that a wine becomes 'more bitter'. This bitterness can come from tannins, found mainly in reds because they come from black grape skins, or from oak used to ferment or mature the wine. Sweetness and umami in food make it stronger."]},{"id":"l180eb393","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quale coppia di elementi del cibo rende il vino meno amaro e meno acido?","Quelle paire d'éléments du plat rend le vin moins amer et moins acide ?","Which pair of food components makes wine seem less bitter and less acidic?"],"o":[["Sale e acidità","Sel et acidité","Salt and acidity"],["Dolcezza e umami","Sucré et umami","Sweetness and umami"],["Dolcezza e piccante","Sucré et piment","Sweetness and chilli"],["Umami e piccante","Umami et piment","Umami and chilli"]],"e":["Sale e acidità sono gli elementi «amici» che ammorbidiscono il vino.","Le sel et l'acidité sont les alliés qui adoucissent le vin.","Salt and acidity are the wine-friendly components that soften it."],"d":["Sale e acidità fanno sembrare il vino meno secco e amaro e meno acido; il sale lo rende anche più fruttato e corposo, l'acidità più dolce e fruttata. Dolcezza e umami fanno l'opposto, mentre il piccante fa risaltare l'alcol e viene a sua volta amplificato da esso.","Le sel et l'acidité font paraître le vin moins asséchant et amer, et moins acide ; le sel le rend aussi plus fruité et corsé, l'acidité plus doux et fruité. Le sucré et l'umami font l'inverse, tandis que le piment fait ressortir l'alcool et est à son tour renforcé par lui.","Salt and acidity make a wine seem less drying and bitter and less acidic; salt also makes it fruitier and fuller, acidity sweeter and fruitier. Sweetness and umami do the opposite, while chilli heat makes alcohol more noticeable and is boosted by it in turn."]},{"id":"l1de7e152","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Con un dessert molto dolce, quale vino è la scelta più sicura?","Avec un dessert très sucré, quel vin est le choix le plus sûr ?","With a very sweet dessert, which wine is the safest choice?"],"o":[["Un vino almeno altrettanto dolce","Un vin au moins aussi doux","A wine at least as sweet"],["Un rosso secco e tannico","Un rouge sec et tannique","A dry, tannic red"],["Un bianco secco e acido","Un blanc sec et acide","A dry, high-acid white"],["Un rosato secco e leggero","Un rosé sec et léger","A dry, light rosé"]],"e":["Il dolce del cibo toglie dolcezza e frutto al vino: serve un vino dolce.","Le sucré du plat retire au vin douceur et fruit : il faut un vin doux.","Sweet food strips sweetness and fruit from wine, so pick a sweet wine."],"d":["Un cibo dolce fa sembrare il vino meno dolce e fruttato, più acido e più amaro. Un vino secco, soprattutto se tannico o molto acido, rischia di risultare aspro e duro. Un vino con almeno la stessa dolcezza del piatto mantiene invece il suo equilibrio.","Un plat sucré fait paraître le vin moins doux et fruité, plus acide et plus amer. Un vin sec, surtout s'il est tannique ou très acide, risque de sembler aigre et dur. Un vin au moins aussi doux que le plat garde au contraire son équilibre.","Sweet food makes a wine seem less sweet and fruity, more acidic and more bitter. A dry wine, especially a tannic or very acidic one, is likely to taste sour and harsh. A wine with at least as much sweetness as the dish keeps its balance instead."]},{"id":"l146d6097","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Con un piatto piccante, quale vino è da evitare in generale?","Avec un plat pimenté, quel vin vaut-il mieux éviter en général ?","With a chilli-hot dish, which wine is generally best avoided?"],"o":[["Un vino molto alcolico","Un vin très alcoolisé","A high-alcohol wine"],["Un vino poco alcolico","Un vin peu alcoolisé","A low-alcohol wine"],["Un vino fruttato","Un vin fruité","A fruity wine"],["Un vino con un po' di dolcezza","Un vin avec un peu de douceur","A wine with some sweetness"]],"e":["Il piccante fa risaltare l'alcol, che a sua volta aumenta il bruciore.","Le piment fait ressortir l'alcool, qui augmente à son tour la brûlure.","Chilli brings out alcohol, which in turn increases the burn."],"d":["L'interazione tra peperoncino e alcol funziona nei due sensi: il piccante rende l'alcol del vino più evidente e l'alcol rende il piatto più bruciante. Un vino molto alcolico rischia quindi di creare un abbinamento sgradevole, mentre uno con meno alcol accompagna il piatto con più equilibrio.","L'interaction entre piment et alcool joue dans les deux sens : le piquant rend l'alcool du vin plus perceptible, et l'alcool rend le plat plus brûlant. Un vin très alcoolisé risque donc de créer un accord désagréable, alors qu'un vin moins alcoolisé accompagne le plat avec plus d'équilibre.","The interaction between chilli and alcohol works both ways: chilli heat makes the wine's alcohol more noticeable, and the alcohol makes the dish burn more. A high-alcohol wine is therefore likely to create an unpleasant pairing, while a wine with less alcohol accompanies the dish in better balance."]},{"id":"l1dc79623","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sull'abbinamento cibo-vino è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur l'accord mets-vins est correcte ?","Which statement about food and wine pairing is correct?"],"o":[["Quasi ogni vino va bene con quasi ogni cibo","Presque tout vin va avec presque tout plat","Most wines suit most foods for most people"],["Ogni piatto ha un solo vino giusto","Chaque plat a un seul bon vin","Every dish has only one right wine"],["Il rosso va solo con la carne","Le rouge ne va qu'avec la viande","Red wine only suits meat"],["Il bianco va solo con il pesce","Le blanc ne va qu'avec le poisson","White wine only suits fish"]],"e":["Per la maggior parte delle persone, la maggior parte dei vini accompagna bene la maggior parte dei cibi.","Pour la plupart des gens, la plupart des vins accompagnent bien la plupart des plats.","For most people, most wines are an acceptable match for most foods."],"d":["L'abbinamento non è fatto di regole rigide. Per quasi tutti, quasi ogni vino è un accompagnamento accettabile per quasi ogni cibo. Basta conoscere le poche interazioni che di solito creano problemi, come dolce, umami e piccante, per avere poi una libertà quasi illimitata nelle scelte.","L'accord mets-vins n'est pas fait de règles rigides. Pour presque tout le monde, presque tout vin accompagne de façon acceptable presque tout plat. Il suffit de connaître les quelques interactions qui posent souvent problème, comme le sucré, l'umami et le piment, pour avoir ensuite une liberté presque illimitée.","Pairing is not a matter of rigid rules. For most people, most wines are an acceptable partner for most foods. You only need to know the few interactions that usually cause trouble, such as sweetness, umami and chilli, and your choices then become almost limitless."]},{"id":"l169eebb3","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Un vino bianco molto acido sembra troppo pungente. Quale piatto lo farà sembrare più morbido?","Un blanc très acide paraît trop vif. Quel plat le fera paraître plus doux ?","A very high-acid white tastes too sharp. Which dish will make it seem softer?"],"o":[["Un piatto con una nota acida","Un plat avec une touche acide","A dish with an acidic touch"],["Un dessert molto dolce","Un dessert très sucré","A very sweet dessert"],["Un piatto ricco di umami","Un plat riche en umami","An umami-rich dish"],["Un piatto molto piccante","Un plat très pimenté","A very hot chilli dish"]],"e":["Il cibo acido fa sembrare il vino meno acido, più dolce e fruttato.","Un plat acide fait paraître le vin moins acide, plus doux et fruité.","Acidic food makes a wine seem less acidic, sweeter and fruitier."],"d":["Un cibo acido «assorbe» parte dell'acidità percepita: il vino sembra meno acido, più dolce e più fruttato. Dolce e umami farebbero invece il contrario, rendendolo ancora più acido. Il piccante non riduce l'acidità ma fa risaltare l'alcol. Anche il sale o il grasso possono aiutare.","Un plat acide « absorbe » une partie de l'acidité perçue : le vin paraît moins acide, plus doux et plus fruité. Le sucré et l'umami feraient au contraire l'inverse, en le rendant encore plus acide. Le piment ne réduit pas l'acidité mais fait ressortir l'alcool. Le sel ou le gras peuvent aussi aider.","Acidic food 'absorbs' some of the perceived acidity: the wine seems less acidic, sweeter and fruitier. Sweetness and umami would do the opposite, making it even more acidic. Chilli does not reduce acidity but brings out alcohol. Salt or fat can also help."]},{"id":"l1d53ecf2","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quale cibo rende un vino più corposo al palato?","Quel type de plat fait paraître un vin plus corsé ?","Which type of food makes a wine seem fuller-bodied?"],"o":[["Un cibo salato","Un plat salé","Salty food"],["Un cibo dolce","Un plat sucré","Sweet food"],["Un cibo ricco di umami","Un plat riche en umami","Umami-rich food"],["Un cibo piccante","Un plat pimenté","Chilli-hot food"]],"e":["Il sale fa sembrare il vino più fruttato e con più corpo.","Le sel fait paraître le vin plus fruité et plus corsé.","Salt makes wine seem fruitier and fuller-bodied."],"d":["Tra gli elementi del cibo, il sale è quello che aggiunge corpo percepito al vino, oltre a renderlo più fruttato, meno amaro e meno acido. Dolce e umami lo fanno sembrare più duro e meno fruttato, mentre il piccante del peperoncino ne fa risaltare soprattutto l'alcol.","Parmi les éléments du plat, le sel est celui qui ajoute du corps perçu au vin, en plus de le rendre plus fruité, moins amer et moins acide. Le sucré et l'umami le font paraître plus dur et moins fruité, tandis que le piment fait surtout ressortir son alcool.","Among the food components, salt is the one that adds perceived body to a wine, as well as making it fruitier, less bitter and less acidic. Sweetness and umami make it seem harsher and less fruity, while chilli heat mainly makes its alcohol stand out."]},{"id":"l1e730b9c","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quale vino è più a rischio con un piatto dolce?","Quel vin est le plus à risque avec un plat sucré ?","Which wine is most at risk with a sweet dish?"],"o":[["Un rosso secco con molti tannini","Un rouge sec très tannique","A dry red with high tannin"],["Un bianco dolce con buona acidità","Un blanc doux bien acide","A sweet white with good acidity"],["Un bianco abboccato e fruttato","Un blanc demi-doux et fruité","A medium-sweet, fruity white"],["Un rosato dolce e fruttato","Un rosé doux et fruité","A sweet, fruity rosé"]],"e":["Il dolce aumenta amaro e secchezza e toglie frutto: un rosso tannico soffre.","Le sucré renforce amertume et assèchement et enlève du fruit : le rouge tannique souffre.","Sweet food boosts bitterness and dryness and removes fruit: a tannic red suffers."],"d":["Un cibo dolce rende il vino più secco e amaro, più acido e meno fruttato. Un rosso secco e tannico ha già una forte sensazione di secchezza e niente dolcezza da opporre, quindi diventa duro. I vini dolci, invece, conservano meglio il loro equilibrio accanto a un piatto dolce.","Un plat sucré rend le vin plus asséchant et amer, plus acide et moins fruité. Un rouge sec et tannique a déjà une forte sensation d'assèchement et aucune douceur à opposer : il devient dur. Les vins doux, eux, gardent mieux leur équilibre à côté d'un plat sucré.","Sweet food makes a wine more drying and bitter, more acidic and less fruity. A dry, tannic red already has a strong drying feel and no sweetness to push back, so it becomes harsh. Sweet wines, by contrast, keep their balance better next to a sweet dish."]},{"id":"l1f65909b","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Un vino rosso sembra più fruttato e meno amaro con un piatto. Quale elemento del piatto è il più probabile?","Un rouge paraît plus fruité et moins amer avec un plat. Quel élément du plat est le plus probable ?","A red wine tastes fruitier and less bitter with a dish. Which food component is most likely responsible?"],"o":[["Il sale","Le sel","Salt"],["La dolcezza","Le sucré","Sweetness"],["L'umami","L'umami","Umami"],["Il piccante","Le piment","Chilli heat"]],"e":["Il sale rende il vino più fruttato e meno amaro.","Le sel rend le vin plus fruité et moins amer.","Salt makes wine fruitier and less bitter."],"d":["Tra gli elementi proposti, solo il sale rende il vino più fruttato e meno amaro, oltre che meno acido e più corposo. Dolcezza e umami hanno l'effetto opposto: più amaro, meno frutto. Il piccante non agisce su frutto e amaro, ma fa risaltare l'alcol del vino.","Parmi les éléments proposés, seul le sel rend le vin plus fruité et moins amer, en plus de le rendre moins acide et plus corsé. Le sucré et l'umami ont l'effet inverse : plus d'amertume, moins de fruit. Le piment n'agit pas sur le fruit et l'amertume, mais fait ressortir l'alcool.","Of the options given, only salt makes a wine fruitier and less bitter, as well as less acidic and fuller-bodied. Sweetness and umami have the opposite effect: more bitterness, less fruit. Chilli heat does not act on fruit and bitterness, but it makes the wine's alcohol stand out."]},{"id":"l1a45562e","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Perché è utile conoscere le interazioni tra cibo e vino?","Pourquoi est-il utile de connaître les interactions entre plat et vin ?","Why is it useful to know the common food and wine interactions?"],"o":[["Per evitare ciò che quasi tutti trovano sgradevole","Pour éviter ce que presque tout le monde trouve désagréable","To avoid what most people find unpleasant"],["Per imporre il proprio gusto agli altri","Pour imposer son goût aux autres","To impose your taste on others"],["Per scegliere sempre lo stesso vino","Pour choisir toujours le même vin","To always choose the same wine"],["Per abbinare solo vini costosi","Pour n'accorder que des vins chers","To pair only expensive wines"]],"e":["Sapendo cosa evitare, le possibilità di abbinamento diventano quasi illimitate.","En sachant quoi éviter, les possibilités d'accord deviennent presque illimitées.","Knowing what to avoid makes your pairing options almost limitless."],"d":["Conoscere le reazioni tipiche, cioè dolce, umami, sale, acido, sapori intensi, grasso e piccante, non serve a trovare l'unico vino giusto, ma a sapere che cosa la maggior parte delle persone vorrebbe evitare. Così non si resta legati a un solo abbinamento e si può sempre partire dai gusti della persona.","Connaître les réactions typiques, c'est-à-dire sucré, umami, sel, acide, saveurs intenses, gras et piment, ne sert pas à trouver l'unique bon vin, mais à savoir ce que la plupart des gens voudraient éviter. On n'est ainsi jamais limité à un seul accord et l'on peut toujours partir des goûts de la personne.","Knowing the typical reactions, from sweetness, umami, salt and acid to intense flavour, fat and chilli, is not about finding the one right wine. It is about knowing what most people would want to avoid. That way you are never tied to one pairing and can always start from the person's own taste."]},{"id":"l1be215d5","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quale elemento del cibo fa sembrare MENO dolce un vino abboccato?","Quel élément du plat fait paraître MOINS doux un vin demi-doux ?","Which food component makes a medium-sweet wine seem LESS sweet?"],"o":[["L'umami","L'umami","Umami"],["L'acidità","L'acidité","Acidity"],["Il sale","Le sel","Salt"],["Il grasso","Le gras","Fat"]],"e":["L'umami toglie al vino dolcezza e frutto, come fa il cibo dolce.","L'umami enlève au vin douceur et fruit, comme le fait un plat sucré.","Umami takes away sweetness and fruit, just as sweet food does."],"d":["L'umami agisce come la dolcezza del cibo: il vino sembra meno dolce e meno fruttato, più amaro e più acido. L'acidità del cibo fa invece l'opposto e rende il vino più dolce e fruttato; il sale lo rende più fruttato e corposo, mentre il grasso ne riduce solo l'acidità percepita.","L'umami agit comme le sucré du plat : le vin paraît moins doux et moins fruité, plus amer et plus acide. L'acidité du plat fait au contraire l'inverse et rend le vin plus doux et fruité ; le sel le rend plus fruité et corsé, tandis que le gras réduit seulement l'acidité perçue.","Umami works like sweetness in food: the wine seems less sweet and less fruity, more bitter and more acidic. Acidity in food does the opposite and makes the wine seem sweeter and fruitier; salt makes it fruitier and fuller, while fat only reduces the perceived acidity."]},{"id":"l195f6c33","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["In che ordine si svolge l'approccio sistematico alla degustazione?","Dans quel ordre se déroule l'approche systématique de la dégustation ?","In what order does the systematic approach to tasting run?"],"o":[["Aspetto, naso, palato","Aspect, nez, bouche","Appearance, nose, palate"],["Naso, aspetto, palato","Nez, aspect, bouche","Nose, appearance, palate"],["Palato, naso, aspetto","Bouche, nez, aspect","Palate, nose, appearance"],["Aspetto, palato, naso","Aspect, bouche, nez","Appearance, palate, nose"]],"e":["Prima si guarda, poi si annusa, infine si assaggia.","On regarde d'abord, puis on sent, enfin on goûte.","First look, then smell, then taste."],"d":["L'approccio sistematico segue sempre lo stesso ordine: aspetto (il colore), naso (aromi di frutta, rovere e altro) e palato (struttura e sapori). Ripetere lo stesso percorso per ogni vino permette di scrivere note coerenti e precise, che si possono confrontare nel tempo.","L'approche systématique suit toujours le même ordre : aspect (la couleur), nez (arômes de fruit, de chêne et autres) et bouche (structure et saveurs). Refaire le même parcours pour chaque vin permet d'écrire des notes cohérentes et précises, que l'on peut comparer dans le temps.","The systematic approach always follows the same order: appearance (colour), nose (fruit, oak and other aromas) and palate (structure and flavours). Repeating the same route for every wine lets you write consistent, accurate notes that you can compare over time."]},{"id":"l156961ab","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Perché è utile seguire sempre lo stesso metodo di degustazione?","Pourquoi est-il utile de suivre toujours la même méthode de dégustation ?","Why is it useful to take the same approach with every wine you taste?"],"o":[["Per scrivere note precise e confrontabili","Pour écrire des notes précises et comparables","To write accurate notes you can compare"],["Per bere più vino in meno tempo","Pour boire plus de vin en moins de temps","To drink more wine in less time"],["Per scaldare il vino nel bicchiere","Pour réchauffer le vin dans le verre","To warm the wine in the glass"],["Per evitare di guardare il colore","Pour éviter de regarder la couleur","To avoid looking at the colour"]],"e":["Un metodo costante dà note accurate da rileggere in futuro.","Une méthode constante donne des notes justes à relire plus tard.","A consistent method gives accurate notes to refer back to."],"d":["Affrontare ogni campione nello stesso modo aiuta a non dimenticare nulla e a descrivere i vini con le stesse parole. Così le note di degustazione risultano accurate e si possono rileggere e confrontare in futuro, per esempio per ricordare le differenze tra due vitigni.","Aborder chaque échantillon de la même façon aide à ne rien oublier et à décrire les vins avec les mêmes mots. Les notes de dégustation sont ainsi justes et peuvent être relues et comparées plus tard, par exemple pour se rappeler les différences entre deux cépages.","Approaching every sample the same way helps you not to miss anything and to describe wines with the same words. Your tasting notes are then accurate and can be read again and compared later, for example to remember the differences between two grape varieties."]},{"id":"l1891238c","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Perché in degustazione serve una superficie bianca?","Pourquoi faut-il une surface blanche pour déguster ?","Why do you need a white surface when tasting?"],"o":[["Per giudicare meglio il colore","Pour mieux juger la couleur","To judge the colour better"],["Per sentire meglio i profumi","Pour mieux sentir les arômes","To smell the aromas better"],["Per tenere il vino fresco","Pour garder le vin frais","To keep the wine cool"],["Per misurare l'alcol","Pour mesurer l'alcool","To measure the alcohol"]],"e":["Lo sfondo bianco aiuta a valutare l'aspetto del vino.","Le fond blanc aide à évaluer l'aspect du vin.","A white background helps you assess the wine's appearance."],"d":["Il colore è ciò che si osserva nella fase dell'aspetto, e uno sfondo bianco permette di vederlo senza interferenze. Gli altri preparativi riguardano il naso e il palato: niente odori che distraggono, un bicchiere che concentra i profumi e una bocca pulita da sapori come caffè o dentifricio.","La couleur est ce que l'on observe à l'étape de l'aspect, et un fond blanc permet de la voir sans interférence. Les autres préparatifs concernent le nez et la bouche : pas d'odeurs gênantes, un verre qui concentre les arômes et une bouche libre de goûts comme le café ou le dentifrice.","Colour is what you look at during the appearance stage, and a white background lets you see it without interference. The other preparations are for the nose and palate: no distracting smells, a glass that concentrates the aromas, and a palate free of flavours such as coffee or toothpaste."]},{"id":"l1ecd45e9","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi può falsare una degustazione?","Lequel de ces éléments peut fausser une dégustation ?","Which of these could spoil a tasting?"],"o":[["Essersi appena lavati i denti","Venir de se brosser les dents","Having just brushed your teeth"],["Usare una superficie bianca","Utiliser une surface blanche","Using a white surface"],["Usare un bicchiere che si restringe in alto","Utiliser un verre qui se resserre en haut","Using a glass that narrows at the top"],["Degustare in una stanza senza odori","Déguster dans une pièce sans odeurs","Tasting in a room with no smells"]],"e":["Sapori residui come dentifricio o caffè alterano il gusto del vino.","Des goûts persistants comme le dentifrice ou le café faussent le vin.","Lingering flavours like toothpaste or coffee distort the wine."],"d":["Per degustare serve un palato pulito, senza sapori che restano in bocca, come quelli del dentifricio o del caffè, che cambierebbero la percezione del vino. Superficie bianca, bicchiere che concentra i profumi e ambiente senza odori sono invece condizioni ideali per una buona degustazione.","Pour déguster, il faut une bouche propre, sans goûts persistants comme ceux du dentifrice ou du café, qui changeraient la perception du vin. Une surface blanche, un verre qui concentre les arômes et une pièce sans odeurs sont au contraire des conditions idéales pour bien déguster.","Tasting needs a clean palate, without flavours lingering in the mouth such as toothpaste or coffee, which would change how the wine tastes. A white surface, a glass that concentrates the aromas and a room free of smells are, on the other hand, ideal conditions for a good tasting."]},{"id":"l15501d1e","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["A questo livello, che cosa si osserva nella fase dell'aspetto?","À ce niveau, qu'observe-t-on à l'étape de l'aspect ?","At this level, what do you assess at the appearance stage?"],"o":[["Il colore: bianco, rosato o rosso","La couleur : blanc, rosé ou rouge","Colour: white, rosé or red"],["Il corpo del vino","Le corps du vin","The wine's body"],["I profumi di frutta","Les arômes de fruit","The fruit aromas"],["Il livello di tannino","Le niveau de tanin","The tannin level"]],"e":["All'aspetto si guarda solo il colore del vino.","À l'aspect, on regarde seulement la couleur du vin.","At appearance you look only at the wine's colour."],"d":["Nell'approccio sistematico di base, l'aspetto riguarda solo il colore del vino, che può essere bianco, rosato o rosso, osservato sopra una superficie bianca. I profumi si valutano al naso, mentre corpo, tannino e le altre caratteristiche strutturali si giudicano al palato, cioè assaggiando il vino.","Dans l'approche systématique de base, l'aspect ne concerne que la couleur : blanc, rosé ou rouge. Les arômes s'évaluent au nez, tandis que le corps, le tanin et les autres caractéristiques de structure se jugent en bouche, c'est-à-dire en goûtant le vin.","In the basic systematic approach, appearance is only about colour: white, rosé or red. Aromas are assessed on the nose, while body, tannin and the other structural characteristics are judged on the palate, meaning when you actually taste the wine."]},{"id":"l1882ccd6","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quali sono le tre famiglie di aromi usate al naso?","Quelles sont les trois familles d'arômes utilisées au nez ?","Which three aroma families are used on the nose?"],"o":[["Frutta, rovere, altro","Fruit, chêne, autres","Fruit, oak, other"],["Dolce, acido, amaro","Sucré, acide, amer","Sweet, sour, bitter"],["Bianco, rosato, rosso","Blanc, rosé, rouge","White, rosé, red"],["Leggero, medio, corposo","Léger, moyen, corsé","Light, medium, full"]],"e":["Gli aromi si classificano in frutta, rovere e altro.","Les arômes se classent en fruit, chêne et autres.","Aromas are grouped into fruit, oak and other."],"d":["Al naso si descrivono gli aromi raggruppandoli in tre famiglie: frutta, che dipende da vitigno e maturazione; rovere, che dà note come vaniglia o cedro; e altro, che comprende erba, fiori, terra, funghi, cuoio e così via. Le stesse famiglie servono poi per i sapori in bocca.","Au nez, on décrit les arômes en les regroupant en trois familles : le fruit, qui dépend du cépage et de la maturité ; le chêne, qui apporte des notes comme la vanille ou le cèdre ; et les autres, qui comprennent herbe, fleurs, terre, champignon, cuir, etc. Les mêmes familles servent ensuite pour les saveurs en bouche.","On the nose, aromas are described by grouping them into three families: fruit, which depends on grape variety and ripeness; oak, which gives notes such as vanilla or cedar; and other, which covers grass, flowers, earth, mushroom, leather and so on. The same families are then used for flavours on the palate."]},{"id":"l17f647ca","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi aromi viene di solito dal rovere?","Lequel de ces arômes vient en général du chêne ?","Which of these aromas usually comes from oak?"],"o":[["Vaniglia","Vanille","Vanilla"],["Limone","Citron","Lemon"],["Erba","Herbe","Grass"],["Fragola","Fraise","Strawberry"]],"e":["Il rovere dà note come vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro e fumo.","Le chêne donne des notes de vanille, coco, clou de girofle, cèdre et fumée.","Oak gives notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke."],"d":["Quando un vino fermenta o matura in botti di rovere può acquisire aromi come vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro e fumo. Limone e fragola appartengono invece alla famiglia della frutta, mentre l'erba rientra nella famiglia «altro», insieme a fiori, terra e cuoio.","Quand un vin fermente ou est élevé en fût de chêne, il peut prendre des arômes de vanille, noix de coco, clou de girofle, cèdre et fumée. Le citron et la fraise appartiennent en revanche à la famille du fruit, tandis que l'herbe entre dans la famille « autres », avec les fleurs, la terre et le cuir.","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, it can pick up aromas such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. Lemon and strawberry belong to the fruit family instead, while grass falls into the 'other' family, along with flowers, earth and leather."]},{"id":"l133a9329","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["In quale famiglia di aromi rientrano funghi e cuoio?","Dans quelle famille d'arômes classe-t-on le champignon et le cuir ?","Which aroma family do mushroom and leather belong to?"],"o":[["Altro","Autres","Other"],["Frutta","Fruit","Fruit"],["Rovere","Chêne","Oak"],["Struttura","Structure","Structure"]],"e":["Funghi e cuoio non sono né frutta né rovere: rientrano in «altro».","Champignon et cuir ne sont ni fruit ni chêne : ils vont dans « autres ».","Mushroom and leather are neither fruit nor oak, so they are 'other'."],"d":["La famiglia «altro» raccoglie tutti gli aromi che non sono né frutta né rovere: erba, fiori, erbe aromatiche, verdure, terra, funghi e cuoio. È questa grande varietà a rendere il vino così interessante. La struttura, invece, non è una famiglia di aromi ma riguarda sensazioni come acidità e tannino.","La famille « autres » regroupe tous les arômes qui ne sont ni du fruit ni du chêne : herbe, fleurs, herbes aromatiques, légumes, terre, champignon et cuir. C'est cette grande variété qui rend le vin si intéressant. La structure, elle, n'est pas une famille d'arômes : elle concerne des sensations comme l'acidité et le tanin.","The 'other' family gathers all aromas that are neither fruit nor oak: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. This wide variety is what makes wine so interesting. Structure, by contrast, is not an aroma family at all; it covers sensations such as acidity and tannin."]},{"id":"l1350c243","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale caratteristica strutturale fa salivare?","Quelle caractéristique de structure fait saliver ?","Which structural characteristic makes your mouth water?"],"o":[["L'acidità","L'acidité","Acidity"],["Il tannino","Le tanin","Tannin"],["Il corpo","Le corps","Body"],["La dolcezza","La douceur","Sweetness"]],"e":["L'acidità fa salivare e dà al vino freschezza.","L'acidité fait saliver et donne de la fraîcheur au vin.","Acidity makes your mouth water and gives freshness."],"d":["L'acidità viene direttamente dal succo d'uva e si riconosce facilmente perché fa salivare. Dà al vino un carattere rinfrescante: troppa lo rende aspro, troppo poca lo rende piatto. Il tannino, al contrario, asciuga la bocca, mentre il corpo descrive quanto il vino la riempie.","L'acidité vient directement du jus de raisin et se reconnaît facilement parce qu'elle fait saliver. Elle donne au vin un caractère rafraîchissant : trop, il devient agressif ; trop peu, il paraît plat. Le tanin, au contraire, assèche la bouche, tandis que le corps décrit à quel point le vin la remplit.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice and is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. It gives wine a refreshing character: too much makes it unpleasantly sharp, too little makes it lose freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth, while body describes how much the wine fills it."]},{"id":"l1b476be5","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Che cosa descrive il «corpo» di un vino?","Que décrit le « corps » d'un vin ?","What does the 'body' of a wine describe?"],"o":[["Quanto il vino riempie la bocca","À quel point le vin remplit la bouche","How mouth-filling the wine feels"],["Quanto è intenso il colore","L'intensité de la couleur","How deep the colour is"],["Quanto zucchero contiene","La quantité de sucre","How much sugar it contains"],["Quanto profuma di frutta","L'intensité des arômes de fruit","How fruity it smells"]],"e":["Il corpo è la sensazione complessiva di pienezza del vino in bocca.","Le corps est la sensation globale de plénitude du vin en bouche.","Body is the overall sense of fullness in the mouth."],"d":["Molti fattori contribuiscono al corpo, quindi il modo più semplice per valutarlo è chiedersi quanto il vino riempie la bocca. I vini corposi sembrano densi e avvolgenti, quelli leggeri più delicati. Il corpo si valuta al palato, non osservando il colore né annusando il vino.","De nombreux facteurs contribuent au corps ; le plus simple pour l'évaluer est donc de se demander à quel point le vin remplit la bouche. Les vins corsés paraissent denses et enveloppants, les vins légers plus délicats. Le corps s'évalue en bouche, pas en observant la couleur ni en sentant le vin.","Many factors contribute to body, so the easiest way to judge it is to ask how mouth-filling the wine is. Full-bodied wines feel dense and mouth-filling, light-bodied wines more delicate. Body is assessed on the palate, not by looking at the colour or smelling the wine."]},{"id":"l1a76bd7d","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale gruppo elenca le caratteristiche strutturali valutate al palato?","Quel groupe énumère les caractéristiques de structure évaluées en bouche ?","Which list shows the structural characteristics assessed on the palate?"],"o":[["Dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol, corpo","Douceur, acidité, tanin, alcool, corps","Sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body"],["Colore, frutta, rovere, alcol, corpo","Couleur, fruit, chêne, alcool, corps","Colour, fruit, oak, alcohol, body"],["Frutta, rovere, altro, acidità, tannino","Fruit, chêne, autres, acidité, tanin","Fruit, oak, other, acidity, tannin"],["Dolcezza, colore, frutta, alcol, corpo","Douceur, couleur, fruit, alcool, corps","Sweetness, colour, fruit, alcohol, body"]],"e":["Le cinque caratteristiche strutturali sono dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol e corpo.","Les cinq caractéristiques de structure sont douceur, acidité, tanin, alcool et corps.","The five structural characteristics are sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body."],"d":["Al palato si valutano due cose: la struttura e i sapori. La struttura comprende dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol e corpo. Frutta, rovere e altro sono invece famiglie di aromi e sapori, mentre il colore appartiene alla fase dell'aspetto. Tenere separate queste categorie rende le note più chiare.","En bouche, on évalue deux choses : la structure et les saveurs. La structure comprend douceur, acidité, tanin, alcool et corps. Fruit, chêne et autres sont en revanche des familles d'arômes et de saveurs, tandis que la couleur relève de l'étape de l'aspect. Séparer ces catégories rend les notes plus claires.","On the palate you assess two things: structure and flavours. Structure covers sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body. Fruit, oak and other, on the other hand, are families of aromas and flavours, while colour belongs to the appearance stage. Keeping these categories apart makes your notes clearer."]},{"id":"l1b54a30d","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Assaggiando un rosso, senti la bocca che si asciuga. Quale caratteristica stai percependo?","En goûtant un rouge, tu sens ta bouche s'assécher. Quelle caractéristique perçois-tu ?","Tasting a red wine, your mouth feels dry. Which characteristic are you noticing?"],"o":[["Il tannino","Le tanin","Tannin"],["L'acidità","L'acidité","Acidity"],["La dolcezza","La douceur","Sweetness"],["Il frutto","Le fruit","Fruitiness"]],"e":["Il tannino, che viene dalle bucce, asciuga la bocca.","Le tanin, qui vient des peaux, assèche la bouche.","Tannin, from the grape skins, dries the mouth."],"d":["Il tannino è tipico dei vini rossi perché proviene dalle bucce delle uve nere, che restano a contatto con il succo durante la fermentazione. Si sente più come una sensazione che come un sapore: la bocca si asciuga. L'acidità, invece, fa salivare.","Le tanin est typique des vins rouges car il vient de la peau des raisins noirs, qui restent au contact du jus pendant la fermentation. On le perçoit davantage comme une sensation que comme un goût : la bouche s'assèche. L'acidité, au contraire, fait saliver.","Tannin is typical of red wines because it comes from the skins of black grapes, which stay in contact with the juice during fermentation. It is felt more than tasted: the mouth dries out. Acidity, by contrast, makes your mouth water."]}],"lessons":[{"c":"p1","t":["Com'è fatto un acino d'uva","Ce qu'il y a dans un grain de raisin","Inside a grape"],"p":[["Il vino nasce da un'idea semplice: si schiaccia l'uva, se ne libera il succo dolce e lo si lascia fermentare. Per questo il vino si può definire succo d'uva fermentato. Per capire che cosa finirà nel bicchiere conviene quindi partire dall'acino, che ha due parti principali: la buccia all'esterno e la polpa all'interno. Ognuna porta qualcosa di diverso al vino.","Le vin repose sur une idée simple : on écrase le raisin pour libérer son jus sucré, puis on le laisse fermenter. On peut donc définir le vin comme du jus de raisin fermenté. Pour comprendre ce que l'on trouvera dans le verre, il faut partir du grain de raisin, qui se compose de deux parties principales : la peau à l'extérieur et la pulpe à l'intérieur. Chacune apporte quelque chose de différent au vin.","Wine starts from a simple idea: crush grapes to free their sweet juice, then let that juice ferment. That is why wine can be described as fermented grape juice. To understand what ends up in the glass, it helps to start with the grape itself, which has two main parts: the skin on the outside and the pulp on the inside. Each one gives something different to the wine."],["Esistono due grandi famiglie di uve: bianche e nere. Tagliate a metà si somigliano molto, perché la differenza sta quasi tutta nella buccia. Le uve nere hanno una buccia dal colore intenso che contiene anche i tannini, sostanze che lasciano in bocca una sensazione di secchezza. Le uve bianche, a maturità, hanno invece una buccia di colore dorato.","Il existe deux grandes familles de raisins : blancs et noirs. Coupés en deux, ils se ressemblent beaucoup, car la différence se trouve surtout dans la peau. Les raisins noirs ont une peau très colorée qui contient aussi des tanins, des substances qui donnent une sensation de sécheresse en bouche. Les raisins blancs, une fois mûrs, ont une peau de couleur dorée.","There are two broad families of grapes: white and black. Cut in half, they look very much alike, because the real difference lies mainly in the skin. Black grapes have deeply coloured skins that also hold tannins, substances that leave your mouth feeling dry. White grapes, once ripe, have skins with a golden colour."],["La polpa è la parte morbida e carnosa dell'acino e contiene il succo. Questo succo è formato soprattutto da acqua, zucchero e acido. Un dettaglio importante: il colore della polpa è lo stesso sia nelle uve bianche sia in quelle nere. Il colore di un vino rosso, quindi, non viene dal succo ma dalle bucce: è una chiave per capire più avanti come si fanno i diversi vini.","La pulpe est la partie tendre et charnue du grain ; c'est elle qui contient le jus. Ce jus est composé surtout d'eau, de sucre et d'acide. Détail important : la couleur de la pulpe est la même pour les raisins blancs et les raisins noirs. La couleur d'un vin rouge ne vient donc pas du jus mais des peaux, une clé pour comprendre plus tard comment on élabore les différents vins.","The pulp is the soft, fleshy part of the grape and it holds the juice. That juice is made up mostly of water, sugar and acid. One important detail: the pulp has the same colour whether the grape is white or black. So the colour of a red wine does not come from the juice but from the skins, a key idea for understanding later how the different wines are made."]],"k":[["Il vino è succo d'uva fermentato.","Le vin est du jus de raisin fermenté.","Wine is fermented grape juice."],["Buccia delle uve nere: colore intenso e tannini.","Peau des raisins noirs : couleur intense et tanins.","Black grape skins: deep colour and tannins."],["I tannini lasciano la bocca secca.","Les tanins assèchent la bouche.","Tannins make the mouth feel dry."],["Polpa: succo fatto di acqua, zucchero e acido.","Pulpe : jus fait d'eau, de sucre et d'acide.","Pulp: juice made of water, sugar and acid."],["La polpa ha lo stesso colore nelle uve bianche e nere.","La pulpe a la même couleur dans les raisins blancs et noirs.","Pulp is the same colour in white and black grapes."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["L'anno della vite","L'année de la vigne","The vine's year"],"p":[["L'uva è il frutto della vite, una pianta che può vivere per diversi decenni. Dopo l'impianto servono un paio d'anni perché la vite diventi adulta; da quel momento produce un raccolto ogni anno. Il suo ciclo segue le stagioni: fiorisce in primavera, i frutti maturano durante l'estate e la vendemmia arriva verso la fine dell'estate.","Le raisin est le fruit de la vigne, une plante qui peut vivre plusieurs dizaines d'années. Après la plantation, il faut environ deux ans pour que la vigne arrive à maturité ; elle donne ensuite une récolte chaque année. Son cycle suit les saisons : floraison au printemps, maturation des fruits pendant l'été et vendanges vers la fin de l'été.","Grapes are the fruit of the grape vine, a plant that can live for several decades. After planting, a vine needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year. Its cycle follows the seasons: it flowers in spring, the fruit ripens through the summer and the grapes are picked towards the end of summer."],["In primavera la vite produce grappoli di piccoli fiori. Ogni singolo fiore è destinato a trasformarsi in un acino. Subito dopo la fioritura gli acini appena formati sono piccoli, duri e verdi, sia che si tratti di uve bianche sia di uve nere: in questa fase non si distinguono ancora e non sono pronti per fare vino.","Au printemps, la vigne produit des grappes de petites fleurs. Chaque fleur est appelée à devenir un grain de raisin. Juste après la floraison, les jeunes grains sont petits, durs et verts, qu'il s'agisse de raisins blancs ou noirs : à ce stade, on ne peut pas encore les distinguer et ils ne sont pas prêts pour faire du vin.","In spring the vine produces clusters of tiny flowers. Each single flower is set to become one grape. Right after flowering, the young grapes are small, hard and green, whether they will end up white or black: at this stage you cannot yet tell them apart, and they are far from ready to make wine."],["Perché la vite cresca bene e dia uva di qualità servono la giusta quantità di sole e di calore: se fa troppo freddo o troppo caldo non ci riesce. La vite preferisce inoltre zone con un inverno abbastanza freddo da permetterle di riposare. Per questo la maggior parte dei vigneti si trova in due fasce del pianeta, all'incirca tra i 30° e i 50° di latitudine, a nord e a sud dell'Equatore.","Pour bien pousser et donner des raisins de qualité, la vigne a besoin de la bonne dose de soleil et de chaleur : s'il fait trop froid ou trop chaud, elle n'y parvient pas. Elle préfère aussi les zones où l'hiver est assez froid pour lui permettre de se reposer. C'est pourquoi la plupart des vignobles se situent dans deux bandes du globe, à peu près entre 30° et 50° de latitude, au nord et au sud de l'équateur.","To grow well and give good quality fruit, a vine needs the right amount of sunlight and heat: if it is too cold or too hot, it cannot manage. Vines also do best where the winter is cold enough to let them rest. That is why most vineyards lie in two bands around the globe, roughly between 30° and 50° of latitude, north and south of the Equator."]],"k":[["Una vite adulta dà un raccolto ogni anno e può vivere decenni.","Une vigne adulte donne une récolte par an et peut vivre des décennies.","A mature vine gives a crop every year and can live for decades."],["Primavera: fioritura; ogni fiore diventa un acino.","Printemps : floraison ; chaque fleur devient un grain.","Spring: flowering; each flower becomes a grape."],["Estate: maturazione; fine estate: vendemmia.","Été : maturation ; fin de l'été : vendanges.","Summer: ripening; late summer: harvest."],["La vite vuole sole e calore giusti e un inverno freddo per riposare.","La vigne veut assez de soleil et de chaleur et un hiver froid pour se reposer.","Vines need the right sun and heat, plus a cold winter to rest."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["Che cosa succede quando l'uva matura","Ce qui se passe quand le raisin mûrit","What happens as grapes ripen"],"p":[["Durante l'estate gli acini piccoli e duri cambiano profondamente. Si gonfiano perché si riempiono d'acqua, e allo stesso tempo il loro contenuto di zucchero sale mentre quello di acido scende. Anche i sapori evolvono e diventano più maturi. Un acino acerbo è quindi aspro e poco saporito, mentre un acino maturo è più grosso, più dolce e meno acido.","Pendant l'été, les petits grains durs changent profondément. Ils gonflent en se remplissant d'eau, tandis que leur teneur en sucre augmente et que leur teneur en acide diminue. Les saveurs évoluent elles aussi et deviennent plus mûres. Un raisin vert est donc acide et peu savoureux, alors qu'un raisin mûr est plus gros, plus sucré et moins acide.","Over the summer the small, hard grapes change a great deal. They swell as they fill with water, while their sugar content goes up and their acid content goes down. Their flavours also develop and become riper. An unripe grape is therefore sour and not very tasty, whereas a ripe grape is bigger, sweeter and less acidic."],["Con la maturazione cambia anche il colore della buccia. Le uve bianche passano dal verde a un colore dorato, mentre le uve nere passano dal verde al viola. Osservare il colore è quindi un primo indizio di quanto l'uva sia vicina alla vendemmia, insieme agli altri cambiamenti: più acqua, più zucchero, meno acido e sapori più maturi.","Avec la maturation, la couleur de la peau change aussi. Les raisins blancs passent du vert au doré, tandis que les raisins noirs passent du vert au violet. La couleur donne donc un premier indice sur la proximité des vendanges, en même temps que les autres changements : plus d'eau, plus de sucre, moins d'acide et des saveurs plus mûres.","Ripening also changes the colour of the skin. White grapes turn from green to golden, while black grapes turn from green to purple. Colour is therefore a first clue to how close the grapes are to harvest, alongside the other changes: more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours."],["Questi cambiamenti contano perché finiscono direttamente nel vino. Lo zucchero dell'uva è ciò che i lieviti trasformeranno in alcol: più zucchero significa, in genere, un vino più alcolico. L'acido resta nel vino e gli dà freschezza. I sapori dell'acino diventano gli aromi di frutta nel bicchiere. Il momento della vendemmia, quindi, orienta già lo stile del vino.","Ces changements comptent car ils passent directement dans le vin. Le sucre du raisin est ce que les levures transformeront en alcool : plus de sucre donne en général un vin plus alcoolisé. L'acide reste dans le vin et lui apporte de la fraîcheur. Les saveurs du raisin deviennent les arômes de fruits dans le verre. Le moment des vendanges oriente donc déjà le style du vin.","These changes matter because they pass straight into the wine. The sugar in the grape is what yeast will turn into alcohol, so more sugar generally means a stronger wine. The acid stays in the wine and gives it freshness. The grape's flavours become the fruit aromas in the glass. The moment of picking therefore already shapes the style of the wine."]],"k":[["Maturando l'uva si gonfia d'acqua.","En mûrissant, le raisin gonfle d'eau.","Ripening grapes swell with water."],["Lo zucchero sale, l'acido scende.","Le sucre augmente, l'acide diminue.","Sugar rises, acid falls."],["I sapori diventano più maturi.","Les saveurs deviennent plus mûres.","Flavours become riper."],["Uve bianche: da verdi a dorate; uve nere: da verdi a viola.","Raisins blancs : du vert au doré ; noirs : du vert au violet.","White grapes: green to golden; black grapes: green to purple."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["Clima fresco e clima caldo","Climat frais et climat chaud","Cool climate and warm climate"],"p":[["Le zone viticole più vicine ai poli hanno un clima fresco. Esempi tipici sono la Germania e il nord della Francia. Qui le temperature medie sono basse e il sole può essere meno forte che vicino all'Equatore; in certe annate l'uva fatica persino a maturare. Nei climi freschi è frequente coltivare uve bianche.","Les régions viticoles les plus proches des pôles ont un climat frais. L'Allemagne et le nord de la France en sont des exemples typiques. Les températures moyennes y sont basses et le soleil peut être moins fort que près de l'équateur ; certaines années, le raisin a même du mal à mûrir. Dans les climats frais, on cultive souvent des raisins blancs.","Wine regions closer to the poles have a cool climate. Germany and northern France are typical examples. Average temperatures are low and the sunshine can be weaker than nearer the Equator; in some years the grapes even struggle to ripen. In cool climates, growing white grapes is common."],["Le zone più vicine all'Equatore hanno invece un clima caldo, come alcune parti dell'Australia e della California. Le temperature medie sono alte, il sole è più intenso e l'uva matura senza difficoltà quasi ogni anno. Nei climi caldi è frequente coltivare uve nere, che approfittano di tutto questo calore.","Les régions plus proches de l'équateur ont au contraire un climat chaud, comme certaines parties de l'Australie et de la Californie. Les températures moyennes y sont élevées, le soleil est plus intense et le raisin mûrit sans difficulté d'une année à l'autre. Dans les climats chauds, on cultive souvent des raisins noirs, qui profitent de cette chaleur.","Regions closer to the Equator have a warm climate instead, such as parts of Australia and parts of California. Average temperatures are high, the sunshine is more intense and the grapes ripen reliably year after year. In warm climates it is common to grow black grapes, which make the most of all that heat."],["Il clima lascia un'impronta precisa sull'uva. In generale, più fa fresco, meno zucchero e più acidità ci sono negli acini; più fa caldo, più zucchero e meno acidità, con sapori più maturi. Ne derivano stili diversi: un vino da clima fresco tende a essere più leggero e vivace, uno da clima caldo più ricco e maturo.","Le climat laisse une empreinte nette sur le raisin. En règle générale, plus il fait frais, moins il y a de sucre et plus il y a d'acidité dans les grains ; plus il fait chaud, plus il y a de sucre et moins d'acidité, avec des saveurs plus mûres. On obtient ainsi des styles différents : un vin de climat frais tend à être plus léger et vif, un vin de climat chaud plus riche et mûr.","Climate leaves a clear mark on the grapes. As a rule, the cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, together with riper flavours. This leads to different styles: a cool-climate wine tends to be lighter and fresher, a warm-climate wine richer and riper."],["Lo Chardonnay è un ottimo esempio. Coltivato in clima fresco dà vini con profumi di frutta verde, come la mela, e di agrumi, come il limone. Coltivato in clima caldo, lo stesso vitigno offre invece frutta a nocciolo, come la pesca, e frutta tropicale, come l'ananas. Stessa uva, stile molto diverso: è il clima a fare la differenza.","Le Chardonnay en est un bon exemple. Cultivé en climat frais, il donne des vins aux arômes de fruits verts comme la pomme et d'agrumes comme le citron. Cultivé en climat chaud, le même cépage offre plutôt des fruits à noyau comme la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas. Même raisin, style très différent : c'est le climat qui fait la différence.","Chardonnay is a good example. Grown in a cool climate, it gives wines with aromas of green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. Grown in a warm climate, the same grape shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple instead. Same grape, very different style: the climate makes the difference."]],"k":[["Clima fresco: vicino ai poli (es. Germania, nord della Francia).","Climat frais : près des pôles (ex. Allemagne, nord de la France).","Cool climate: nearer the poles (e.g. Germany, northern France)."],["Clima caldo: vicino all'Equatore (es. parti di Australia e California).","Climat chaud : près de l'équateur (ex. parties de l'Australie et de la Californie).","Warm climate: nearer the Equator (e.g. parts of Australia and California)."],["Più fresco → meno zucchero, più acidità → vino più leggero e fresco.","Plus frais → moins de sucre, plus d'acidité → vin plus léger et frais.","Cooler → less sugar, more acidity → lighter, fresher wine."],["Più caldo → più zucchero, meno acidità, sapori più maturi.","Plus chaud → plus de sucre, moins d'acidité, saveurs plus mûres.","Warmer → more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours."],["Fresco: spesso uve bianche; caldo: spesso uve nere.","Frais : souvent raisins blancs ; chaud : souvent raisins noirs.","Cool: often white grapes; warm: often black grapes."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["La fermentazione alcolica","La fermentation alcoolique","Alcoholic fermentation"],"p":[["Il passaggio che trasforma il succo d'uva in vino si chiama fermentazione alcolica. Ne sono protagonisti i lieviti, organismi così piccoli da essere invisibili a occhio nudo. I lieviti si nutrono dello zucchero contenuto nel succo e lo trasformano in due prodotti: alcol e anidride carbonica, un gas. In sintesi: zucchero + lieviti → alcol + anidride carbonica.","L'étape qui transforme le jus de raisin en vin s'appelle la fermentation alcoolique. Ses actrices sont les levures, des organismes si petits qu'on ne peut pas les voir à l'œil nu. Les levures se nourrissent du sucre contenu dans le jus et le transforment en deux produits : de l'alcool et du gaz carbonique. En résumé : sucre + levures → alcool + gaz carbonique.","The step that turns grape juice into wine is called alcoholic fermentation. The workers behind it are yeast, organisms so tiny you cannot see them with the naked eye. Yeast feed on the sugar in the juice and turn it into two products: alcohol and carbon dioxide, which is a gas. In short: sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide."],["Nella maggior parte dei casi la fermentazione va avanti finché i lieviti non hanno consumato tutto lo zucchero: il risultato è un vino secco. L'alcol resta nel vino appena nato, mentre l'anidride carbonica di solito si disperde nell'aria. Esistono però delle eccezioni, come i vini dolci o gli spumanti, che si vedranno parlando dei tipi e degli stili di vino.","Dans la plupart des cas, la fermentation se poursuit jusqu'à ce que les levures aient consommé tout le sucre : on obtient alors un vin sec. L'alcool reste dans le vin nouveau, tandis que le gaz carbonique s'échappe en général dans l'air. Il existe toutefois des exceptions, comme les vins doux ou les vins effervescents, que l'on verra avec les types et styles de vins.","In most cases fermentation carries on until the yeast have used up all the sugar, which gives a dry wine. The alcohol stays in the newly made wine, while the carbon dioxide usually escapes into the air. There are exceptions, such as sweet wines and sparkling wines, which you will meet when looking at the types and styles of wine."],["La quantità di alcol di un vino si indica di solito come percentuale del volume, abbreviata in vol. o abv. Un vino al 10% significa che un decimo del liquido è alcol. Ricorda il legame con la vigna: è lo zucchero accumulato dall'uva durante la maturazione che i lieviti trasformano in alcol.","La teneur en alcool d'un vin s'indique en général en pourcentage du volume, noté % vol. Un vin à 10 % vol. signifie qu'un dixième du liquide est de l'alcool. Pense au lien avec la vigne : c'est le sucre accumulé par le raisin pendant la maturation que les levures transforment en alcool.","The amount of alcohol in a wine is usually given as alcohol by volume, shortened to abv. A wine at 10% abv means that one tenth of the liquid is alcohol. Remember the link with the vineyard: it is the sugar the grapes built up while ripening that the yeast turn into alcohol."]],"k":[["Zucchero + lieviti → alcol + anidride carbonica.","Sucre + levures → alcool + gaz carbonique.","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide."],["I lieviti sono organismi microscopici che mangiano zucchero.","Les levures sont des organismes microscopiques qui mangent le sucre.","Yeast are microscopic organisms that eat sugar."],["Di solito i lieviti consumano tutto lo zucchero: vino secco.","En général, les levures consomment tout le sucre : vin sec.","Usually the yeast eat all the sugar: a dry wine."],["L'alcol resta nel vino; l'anidride carbonica di solito se ne va.","L'alcool reste dans le vin ; le gaz carbonique s'échappe en général.","Alcohol stays in the wine; carbon dioxide usually escapes."],["10% vol. = un decimo del liquido è alcol.","10 % vol. = un dixième du liquide est de l'alcool.","10% abv = one tenth of the liquid is alcohol."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["Come si fa un vino bianco","Comment on fait un vin blanc","How white wine is made"],"p":[["Il vino bianco si ottiene di solito da uve bianche. Dopo la vendemmia l'uva viene pigiata, cioè schiacciata, così da liberare una parte del succo. Subito dopo l'uva pigiata passa alla pressatura, che spreme le bucce e recupera il succo rimasto. L'idea chiave è che nel bianco il succo viene separato dalle bucce prima della fermentazione.","Le vin blanc s'obtient généralement à partir de raisins blancs. Après la vendange, le raisin est foulé, c'est-à-dire écrasé, pour libérer une partie du jus. Juste après, le raisin foulé passe au pressurage, qui presse les peaux et récupère le reste du jus. L'idée clé : pour le blanc, le jus est séparé des peaux avant la fermentation.","White wine is usually made from white grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed, which releases some of the juice. Straight afterwards the crushed grapes are pressed, squeezing the skins to collect the rest of the juice. The key idea is that, for white wine, the juice is separated from the skins before fermentation begins."],["A questo punto si aggiungono i lieviti al succo e comincia la fermentazione. Può avvenire in vasche di acciaio inossidabile oppure in botti di rovere. Terminata la fermentazione arriva la fase di maturazione, in cui il vino riposa, di nuovo in acciaio o in rovere. L'ultima tappa è l'imbottigliamento, dopo il quale il vino è pronto per arrivare sulla tavola.","On ajoute ensuite les levures au jus et la fermentation commence. Elle peut se dérouler en cuves en acier inoxydable ou en fûts de chêne. Une fois la fermentation terminée vient l'élevage, pendant lequel le vin repose, là encore en inox ou en chêne. La dernière étape est la mise en bouteille, après laquelle le vin est prêt à arriver sur la table.","Yeast are then added to the juice and fermentation starts. It can take place in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Once fermentation is over comes maturation, when the wine rests, again either in stainless steel or in oak. The final step is bottling, after which the wine is ready to reach the table."],["Curiosità utile per l'esame: un vino bianco si può fare anche con uve nere. Il colore delle uve nere sta tutto nella buccia, mentre il loro succo è incolore. Se l'uva nera viene pressata con delicatezza prima della fermentazione, e le bucce vengono tolte subito, si ottiene un succo adatto a produrre un vino bianco.","Point utile pour l'examen : on peut aussi faire du vin blanc avec des raisins noirs. La couleur des raisins noirs se trouve entièrement dans la peau, et leur jus est incolore. Si le raisin noir est pressé délicatement avant la fermentation et que les peaux sont retirées tout de suite, on obtient un jus adapté à l'élaboration d'un vin blanc.","A useful point for the exam: white wine can also be made from black grapes. The colour of black grapes is all in the skin, and their juice is colourless. If black grapes are pressed gently before fermentation and the skins are removed straight away, the juice obtained is suitable for making a white wine."]],"k":[["Bianco: pigiatura → pressatura → fermentazione → maturazione → imbottigliamento.","Blanc : foulage → pressurage → fermentation → élevage → mise en bouteille.","White: crushing → pressing → fermentation → maturation → bottling."],["Nel bianco la pressatura avviene prima della fermentazione.","Pour le blanc, le pressurage a lieu avant la fermentation.","For white wine, pressing comes before fermentation."],["Fermentazione e maturazione: in acciaio inox o in rovere.","Fermentation et élevage : en inox ou en chêne.","Fermentation and maturation: stainless steel or oak."],["Il succo delle uve nere è incolore: si può fare bianco da uve nere.","Le jus des raisins noirs est incolore : on peut faire du blanc avec du noir.","Black grape juice is colourless, so it can make white wine."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["Come si fa un vino rosso","Comment on fait un vin rouge","How red wine is made"],"p":[["Il vino rosso si fa sempre con uve nere. Dopo la vendemmia l'uva viene pigiata e, a differenza del bianco, il succo non viene separato: succo e bucce finiscono insieme nel recipiente di fermentazione. Questa è la grande differenza rispetto al vino bianco, perché è proprio dalle bucce che arriveranno colore e tannini.","Le vin rouge se fait toujours avec des raisins noirs. Après la vendange, le raisin est foulé et, contrairement au blanc, le jus n'est pas séparé : jus et peaux vont ensemble dans la cuve de fermentation. C'est la grande différence avec le vin blanc, car c'est précisément des peaux que viendront la couleur et les tanins.","Red wine is always made from black grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed and, unlike white wine, the juice is not separated: juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This is the big difference from white winemaking, because it is the skins that will provide the colour and the tannins."],["Si aggiungono i lieviti e la fermentazione comincia. Durante questa fase succo e bucce vengono mescolati con cura, in modo da estrarre dalle bucce il colore e i tannini. Più il contatto è intenso, più il vino ne beneficia in colore e struttura. Quando la fermentazione è finita, il vino nuovo viene svinato, cioè fatto scolare via dalle bucce.","On ajoute les levures et la fermentation commence. Pendant cette phase, le jus et les peaux sont soigneusement mélangés pour extraire des peaux la couleur et les tanins. Plus le contact est poussé, plus le vin gagne en couleur et en structure. Quand la fermentation est terminée, le vin nouveau est écoulé, c'est-à-dire séparé des peaux.","Yeast are added and fermentation begins. During this stage the juice and skins are mixed thoroughly so that colour and tannin are drawn out of the skins. The more thorough the contact, the more colour and structure the wine gains. When fermentation has finished, the new red wine is drained off the skins."],["Le bucce rimaste trattengono ancora del vino, quindi vengono pressate per recuperarlo: nel rosso la pressatura arriva dopo la fermentazione, mentre nel bianco avviene prima. Seguono la maturazione, in vasche di acciaio inox o in botti di rovere, e infine l'imbottigliamento. Sequenza da ricordare: pigiatura, fermentazione, svinatura, pressatura, maturazione, imbottigliamento.","Les peaux restantes retiennent encore du vin ; on les presse donc pour le récupérer : pour le rouge, le pressurage vient après la fermentation, alors que pour le blanc il a lieu avant. Viennent ensuite l'élevage, en cuves inox ou en fûts de chêne, puis la mise en bouteille. Séquence à retenir : foulage, fermentation, écoulage, pressurage, élevage, mise en bouteille.","The leftover skins still hold some wine, so they are pressed to release it: for red wine pressing comes after fermentation, whereas for white it comes before. Next is maturation, in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels, and finally bottling. The sequence to remember: crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing, maturation, bottling."]],"k":[["Il rosso si fa con uve nere fermentate insieme alle bucce.","Le rouge se fait avec des raisins noirs fermentés avec leurs peaux.","Red wine: black grapes fermented with their skins."],["Mescolare succo e bucce estrae colore e tannini.","Mélanger jus et peaux extrait couleur et tanins.","Mixing juice and skins extracts colour and tannin."],["Dopo la fermentazione: svinatura, poi pressatura delle bucce.","Après la fermentation : écoulage, puis pressurage des peaux.","After fermentation: draining, then pressing the skins."],["Rosso: pigiatura → fermentazione → svinatura → pressatura → maturazione → imbottigliamento.","Rouge : foulage → fermentation → écoulage → pressurage → élevage → mise en bouteille.","Red: crushing → fermentation → draining → pressing → maturation → bottling."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["Come si fa un vino rosato","Comment on fait un vin rosé","How rosé wine is made"],"p":[["Anche il rosato nasce da uve nere, e all'inizio il procedimento è lo stesso del rosso: l'uva viene pigiata, succo e bucce vanno insieme nel recipiente, si aggiungono i lieviti e parte la fermentazione. Il colore comincia a passare dalle bucce al succo, ma il rosato si distingue per una scelta precisa: il contatto dura pochissimo.","Le rosé naît lui aussi de raisins noirs, et au début la méthode est la même que pour le rouge : le raisin est foulé, jus et peaux vont ensemble en cuve, on ajoute les levures et la fermentation démarre. La couleur commence à passer des peaux au jus, mais le rosé se distingue par un choix précis : le contact dure très peu.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, and at first the method is the same as for red: the grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the vessel together, yeast are added and fermentation starts. Colour begins to move from the skins into the juice, but rosé stands out for one clear choice: the contact is kept very short."],["Dopo appena qualche ora il succo viene separato dalle bucce. In quel momento ha preso solo un colore rosa, e senza le bucce non può scurirsi ulteriormente. La fermentazione prosegue quindi senza le bucce fino alla fine. È il tempo di contatto con le bucce, ore invece di giorni, che spiega perché il rosato è rosa e non rosso.","Au bout de quelques heures seulement, le jus est séparé des peaux. À ce moment-là, il n'a pris qu'une couleur rose et, sans les peaux, il ne peut plus foncer. La fermentation se poursuit donc sans les peaux jusqu'à la fin. C'est la durée du contact avec les peaux, quelques heures au lieu de plusieurs jours, qui explique pourquoi le rosé est rose et non rouge.","After only a few hours the juice is drained off the skins. At that point it has picked up just a pink colour, and without the skins it cannot get any darker. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. It is the time spent in contact with the skins, a few hours rather than the whole fermentation, that explains why rosé is pink rather than red."],["Dopo la fermentazione il rosato passa alla maturazione, che può avvenire in acciaio inox o in rovere, anche se per i rosati il rovere si usa raramente. Poi viene imbottigliato. Rispetto al rosso manca la pressatura delle bucce dopo la fermentazione, perché le bucce sono già state tolte all'inizio. Sequenza: pigiatura, fermentazione, svinatura, maturazione, imbottigliamento.","Après la fermentation, le rosé passe à l'élevage, qui peut se faire en inox ou en chêne, même si le chêne est rarement utilisé pour les rosés. Il est ensuite mis en bouteille. Par rapport au rouge, il n'y a pas de pressurage des peaux après la fermentation, car elles ont déjà été retirées au début. Séquence : foulage, fermentation, écoulage, élevage, mise en bouteille.","After fermentation the rosé moves on to maturation, which can take place in stainless steel or oak, although oak is rarely used for rosé wines. Then it is bottled. Compared with red wine there is no pressing of the skins after fermentation, because the skins were removed early on. Sequence: crushing, fermentation, draining, maturation, bottling."]],"k":[["Il rosato si fa con uve nere.","Le rosé se fait avec des raisins noirs.","Rosé is made from black grapes."],["Contatto con le bucce di poche ore: il succo diventa solo rosa.","Contact avec les peaux de quelques heures : le jus devient juste rose.","Only a few hours on the skins: the juice turns just pink."],["La fermentazione finisce senza le bucce.","La fermentation se termine sans les peaux.","Fermentation finishes without the skins."],["Il rosato matura raramente in rovere.","Le rosé est rarement élevé en chêne.","Rosé is rarely matured in oak."],["Rosato: pigiatura → fermentazione → svinatura → maturazione → imbottigliamento.","Rosé : foulage → fermentation → écoulage → élevage → mise en bouteille.","Rosé: crushing → fermentation → draining → maturation → bottling."]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Tre tipi di vino: fermo, spumante, fortificato","Trois types de vin : tranquille, effervescent, fortifié","Three types of wine: still, sparkling, fortified"],"p":[["Quando qualcuno dice semplicemente «vino», di solito pensa a un vino fermo, cioè senza bollicine. È la categoria più grande. Il grado alcolico dei vini fermi va dall'8% al 15% vol., ma nella maggior parte dei casi resta tra l'11,5% e il 14%. Il valore «% vol.» (abv in inglese) indica la quota di alcol nel liquido: 10% vol. significa che un decimo del vino è alcol.","Quand on parle simplement de « vin », on pense en général à un vin tranquille, c'est-à-dire sans bulles. C'est de loin la catégorie la plus vaste. Les vins tranquilles titrent entre 8 % et 15 % vol., mais la plupart se situent entre 11,5 % et 14 %. Le chiffre « % vol. » (abv en anglais) indique la part d'alcool dans le liquide : 10 % vol. signifie qu'un dixième du vin est de l'alcool.","When people simply say «wine», they usually mean a still wine: one without bubbles. This is by far the biggest category. Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, though most sit between 11.5% and 14%. The abv figure (alcohol by volume) tells you how much of the liquid is alcohol, so a wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol."],["Molti vini fermi prendono il nome dalla zona di produzione: Sancerre e Burgundy (Bourgogne) in Francia, Rioja in Spagna, Chianti in Italia. Altri invece portano in etichetta il nome del vitigno, come un Pinot Grigio. Imparare a riconoscere queste due logiche aiuta subito a leggere le etichette e a capire che cosa aspettarsi nel bicchiere.","Beaucoup de vins tranquilles portent le nom de leur région de production : Sancerre et Burgundy (Bourgogne) en France, Rioja en Espagne, Chianti en Italie. D'autres affichent plutôt le nom du cépage, comme un Pinot Grigio. Savoir distinguer ces deux logiques aide tout de suite à lire une étiquette et à deviner ce qu'il y aura dans le verre.","Many still wines take their name from the place where they are made: Sancerre and Burgundy in France, Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy. Others carry the name of the grape variety instead, such as a Pinot Grigio. Spotting which of the two naming logics a label uses is a quick first step towards knowing what will be in the glass."],["I vini spumanti hanno bollicine. Durante la fermentazione si forma anidride carbonica: se il gas resta intrappolato nel vino, all'apertura della bottiglia si libera sotto forma di bollicine. Il più famoso è lo Champagne francese; molto noti anche il Cava spagnolo e il Prosecco italiano. Ma gli spumanti si producono ormai in tutto il mondo.","Les vins effervescents ont des bulles. La fermentation produit du dioxyde de carbone : si ce gaz reste piégé dans le vin, il s'échappe en bulles à l'ouverture de la bouteille. Le plus célèbre est le Champagne, en France ; le Cava espagnol et le Prosecco italien sont aussi très connus. On en produit aujourd'hui partout dans le monde.","Sparkling wines are fizzy. Fermentation creates carbon dioxide gas, and if that gas is kept trapped inside the wine, it is released as bubbles once the bottle is opened. Champagne from France is the most famous example; Cava from Spain and Prosecco from Italy are also very well known. Sparkling wine is now made all around the world."],["I vini fortificati sono vini a cui è stato aggiunto altro alcol. Per questo il loro grado è più alto rispetto a quello dei vini fermi: di solito tra il 15% e il 22% vol. Due esempi classici da ricordare sono lo Sherry, dalla Spagna, e il Port (Porto), dal Portogallo. Li ritroveremo nel capitolo sugli altri vini da conoscere.","Les vins fortifiés sont des vins auxquels on a ajouté de l'alcool. Leur degré est donc plus élevé que celui des vins tranquilles : en général entre 15 % et 22 % vol. Deux exemples classiques à retenir : le Sherry (Xérès), d'Espagne, et le Port (Porto), du Portugal. Nous les retrouverons dans le chapitre consacré aux autres vins à connaître.","Fortified wines have had extra alcohol added to them. That is why they are stronger than still wines, usually somewhere between 15% and 22% abv. Two classic examples to remember are Sherry, from Spain, and Port, from Portugal. You will meet both again in the chapter on other wines to know."]],"k":[["Fermo: niente bollicine, 8–15% vol. (di solito 11,5–14%)","Tranquille : sans bulles, 8–15 % vol. (le plus souvent 11,5–14 %)","Still: no bubbles, 8–15% abv (mostly 11.5–14%)"],["Spumante: anidride carbonica della fermentazione intrappolata nel vino","Effervescent : dioxyde de carbone de la fermentation piégé dans le vin","Sparkling: carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine"],["Fortificato: alcol aggiunto, 15–22% vol. (Sherry, Port)","Fortifié : alcool ajouté, 15–22 % vol. (Sherry, Port)","Fortified: extra alcohol added, 15–22% abv (Sherry, Port)"],["Un vino può chiamarsi come la sua zona o come il suo vitigno","Un vin peut porter le nom de sa région ou de son cépage","A wine may be named after its region or its grape"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Il colore: bianco, rosso, rosato","La couleur : blanc, rouge, rosé","Colour: white, red, rosé"],"p":[["Il colore di un vino dipende da due cose: il vitigno usato e il modo in cui il vino viene fatto. Esistono uve bianche e uve nere, ma dentro si somigliano molto: la polpa ha lo stesso colore in entrambe e il succo è incolore. Il colore delle uve nere si trova tutto nella buccia, che contiene anche i tannini.","La couleur d'un vin dépend de deux choses : le cépage et la façon dont le vin est élaboré. Il existe des raisins blancs et des raisins noirs, mais à l'intérieur ils se ressemblent beaucoup : la pulpe a la même couleur et le jus est incolore. Toute la couleur des raisins noirs se trouve dans la peau, qui contient aussi les tanins.","A wine's colour depends on two things: the grape variety and the way the wine is made. There are white grapes and black grapes, but inside they look very alike: the pulp is the same colour in both and the juice has no colour. All the colour of a black grape sits in its skin, which also holds the tannins."],["I vini bianchi si fanno di solito con uve bianche: pensiamo a uno Chablis o a un Riesling. Però si può ottenere un vino bianco anche da uve nere. Basta separare le bucce dal succo prima della fermentazione, per esempio con una pressatura delicata: dato che il colore è nella buccia, il succo resta chiaro e il vino sarà bianco.","Les vins blancs sont en général faits avec des raisins blancs : pensons à un Chablis ou à un Riesling. Mais on peut aussi obtenir un vin blanc à partir de raisins noirs. Il suffit de séparer les peaux du jus avant la fermentation, par exemple avec un pressurage doux : comme la couleur est dans la peau, le jus reste clair et le vin sera blanc.","White wines are usually made from white grapes, as in Chablis or a Riesling. Yet black grapes can also give a white wine. The trick is to separate the skins from the juice before fermentation, for example by pressing gently: since the colour lives in the skins, the juice stays pale and the finished wine is white."],["Un vino rosso, invece, richiede per forza uve nere. Durante la fermentazione le bucce restano a contatto con il succo e vengono mescolate bene: così cedono colore e tannino al vino. Quando la fermentazione è finita, il vino viene separato dalle bucce. Esempi di rossi sono il Rioja spagnolo e i vini di Cabernet Sauvignon.","Un vin rouge, lui, exige des raisins noirs. Pendant la fermentation, les peaux restent au contact du jus et sont bien mélangées : elles cèdent ainsi couleur et tanins au vin. Une fois la fermentation terminée, le vin est séparé des peaux. Le Rioja espagnol et les vins de Cabernet Sauvignon sont des exemples de vins rouges.","A red wine, on the other hand, must come from black grapes. During fermentation the skins stay in the juice and are mixed in thoroughly, so they pass colour and tannin into the wine. Once fermentation is over, the new wine is drained off the skins. Rioja from Spain and Cabernet Sauvignon wines are red examples."],["Anche il rosato nasce da uve nere, ma il contatto con le bucce dura poco: solo qualche ora. Poi il succo, appena rosa, viene separato e termina la fermentazione senza bucce. Il risultato è un vino di colore tenue. Il White Zinfandel della California è un esempio di rosato. I rosati, inoltre, vengono affinati in legno molto raramente.","Le rosé naît lui aussi de raisins noirs, mais le contact avec les peaux est bref : seulement quelques heures. Le jus, à peine rose, est alors écoulé et termine sa fermentation sans les peaux. On obtient un vin à la couleur légère. Le White Zinfandel de Californie en est un exemple. Les rosés sont d'ailleurs rarement élevés en fût de chêne.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, but the skin contact is short: just a few hours. The juice, by then only pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins, giving a lightly coloured wine. White Zinfandel from California is a rosé example. Rosé wines are also only rarely aged in oak."]],"k":[["Il colore delle uve nere è nella buccia; il succo è incolore","La couleur des raisins noirs est dans la peau ; le jus est incolore","Black grape colour is in the skin; the juice is colourless"],["Bianco: di solito uve bianche, ma anche uve nere senza bucce","Blanc : en général raisins blancs, mais aussi raisins noirs sans les peaux","White: usually white grapes, possible from black grapes without skins"],["Rosso: solo uve nere, bucce presenti per tutta la fermentazione","Rouge : uniquement raisins noirs, peaux présentes pendant toute la fermentation","Red: black grapes only, skins kept through fermentation"],["Rosato: uve nere, poche ore di contatto con le bucce","Rosé : raisins noirs, quelques heures de contact avec les peaux","Rosé: black grapes, a few hours of skin contact"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Struttura (1): dolcezza e acidità","Structure (1) : sucrosité et acidité","Structure (1): sweetness and acidity"],"p":[["La dolcezza dipende dalla quantità di zucchero rimasta nel vino. La maggior parte dei vini è secca: per ottenerla, i lieviti devono trasformare in alcol tutto lo zucchero del succo, così nel vino ne resta pochissimo o nulla. Sono secchi, per esempio, lo Chablis e i Sauvignon Blanc tra i bianchi, il Côtes du Rhône, il Chianti e i Cabernet Sauvignon tra i rossi.","La sucrosité dépend du sucre resté dans le vin. La plupart des vins sont secs : pour cela, les levures doivent transformer en alcool tout le sucre du jus, si bien qu'il n'en reste presque pas. Sont secs, par exemple, le Chablis et les Sauvignon Blanc côté blancs, le Côtes du Rhône, le Chianti et les Cabernet Sauvignon côté rouges.","Sweetness comes from sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry: to make one, the yeast must turn all the sugar in the juice into alcohol, leaving little or none behind. Dry examples include Chablis and Sauvignon Blanc wines among whites, and Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon wines among reds."],["I vini di dolcezza media sono per lo più bianchi o rosati. Si ottengono in due modi: si tolgono i lieviti prima che abbiano trasformato tutto lo zucchero, oppure si aggiunge succo d'uva non fermentato a un vino secco. Ne sono esempi alcuni Riesling tedeschi e il White Zinfandel, il rosato californiano.","Les vins de sucrosité moyenne sont surtout des blancs ou des rosés. On les obtient de deux façons : soit on retire les levures avant qu'elles aient transformé tout le sucre, soit on ajoute du jus de raisin non fermenté à un vin sec. Exemples : certains Riesling allemands et le White Zinfandel, rosé californien.","Medium-sweet wines are mostly white or rosé. There are two main ways to make them: remove the yeast before it has turned all the sugar into alcohol, or blend some unfermented grape juice into a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, are good examples."],["I vini dolci contengono così tanto zucchero da sembrare quasi densi e sciropposi. Possono nascere da uve talmente zuccherine che i lieviti si fermano prima di averlo consumato tutto, come nel Sauternes o in alcuni Riesling tedeschi. Nei vini fortificati, invece, si aggiunge alcol distillato ad alta gradazione che uccide i lieviti: lo zucchero rimasto rende dolci il Port e alcuni Sherry.","Les vins doux sont si riches en sucre qu'ils peuvent paraître épais, presque sirupeux. Ils peuvent venir de raisins tellement sucrés que les levures s'arrêtent avant d'avoir tout consommé, comme pour le Sauternes ou certains Riesling allemands. Dans les vins fortifiés, on ajoute un alcool distillé très fort qui tue les levures : le sucre restant rend doux le Port et certains Sherry.","Sweet wines hold so much sugar that they can feel thick, almost syrupy. They can come from grapes so rich in sugar that the yeast stop before eating it all, as in Sauternes or some German Rieslings. In fortified wines, strong distilled alcohol is added, killing the yeast early; the sugar left behind makes Port and some Sherries sweet."],["L'acidità arriva direttamente dal succo d'uva ed è ciò che rende un vino rinfrescante. Si riconosce facilmente perché fa venire l'acquolina in bocca. Troppa acidità rende il vino sgradevolmente aspro; troppo poca lo rende piatto. Sono vini molto acidi lo Chablis, il Chianti e i vini di Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon e Pinot Noir.","L'acidité vient directement du jus de raisin et c'est elle qui rend un vin rafraîchissant. On la reconnaît facilement : elle fait saliver. Trop d'acidité rend le vin désagréablement acide ; trop peu, et il perd sa fraîcheur. Le Chablis, le Chianti et les vins de Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon et Pinot Noir ont une acidité élevée.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. Too much tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its freshness. Chablis, Chianti and wines from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir all have high acidity."],["Nei vini dolci l'acidità è fondamentale. Fa da contrappeso allo zucchero ed evita che il vino risulti stucchevole. Per questo un buon Sauternes o un Riesling dolce hanno sempre un'acidità alta: dolcezza e freschezza si bilanciano a vicenda e il sorso resta piacevole fino alla fine.","Dans les vins doux, l'acidité est essentielle. Elle fait contrepoids au sucre et évite que le vin devienne écœurant. C'est pourquoi un bon Sauternes ou un Riesling doux ont toujours une acidité élevée : douceur et fraîcheur s'équilibrent et la gorgée reste agréable jusqu'au bout.","In sweet wines, acidity is vital. It acts as a counterweight to the sugar and stops the wine from tasting cloying. That is why a good Sauternes or a sweet Riesling always has high acidity: sweetness and freshness balance each other, and every sip stays enjoyable to the end."]],"k":[["Secco: i lieviti trasformano tutto lo zucchero in alcol","Sec : les levures transforment tout le sucre en alcool","Dry: yeast turn all the sugar into alcohol"],["Medio: lieviti tolti prima, o succo non fermentato aggiunto","Moyen : levures retirées tôt, ou jus non fermenté ajouté","Medium: yeast removed early, or unfermented juice added"],["Dolce: uve molto zuccherine, o alcol aggiunto che uccide i lieviti","Doux : raisins très sucrés, ou alcool ajouté qui tue les levures","Sweet: very sugary grapes, or added alcohol killing the yeast"],["Acidità: viene dal succo, fa salivare, rinfresca e bilancia la dolcezza","Acidité : vient du jus, fait saliver, rafraîchit et équilibre la douceur","Acidity: from the juice, makes the mouth water, balances sweetness"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Struttura (2): tannino, alcol e corpo","Structure (2) : tanins, alcool et corps","Structure (2): tannin, alcohol and body"],"p":[["Il tannino è tipico dei vini rossi e proviene dalle bucce delle uve nere. La sua quantità dipende dal vitigno e da come si fa il vino. A volte ha un gusto amaro, ma soprattutto si sente come una sensazione: lascia la bocca asciutta. Sono ricchi di tannino il Bordeaux rosso e il Chianti; ne hanno poco il Beaujolais e alcuni Pinot Noir.","Le tanin est propre aux vins rouges et vient de la peau des raisins noirs. Sa quantité dépend du cépage et de la vinification. Il peut paraître amer, mais on le perçoit surtout comme une sensation : il assèche la bouche. Le Bordeaux rouge et le Chianti sont riches en tanins ; le Beaujolais et certains Pinot Noir en ont peu.","Tannin belongs to red wines and comes from the skins of black grapes. How much a wine has depends on the grape variety and on the winemaking. It can taste a little bitter, but mostly it is something you feel: it leaves your mouth dry. Red Bordeaux and Chianti are high in tannin; Beaujolais and some Pinot Noir wines are low."],["Quasi tutti i vini fermi e spumanti hanno tra l'11,5% e il 14% vol. Alcuni arrivano fino al 15%, altri scendono fino all'8%. Un esempio di vino molto alcolico è lo Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rosso francese; un esempio di vino poco alcolico è il White Zinfandel californiano. Ricorda: l'alcol nasce dalla fermentazione dello zucchero.","Presque tous les vins tranquilles et effervescents titrent entre 11,5 % et 14 % vol. Certains montent jusqu'à 15 %, d'autres descendent jusqu'à 8 %. Le Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rouge français, est un exemple de vin riche en alcool ; le White Zinfandel californien, un exemple de vin peu alcoolisé. Rappel : l'alcool naît de la fermentation du sucre.","Nearly all still and sparkling wines sit between 11.5% and 14% abv. A few reach 15%, while others go as low as 8%. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a French red, is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. Remember that alcohol is produced when yeast ferment sugar."],["Il corpo descrive la sensazione generale del vino in bocca. Molti fattori lo influenzano, quindi la domanda più semplice è: quanto riempie la bocca? Un vino di corpo pieno sembra denso e avvolgente, uno leggero più delicato. Leggeri: Pinot Grigio e Beaujolais. Medi: Sancerre e Côtes du Rhône. Pieni: Cabernet Sauvignon della California e Sauternes.","Le corps décrit la sensation globale du vin en bouche. Beaucoup de facteurs y contribuent, alors la question la plus simple est : à quel point remplit-il la bouche ? Un vin corsé paraît dense et enveloppant, un vin léger plus délicat. Légers : Pinot Grigio, Beaujolais. Moyens : Sancerre, Côtes du Rhône. Corsés : Cabernet Sauvignon de Californie, Sauternes.","Body describes the overall feel of a wine in your mouth. Many things contribute to it, so the easiest question to ask is: how mouth-filling is it? Full-bodied wines feel dense and rich, while light-bodied ones feel more delicate. Light: Pinot Grigio, Beaujolais. Medium: Sancerre, Côtes du Rhône. Full: Californian Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauternes."]],"k":[["Tannino: dalle bucce, asciuga la bocca, tipico dei rossi","Tanin : vient des peaux, assèche la bouche, typique des rouges","Tannin: from skins, dries the mouth, a red-wine feature"],["Alcol: di solito 11,5–14% vol., tra 8% e 15% per vini fermi e spumanti","Alcool : en général 11,5–14 % vol., entre 8 et 15 % pour tranquilles et effervescents","Alcohol: usually 11.5–14% abv, 8–15% for still and sparkling"],["Corpo: quanto il vino riempie la bocca (leggero, medio, pieno)","Corps : à quel point le vin remplit la bouche (léger, moyen, corsé)","Body: how mouth-filling the wine is (light, medium, full)"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Aromi e sapori: frutta, legno, altro","Arômes et saveurs : fruit, bois, autres","Aromas and flavours: fruit, oak, other"],"p":[["Gli aromi e i sapori di un vino hanno origini diverse. Alcuni arrivano direttamente dalle uve, altri si sviluppano durante la vinificazione e l'affinamento. All'inizio descriverli può sembrare difficile, ma è un'abilità che migliora con la pratica. Un metodo semplice è chiedersi: sento frutta? Sento legno? Sento qualcos'altro?","Les arômes et saveurs d'un vin ont des origines variées. Certains viennent directement du raisin, d'autres apparaissent pendant la vinification et l'élevage. Les décrire peut sembler difficile au début, mais cela s'apprend avec la pratique. Une méthode simple : se demander si l'on sent du fruit, du bois ou autre chose.","A wine's aromas and flavours come from different places. Some come straight from the grapes, while others develop during winemaking and maturation. Putting them into words feels hard at first, but it is a skill that grows with practice. A simple method is to ask three questions: do I notice fruit? Oak? Something else?"],["Quasi tutti i vini profumano di frutta. Il tipo di frutta dipende prima di tutto dal vitigno: il Cabernet Sauvignon, per esempio, sa di ribes nero. Conta anche la maturità delle uve: uno Chardonnay di clima fresco ricorda la mela verde e il limone, mentre uno di clima caldo ricorda la pesca e frutti tropicali come l'ananas.","Presque tous les vins sentent le fruit. Le type de fruit dépend d'abord du cépage : le Cabernet Sauvignon, par exemple, évoque le cassis. La maturité du raisin compte aussi : un Chardonnay de climat frais rappelle la pomme verte et le citron, tandis qu'un Chardonnay de climat chaud évoque la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas.","Almost every wine smells of fruit. The kind of fruit depends first on the grape variety: Cabernet Sauvignon, for instance, smells of blackcurrant. Ripeness matters too. A Chardonnay from a cool climate shows green apple and lemon, whereas one from a warm climate leans towards peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple."],["Il vino può fermentare e/o affinarsi in botti di rovere. In quel caso il legno aggiunge note come vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro e affumicato. A volte l'uso del legno è indicato in etichetta. Quando senti questi profumi accanto alla frutta, è un buon indizio che il vino sia passato in botte.","Le vin peut fermenter et/ou être élevé en fût de chêne. Le bois apporte alors des notes de vanille, de noix de coco, de clou de girofle, de cèdre ou de fumé. L'usage du chêne est parfois indiqué sur l'étiquette. Quand on perçoit ces arômes à côté du fruit, c'est un bon indice d'un passage en fût.","Wine can be fermented and/or matured in oak barrels. When it is, the wood adds notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The use of oak is sometimes mentioned on the label. If you pick up these aromas alongside the fruit, it is a good clue that the wine has spent time in barrel."],["Infine ci sono gli «altri» aromi, che rendono il vino così vario e interessante: erba, fiori, erbe aromatiche, ortaggi, terra, funghi, cuoio. Per esempio, un Sauvignon Blanc può far pensare all'erba appena tagliata, mentre il Chianti può avere note di erbe secche. Raggrupparli in una famiglia a parte aiuta a non confonderli con la frutta.","Restent les « autres » arômes, qui rendent le vin si varié et passionnant : herbe, fleurs, herbes aromatiques, légumes, terre, champignon, cuir. Un Sauvignon Blanc peut par exemple évoquer l'herbe coupée, et le Chianti des herbes séchées. Les ranger dans une famille à part évite de les confondre avec le fruit.","Finally, there are the «other» aromas that make wine so varied and interesting: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. A Sauvignon Blanc, for example, can bring cut grass to mind, while Chianti can show dried herbs. Keeping them in a family of their own stops you confusing them with fruit."]],"k":[["Frutta: dipende dal vitigno e dalla maturità delle uve","Fruit : dépend du cépage et de la maturité du raisin","Fruit: depends on the grape variety and its ripeness"],["Clima fresco = mela, limone; clima caldo = pesca, ananas","Climat frais = pomme, citron ; climat chaud = pêche, ananas","Cool climate = apple, lemon; warm climate = peach, pineapple"],["Legno di rovere: vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro, affumicato","Chêne : vanille, noix de coco, clou de girofle, cèdre, fumé","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke"],["Altro: erba, fiori, erbe, ortaggi, terra, funghi, cuoio","Autres : herbe, fleurs, herbes, légumes, terre, champignon, cuir","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Lo stile: la somma delle caratteristiche","Le style : la somme des caractéristiques","Style: the sum of the characteristics"],"p":[["Ognuno dei tre tipi di vino, fermo, spumante o fortificato, può presentarsi in tanti stili diversi. Lo stile è l'insieme di tre elementi: il colore, la struttura (dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol, corpo) e gli aromi e sapori. Descrivere uno stile significa mettere insieme questi pezzi in un ritratto unico del vino.","Chacun des trois types de vin, tranquille, effervescent ou fortifié, peut se décliner en de nombreux styles. Le style réunit trois éléments : la couleur, la structure (sucrosité, acidité, tanins, alcool, corps) et les arômes et saveurs. Décrire un style, c'est assembler ces pièces pour dresser le portrait complet d'un vin.","Each of the three types of wine, still, sparkling or fortified, can come in many different styles. A style brings together three elements: colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. Describing a style means putting these pieces together into one complete portrait of the wine."],["Un confronto lo rende chiaro. Lo Chablis e il Sauternes sono entrambi bianchi francesi, eppure hanno stili opposti. Lo Chablis è secco, molto acido, di corpo leggero o medio, con mela verde e limone e senza legno. Il Sauternes è dolce, di corpo pieno, con albicocca, miele e vaniglia del rovere, sostenuto da un'acidità alta.","Une comparaison rend l'idée claire. Le Chablis et le Sauternes sont tous deux des blancs français, et pourtant leurs styles s'opposent. Le Chablis est sec, très acide, léger à moyen en corps, avec pomme verte et citron, sans bois. Le Sauternes est doux, corsé, avec abricot, miel et vanille du chêne, porté par une acidité élevée.","A comparison makes this clear. Chablis and Sauternes are both French white wines, yet their styles are opposites. Chablis is dry, high in acidity, light to medium in body, with green apple and lemon and no oak. Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla from oak, held up by high acidity."],["Lo stile dipende molto dal clima in cui crescono le uve. Più fa fresco, meno zucchero e più acidità hanno le uve: ne nascono vini più freschi e leggeri, con frutta verde e agrumi. Più fa caldo, più zucchero e meno acidità: i sapori sono più maturi e, dato che lo zucchero diventa alcol, i vini tendono a essere più alcolici e corposi.","Le style dépend beaucoup du climat où pousse le raisin. Plus il fait frais, moins le raisin a de sucre et plus il a d'acidité : on obtient des vins plus frais et légers, aux fruits verts et agrumes. Plus il fait chaud, plus il y a de sucre et moins d'acidité : les saveurs sont plus mûres et, le sucre devenant alcool, les vins sont plus alcoolisés et plus amples.","Style depends a lot on the climate where the grapes grow. The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have, giving fresher, lighter wines with green fruit and citrus. The warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity: flavours taste riper and, since sugar becomes alcohol, wines tend to be stronger and fuller."],["Per descrivere uno stile si segue un approccio sistematico alla degustazione. Prima l'aspetto: il colore (bianco, rosso, rosato). Poi il naso: aromi di frutta, legno o altro. Infine il palato: dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol e corpo, più i sapori. Usare sempre lo stesso ordine aiuta chi studia a confrontare i vini e a ricordarli.","Pour décrire un style, on suit une approche systématique de la dégustation. D'abord l'aspect : la couleur (blanc, rouge, rosé). Puis le nez : arômes de fruit, de bois ou autres. Enfin la bouche : sucrosité, acidité, tanins, alcool et corps, plus les saveurs. Suivre toujours le même ordre aide les personnes qui étudient à comparer les vins et à s'en souvenir.","To describe a style, you follow a systematic approach to tasting. First the appearance: the colour (white, red, rosé). Then the nose: aromas of fruit, oak or other. Finally the palate: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body, plus the flavours. Always using the same order makes it easier to compare wines and remember them."]],"k":[["Stile = colore + struttura + aromi e sapori","Style = couleur + structure + arômes et saveurs","Style = colour + structure + aromas and flavours"],["Clima fresco: più acidità, meno zucchero, vini più leggeri e freschi","Climat frais : plus d'acidité, moins de sucre, vins plus légers et frais","Cool climate: more acid, less sugar, lighter and fresher wines"],["Clima caldo: più zucchero, meno acidità, sapori più maturi","Climat chaud : plus de sucre, moins d'acidité, saveurs plus mûres","Warm climate: more sugar, less acid, riper flavours"],["Degustazione: aspetto, naso, palato, sempre nello stesso ordine","Dégustation : aspect, nez, bouche, toujours dans le même ordre","Tasting: appearance, nose, palate, always in the same order"]]},{"c":"w2","t":["Chardonnay","Chardonnay","Chardonnay"],"p":[["Lo Chardonnay è uno dei vitigni più amati e più coltivati al mondo. Dà vini secchi, ma in stili molto diversi tra loro. Il motivo principale è che si adatta bene sia ai climi freschi sia a quelli caldi, e cambia carattere a seconda di quanto maturano le uve. Anche le scelte in cantina, soprattutto l'uso del rovere, ne modificano lo stile.","Le Chardonnay est l'un des cépages les plus appréciés et les plus plantés au monde. Il donne des vins secs, mais dans des styles très différents. La raison principale : il pousse aussi bien en climat frais qu'en climat chaud et change de caractère selon la maturité du raisin. Les choix en cave, surtout l'usage du chêne, modifient aussi son style.","Chardonnay is one of the most popular and widely planted grape varieties in the world. It makes dry wines, but in very different styles. The main reason is that it does well in both cool and warm climates and changes character with the ripeness of the grapes. Choices in the winery, above all the use of oak, also shape its style."],["In un clima fresco le uve maturano meno: restano più acide e meno zuccherine. Ne nasce uno Chardonnay con acidità alta, corpo da leggero a medio e aromi di frutta verde (mela) e agrumi (limone). In un clima caldo le uve maturano di più: il vino ha acidità media, corpo da medio a pieno e sapori di frutta a nocciolo (pesca) e tropicale (ananas, banana).","En climat frais, le raisin mûrit moins : il reste plus acide et moins sucré. On obtient un Chardonnay à l'acidité élevée, au corps léger à moyen, aux arômes de fruit vert (pomme) et d'agrumes (citron). En climat chaud, le raisin mûrit davantage : le vin a une acidité moyenne, un corps moyen à ample et des saveurs de fruit à noyau (pêche) et tropical (ananas, banane).","In a cool climate the grapes ripen less, so they stay more acidic and less sugary. The result is a Chardonnay with high acidity, a light to medium body and aromas of green fruit (apple) and citrus (lemon). In a warm climate the grapes ripen further: the wine has medium acidity, a medium to full body and flavours of stone fruit (peach) and tropical fruit (pineapple, banana)."],["Lo Chardonnay può fermentare e affinarsi in serbatoi d'acciaio inox oppure in botti di rovere. Senza legno conserva una frutta pura e fresca. Con il rovere acquista note di vaniglia e spesso un carattere più ricco. Un esempio tipico di stile caldo e passato in legno è uno Chardonnay californiano di corpo pieno, con frutta tropicale matura e vaniglia.","Le Chardonnay peut fermenter et être élevé en cuve inox ou en fût de chêne. Sans bois, il garde un fruit pur et frais. Avec le chêne, il prend des notes de vanille et souvent un caractère plus riche. Un exemple typique de style chaud et boisé : un Chardonnay californien corsé, au fruit tropical mûr et à la vanille.","Chardonnay can be fermented and matured in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Without oak it keeps pure, fresh fruit. With oak it picks up vanilla notes and often a richer character. A typical example of the warm, oaked style is a full-bodied Californian Chardonnay with ripe tropical fruit and vanilla."],["Lo Chardonnay è l'uva dei bianchi di Burgundy (Bourgogne), in Francia: vini di corpo medio, molto freschi, con limone e pesca e talvolta vaniglia del rovere. Lo Chablis viene dalla parte più fresca di Burgundy: acidità alta, corpo da leggero a medio, mela e limone, di solito senza legno. Fuori dalla Francia sono famosi gli Chardonnay di Australia e California.","Le Chardonnay est le cépage des blancs de Burgundy (Bourgogne), en France : vins de corps moyen, très frais, aux notes de citron et de pêche, parfois de vanille du chêne. Le Chablis vient de la partie la plus fraîche de la Bourgogne : acidité élevée, corps léger à moyen, pomme et citron, en général sans bois. Hors de France, l'Australie et la Californie sont réputées.","Chardonnay is the grape behind white Burgundy (Bourgogne) in France: medium-bodied, high-acid wines with lemon and peach, sometimes with vanilla from oak. Chablis comes from the coolest part of Burgundy: high acidity, light to medium body, apple and lemon, and usually no oak. Outside France, Australia and California are well known for Chardonnay."],["Lo Chardonnay serve anche a fare lo Champagne, dove viene spesso unito al Pinot Noir. In sintesi, per riconoscere uno Chardonnay chiediti due cose: il clima era fresco o caldo (mela e limone oppure pesca e ananas)? E il vino è passato in rovere (vaniglia sì o no)? Le risposte ti dicono quasi tutto sullo stile.","Le Chardonnay entre aussi dans l'élaboration du Champagne, où il est souvent assemblé au Pinot Noir. En résumé, face à un Chardonnay, posez-vous deux questions : climat frais ou chaud (pomme et citron, ou pêche et ananas) ? Passage en chêne ou non (vanille ou pas) ? Les réponses disent presque tout du style.","Chardonnay is also used to make Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir. In short, when you meet a Chardonnay, ask two questions: was the climate cool or warm (apple and lemon, or peach and pineapple)? And did the wine see oak (vanilla or not)? The answers tell you almost everything about its style."]],"k":[["Vini secchi in molti stili; uno dei vitigni più coltivati","Vins secs de nombreux styles ; l'un des cépages les plus plantés","Dry wines in many styles; one of the most planted grapes"],["Clima fresco: acidità alta, mela e limone; clima caldo: pesca, ananas, banana","Climat frais : acidité élevée, pomme et citron ; climat chaud : pêche, ananas, banane","Cool: high acidity, apple and lemon; warm: peach, pineapple, banana"],["Il rovere aggiunge vaniglia","Le chêne apporte la vanille","Oak adds vanilla"],["Burgundy bianco e Chablis (senza legno); anche Australia e California","Bourgogne blanc et Chablis (sans bois) ; aussi Australie et Californie","White Burgundy and Chablis (unoaked); also Australia and California"],["Nello Champagne insieme al Pinot Noir","Dans le Champagne avec le Pinot Noir","In Champagne with Pinot Noir"]]},{"c":"w2","t":["Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc"],"p":[["Il Sauvignon Blanc dà vini secchi dai profumi intensi e con un'acidità alta e rinfrescante. Il corpo va da leggero a medio. È un vitigno facile da riconoscere proprio per il naso: già avvicinando il bicchiere si sentono aromi netti e vivaci, che lo distinguono da bianchi più delicati come il Pinot Grigio.","Le Sauvignon Blanc donne des vins secs aux arômes intenses, avec une acidité élevée et rafraîchissante. Le corps va de léger à moyen. C'est un cépage facile à reconnaître grâce au nez : dès qu'on approche le verre, on perçoit des arômes nets et vifs qui le distinguent de blancs plus discrets comme le Pinot Grigio.","Sauvignon Blanc makes dry wines with intense aromas and refreshingly high acidity. The body ranges from light to medium. It is an easy grape to spot by its nose: as soon as you lift the glass, you notice sharp, lively aromas that set it apart from more delicate whites such as Pinot Grigio."],["La frutta va dalla mela verde agli agrumi, come il pompelmo, fino ai frutti tropicali, come il frutto della passione. Accanto alla frutta compaiono spesso note erbacee: asparago, peperone verde, erba appena tagliata. Questa combinazione di frutta fresca e note «verdi» è la firma del Sauvignon Blanc.","Le fruit va de la pomme verte aux agrumes, comme le pamplemousse, jusqu'aux fruits tropicaux, comme le fruit de la passion. À côté du fruit apparaissent souvent des notes herbacées : asperge, poivron vert, herbe fraîchement coupée. Ce mélange de fruit frais et de notes « vertes » est la signature du Sauvignon Blanc.","The fruit ranges from green apple to citrus such as grapefruit, and on to tropical fruit such as passion fruit. Alongside the fruit there are often herbaceous notes: asparagus, green bell pepper and freshly cut grass. This mix of fresh fruit and «green» notes is Sauvignon Blanc's signature."],["In cantina l'obiettivo è proteggere questi profumi. Per questo il Sauvignon Blanc fermenta spesso in serbatoi d'acciaio inox e di solito non viene affinato in rovere: il legno aggiungerebbe vaniglia e note tostate che coprirebbero gli aromi tipici del vitigno. Il risultato è un vino fresco, diretto, molto aromatico.","En cave, l'objectif est de protéger ces arômes. C'est pourquoi le Sauvignon Blanc fermente souvent en cuve inox et n'est en général pas élevé en chêne : le bois ajouterait de la vanille et des notes grillées qui masqueraient les arômes typiques du cépage. On obtient un vin frais, direct, très aromatique.","In the winery the aim is to protect those aromas. So Sauvignon Blanc is often fermented in stainless steel tanks and usually not matured in oak: wood would add vanilla and toasty notes that would hide the grape's typical aromas. The result is a fresh, direct and very aromatic wine."],["Due vini molto popolari da ricordare: il Sauvignon Blanc della Nuova Zelanda (per esempio di Marlborough), spesso con pompelmo, limone ed erba, e il Sancerre, bianco della Valle della Loira in Francia, secco, di corpo medio, con mela verde e note erbacee. Nel Sancerre il nome del vitigno di solito non compare in etichetta: bisogna sapere che è Sauvignon Blanc.","Deux vins très populaires à retenir : le Sauvignon Blanc de Nouvelle-Zélande (par exemple de Marlborough), souvent sur le pamplemousse, le citron et l'herbe, et le Sancerre, blanc de la vallée de la Loire, sec, de corps moyen, avec pomme verte et notes herbacées. Le cépage n'apparaît en général pas sur l'étiquette du Sancerre : il faut savoir que c'est du Sauvignon Blanc.","Two very popular wines to remember: New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc (from Marlborough, for example), often showing grapefruit, lemon and grass, and Sancerre, a dry, medium-bodied white from France's Loire Valley with green apple and herbaceous notes. Sancerre labels usually do not name the grape, so you need to know it is Sauvignon Blanc."]],"k":[["Secco, profumi intensi, acidità alta, corpo leggero-medio","Sec, arômes intenses, acidité élevée, corps léger à moyen","Dry, pronounced aromas, high acidity, light to medium body"],["Mela, pompelmo, frutto della passione + asparago, peperone verde, erba","Pomme, pamplemousse, fruit de la passion + asperge, poivron vert, herbe","Apple, grapefruit, passion fruit + asparagus, green pepper, grass"],["Acciaio inox, di solito niente rovere, per proteggere gli aromi","Cuve inox, en général sans chêne, pour protéger les arômes","Stainless steel, usually no oak, to keep its aromas"],["Vini chiave: Nuova Zelanda e Sancerre (Loira)","Vins clés : Nouvelle-Zélande et Sancerre (Loire)","Key wines: New Zealand and Sancerre (Loire)"]]},{"c":"w2","t":["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],"p":[["Il Pinot Grigio è un vitigno molto popolare. I suoi vini sono di solito secchi, di corpo leggero e con un'acidità da media ad alta. I sapori sono semplici e delicati: soprattutto pera e limone. Non cerca la potenza o la complessità: è un bianco facile, fresco e immediato, pensato per essere bevuto con piacere.","Le Pinot Grigio est un cépage très populaire. Ses vins sont en général secs, légers en corps, avec une acidité moyenne à élevée. Les saveurs sont simples et délicates : surtout la poire et le citron. Il ne cherche ni la puissance ni la complexité : c'est un blanc facile, frais et direct, fait pour être bu avec plaisir.","Pinot Grigio is a hugely popular grape variety. Its wines are usually dry and light-bodied, with medium to high acidity. The flavours are simple and delicate: mostly pear and lemon. It is not about power or complexity; it is an easy, fresh and straightforward white made to be enjoyed without fuss."],["Anche qui le scelte di cantina servono a proteggere la frutta. Il Pinot Grigio fermenta di solito in serbatoi d'acciaio inox e non passa in rovere. Così conserva i suoi sapori fruttati e la sua leggerezza: il legno, con vaniglia e note tostate, coprirebbe una frutta così delicata.","Ici aussi, les choix en cave servent à protéger le fruit. Le Pinot Grigio fermente en général en cuve inox et ne passe pas en chêne. Il garde ainsi ses saveurs fruitées et sa légèreté : le bois, avec sa vanille et ses notes grillées, couvrirait un fruit aussi délicat.","Here too, winemaking choices are about protecting the fruit. Pinot Grigio is usually fermented in stainless steel tanks and not matured in oak. That way it keeps its fruity flavours and its lightness: oak, with its vanilla and toasty notes, would easily cover such delicate fruit."],["Il Pinot Grigio è legato soprattutto all'Italia, per esempio a zone come il Veneto o il Trentino, ma si coltiva anche in altri paesi. Il nome in etichetta è quello del vitigno: è proprio l'esempio tipico di vino chiamato con il nome dell'uva. Essendo leggero, si serve fresco, come gli altri bianchi di corpo leggero o medio.","Le Pinot Grigio est surtout associé à l'Italie, par exemple à des zones comme la Vénétie ou le Trentin, mais il est aussi cultivé dans d'autres pays. Le nom sur l'étiquette est celui du cépage : c'est l'exemple type du vin désigné par son raisin. Léger, il se sert frais, comme les autres blancs légers ou moyens.","Pinot Grigio is linked above all with Italy, for example areas such as Veneto or Trentino, but it is grown in other countries too. The name on the label is the grape's name, making it the classic example of a wine named after its variety. Being light, it is served chilled, like other light and medium-bodied whites."]],"k":[["Di solito secco, corpo leggero, acidità media-alta","En général sec, corps léger, acidité moyenne à élevée","Usually dry, light body, medium to high acidity"],["Sapori semplici di pera e limone","Saveurs simples de poire et de citron","Simple pear and lemon flavours"],["Acciaio inox, niente rovere, per conservare la frutta","Cuve inox, sans chêne, pour garder le fruit","Stainless steel, no oak, to keep the fruit"],["Legato soprattutto all'Italia","Surtout associé à l'Italie","Mainly associated with Italy"]]},{"c":"w2","t":["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"],"p":[["Il Riesling è un vitigno versatile: dà vini che vanno dal secco al dolce, passando per la dolcezza media. C'è però un punto fermo: tutti i Riesling hanno un'acidità alta. È proprio questa acidità a bilanciare l'eventuale zucchero, così anche un Riesling dolce resta fresco e non stanca. Il corpo va da leggero a medio.","Le Riesling est un cépage polyvalent : il donne des vins secs, demi-doux ou doux. Un point ne change jamais : tous les Riesling ont une acidité élevée. C'est elle qui équilibre le sucre éventuel, si bien que même un Riesling doux reste frais et n'écœure pas. Le corps va de léger à moyen.","Riesling is a versatile grape: it makes wines from dry through medium to sweet. One thing never changes, though: every Riesling has high acidity. That acidity balances any sugar, so even a sweet Riesling stays fresh rather than cloying. The body ranges from light to medium."],["I profumi sono intensi e possono andare dai fiori e dalla mela verde agli agrumi (lime, limone) fino alla frutta a nocciolo (pesca, albicocca). Come per Sauvignon Blanc e Pinot Grigio, il Riesling fermenta spesso in acciaio inox e non passa in rovere: lo scopo è mettere in primo piano gli aromi puri del vitigno.","Les arômes sont intenses et peuvent aller des fleurs et de la pomme verte aux agrumes (citron vert, citron) jusqu'aux fruits à noyau (pêche, abricot). Comme le Sauvignon Blanc et le Pinot Grigio, le Riesling fermente souvent en cuve inox et ne passe pas en chêne : le but est de mettre en avant les arômes purs du cépage.","The aromas are pronounced and can range from flowers and green apple to citrus (lime, lemon) and on to stone fruit (peach, apricot). Like Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Grigio, Riesling is often fermented in stainless steel and not matured in oak, so that the grape's pure aromas take centre stage."],["Il Riesling è il vitigno classico della Germania, dove si producono vini in tutta la gamma, da secchi a dolci; alcuni Riesling tedeschi, per esempio della Mosella, hanno una dolcezza media bilanciata dall'acidità e un grado alcolico basso. L'Alsazia, in Francia, e l'Australia fanno invece Riesling in stile secco, spesso con agrumi come lime e limone e note floreali.","Le Riesling est le cépage classique de l'Allemagne, qui produit toute la gamme, du sec au doux ; certains Riesling allemands, par exemple de Moselle, sont demi-doux, équilibrés par l'acidité et peu alcoolisés. L'Alsace, en France, et l'Australie font en revanche des Riesling de style sec, souvent sur le citron vert, le citron et les fleurs.","Riesling is the classic grape of Germany, where it is made across the whole range from dry to sweet; some German Rieslings, from the Mosel for example, are medium-sweet, balanced by acidity and low in alcohol. Alsace in France and Australia, on the other hand, make Riesling in a dry style, often with lime, lemon and floral notes."],["Attenzione in etichetta: dato che lo stesso vitigno può dare vini secchi, medi o dolci, il nome «Riesling» da solo non dice quanto sarà dolce il vino. L'origine aiuta: Alsazia e Australia fanno pensare a uno stile secco, mentre la Germania copre tutta la gamma. Vale la pena leggere anche la descrizione del vino.","Attention à l'étiquette : comme le même cépage peut donner des vins secs, demi-doux ou doux, le nom « Riesling » seul ne dit pas si le vin sera sucré. L'origine aide : l'Alsace et l'Australie évoquent un style sec, tandis que l'Allemagne couvre toute la gamme. Mieux vaut aussi lire la description du vin.","Watch the label: because the same grape can make dry, medium or sweet wines, the word «Riesling» alone does not tell you how sweet the wine will be. The origin helps: Alsace and Australia point to a dry style, while Germany covers the whole range. It is also worth reading the wine's description."]],"k":[["Da secco a dolce, ma sempre con acidità alta","Du sec au doux, mais toujours avec une acidité élevée","Dry to sweet, but always high in acidity"],["Fiori, mela, lime, limone, pesca, albicocca","Fleurs, pomme, citron vert, citron, pêche, abricot","Floral, apple, lime, lemon, peach, apricot"],["Acciaio inox, niente rovere","Cuve inox, sans chêne","Stainless steel, no oak"],["Germania: tutta la gamma; Alsazia e Australia: stile secco","Allemagne : toute la gamme ; Alsace et Australie : style sec","Germany: full range; Alsace and Australia: dry style"]]},{"c":"w3","t":["Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon"],"p":[["Il Cabernet Sauvignon è un'uva nera coltivata in tutto il mondo. Dà vini rossi secchi, con molto tannino e un'acidità alta: si sentono subito la bocca che si asciuga e la freschezza che fa salivare. Il corpo va da medio a pieno. Come gli altri vitigni neri, si trova bene nelle regioni calde, dove le uve maturano con regolarità.","Le Cabernet Sauvignon est un raisin noir cultivé dans le monde entier. Il donne des rouges secs, riches en tanins et à l'acidité élevée : on sent tout de suite la bouche qui s'assèche et la fraîcheur qui fait saliver. Le corps va de moyen à ample. Comme les autres cépages noirs, il se plaît dans les régions chaudes, où le raisin mûrit régulièrement.","Cabernet Sauvignon is a black grape planted all over the world. It makes dry red wines with high tannin and high acidity: you notice both the drying grip and the mouth-watering freshness straight away. The body ranges from medium to full. Like other black grapes, it does well in warm regions, where the grapes ripen reliably."],["Il profumo più tipico è il ribes nero, spesso con ciliegia nera. Accanto alla frutta compaiono note erbacee come peperone verde e menta. Molti Cabernet Sauvignon vengono affinati in rovere, che aggiunge cedro e vaniglia. Un Cabernet californiano, per esempio, può essere di corpo pieno, con ribes nero intenso e note di cedro.","L'arôme le plus typique est le cassis, souvent accompagné de cerise noire. À côté du fruit apparaissent des notes herbacées comme le poivron vert et la menthe. Beaucoup de Cabernet Sauvignon sont élevés en chêne, qui ajoute cèdre et vanille. Un Cabernet de Californie, par exemple, peut être corsé, avec un cassis intense et des notes de cèdre.","Its signature aroma is blackcurrant, often with black cherry. Alongside the fruit there are herbaceous notes such as green bell pepper and mint. Many Cabernet Sauvignons are matured in oak, which adds cedar and vanilla. A Californian Cabernet, for example, can be full-bodied, with intense blackcurrant and cedar notes."],["Dato che il tannino è così alto, il Cabernet Sauvignon viene spesso unito ad altri vitigni. A Bordeaux si sposa con il Merlot, che ammorbidisce il vino e gli dà più corpo. In Australia a volte viene unito allo Shiraz, che porta note speziate. Il taglio serve quindi a correggere o arricchire lo stile.","Ses tanins étant très présents, le Cabernet Sauvignon est souvent assemblé à d'autres cépages. À Bordeaux, il s'allie au Merlot, qui assouplit le vin et lui donne plus de corps. En Australie, il est parfois assemblé à la Shiraz, qui apporte des notes épicées. L'assemblage sert donc à corriger ou enrichir le style.","Because its tannin is so high, Cabernet Sauvignon is often blended with other grapes. In Bordeaux it is paired with Merlot, which softens the wine and adds body. In Australia it is sometimes blended with Shiraz, which brings spicy aromas. Blending is therefore a way to round out or enrich the style."],["Oltre a Bordeaux, il Cabernet Sauvignon è molto coltivato in California, Australia, Cile e Sudafrica. In questi paesi spesso compare in etichetta da solo, con il nome del vitigno. A Bordeaux, invece, l'etichetta riporta il nome della zona e il vino è di solito un taglio: bisogna sapere che dentro ci sono Cabernet Sauvignon e Merlot.","Outre Bordeaux, le Cabernet Sauvignon est très cultivé en Californie, en Australie, au Chili et en Afrique du Sud. Dans ces pays, il apparaît souvent seul sur l'étiquette, sous le nom du cépage. À Bordeaux, l'étiquette indique plutôt la région et le vin est en général un assemblage : il faut savoir qu'il contient du Cabernet Sauvignon et du Merlot.","Beyond Bordeaux, Cabernet Sauvignon is widely grown in California, Australia, Chile and South Africa. In these countries it often appears on its own on the label, under the grape's name. In Bordeaux, by contrast, the label shows the region and the wine is usually a blend, so you need to know it contains Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot."]],"k":[["Secco, tannino alto, acidità alta, corpo medio-pieno","Sec, tanins élevés, acidité élevée, corps moyen à ample","Dry, high tannin, high acidity, medium to full body"],["Ribes nero, ciliegia nera, peperone verde, menta; rovere: cedro, vaniglia","Cassis, cerise noire, poivron vert, menthe ; chêne : cèdre, vanille","Blackcurrant, black cherry, green pepper, mint; oak: cedar, vanilla"],["Bordeaux: con il Merlot (più morbidezza e corpo)","Bordeaux : avec le Merlot (souplesse et corps)","Bordeaux: blended with Merlot (softness and body)"],["Anche California, Australia (a volte con Shiraz), Cile, Sudafrica","Aussi Californie, Australie (parfois avec la Shiraz), Chili, Afrique du Sud","Also California, Australia (sometimes with Shiraz), Chile, South Africa"]]},{"c":"w3","t":["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"],"p":[["Il Merlot dà vini generalmente secchi, di corpo da medio a pieno, con acidità e tannino medi. È quindi più morbido e rotondo del Cabernet Sauvignon. La frutta va dai frutti rossi, come fragola e prugna rossa, ai frutti neri, come mora e prugna nera: più l'uva è matura, più ci si sposta verso la frutta nera.","Le Merlot donne des vins généralement secs, au corps moyen à ample, avec une acidité et des tanins moyens. Il est donc plus souple et rond que le Cabernet Sauvignon. Le fruit va des fruits rouges, comme la fraise et la prune rouge, aux fruits noirs, comme la mûre et la prune noire.","Merlot makes wines that are generally dry and medium- to full-bodied, with medium acidity and medium tannin. That makes it softer and rounder than Cabernet Sauvignon. Its fruit ranges from red fruit such as strawberry and red plum to black fruit such as blackberry and black plum."],["Il Merlot viene spesso affinato in rovere, che aggiunge note di vaniglia alla frutta. In Cile e in California se ne fanno vini morbidi e fruttati, facili da bere: in carta potresti trovare un Merlot cileno descritto come «morbido, con prugna nera e mora». È uno dei rossi più accessibili per chi inizia.","Le Merlot est souvent élevé en chêne, qui ajoute des notes de vanille au fruit. Au Chili et en Californie, on en fait des vins souples et fruités, faciles à boire : sur une carte, un Merlot chilien peut être décrit comme « souple, prune noire et mûre ». C'est l'un des rouges les plus accessibles pour débuter.","Merlot is often matured in oak, which adds vanilla notes to the fruit. Chile and California use it to make soft, fruity, easy-drinking wines: on a wine list, a Chilean Merlot might be described as «smooth, with black plum and blackberry». It is one of the most approachable reds for beginners."],["Il Merlot è il compagno classico del Cabernet Sauvignon. Nel taglio i due si completano: il Merlot porta morbidezza e corpo, il Cabernet Sauvignon aggiunge tannino e acidità. La regione più famosa per questo taglio è Bordeaux; in alcune zone di Bordeaux, come Saint-Émilion, il Merlot è spesso il vitigno principale. Oggi questo taglio si fa in molti altri paesi.","Le Merlot est le partenaire classique du Cabernet Sauvignon. Dans l'assemblage, ils se complètent : le Merlot apporte souplesse et corps, le Cabernet Sauvignon ajoute tanins et acidité. La région la plus célèbre pour cet assemblage est Bordeaux ; dans certaines zones, comme Saint-Émilion, le Merlot domine souvent. Cet assemblage se fait aujourd'hui dans bien d'autres pays.","Merlot is Cabernet Sauvignon's classic partner. In a blend the two complete each other: Merlot brings softness and body, while Cabernet Sauvignon adds tannin and acidity. Bordeaux is the most famous region for this blend; in some parts of Bordeaux, such as Saint-Émilion, Merlot is often the main grape. The blend is now common in many other countries."]],"k":[["Secco, corpo medio-pieno, acidità e tannino medi","Sec, corps moyen à ample, acidité et tanins moyens","Dry, medium to full body, medium acidity and tannin"],["Da fragola e prugna rossa a mora e prugna nera; rovere: vaniglia","De la fraise et prune rouge à la mûre et prune noire ; chêne : vanille","From strawberry and red plum to blackberry and black plum; oak: vanilla"],["Cile e California: vini morbidi e fruttati","Chili et Californie : vins souples et fruités","Chile and California: soft, fruity wines"],["Bordeaux: taglio con il Cabernet Sauvignon (che aggiunge tannino e acidità)","Bordeaux : assemblage avec le Cabernet Sauvignon (qui ajoute tanins et acidité)","Bordeaux: blend with Cabernet Sauvignon (which adds tannin and acidity)"]]},{"c":"w3","t":["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],"p":[["Il Pinot Noir dà rossi di solito secchi, di corpo da leggero a medio, con acidità alta e tannino da basso a medio. È quindi un rosso elegante e delicato, molto diverso dal Cabernet Sauvignon. I suoi aromi sono di frutti rossi: fragola, ciliegia rossa, lampone. Se passa in rovere, cosa frequente, aggiunge note di vaniglia e di affumicato.","Le Pinot Noir donne des rouges en général secs, au corps léger à moyen, à l'acidité élevée et aux tanins faibles à moyens. C'est donc un rouge élégant et délicat, très différent du Cabernet Sauvignon. Ses arômes sont de fruits rouges : fraise, cerise rouge, framboise. S'il passe en chêne, ce qui est fréquent, il ajoute vanille et fumé.","Pinot Noir makes reds that are usually dry and light- to medium-bodied, with high acidity and low to medium tannin. It is an elegant, delicate red, very different from Cabernet Sauvignon. Its aromas are of red fruit: strawberry, red cherry and raspberry. It is often matured in oak, which adds notes of vanilla and smoke."],["Il Pinot Noir è l'uva dei rossi di Burgundy (Bourgogne), in Francia: vini secchi, leggeri o medi, molto freschi, con lampone e ciliegia rossa e talvolta vaniglia e affumicato del rovere. È anche il principale vitigno nero della Nuova Zelanda, per esempio nella zona di Central Otago.","Le Pinot Noir est le cépage des rouges de Bourgogne (Burgundy), en France : vins secs, légers à moyens, très frais, sur la framboise et la cerise rouge, parfois avec vanille et fumé du chêne. C'est aussi le principal cépage noir de Nouvelle-Zélande, par exemple dans la région de Central Otago.","Pinot Noir is the grape of red Burgundy (Bourgogne) in France: dry, light to medium-bodied, very fresh wines with raspberry and red cherry, and sometimes vanilla and smoke from oak. It is also the main black grape of New Zealand, for example in the Central Otago region."],["A differenza del Cabernet Sauvignon e del Merlot, quando si fa un vino rosso il Pinot Noir di solito non viene unito ad altri vitigni: si preferisce mostrarne il carattere puro. C'è però un'eccezione importante: nello Champagne il Pinot Noir viene spesso unito allo Chardonnay. Qui le bucce vengono separate subito, così il succo resta chiaro.","Contrairement au Cabernet Sauvignon et au Merlot, le Pinot Noir n'est en général pas assemblé quand on fait un vin rouge : on préfère montrer son caractère pur. Il y a toutefois une exception importante : dans le Champagne, le Pinot Noir est souvent assemblé au Chardonnay. Les peaux sont alors séparées tout de suite, et le jus reste clair.","Unlike Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, Pinot Noir is not usually blended with other grapes when making red wine; producers prefer to show its pure character. There is one important exception: in Champagne, Pinot Noir is often blended with Chardonnay. There the skins are removed straight away, so the juice stays pale."]],"k":[["Secco, corpo leggero-medio, acidità alta, tannino basso-medio","Sec, corps léger à moyen, acidité élevée, tanins faibles à moyens","Dry, light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin"],["Fragola, ciliegia rossa, lampone; rovere: vaniglia, affumicato","Fraise, cerise rouge, framboise ; chêne : vanille, fumé","Strawberry, red cherry, raspberry; oak: vanilla, smoke"],["Burgundy rosso; principale uva nera della Nuova Zelanda","Bourgogne rouge ; principal cépage noir de Nouvelle-Zélande","Red Burgundy; New Zealand's main black grape"],["Di solito non in taglio per i rossi; nello Champagne con lo Chardonnay","En général pas d'assemblage en rouge ; dans le Champagne avec le Chardonnay","Not usually blended for reds; in Champagne with Chardonnay"]]},{"c":"w3","t":["Syrah / Shiraz","Syrah / Shiraz","Syrah / Shiraz"],"p":[["È lo stesso vitigno con due nomi: in Francia si chiama Syrah, in Australia Shiraz. Il nome in etichetta suggerisce quindi anche l'origine e, spesso, lo stile. Dà vini secchi, di corpo da medio a pieno, con tannino da medio ad alto e acidità media. I sapori tipici sono frutta nera (mora, ciliegia nera) e spezie (pepe nero, liquirizia).","C'est le même cépage sous deux noms : Syrah en France, Shiraz en Australie. Le nom sur l'étiquette suggère donc aussi l'origine et, souvent, le style. Il donne des vins secs, au corps moyen à ample, aux tanins moyens à élevés et à l'acidité moyenne. Les saveurs typiques sont les fruits noirs (mûre, cerise noire) et les épices (poivre noir, réglisse).","This is one grape with two names: it is called Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia, so the name on the label also hints at the origin and often the style. It makes dry wines with medium to full body, medium to high tannin and medium acidity. Typical flavours are black fruit (blackberry, black cherry) and spice (black pepper, liquorice)."],["Molti Syrah e Shiraz vengono affinati in rovere, che aggiunge note di vaniglia o di cocco. Accanto alla frutta nera e alle spezie, questi aromi del legno rendono il vino più ricco. Per chi studia, la coppia «frutta nera + pepe nero» è un ottimo indizio per riconoscere questo vitigno.","Beaucoup de Syrah et de Shiraz sont élevées en chêne, qui ajoute des notes de vanille ou de noix de coco. À côté du fruit noir et des épices, ces arômes boisés rendent le vin plus riche. Pour les personnes qui étudient, le duo « fruit noir + poivre noir » est un excellent indice pour reconnaître ce cépage.","Many Syrahs and Shirazes are matured in oak, which adds vanilla or coconut notes. Alongside the black fruit and spice, these oak aromas make the wine richer. For anyone studying, the pairing «black fruit + black pepper» is an excellent clue for recognising this grape."],["Il clima cambia molto lo stile. Nel Rodano settentrionale, in Francia, il Syrah può dare vini di corpo medio, con mora fresca e pepe nero. Nelle zone calde dell'Australia, come la Barossa Valley, le uve maturano di più: lo Shiraz diventa di corpo pieno, con ciliegia nera dal gusto quasi di confettura e liquirizia.","Le climat change beaucoup le style. Dans le nord de la vallée du Rhône, en France, la Syrah peut donner des vins de corps moyen, avec mûre fraîche et poivre noir. Dans les régions chaudes d'Australie, comme la Barossa Valley, le raisin mûrit davantage : la Shiraz devient corsée, avec une cerise noire presque confiturée et de la réglisse.","Climate changes the style a great deal. In France's Northern Rhône, Syrah can make medium-bodied wines with fresh blackberry and black pepper. In warm parts of Australia, such as the Barossa Valley, the grapes ripen further, and Shiraz becomes full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice."],["Lo Shiraz australiano viene anche unito al Cabernet Sauvignon: in questo taglio lo Shiraz porta aromi speziati. Riassumendo: Francia e Rodano settentrionale = Syrah più fresco e pepato; Australia calda = Shiraz pieno e maturo. Stesso vitigno, due climi, due stili diversi.","La Shiraz australienne est aussi assemblée au Cabernet Sauvignon : dans cet assemblage, elle apporte des arômes épicés. En résumé : France et nord du Rhône = Syrah plus fraîche et poivrée ; Australie chaude = Shiraz ample et mûre. Même cépage, deux climats, deux styles différents.","Australian Shiraz is also blended with Cabernet Sauvignon, and in that blend it contributes spicy aromas. To sum up: France and the Northern Rhône = fresher, peppery Syrah; warm Australia = full, ripe Shiraz. Same grape, two climates, two different styles."]],"k":[["Syrah in Francia, Shiraz in Australia: stesso vitigno","Syrah en France, Shiraz en Australie : même cépage","Syrah in France, Shiraz in Australia: the same grape"],["Secco, corpo medio-pieno, tannino medio-alto, acidità media","Sec, corps moyen à ample, tanins moyens à élevés, acidité moyenne","Dry, medium to full body, medium to high tannin, medium acidity"],["Mora, ciliegia nera, pepe nero, liquirizia; rovere: vaniglia, cocco","Mûre, cerise noire, poivre noir, réglisse ; chêne : vanille, coco","Blackberry, black cherry, black pepper, liquorice; oak: vanilla, coconut"],["Rodano settentrionale: medio e pepato; Australia calda: pieno, confettura, liquirizia","Nord du Rhône : moyen et poivré ; Australie chaude : ample, confituré, réglisse","Northern Rhône: medium, peppery; warm Australia: full, jammy, liquorice"]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Conservare il vino","Conserver le vin","Storing wine"],"p":[["Un vino conservato male perde qualità. All'inizio può semplicemente perdere parte del suo carattere; con il tempo può arrivare a sviluppare veri e propri difetti. Per evitarlo bastano tre regole semplici, che riguardano la temperatura, la luce e la posizione della bottiglia. Valgono a casa come in un ristorante o in un'enoteca.","Un vin mal conservé perd en qualité. Au début, il peut simplement perdre une partie de son caractère ; avec le temps, il peut finir par développer de vrais défauts. Pour l'éviter, trois règles simples suffisent : elles concernent la température, la lumière et la position de la bouteille. Elles valent à la maison comme au restaurant ou chez un caviste.","A wine that is stored badly loses quality. At first it may simply lose some of its character; over time it can end up developing real faults. Three simple rules are enough to prevent this, covering temperature, light and the position of the bottle. They apply at home just as much as in a restaurant or a wine shop."],["Prima regola: per una conservazione lunga il vino va tenuto in un luogo fresco e a temperatura costante. Sia il freddo o il caldo estremi sia i grandi sbalzi di temperatura possono rovinarlo. Seconda regola: tenere le bottiglie lontano dal sole forte e dalle luci artificiali intense. La luce, e il calore che produce, possono far perdere al vino il suo carattere fruttato.","Première règle : pour une conservation longue, le vin doit être gardé dans un endroit frais, à température constante. Le froid ou la chaleur extrêmes, comme les fortes variations de température, peuvent l'abîmer. Deuxième règle : tenir les bouteilles à l'écart du soleil fort et des lumières artificielles vives. La lumière, et la chaleur qu'elle produit, peuvent faire perdre au vin son caractère fruité.","Rule one: for long-term storage, keep wine somewhere cool at a steady temperature. Extreme cold or heat, as well as big swings in temperature, can damage it. Rule two: keep bottles away from strong sunshine and bright artificial light. Light, and the heat that comes with it, can make a wine lose its fruity character."],["Terza regola: le bottiglie chiuse con tappo di sughero si conservano coricate. In questo modo il sughero resta a contatto con il vino e rimane umido. Se il tappo si secca può lasciar entrare aria nella bottiglia, e il vino perde il suo frutto. Le bottiglie con tappo a vite non hanno questo problema e possono essere conservate in piedi.","Troisième règle : les bouteilles fermées par un bouchon en liège se conservent couchées. Ainsi, le liège reste au contact du vin et demeure humide. Si le bouchon se dessèche, il peut laisser entrer de l'air dans la bouteille, et le vin perd son fruit. Les bouteilles à capsule à vis n'ont pas ce problème et peuvent être conservées debout.","Rule three: bottles closed with a cork should be stored on their side. This keeps the cork in contact with the wine so that it stays moist. If the cork dries out, it can let air into the bottle and the wine loses its fruitiness. Bottles with a screwcap do not have this problem and can be stored standing up."]],"k":[["Conservare male il vino gli fa perdere carattere e può causare difetti.","Mal conserver un vin lui fait perdre son caractère et peut créer des défauts.","Poor storage makes wine lose character and can cause faults."],["Temperatura fresca e costante; niente estremi né sbalzi.","Température fraîche et constante ; ni extrêmes ni variations.","Cool, constant temperature; no extremes or big swings."],["Lontano da sole e luce artificiale forte.","À l'abri du soleil et des lumières vives.","Away from sunshine and bright artificial light."],["Tappo di sughero: bottiglia coricata. Tappo a vite: anche in piedi.","Bouchon en liège : bouteille couchée. Capsule à vis : debout possible.","Cork: store on its side. Screwcap: can stand up."]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Conservare un vino aperto","Conserver un vin ouvert","Keeping opened wine fresh"],"p":[["Una volta aperta, la bottiglia entra in contatto con l'aria e il vino comincia lentamente a perdere freschezza, fino a sapere di stantio. Il primo rimedio è semplice: rimettere il tappo e tenere la bottiglia in frigorifero. Il freddo rallenta il processo e aiuta il vino a restare fresco più a lungo.","Une fois la bouteille ouverte, le vin entre en contact avec l'air et commence lentement à perdre sa fraîcheur, jusqu'à prendre un goût éventé. Le premier remède est simple : remettre le bouchon et garder la bouteille au réfrigérateur. Le froid ralentit le processus et aide le vin à rester frais plus longtemps.","Once a bottle is opened, the wine comes into contact with air and slowly starts to lose its freshness, eventually tasting stale. The first fix is simple: put the cork back in and keep the bottle in the fridge. The cold slows things down and helps the wine stay fresh for longer."],["Per prolungare ancora la vita del vino esistono sistemi pensati per tenerlo lontano dall'aria. I sistemi sottovuoto usano una piccola pompa che aspira l'aria dalla bottiglia. I sistemi a «coperta» di gas pompano nella bottiglia un gas che spinge fuori l'aria e resta sopra il vino senza danneggiarlo. Entrambi hanno lo stesso obiettivo: limitare il contatto con l'aria.","Pour prolonger encore la vie du vin, il existe des systèmes conçus pour le tenir à l'écart de l'air. Les systèmes sous vide utilisent une petite pompe qui aspire l'air de la bouteille. Les systèmes à « couverture » de gaz injectent dans la bouteille un gaz qui chasse l'air et reste au-dessus du vin sans l'abîmer. Les deux ont le même but : limiter le contact avec l'air.","To keep a wine going for even longer, there are systems designed to keep it away from air. Vacuum systems use a small pump to draw the air out of the bottle. Blanket systems pump a gas into the bottle that pushes the air out and sits over the wine without harming it. Both share the same goal: limiting contact with air."],["Il ragionamento da ricordare è sempre lo stesso: è l'aria il nemico del vino aperto, ed è sempre l'aria che rovina il vino quando un tappo di sughero si secca in cantina. Frigorifero, sottovuoto e gas inerte sono tre modi diversi per rallentare questo processo e servire anche il giorno dopo un vino ancora piacevole.","Le raisonnement à retenir est toujours le même : l'air est l'ennemi du vin ouvert, et c'est aussi l'air qui abîme le vin quand un bouchon en liège se dessèche en cave. Réfrigérateur, vide et gaz inerte sont trois façons différentes de ralentir ce processus et de servir le lendemain un vin encore agréable.","The reasoning to remember is always the same: air is the enemy of opened wine, and it is also air that spoils wine when a cork dries out in storage. The fridge, a vacuum pump and an inert gas are three different ways to slow this down so that the wine is still enjoyable the next day."]],"k":[["Il vino aperto diventa stantio a contatto con l'aria.","Le vin ouvert s'évente au contact de l'air.","Opened wine goes stale as it reacts with air."],["Tappo e frigorifero lo mantengono fresco più a lungo.","Bouchon et réfrigérateur le gardent frais plus longtemps.","Cork back in and fridge keep it fresher for longer."],["Sottovuoto: una pompa aspira l'aria.","Sous vide : une pompe aspire l'air.","Vacuum system: a pump removes the air."],["Coperta di gas: un gas innocuo spinge fuori l'aria.","Couverture de gaz : un gaz sans danger chasse l'air.","Blanket system: a harmless gas pushes the air out."]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Le temperature di servizio","Les températures de service","Service temperatures"],"p":[["La temperatura cambia molto il modo in cui percepiamo un vino. In generale bianchi, rosati e spumanti si servono freschi, mentre i rossi si servono a temperatura ambiente o appena freschi. Sono indicazioni, non leggi: se un ospite preferisce bere un vino a un'altra temperatura, chi serve deve rispettare il suo gusto.","La température change beaucoup notre perception d'un vin. En général, les blancs, les rosés et les effervescents se servent frais, tandis que les rouges se servent à température ambiante ou légèrement rafraîchis. Ce sont des repères, pas des lois : si une personne préfère boire un vin à une autre température, il faut respecter son goût.","Temperature makes a big difference to how we experience a wine. In general, whites, rosés and sparkling wines are served chilled, while reds are served at room temperature or lightly chilled. These are guidelines, not laws: if a guest prefers a wine at a different temperature, the host should respect that preference."],["I vini più freddi sono i dolci, come il Sauternes, da servire molto freschi a 6–8 °C, e gli spumanti, come lo Champagne, molto freschi a 6–10 °C. I bianchi leggeri o di medio corpo e i rosati, per esempio un Pinot Grigio, vanno serviti freschi a 7–10 °C. I bianchi di corpo pieno, come uno Chardonnay maturato in rovere, si servono appena freschi, a 10–13 °C.","Les vins servis le plus froid sont les vins doux, comme le Sauternes, bien frais à 6–8 °C, et les effervescents, comme le Champagne, bien frais à 6–10 °C. Les blancs légers ou de corps moyen et les rosés, par exemple un Pinot Grigio, se servent frais à 7–10 °C. Les blancs corsés, comme un Chardonnay élevé en chêne, se servent légèrement rafraîchis, à 10–13 °C.","The coldest wines are sweet wines such as Sauternes, served well chilled at 6–8°C (43–45°F), and sparkling wines such as Champagne, well chilled at 6–10°C (43–50°F). Light- and medium-bodied whites and rosés, such as Pinot Grigio, are served chilled at 7–10°C (45–50°F). Full-bodied whites, such as an oaked Chardonnay, are served lightly chilled at 10–13°C (50–55°F)."],["Tra i rossi, quelli leggeri come il Beaujolais si servono appena freschi, intorno ai 13 °C. I rossi di medio corpo o corposi, come uno Shiraz, si servono a temperatura ambiente, tra 15 e 18 °C. Poiché riscaldamento e aria condizionata rendono la «temperatura ambiente» molto variabile, conviene affidarsi all'intervallo di gradi più che alla stanza.","Parmi les rouges, les plus légers, comme le Beaujolais, se servent légèrement rafraîchis, autour de 13 °C. Les rouges de corps moyen ou corsés, comme un Shiraz, se servent à température ambiante, entre 15 et 18 °C. Comme le chauffage et la climatisation rendent la « température ambiante » très variable, mieux vaut se fier à la fourchette de degrés qu'à la pièce.","Among reds, light ones such as Beaujolais are served lightly chilled, at around 13°C (55°F). Medium- and full-bodied reds, such as Shiraz, are served at room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F). Because central heating and air conditioning make 'room temperature' very variable, the range of degrees is a better guide than the room itself."],["Per tenere fresco il vino fino alla fine della bottiglia si può usare un contenitore isolante oppure un secchiello. In questo caso il secchiello va riempito di ghiaccio e anche di acqua fredda: con il solo ghiaccio raffredda molto meno bene. Al contrario, un rosso troppo freddo non va mai scaldato vicino a un termosifone, perché il calore ne rovina i sapori: meglio lasciarlo nella stanza in cui si servirà, finché si scalda da solo.","Pour garder le vin frais jusqu'à la fin de la bouteille, on peut utiliser un contenant isotherme ou un seau. Dans ce cas, le seau se remplit de glace et aussi d'eau froide : avec de la glace seule, il refroidit beaucoup moins bien. À l'inverse, un rouge trop froid ne doit jamais être réchauffé près d'un radiateur, car la chaleur abîme ses saveurs : mieux vaut le laisser dans la pièce où il sera servi, jusqu'à ce qu'il se réchauffe naturellement.","To keep wine cool until the bottle is finished, you can use an insulated container or an ice bucket. If you use a bucket, fill it with ice and cold water: ice alone cools far less efficiently. On the other hand, a red that is too cold should never be warmed next to a radiator, because heat damages its flavours; instead, leave it in the room where it will be served and let it warm up naturally."]],"k":[["Dolci e spumanti: molto freschi (6–8 °C / 6–10 °C).","Doux et effervescents : bien frais (6–8 °C / 6–10 °C).","Sweet and sparkling: well chilled (6–8°C / 6–10°C)."],["Bianchi leggeri-medi e rosati: freschi, 7–10 °C.","Blancs légers à moyens et rosés : frais, 7–10 °C.","Light/medium whites and rosés: chilled, 7–10°C."],["Bianchi corposi: appena freschi, 10–13 °C; rossi leggeri: appena freschi, 13 °C.","Blancs corsés : légèrement frais, 10–13 °C ; rouges légers : légèrement frais, 13 °C.","Full whites: lightly chilled, 10–13°C; light reds: lightly chilled, 13°C."],["Rossi medi e corposi: temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C.","Rouges moyens et corsés : température ambiante, 15–18 °C.","Medium/full reds: room temperature, 15–18°C."],["Secchiello con ghiaccio e acqua; mai scaldare il vino vicino a una fonte di calore.","Seau avec glace et eau ; ne jamais chauffer le vin près d'une source de chaleur.","Ice bucket with ice and water; never heat wine by a radiator."]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Aprire una bottiglia","Ouvrir une bouteille","Opening a bottle"],"p":[["Per un vino fermo chiuso con tappo di sughero si procede così. Prima si toglie la parte superiore della capsula, con un taglia-capsula o con il coltellino di un cavatappi da sommelier, e si pulisce il collo della bottiglia con un panno. Poi si centra la vite del cavatappi nel mezzo del tappo, la si avvita e si estrae il sughero con delicatezza. Infine si pulisce di nuovo il collo, dentro e fuori.","Pour un vin tranquille fermé par un bouchon en liège, on procède ainsi. D'abord, on retire le haut de la capsule, avec un coupe-capsule ou la lame d'un tire-bouchon de sommelier, et on nettoie le col de la bouteille avec un linge. Ensuite, on centre la mèche du tire-bouchon au milieu du bouchon, on la visse et on retire le liège en douceur. Enfin, on essuie à nouveau le col, à l'intérieur et à l'extérieur.","For a still wine sealed with a cork, the method is as follows. First remove the top of the capsule, using a foil cutter or the blade of a waiter's friend corkscrew, and wipe the neck of the bottle with a cloth. Then centre the corkscrew in the middle of the cork, screw it in and draw the cork out gently. Finally, wipe the neck again, both inside and outside."],["Con gli spumanti serve più attenzione, perché nella bottiglia c'è molta pressione. Raffreddare il vino la riduce, ma anche da freddo il tappo può schizzare via e ferire qualcuno. La regola d'oro: dal momento in cui si allenta la gabbietta di metallo, il tappo deve restare sempre sotto la mano, finché non è completamente fuori dalla bottiglia.","Avec les effervescents, il faut plus de prudence, car la bouteille est sous forte pression. Rafraîchir le vin réduit cette pression, mais même froid, le bouchon peut partir d'un coup et blesser quelqu'un. Règle d'or : dès que l'on desserre le muselet, le bouchon doit toujours rester sous la main, jusqu'à ce qu'il soit complètement sorti.","Sparkling wine needs more care, because there is a lot of pressure inside the bottle. Chilling reduces it, but even when the wine is cold the cork can shoot out and injure someone. The golden rule: from the moment the wire cage is loosened, the cork must stay under your hand until it is completely out of the bottle."],["I passaggi sono questi: togliere la stagnola e allentare la gabbietta tenendo il tappo coperto con la mano. Inclinare la bottiglia, tenere il tappo con una mano e la base con l'altra, e far ruotare la bottiglia, non il tappo. Tenendo il tappo ben fermo, la pressione esce lentamente, con un leggero sospiro e senza perdere vino.","Les étapes sont les suivantes : retirer la feuille d'aluminium et desserrer le muselet en gardant la main sur le bouchon. Incliner la bouteille, tenir le bouchon d'une main et le fond de la bouteille de l'autre, puis faire tourner la bouteille, pas le bouchon. En tenant fermement le bouchon, la pression s'échappe doucement, dans un léger soupir et sans perte de vin.","The steps are: remove the foil and loosen the cage while keeping the cork covered with your hand. Tilt the bottle at an angle, hold the cork in one hand and the base in the other, and turn the bottle, not the cork. Holding the cork firmly lets the pressure escape slowly, with a quiet sigh and no wine lost."]],"k":[["Vino fermo: togliere la capsula, pulire, estrarre il tappo con delicatezza, ripulire il collo.","Vin tranquille : retirer la capsule, essuyer, tirer doucement le bouchon, essuyer le col.","Still wine: remove capsule top, wipe, ease the cork out, wipe the neck."],["Spumante: molta pressione; il tappo può ferire.","Effervescent : forte pression ; le bouchon peut blesser.","Sparkling: high pressure; the cork can injure."],["Dopo aver allentato la gabbietta, mano sempre sul tappo.","Après avoir desserré le muselet, toujours la main sur le bouchon.","Once the cage is loosened, keep a hand on the cork."],["Bottiglia inclinata; si gira la bottiglia, non il tappo.","Bouteille inclinée ; on tourne la bouteille, pas le bouchon.","Bottle at an angle; turn the bottle, not the cork."]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Bicchieri e controlli prima di servire","Verres et vérifications avant le service","Glasses and checks before serving"],"p":[["Esistono centinaia di forme di bicchieri, ma i migliori hanno un punto in comune: la coppa si restringe verso il bordo. Questa forma trattiene e concentra i profumi all'interno del bicchiere, così si apprezzano meglio. Di solito i bicchieri da rosso sono un po' più grandi di quelli da bianco, mentre gli spumanti si servono nei flûte.","Il existe des centaines de formes de verres, mais les meilleurs ont un point commun : le calice se resserre vers le bord. Cette forme retient et concentre les arômes dans le verre, ce qui permet de mieux les apprécier. En général, les verres à vin rouge sont un peu plus grands que les verres à vin blanc, et les effervescents se servent en flûte.","There are hundreds of glass shapes, but the best ones share one feature: the bowl narrows towards the rim. This shape holds and concentrates the aromas inside the glass, so they can be appreciated better. Red wine glasses are usually slightly larger than white wine glasses, and sparkling wines are served in flutes."],["Il bicchiere deve essere perfettamente pulito. Sporco o residui di detersivo possono rovinare il vino, alterandone profumi e sapori. Per questo i bicchieri vanno sempre lucidati prima dell'uso, così da eliminare eventuali tracce di sporco o impronte di dita. È un gesto semplice che fa una differenza reale nel bicchiere.","Le verre doit être parfaitement propre. La saleté ou un reste de liquide vaisselle peuvent gâcher le vin en altérant ses arômes et ses saveurs. C'est pourquoi les verres doivent toujours être essuyés et lustrés avant usage, afin d'éliminer toute trace de saleté ou de doigts. C'est un geste simple qui fait une vraie différence dans le verre.","The glass must be perfectly clean. Dirt or traces of detergent can spoil a wine by changing its aromas and flavours. That is why glasses should always be polished before use, to remove any lingering dirt or finger marks. It is a simple habit that makes a real difference to what ends up in the glass."],["Prima di servire, è buona abitudine controllare il vino. Si osserva l'aspetto: una velatura, cioè un vino torbido, può indicare un difetto, e non devono esserci pezzetti che galleggiano. Poi si annusa: il vino non deve sapere di stantio né avere odori di cartone bagnato o di aceto. Se qualcosa non va, è meglio non servirlo.","Avant de servir, il est bon de vérifier le vin. On regarde son aspect : un voile, c'est-à-dire un vin trouble, peut signaler un défaut, et aucun petit morceau ne doit flotter. Puis on le sent : le vin ne doit pas sentir l'éventé, ni avoir des odeurs de carton mouillé ou de vinaigre. Si quelque chose ne va pas, mieux vaut ne pas le servir.","Before serving, it is good practice to check the wine. Look at its appearance: haziness can point to a fault, and there should be no bits floating in it. Then smell it: the wine should not smell stale or have aromas of wet cardboard or vinegar. If something seems wrong, it is better not to serve it."]],"k":[["Il bicchiere migliore si restringe verso il bordo e concentra i profumi.","Le meilleur verre se resserre vers le bord et concentre les arômes.","The best glasses narrow at the rim to concentrate aromas."],["Rosso: bicchiere un po' più grande; spumante: flûte.","Rouge : verre un peu plus grand ; effervescent : flûte.","Red: slightly larger glass; sparkling: flute."],["Bicchieri puliti e lucidati: sporco e detersivo rovinano il vino.","Verres propres et lustrés : saleté et détergent gâchent le vin.","Clean, polished glasses: dirt and detergent spoil wine."],["Controlli: niente velature né pezzetti; niente odori di stantio, cartone bagnato o aceto.","Vérifier : ni voile ni morceaux ; ni odeur d'éventé, de carton mouillé ou de vinaigre.","Check: no haze or bits; no stale, wet cardboard or vinegar smells."]]},{"c":"t2","t":["Abbinare cibo e vino: le basi","Accorder mets et vins : les bases","Food and wine: the basics"],"p":[["L'abbinamento cibo-vino sembra complicato, ma a questo livello si riduce a due idee semplici: i gusti personali e alcune reazioni prevedibili tra cibo e vino. La prima idea è la più importante. Quando si consiglia un vino a un cliente o a un amico, conta prima di tutto ciò che quella persona ama o non ama.","L'accord mets-vins paraît compliqué, mais à ce niveau il se résume à deux idées simples : les goûts personnels et quelques réactions prévisibles entre plat et vin. La première idée est la plus importante. Quand on conseille un vin à une cliente, un client ou une personne amie, ce qui compte d'abord, c'est ce qu'elle aime ou n'aime pas.","Food and wine pairing can look complicated, but at this level it comes down to two simple ideas: personal preference and a few predictable reactions between food and wine. The first idea matters most. When recommending a wine to a customer or a friend, what counts above all is what that person likes or dislikes."],["Un abbinamento può sembrare perfetto a chi lo propone, ma se l'altra persona non apprezza quello stile di vino, non ha senso consigliarlo. Va ricordato anche che, per la maggior parte delle persone, la maggior parte dei vini accompagna in modo accettabile la maggior parte dei cibi. Non esiste quindi un solo vino giusto per ogni piatto.","Un accord peut sembler parfait à la personne qui le propose, mais si l'autre n'aime pas ce style de vin, il ne sert à rien de le conseiller. Il faut aussi rappeler que, pour la plupart des gens, la plupart des vins accompagnent de façon acceptable la plupart des plats. Il n'existe donc pas un seul bon vin pour chaque plat.","A pairing may seem perfect to the person suggesting it, but if the other person does not enjoy that style of wine, there is no point recommending it. It also helps to remember that, for most people, most wines go acceptably with most foods. So there is not just one right wine for each dish."],["Ci sono però alcune caratteristiche del cibo che di solito cambiano il modo in cui percepiamo il vino: dolcezza, umami, sale, acidità, intensità di sapore, grasso e piccante del peperoncino. Ognuna può rendere il vino più gradevole o meno. Conoscerle permette di evitare gli abbinamenti che quasi tutti trovano sgradevoli, lasciando poi una libertà quasi illimitata.","Certaines caractéristiques des plats changent toutefois en général notre perception du vin : le sucré, l'umami, le sel, l'acidité, l'intensité des saveurs, le gras et le piquant du piment. Chacune peut rendre le vin plus agréable ou moins agréable. Les connaître permet d'éviter les accords que presque tout le monde trouve déplaisants, et laisse ensuite une liberté presque illimitée.","Some features of food do, however, usually change how we perceive a wine: sweetness, umami, salt, acidity, flavour intensity, fat and chilli heat. Each one can make a wine seem better or worse. Knowing them lets you avoid the pairings most people dislike, and after that your options become almost limitless."],["Dal lato del vino, gli elementi che cambiano sono quelli che si imparano a riconoscere in degustazione: dolcezza, acidità, amaro, frutto, alcol e corpo. L'amaro nel vino, e la sensazione che asciuga la bocca, possono venire dai tannini dei rossi oppure dal rovere. Tenere a mente queste parole rende la tabella degli abbinamenti molto più facile da ricordare.","Côté vin, les éléments qui changent sont ceux que l'on apprend à reconnaître en dégustation : douceur, acidité, amertume, fruit, alcool et corps. L'amertume du vin, et la sensation qui assèche la bouche, peuvent venir des tanins des rouges ou du chêne. Garder ces mots en tête rend le tableau des accords beaucoup plus facile à mémoriser.","On the wine side, the elements that change are the ones you learn to spot when tasting: sweetness, acidity, bitterness, fruitiness, alcohol and body. Bitterness in wine, and the drying feel in the mouth, can come from the tannins in red wines or from oak. Keeping these words in mind makes the pairing table much easier to remember."]],"k":[["Il gusto della persona viene prima di tutto.","Les goûts de la personne passent avant tout.","The person's own taste comes first."],["Per quasi tutti, quasi ogni vino va bene con quasi ogni cibo.","Pour presque tout le monde, presque tout vin va avec presque tout plat.","For most people, most wines suit most foods."],["Cibo: dolce, umami, sale, acido, sapori intensi, grasso, piccante.","Plat : sucré, umami, sel, acide, saveurs intenses, gras, piment.","Food: sweet, umami, salt, acid, intense flavour, fat, chilli."],["Vino: dolcezza, acidità, amaro, frutto, alcol, corpo.","Vin : douceur, acidité, amertume, fruit, alcool, corps.","Wine: sweetness, acidity, bitterness, fruit, alcohol, body."],["L'amaro nel vino viene dai tannini o dal rovere.","L'amertume du vin vient des tanins ou du chêne.","Bitterness in wine comes from tannin or oak."]]},{"c":"t2","t":["Che cosa fa il cibo al vino","Ce que le plat fait au vin","What food does to wine"],"p":[["Dolcezza e umami sono i due elementi più «difficili». Un cibo dolce o ricco di umami fa sembrare il vino più secco e amaro, più acido, meno dolce e meno fruttato. Un rosso tannico o un vino molto segnato dal rovere può quindi diventare duro. Con un dessert, per esempio, un vino secco rischia di sembrare aspro e povero di frutto.","Le sucré et l'umami sont les deux éléments les plus « difficiles ». Un plat sucré ou riche en umami fait paraître le vin plus asséchant et amer, plus acide, moins doux et moins fruité. Un rouge tannique ou un vin très marqué par le chêne peut donc devenir dur. Avec un dessert, par exemple, un vin sec risque de paraître acide et sans fruit.","Sweetness and umami are the two 'difficult' elements. Sweet or umami-rich food makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. A tannic red or a heavily oaked wine can therefore turn harsh. With a dessert, for example, a dry wine is likely to taste sour and lacking in fruit."],["Sale e acidità sono invece elementi «amici» del vino. Un cibo salato fa sembrare il vino meno secco e amaro, meno acido, più fruttato e con più corpo. Un cibo acido lo fa sembrare meno secco e amaro e meno acido, ma anche più dolce e fruttato. Un piatto con una nota acida può quindi ammorbidire un vino molto vivace.","Le sel et l'acidité sont au contraire des alliés du vin. Un plat salé fait paraître le vin moins asséchant et amer, moins acide, plus fruité et avec plus de corps. Un plat acide le rend moins asséchant et amer, moins acide, mais aussi plus doux et plus fruité. Un plat avec une touche acide peut donc adoucir un vin très vif.","Salt and acidity, on the other hand, are wine-friendly. Salty food makes a wine seem less drying and bitter, less acidic, fruitier and fuller in body. Acidic food makes it seem less drying and bitter and less acidic, but also sweeter and fruitier. A dish with a sharp, acidic touch can therefore soften a very crisp wine."],["Restano tre casi. Un piatto dai sapori molto intensi può sovrastare il vino, che sembrerà sparire: meglio scegliere un vino dal sapore abbastanza deciso. Un cibo grasso o oleoso fa sembrare il vino meno acido. Il piccante del peperoncino, infine, fa risaltare l'alcol del vino, e a sua volta l'alcol aumenta la sensazione di bruciore del peperoncino.","Restent trois cas. Un plat aux saveurs très intenses peut écraser le vin, qui semblera disparaître : mieux vaut choisir un vin au goût assez marqué. Un plat gras ou huileux fait paraître le vin moins acide. Enfin, le piquant du piment fait ressortir l'alcool du vin, et l'alcool, à son tour, augmente la sensation de brûlure du piment.","Three cases remain. A dish with very intense flavours can overwhelm a wine, which will seem to disappear, so a wine with enough flavour of its own works better. Fatty or oily food makes a wine seem less acidic. Finally, chilli heat makes the alcohol in a wine more noticeable, and the alcohol in turn increases the burning sensation of the chilli."],["Un trucco per ricordare tutto: dolce e umami «tolgono» al vino dolcezza e frutto e ne aumentano acidità e amaro; sale e acido fanno il contrario. Da qui nascono ragionamenti utili: con un piatto dolce conviene un vino almeno altrettanto dolce, con un piatto piccante un vino non troppo alcolico, con un piatto ricco di umami un vino non troppo tannico.","Un moyen mnémotechnique : le sucré et l'umami « enlèvent » au vin sa douceur et son fruit et augmentent son acidité et son amertume ; le sel et l'acide font l'inverse. On en tire des raisonnements utiles : avec un plat sucré, un vin au moins aussi doux ; avec un plat pimenté, un vin pas trop alcoolisé ; avec un plat riche en umami, un vin pas trop tannique.","A way to remember it all: sweetness and umami 'take away' a wine's sweetness and fruit and boost its acidity and bitterness, while salt and acid do the opposite. Useful reasoning follows: with a sweet dish, choose a wine at least as sweet; with a spicy dish, a wine that is not too high in alcohol; with an umami-rich dish, a wine that is not too tannic."]],"k":[["Dolce o umami → vino più secco, amaro e acido, meno dolce e fruttato.","Sucré ou umami → vin plus asséchant, amer et acide, moins doux et fruité.","Sweet or umami → wine more drying, bitter, acidic; less sweet, fruity."],["Salato → vino meno amaro e acido, più fruttato e corposo.","Salé → vin moins amer et acide, plus fruité et corsé.","Salty → wine less bitter and acidic; fruitier, fuller."],["Acido → vino meno amaro e acido, più dolce e fruttato.","Acide → vin moins amer et acide, plus doux et fruité.","Acidic → wine less bitter and acidic; sweeter, fruitier."],["Sapori intensi sovrastano il vino; il grasso lo fa sembrare meno acido.","Les saveurs intenses écrasent le vin ; le gras le rend moins acide.","Intense flavours overwhelm wine; fat makes it seem less acidic."],["Peperoncino + alcol: più bruciore e alcol più evidente.","Piment + alcool : plus de brûlure et alcool plus marqué.","Chilli + alcohol: more burn, alcohol more noticeable."]]},{"c":"t3","t":["Prepararsi e osservare il colore","Se préparer et observer la couleur","Getting ready and looking at colour"],"p":[["Per degustare bene serve un metodo: affrontare ogni vino sempre nello stesso ordine. Questo approccio sistematico alla degustazione permette di scrivere note precise, da rileggere e confrontare in futuro. A questo livello le tappe sono tre: aspetto, naso e palato. In ognuna si guarda a poche cose, ma sempre le stesse.","Pour bien déguster, il faut une méthode : aborder chaque vin toujours dans le même ordre. Cette approche systématique de la dégustation permet d'écrire des notes précises, que l'on pourra relire et comparer plus tard. À ce niveau, il y a trois étapes : l'aspect, le nez et la bouche. À chaque étape, on observe peu de choses, mais toujours les mêmes.","Tasting well needs a method: approach every wine in the same order each time. This systematic approach to tasting lets you write accurate notes that you can look back on and compare in the future. At this level there are three stages: appearance, nose and palate. At each stage you look at only a few things, but always the same ones."],["Prima di cominciare conviene preparare l'ambiente. Non devono esserci odori che distraggono, come profumi forti o cucina. Serve una superficie bianca, per giudicare bene il colore. Il bicchiere ideale ha una coppa ampia che si restringe in alto, per concentrare i profumi. Anche la bocca deve essere pulita, senza sapori residui come dentifricio o caffè.","Avant de commencer, il vaut mieux préparer l'environnement. Il ne doit pas y avoir d'odeurs gênantes, comme des parfums forts ou de la cuisine. Il faut une surface blanche pour bien juger la couleur. Le verre idéal a un large calice qui se resserre en haut, pour concentrer les arômes. La bouche doit aussi être propre, sans goûts persistants comme le dentifrice ou le café.","Before starting, it is worth preparing your surroundings. There should be no distracting smells, such as strong perfume or cooking. You need a white surface to judge the colour properly. The ideal glass has a wide bowl that narrows at the top, to concentrate the aromas. Your palate should be clean too, with no lingering flavours such as toothpaste or coffee."],["La prima tappa è l'aspetto. A questo livello si osserva una sola cosa: il colore, che può essere bianco, rosato o rosso. Il colore è già un indizio su come è stato fatto il vino: un rosso ha fermentato a lungo con le bucce, un rosato solo per poche ore.","La première étape est l'aspect. À ce niveau, on observe une seule chose : la couleur, qui peut être blanche, rosée ou rouge. La couleur est déjà un indice sur la façon dont le vin a été fait : un rouge a longtemps fermenté avec les peaux, un rosé quelques heures seulement.","The first stage is appearance. At this level you look at just one thing: the colour, which can be white, rosé or red. Colour is already a clue to how the wine was made: a red fermented with its skins for a long time, a rosé for only a few hours."]],"k":[["Approccio sistematico: aspetto, naso, palato, sempre in quest'ordine.","Approche systématique : aspect, nez, bouche, toujours dans cet ordre.","Systematic approach: appearance, nose, palate, always in that order."],["Niente odori che distraggono; superficie bianca.","Pas d'odeurs gênantes ; surface blanche.","No distracting smells; a white surface."],["Bicchiere ampio che si restringe in alto; bocca pulita.","Verre large qui se resserre en haut ; bouche propre.","Wide glass narrowing at the top; a clean palate."],["Aspetto: colore bianco, rosato o rosso.","Aspect : couleur blanche, rosée ou rouge.","Appearance: colour white, rosé or red."]]},{"c":"t3","t":["Il naso: frutta, rovere e altro","Le nez : fruit, chêne et autres","The nose: fruit, oak and other"],"p":[["La seconda tappa è il naso, cioè gli aromi del vino. Si porta il bicchiere al naso e si cerca di riconoscere che cosa ricordano i profumi. All'inizio è difficile trovare le parole, ma è un'abilità che migliora con la pratica. Per orientarsi si usano tre grandi famiglie: frutta, rovere e «altro».","La deuxième étape est le nez, c'est-à-dire les arômes du vin. On porte le verre au nez et l'on essaie de reconnaître ce que rappellent les odeurs. Au début, il est difficile de trouver les mots, mais c'est une compétence qui progresse avec la pratique. Pour s'orienter, on utilise trois grandes familles : fruit, chêne et « autres ».","The second stage is the nose, meaning the wine's aromas. Bring the glass to your nose and try to recognise what the smells remind you of. Finding the words is hard at first, but it is a skill that improves with practice. To find your way, three broad families are used: fruit, oak and 'other'."],["La frutta è la famiglia più comune: quasi tutti i vini profumano di frutta. Il tipo di frutta dipende dal vitigno, per esempio il Cabernet Sauvignon ricorda il ribes nero, e dalla maturazione dell'uva. Lo Chardonnay da clima fresco dà mela e limone; da clima caldo, pesca e ananas. Ecco come il clima si ritrova direttamente nel bicchiere.","Le fruit est la famille la plus courante : presque tous les vins sentent le fruit. Le type de fruit dépend du cépage, par exemple le Cabernet Sauvignon rappelle le cassis, et de la maturité du raisin. Un Chardonnay de climat frais donne pomme et citron ; de climat chaud, pêche et ananas. Voilà comment le climat se retrouve directement dans le verre.","Fruit is the most common family: nearly all wines smell of fruit. The type of fruit depends on the grape variety, for example Cabernet Sauvignon reminds you of blackcurrant, and on how ripe the grapes were. Cool-climate Chardonnay gives apple and lemon; warm-climate Chardonnay gives peach and pineapple. This is how climate shows up directly in the glass."],["Il rovere compare quando il vino ha fermentato o maturato in botte. Porta profumi come vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro e fumo. Nella famiglia «altro» rientra tutto il resto: erba, fiori, erbe aromatiche, verdure, terra, funghi, cuoio. Questa varietà è proprio ciò che rende il vino così interessante da annusare.","Le chêne apparaît quand le vin a fermenté ou a été élevé en fût. Il apporte des arômes comme la vanille, la noix de coco, le clou de girofle, le cèdre et la fumée. Dans la famille « autres » entre tout le reste : herbe, fleurs, herbes aromatiques, légumes, terre, champignon, cuir. Cette variété est justement ce qui rend le vin si intéressant à sentir.","Oak shows up when the wine has been fermented or matured in barrels. It brings aromas such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The 'other' family covers everything else: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. This variety is exactly what makes wine so interesting to smell."]],"k":[["Naso: aromi di frutta, rovere e «altro».","Nez : arômes de fruit, de chêne et « autres ».","Nose: fruit, oak and 'other' aromas."],["La frutta dipende dal vitigno e dalla maturazione dell'uva.","Le fruit dépend du cépage et de la maturité du raisin.","Fruit depends on grape variety and ripeness."],["Rovere: vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro, fumo.","Chêne : vanille, coco, clou de girofle, cèdre, fumée.","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke."],["Altro: erba, fiori, erbe, verdure, terra, funghi, cuoio.","Autres : herbe, fleurs, herbes, légumes, terre, champignon, cuir.","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather."]]},{"c":"t3","t":["Il palato: struttura e sapori","La bouche : structure et saveurs","The palate: structure and flavours"],"p":[["La terza tappa è il palato: si assaggia un piccolo sorso e lo si fa girare in bocca. Qui si valutano cinque caratteristiche strutturali. La dolcezza dipende dallo zucchero rimasto nel vino: la maggior parte dei vini è secca. L'acidità fa salivare e dà freschezza. Il tannino, tipico dei rossi, asciuga la bocca.","La troisième étape est la bouche : on prend une petite gorgée et on la fait circuler en bouche. On y évalue cinq caractéristiques de structure. La douceur dépend du sucre resté dans le vin : la plupart des vins sont secs. L'acidité fait saliver et apporte de la fraîcheur. Le tanin, typique des rouges, assèche la bouche.","The third stage is the palate: take a small sip and move it around your mouth. Here you assess five structural characteristics. Sweetness depends on how much sugar is left in the wine, and most wines are dry. Acidity makes your mouth water and gives freshness. Tannin, typical of red wines, dries the mouth."],["Le altre due caratteristiche sono alcol e corpo. Molti vini fermi e spumanti hanno tra l'11,5% e il 14% di alcol, ma alcuni scendono fino all'8% e altri salgono fino al 15%. Il corpo è la sensazione complessiva del vino in bocca: basta chiedersi quanto «riempie» la bocca. Un vino leggero sembra delicato, uno corposo sembra denso e avvolgente.","Les deux autres caractéristiques sont l'alcool et le corps. Beaucoup de vins tranquilles et effervescents ont entre 11,5 % et 14 % d'alcool, mais certains descendent à 8 % et d'autres montent jusqu'à 15 %. Le corps est la sensation globale du vin en bouche : il suffit de se demander à quel point il « remplit » la bouche. Un vin léger semble délicat, un vin corsé paraît dense et enveloppant.","The other two characteristics are alcohol and body. Many still and sparkling wines have between 11.5% and 14% abv, though some are as low as 8% and others reach 15%. Body is the overall feel of the wine in your mouth: simply ask yourself how mouth-filling it is. A light-bodied wine feels delicate, a full-bodied one feels dense and mouth-filling."],["Infine, in bocca si cercano i sapori, con le stesse famiglie usate al naso: frutta, rovere e altro. Spesso si ritrovano gli aromi già sentiti, a volte se ne scoprono di nuovi. Un'ultima nota importante: con moderazione l'alcol non è considerato dannoso, ma in eccesso nuoce alla salute e al comportamento. Molti Paesi pubblicano linee guida ufficiali sui consumi a basso rischio.","Enfin, en bouche, on cherche les saveurs, avec les mêmes familles qu'au nez : fruit, chêne et autres. On retrouve souvent les arômes déjà sentis, et on en découvre parfois de nouveaux. Dernière remarque importante : consommé avec modération, l'alcool n'est pas considéré comme nocif, mais en excès il nuit à la santé et au comportement. De nombreux pays publient des repères officiels de consommation à faible risque.","Finally, on the palate you look for flavours, using the same families as on the nose: fruit, oak and other. You will often find the aromas you already smelled, and sometimes discover new ones. One last important note: in moderation alcohol is not regarded as harmful, but in excess it damages health and behaviour. Many countries publish official guidelines on low-risk drinking."]],"k":[["Struttura: dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol, corpo.","Structure : douceur, acidité, tanin, alcool, corps.","Structure: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body."],["Acidità = la bocca saliva; tannino = la bocca si asciuga.","Acidité = on salive ; tanin = la bouche s'assèche.","Acidity = mouth waters; tannin = mouth dries."],["Corpo = quanto il vino riempie la bocca.","Corps = à quel point le vin remplit la bouche.","Body = how mouth-filling the wine feels."],["Sapori: frutta, rovere, altro.","Saveurs : fruit, chêne, autres.","Flavours: fruit, oak, other."]]}],"flash":[{"c":"p1","f":["Buccia dell'uva nera","Peau du raisin noir","Black grape skin"],"b":["Colore intenso e tannini, che lasciano la bocca secca.","Couleur intense et tanins, qui assèchent la bouche.","Deep colour and tannins, which make the mouth feel dry."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Polpa dell'uva","Pulpe du raisin","Grape pulp"],"b":["Parte morbida con il succo: acqua, zucchero e acido. Stesso colore in tutte le uve.","Partie tendre contenant le jus : eau, sucre et acide. Même couleur dans tous les raisins.","Soft part holding the juice: water, sugar and acid. Same colour in all grapes."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Tannini","Tanins","Tannins"],"b":["Sostanze della buccia delle uve nere che asciugano la bocca.","Substances de la peau des raisins noirs qui assèchent la bouche.","Substances in black grape skins that dry out the mouth."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Ciclo annuale della vite","Cycle annuel de la vigne","The vine's yearly cycle"],"b":["Fioritura in primavera, maturazione in estate, vendemmia a fine estate.","Floraison au printemps, maturation en été, vendanges en fin d'été.","Flowering in spring, ripening in summer, picking in late summer."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Che cosa cambia quando l'uva matura?","Que change-t-il quand le raisin mûrit ?","What changes as grapes ripen?"],"b":["Più acqua e zucchero, meno acido, sapori più maturi, cambio di colore.","Plus d'eau et de sucre, moins d'acide, saveurs plus mûres, changement de couleur.","More water and sugar, less acid, riper flavours, colour change."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Clima fresco","Climat frais","Cool climate"],"b":["Vicino ai poli (Germania, nord della Francia): meno zucchero, più acidità; spesso uve bianche.","Près des pôles (Allemagne, nord de la France) : moins de sucre, plus d'acidité ; souvent raisins blancs.","Nearer the poles (Germany, northern France): less sugar, more acidity; often white grapes."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Clima caldo","Climat chaud","Warm climate"],"b":["Vicino all'Equatore (parti di Australia e California): più zucchero, meno acidità, sapori maturi; spesso uve nere.","Près de l'équateur (parties de l'Australie et de la Californie) : plus de sucre, moins d'acidité, saveurs mûres ; souvent raisins noirs.","Nearer the Equator (parts of Australia and California): more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours; often black grapes."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Chardonnay: clima fresco o caldo?","Chardonnay : climat frais ou chaud ?","Chardonnay: cool or warm climate?"],"b":["Fresco: mela e limone. Caldo: pesca e ananas.","Frais : pomme et citron. Chaud : pêche et ananas.","Cool: apple and lemon. Warm: peach and pineapple."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Fermentazione alcolica","Fermentation alcoolique","Alcoholic fermentation"],"b":["Zucchero + lieviti → alcol + anidride carbonica.","Sucre + levures → alcool + gaz carbonique.","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Lieviti","Levures","Yeast"],"b":["Organismi microscopici che mangiano lo zucchero e producono alcol e anidride carbonica.","Organismes microscopiques qui mangent le sucre et produisent alcool et gaz carbonique.","Microscopic organisms that eat sugar and make alcohol and carbon dioxide."]},{"c":"p2","f":["% vol. (abv)","% vol.","abv"],"b":["Quota di alcol nel volume del vino: 10% = un decimo è alcol.","Part d'alcool dans le volume du vin : 10 % = un dixième d'alcool.","Alcohol by volume: 10% abv = one tenth of the liquid is alcohol."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Sequenza del vino bianco","Étapes du vin blanc","White wine steps"],"b":["Pigiatura, pressatura, fermentazione, maturazione, imbottigliamento.","Foulage, pressurage, fermentation, élevage, mise en bouteille.","Crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation, bottling."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Sequenza del vino rosso","Étapes du vin rouge","Red wine steps"],"b":["Pigiatura, fermentazione con le bucce, svinatura, pressatura, maturazione, imbottigliamento.","Foulage, fermentation avec les peaux, écoulage, pressurage, élevage, mise en bouteille.","Crushing, fermentation on skins, draining, pressing, maturation, bottling."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Sequenza del vino rosato","Étapes du vin rosé","Rosé wine steps"],"b":["Pigiatura, fermentazione, svinatura dopo poche ore, maturazione, imbottigliamento.","Foulage, fermentation, écoulage après quelques heures, élevage, mise en bouteille.","Crushing, fermentation, draining after a few hours, maturation, bottling."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Bianco da uve nere?","Du blanc avec des raisins noirs ?","White wine from black grapes?"],"b":["Sì: il succo è incolore; si pressa con delicatezza prima della fermentazione.","Oui : le jus est incolore ; on presse délicatement avant la fermentation.","Yes: the juice is colourless; press gently before fermentation."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Acciaio inox o rovere","Inox ou chêne","Stainless steel or oak"],"b":["Recipienti per fermentare e maturare il vino; per i rosati il rovere è raro.","Contenants pour fermenter et élever le vin ; le chêne est rare pour les rosés.","Vessels for fermenting and maturing wine; oak is rare for rosé."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino fermo","Vin tranquille","Still wine"],"b":["Vino senza bollicine; 8–15% vol., di solito 11,5–14%.","Vin sans bulles ; 8–15 % vol., le plus souvent 11,5–14 %.","Wine without bubbles; 8–15% abv, mostly 11.5–14%."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino spumante","Vin effervescent","Sparkling wine"],"b":["Bollicine di anidride carbonica della fermentazione. Es.: Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.","Bulles de dioxyde de carbone issu de la fermentation. Ex. : Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.","Bubbles of carbon dioxide from fermentation. E.g. Champagne, Cava, Prosecco."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino fortificato","Vin fortifié","Fortified wine"],"b":["Vino con alcol aggiunto, 15–22% vol. Es.: Sherry, Port.","Vin additionné d'alcool, 15–22 % vol. Ex. : Sherry, Port.","Wine with added alcohol, 15–22% abv. E.g. Sherry, Port."]},{"c":"w1","f":["% vol. (abv)","% vol. (abv)","abv"],"b":["Percentuale di alcol nel volume: 10% = un decimo del vino è alcol.","Part d'alcool dans le volume : 10 % = un dixième du vin est de l'alcool.","Alcohol by volume: 10% means one tenth of the liquid is alcohol."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino secco","Vin sec","Dry wine"],"b":["Zucchero assente o minimo: i lieviti l'hanno trasformato tutto in alcol.","Pas ou très peu de sucre : les levures l'ont tout transformé en alcool.","No or very little sugar: the yeast turned it all into alcohol."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Acidità","Acidité","Acidity"],"b":["Viene dal succo d'uva, fa salivare, rinfresca e bilancia la dolcezza.","Vient du jus de raisin, fait saliver, rafraîchit et équilibre la douceur.","Comes from the juice, makes the mouth water, refreshes and balances sweetness."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Tannino","Tanin","Tannin"],"b":["Dalle bucce delle uve nere; asciuga la bocca. Alto: Bordeaux rosso, Chianti.","Vient de la peau des raisins noirs ; assèche la bouche. Élevé : Bordeaux rouge, Chianti.","From black grape skins; dries the mouth. High: red Bordeaux, Chianti."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Corpo","Corps","Body"],"b":["Quanto il vino riempie la bocca: leggero (Pinot Grigio), medio (Sancerre), pieno (Sauternes).","À quel point le vin remplit la bouche : léger (Pinot Grigio), moyen (Sancerre), corsé (Sauternes).","How mouth-filling a wine is: light (Pinot Grigio), medium (Sancerre), full (Sauternes)."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Aromi del rovere","Arômes du chêne","Oak aromas"],"b":["Vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro, affumicato.","Vanille, noix de coco, clou de girofle, cèdre, fumé.","Vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino rosato","Vin rosé","Rosé wine"],"b":["Uve nere, poche ore di contatto con le bucce, poi fermentazione senza bucce.","Raisins noirs, quelques heures avec les peaux, puis fermentation sans elles.","Black grapes, a few hours on the skins, then fermented without them."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Chardonnay di clima fresco","Chardonnay de climat frais","Cool-climate Chardonnay"],"b":["Acidità alta, corpo leggero-medio, mela verde e limone (es. Chablis).","Acidité élevée, corps léger à moyen, pomme verte et citron (ex. Chablis).","High acidity, light to medium body, green apple and lemon (e.g. Chablis)."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Chardonnay di clima caldo","Chardonnay de climat chaud","Warm-climate Chardonnay"],"b":["Acidità media, corpo medio-pieno, pesca, ananas, banana; spesso vaniglia dal rovere.","Acidité moyenne, corps moyen à ample, pêche, ananas, banane ; souvent vanille du chêne.","Medium acidity, medium to full body, peach, pineapple, banana; often vanilla from oak."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Burgundy bianco: quale vitigno?","Bourgogne blanc : quel cépage ?","White Burgundy: which grape?"],"b":["Chardonnay; corpo medio, acidità alta, limone e pesca, a volte vaniglia.","Chardonnay ; corps moyen, acidité élevée, citron et pêche, parfois vanille.","Chardonnay; medium body, high acidity, lemon and peach, sometimes vanilla."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc"],"b":["Secco, profumi intensi, acidità alta; frutta da mela a pompelmo a frutto della passione.","Sec, arômes intenses, acidité élevée ; fruit de la pomme au pamplemousse et au fruit de la passion.","Dry, pronounced aromas, high acidity; fruit from apple to grapefruit to passion fruit."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Note erbacee del Sauvignon Blanc","Notes herbacées du Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc herbaceous notes"],"b":["Asparago, peperone verde, erba tagliata.","Asperge, poivron vert, herbe coupée.","Asparagus, green bell pepper, cut grass."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Vini chiave di Sauvignon Blanc","Vins clés de Sauvignon Blanc","Key Sauvignon Blanc wines"],"b":["Sauvignon Blanc della Nuova Zelanda e Sancerre (Loira, Francia).","Sauvignon Blanc de Nouvelle-Zélande et Sancerre (Loire, France).","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre (Loire, France)."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],"b":["Di solito secco, leggero, acidità media-alta, pera e limone; soprattutto Italia.","En général sec, léger, acidité moyenne à élevée, poire et citron ; surtout l'Italie.","Usually dry, light, medium to high acidity, pear and lemon; mainly Italy."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Riesling","Riesling","Riesling"],"b":["Da secco a dolce, sempre acidità alta; fiori, lime, limone, pesca, albicocca.","Du sec au doux, toujours acidité élevée ; fleurs, citron vert, citron, pêche, abricot.","Dry to sweet, always high acidity; floral, lime, lemon, peach, apricot."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Riesling: dove e in che stile?","Riesling : où et dans quel style ?","Riesling: where and in what style?"],"b":["Germania: dal secco al dolce. Alsazia e Australia: secco.","Allemagne : du sec au doux. Alsace et Australie : sec.","Germany: dry to sweet. Alsace and Australia: dry."]},{"c":"w2","f":["Bianchi aromatici senza rovere","Blancs aromatiques sans chêne","Aromatic whites without oak"],"b":["Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio e Riesling: di solito acciaio inox, per conservare la frutta.","Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio et Riesling : en général cuve inox, pour garder le fruit.","Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling: usually stainless steel, to keep the fruit."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon"],"b":["Secco, tannino e acidità alti, corpo medio-pieno; ribes nero, peperone verde, menta.","Sec, tanins et acidité élevés, corps moyen à ample ; cassis, poivron vert, menthe.","Dry, high tannin and acidity, medium to full body; blackcurrant, green pepper, mint."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Cabernet Sauvignon + rovere","Cabernet Sauvignon + chêne","Cabernet Sauvignon + oak"],"b":["Note di cedro e vaniglia.","Notes de cèdre et de vanille.","Cedar and vanilla notes."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Merlot","Merlot","Merlot"],"b":["Secco, corpo medio-pieno, acidità e tannino medi; frutti rossi e neri, vaniglia dal rovere.","Sec, corps moyen à ample, acidité et tanins moyens ; fruits rouges et noirs, vanille du chêne.","Dry, medium to full body, medium acidity and tannin; red and black fruit, vanilla from oak."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Taglio di Bordeaux","Assemblage bordelais","Bordeaux blend"],"b":["Cabernet Sauvignon (tannino, acidità) + Merlot (morbidezza, corpo).","Cabernet Sauvignon (tanins, acidité) + Merlot (souplesse, corps).","Cabernet Sauvignon (tannin, acidity) + Merlot (softness, body)."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir"],"b":["Secco, leggero-medio, acidità alta, tannino basso-medio; fragola, ciliegia rossa, lampone.","Sec, léger à moyen, acidité élevée, tanins faibles à moyens ; fraise, cerise rouge, framboise.","Dry, light to medium, high acidity, low to medium tannin; strawberry, red cherry, raspberry."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Dove si trova il Pinot Noir?","Où trouve-t-on le Pinot Noir ?","Where is Pinot Noir key?"],"b":["Burgundy rosso, Nuova Zelanda (uva nera principale) e Champagne con lo Chardonnay.","Bourgogne rouge, Nouvelle-Zélande (premier cépage noir) et Champagne avec le Chardonnay.","Red Burgundy, New Zealand (main black grape) and Champagne with Chardonnay."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Syrah o Shiraz?","Syrah ou Shiraz ?","Syrah or Shiraz?"],"b":["Stesso vitigno: Syrah in Francia, Shiraz in Australia.","Même cépage : Syrah en France, Shiraz en Australie.","Same grape: Syrah in France, Shiraz in Australia."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Syrah/Shiraz: aromi","Syrah/Shiraz : arômes","Syrah/Shiraz: aromas"],"b":["Mora, ciliegia nera, pepe nero, liquirizia; rovere: vaniglia, cocco.","Mûre, cerise noire, poivre noir, réglisse ; chêne : vanille, noix de coco.","Blackberry, black cherry, black pepper, liquorice; oak: vanilla, coconut."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Rodano settentrionale vs Australia calda","Nord du Rhône vs Australie chaude","Northern Rhône vs warm Australia"],"b":["Rodano: corpo medio, mora fresca, pepe nero. Australia: corpo pieno, ciliegia nera in confettura, liquirizia.","Rhône : corps moyen, mûre fraîche, poivre noir. Australie : corsé, cerise noire confiturée, réglisse.","Rhône: medium body, fresh blackberry, black pepper. Australia: full, jammy black cherry, liquorice."]},{"c":"w3","f":["Dove si coltiva molto il Cabernet Sauvignon?","Où le Cabernet Sauvignon est-il très cultivé ?","Where is Cabernet Sauvignon widely grown?"],"b":["Bordeaux, California, Australia, Cile, Sudafrica.","Bordeaux, Californie, Australie, Chili, Afrique du Sud.","Bordeaux, California, Australia, Chile, South Africa."]},{"c":"t1","f":["3 regole per conservare il vino","3 règles pour conserver le vin","3 storage rules"],"b":["Fresco e costante; lontano dalla luce; tappo di sughero = bottiglia coricata.","Frais et constant ; à l'abri de la lumière ; liège = bouteille couchée.","Cool and constant; away from light; cork = bottle on its side."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Perché coricare le bottiglie col sughero?","Pourquoi coucher les bouteilles bouchées au liège ?","Why lay corked bottles down?"],"b":["Il sughero resta umido; se si secca entra aria e il vino perde il frutto.","Le liège reste humide ; s'il sèche, l'air entre et le vin perd son fruit.","The cork stays moist; a dry cork lets air in and the wine loses fruit."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Sistema sottovuoto","Système sous vide","Vacuum system"],"b":["Una pompa toglie l'aria dalla bottiglia aperta.","Une pompe retire l'air de la bouteille ouverte.","A pump removes air from the opened bottle."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Sistema a coperta di gas","Système à couverture de gaz","Blanket system"],"b":["Un gas innocuo spinge fuori l'aria dalla bottiglia.","Un gaz inoffensif chasse l'air de la bouteille.","A harmless gas is pumped in to push the air out."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Sauternes e Champagne","Sauternes et Champagne","Sauternes and Champagne"],"b":["Molto freschi: 6–8 °C (dolce) e 6–10 °C (spumante).","Bien frais : 6–8 °C (doux) et 6–10 °C (effervescent).","Well chilled: 6–8°C (sweet) and 6–10°C (sparkling)."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Pinot Grigio e Chardonnay in rovere","Pinot Grigio et Chardonnay boisé","Pinot Grigio and oaked Chardonnay"],"b":["Freschi 7–10 °C (bianco leggero); appena freschi 10–13 °C (bianco corposo).","Frais 7–10 °C (blanc léger) ; légèrement frais 10–13 °C (blanc corsé).","Chilled 7–10°C (light white); lightly chilled 10–13°C (full white)."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Beaujolais e Shiraz","Beaujolais et Shiraz","Beaujolais and Shiraz"],"b":["Appena fresco, 13 °C (rosso leggero); ambiente 15–18 °C (rosso corposo).","Légèrement frais, 13 °C (rouge léger) ; ambiante 15–18 °C (rouge corsé).","Lightly chilled 13°C (light red); room temperature 15–18°C (full red)."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Aprire uno spumante","Ouvrir un effervescent","Opening sparkling wine"],"b":["Mano sempre sul tappo dopo la gabbietta; bottiglia inclinata; si gira la bottiglia.","Main toujours sur le bouchon après le muselet ; bouteille inclinée ; on tourne la bouteille.","Hand on the cork once the cage is loose; bottle tilted; turn the bottle."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Regola n. 1 dell'abbinamento","Règle n° 1 de l'accord","Pairing rule no. 1"],"b":["Partire dai gusti della persona: non si consiglia uno stile che non le piace.","Partir des goûts de la personne : on ne conseille pas un style qu'elle n'aime pas.","Start with the person's taste: never push a style they dislike."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Cibo dolce","Plat sucré","Sweet food"],"b":["Vino più secco, amaro e acido; meno dolce e fruttato.","Vin plus asséchant, amer et acide ; moins doux et fruité.","Wine more drying, bitter and acidic; less sweet and fruity."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Umami","Umami","Umami"],"b":["Stesso effetto del dolce: vino più amaro e acido, meno fruttato.","Même effet que le sucré : vin plus amer et acide, moins fruité.","Same as sweetness: wine more bitter and acidic, less fruity."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Cibo salato","Plat salé","Salty food"],"b":["Vino meno amaro e acido; più fruttato e corposo.","Vin moins amer et acide ; plus fruité et corsé.","Wine less bitter and acidic; fruitier and fuller."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Cibo acido","Plat acide","Acidic food"],"b":["Vino meno amaro e acido; più dolce e fruttato.","Vin moins amer et acide ; plus doux et fruité.","Wine less bitter and acidic; sweeter and fruitier."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Sapori molto intensi","Saveurs très intenses","Highly flavoured food"],"b":["Possono sovrastare il vino.","Peuvent écraser le vin.","Can overwhelm the wine."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Cibo grasso o oleoso","Plat gras ou huileux","Fatty or oily food"],"b":["Fa sembrare il vino meno acido.","Fait paraître le vin moins acide.","Makes the wine seem less acidic."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Peperoncino","Piment","Chilli heat"],"b":["L'alcol aumenta il bruciore; l'alcol del vino risalta di più.","L'alcool augmente la brûlure ; l'alcool du vin ressort davantage.","Alcohol increases the burn; the wine's alcohol stands out more."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Approccio sistematico alla degustazione","Approche systématique de la dégustation","Systematic approach to tasting"],"b":["Aspetto (colore) → naso (aromi) → palato (struttura e sapori).","Aspect (couleur) → nez (arômes) → bouche (structure et saveurs).","Appearance (colour) → nose (aromas) → palate (structure and flavours)."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Prepararsi a degustare","Se préparer à déguster","Preparing to taste"],"b":["Niente odori, superficie bianca, bicchiere ampio che si stringe in alto, bocca pulita.","Pas d'odeurs, surface blanche, verre large resserré en haut, bouche propre.","No smells, white surface, wide glass narrowing at the top, clean palate."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Aromi del rovere","Arômes du chêne","Oak aromas"],"b":["Vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro, fumo.","Vanille, coco, clou de girofle, cèdre, fumée.","Vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Aromi «altro»","Arômes « autres »","'Other' aromas"],"b":["Erba, fiori, erbe, verdure, terra, funghi, cuoio.","Herbe, fleurs, herbes, légumes, terre, champignon, cuir.","Grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Struttura al palato","Structure en bouche","Structure on the palate"],"b":["Dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol, corpo.","Douceur, acidité, tanin, alcool, corps.","Sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Corpo","Corps","Body"],"b":["Quanto il vino riempie la bocca: leggero = delicato, corposo = denso.","À quel point le vin remplit la bouche : léger = délicat, corsé = dense.","How mouth-filling the wine is: light = delicate, full = dense."]}]};
window.TWG_ESX={"es":{"Inside a grape":"Cómo es una uva por dentro","Wine starts from a simple idea: crush grapes to free their sweet juice, then let that juice ferment. That is why wine can be described as fermented grape juice. To understand what ends up in the glass, it helps to start with the grape itself, which has two main parts: the skin on the outside and the pulp on the inside. Each one gives something different to the wine.":"El vino parte de una idea sencilla: se estrujan las uvas para liberar su zumo dulce y después se deja fermentar. Por eso el vino se puede definir como zumo de uva fermentado. Para entender lo que acabará en la copa, conviene empezar por la uva, que tiene dos partes principales: la piel por fuera y la pulpa por dentro. Cada una aporta algo distinto al vino.","There are two broad families of grapes: white and black. Cut in half, they look very much alike, because the real difference lies mainly in the skin. Black grapes have deeply coloured skins that also hold tannins, substances that leave your mouth feeling dry. White grapes, once ripe, have skins with a golden colour.":"Hay dos grandes familias de uvas: blancas y tintas. Cortadas por la mitad se parecen mucho, porque la diferencia está sobre todo en la piel. Las uvas tintas tienen una piel de color intenso que además contiene taninos, unas sustancias que dejan la boca con sensación de sequedad. Las uvas blancas, cuando están maduras, tienen la piel de color dorado.","The pulp is the soft, fleshy part of the grape and it holds the juice. That juice is made up mostly of water, sugar and acid. One important detail: the pulp has the same colour whether the grape is white or black. So the colour of a red wine does not come from the juice but from the skins, a key idea for understanding later how the different wines are made.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda y carnosa de la uva y es la que contiene el zumo. Ese zumo está formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Un detalle importante: la pulpa tiene el mismo color tanto en las uvas blancas como en las tintas. Por eso el color de un vino tinto no viene del zumo sino de las pieles, una idea clave para entender después cómo se elaboran los distintos vinos.","Wine is fermented grape juice.":"El vino es zumo de uva fermentado.","Black grape skins: deep colour and tannins.":"Piel de las uvas tintas: color intenso y taninos.","Tannins make the mouth feel dry.":"Los taninos dejan la boca seca.","Pulp: juice made of water, sugar and acid.":"Pulpa: zumo de agua, azúcar y ácido.","Pulp is the same colour in white and black grapes.":"La pulpa tiene el mismo color en uvas blancas y tintas.","The vine's year":"El año de la vid","Grapes are the fruit of the grape vine, a plant that can live for several decades. After planting, a vine needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year. Its cycle follows the seasons: it flowers in spring, the fruit ripens through the summer and the grapes are picked towards the end of summer.":"La uva es el fruto de la vid, una planta que puede vivir varias décadas. Tras plantarla, la vid necesita un par de años para llegar a la madurez; a partir de entonces da una cosecha cada año. Su ciclo sigue las estaciones: florece en primavera, el fruto madura durante el verano y la vendimia llega hacia el final del verano.","In spring the vine produces clusters of tiny flowers. Each single flower is set to become one grape. Right after flowering, the young grapes are small, hard and green, whether they will end up white or black: at this stage you cannot yet tell them apart, and they are far from ready to make wine.":"En primavera la vid produce racimos de flores diminutas. Cada flor está destinada a convertirse en una uva. Justo después de la floración, las uvas recién formadas son pequeñas, duras y verdes, tanto si serán blancas como tintas: en esta fase todavía no se distinguen y están lejos de servir para hacer vino.","To grow well and give good quality fruit, a vine needs the right amount of sunlight and heat: if it is too cold or too hot, it cannot manage. Vines also do best where the winter is cold enough to let them rest. That is why most vineyards lie in two bands around the globe, roughly between 30° and 50° of latitude, north and south of the Equator.":"Para crecer bien y dar uva de calidad, la vid necesita la cantidad justa de sol y de calor: si hace demasiado frío o demasiado calor, no lo consigue. Además, prefiere zonas donde el invierno sea lo bastante frío para que pueda descansar. Por eso la mayoría de los viñedos están en dos franjas del planeta, más o menos entre los 30° y los 50° de latitud, al norte y al sur del ecuador.","A mature vine gives a crop every year and can live for decades.":"Una vid adulta da una cosecha al año y puede vivir décadas.","Spring: flowering; each flower becomes a grape.":"Primavera: floración; cada flor se convierte en una uva.","Summer: ripening; late summer: harvest.":"Verano: maduración; final del verano: vendimia.","Vines need the right sun and heat, plus a cold winter to rest.":"La vid necesita sol y calor justos y un invierno frío para descansar.","What happens as grapes ripen":"Qué ocurre cuando la uva madura","Over the summer the small, hard grapes change a great deal. They swell as they fill with water, while their sugar content goes up and their acid content goes down. Their flavours also develop and become riper. An unripe grape is therefore sour and not very tasty, whereas a ripe grape is bigger, sweeter and less acidic.":"Durante el verano, las uvas pequeñas y duras cambian mucho. Se hinchan al llenarse de agua y, al mismo tiempo, su contenido de azúcar sube y el de ácido baja. Los sabores también evolucionan y se vuelven más maduros. Una uva verde es, por tanto, agria y poco sabrosa, mientras que una uva madura es más grande, más dulce y menos ácida.","Ripening also changes the colour of the skin. White grapes turn from green to golden, while black grapes turn from green to purple. Colour is therefore a first clue to how close the grapes are to harvest, alongside the other changes: more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours.":"Con la maduración también cambia el color de la piel. Las uvas blancas pasan del verde a un tono dorado, y las uvas tintas pasan del verde al morado. El color es, por tanto, una primera pista de lo cerca que está la vendimia, junto con los demás cambios: más agua, más azúcar, menos ácido y sabores más maduros.","These changes matter because they pass straight into the wine. The sugar in the grape is what yeast will turn into alcohol, so more sugar generally means a stronger wine. The acid stays in the wine and gives it freshness. The grape's flavours become the fruit aromas in the glass. The moment of picking therefore already shapes the style of the wine.":"Estos cambios importan porque pasan directamente al vino. El azúcar de la uva es lo que las levaduras convertirán en alcohol, así que más azúcar suele significar un vino con más alcohol. El ácido se queda en el vino y le da frescura. Los sabores de la uva se convierten en los aromas de fruta de la copa. El momento de la vendimia ya orienta, por tanto, el estilo del vino.","Ripening grapes swell with water.":"Al madurar, la uva se hincha de agua.","Sugar rises, acid falls.":"El azúcar sube y el ácido baja.","Flavours become riper.":"Los sabores se vuelven más maduros.","White grapes: green to golden; black grapes: green to purple.":"Uvas blancas: de verde a dorado; tintas: de verde a morado.","Cool climate and warm climate":"Clima fresco y clima cálido","Wine regions closer to the poles have a cool climate. Germany and northern France are typical examples. Average temperatures are low and the sunshine can be weaker than nearer the Equator; in some years the grapes even struggle to ripen. In cool climates, growing white grapes is common.":"Las regiones vitícolas más cercanas a los polos tienen un clima fresco. Alemania y el norte de Francia son ejemplos típicos. Allí las temperaturas medias son bajas y el sol puede ser más débil que cerca del ecuador; algunos años a la uva incluso le cuesta madurar. En los climas frescos es habitual cultivar uvas blancas.","Regions closer to the Equator have a warm climate instead, such as parts of Australia and parts of California. Average temperatures are high, the sunshine is more intense and the grapes ripen reliably year after year. In warm climates it is common to grow black grapes, which make the most of all that heat.":"Las regiones más cercanas al ecuador tienen, en cambio, un clima cálido, como algunas partes de Australia y de California. Las temperaturas medias son altas, el sol es más intenso y la uva madura sin problemas año tras año. En los climas cálidos es habitual cultivar uvas tintas, que aprovechan todo ese calor.","Climate leaves a clear mark on the grapes. As a rule, the cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, together with riper flavours. This leads to different styles: a cool-climate wine tends to be lighter and fresher, a warm-climate wine richer and riper.":"El clima deja una huella clara en la uva. Por regla general, cuanto más fresco, menos azúcar y más acidez tienen las uvas; cuanto más calor, más azúcar y menos acidez, con sabores más maduros. De ahí salen estilos distintos: un vino de clima fresco tiende a ser más ligero y vivo, y uno de clima cálido, más rico y maduro.","Chardonnay is a good example. Grown in a cool climate, it gives wines with aromas of green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. Grown in a warm climate, the same grape shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple instead. Same grape, very different style: the climate makes the difference.":"La Chardonnay es un buen ejemplo. Cultivada en clima fresco, da vinos con aromas de fruta verde, como la manzana, y de cítricos, como el limón. Cultivada en clima cálido, la misma uva ofrece en cambio fruta de hueso, como el melocotón, y fruta tropical, como la piña. Misma uva, estilo muy distinto: el clima marca la diferencia.","Cool climate: nearer the poles (e.g. Germany, northern France).":"Clima fresco: cerca de los polos (p. ej. Alemania, norte de Francia).","Warm climate: nearer the Equator (e.g. parts of Australia and California).":"Clima cálido: cerca del ecuador (p. ej. partes de Australia y California).","Cooler → less sugar, more acidity → lighter, fresher wine.":"Más fresco → menos azúcar, más acidez → vino más ligero y fresco.","Warmer → more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours.":"Más cálido → más azúcar, menos acidez, sabores más maduros.","Cool: often white grapes; warm: often black grapes.":"Fresco: a menudo uvas blancas; cálido: a menudo uvas tintas.","Alcoholic fermentation":"La fermentación alcohólica","The step that turns grape juice into wine is called alcoholic fermentation. The workers behind it are yeast, organisms so tiny you cannot see them with the naked eye. Yeast feed on the sugar in the juice and turn it into two products: alcohol and carbon dioxide, which is a gas. In short: sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide.":"El paso que convierte el zumo de uva en vino se llama fermentación alcohólica. Sus protagonistas son las levaduras, organismos tan pequeños que no se ven a simple vista. Las levaduras se alimentan del azúcar del zumo y lo transforman en dos productos: alcohol y dióxido de carbono, que es un gas. En resumen: azúcar + levadura → alcohol + dióxido de carbono.","In most cases fermentation carries on until the yeast have used up all the sugar, which gives a dry wine. The alcohol stays in the newly made wine, while the carbon dioxide usually escapes into the air. There are exceptions, such as sweet wines and sparkling wines, which you will meet when looking at the types and styles of wine.":"En la mayoría de los casos la fermentación continúa hasta que las levaduras se han comido todo el azúcar, y el resultado es un vino seco. El alcohol se queda en el vino recién hecho, mientras que el dióxido de carbono suele escaparse al aire. Hay excepciones, como los vinos dulces o los espumosos, que verás al estudiar los tipos y estilos de vino.","The amount of alcohol in a wine is usually given as alcohol by volume, shortened to abv. A wine at 10% abv means that one tenth of the liquid is alcohol. Remember the link with the vineyard: it is the sugar the grapes built up while ripening that the yeast turn into alcohol.":"La cantidad de alcohol de un vino se suele indicar como porcentaje del volumen, abreviado % vol. Un vino de 10 % vol. significa que una décima parte del líquido es alcohol. Recuerda el vínculo con el viñedo: es el azúcar que la uva acumuló al madurar lo que las levaduras convierten en alcohol.","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide.":"Azúcar + levadura → alcohol + dióxido de carbono.","Yeast are microscopic organisms that eat sugar.":"Las levaduras son organismos microscópicos que comen azúcar.","Usually the yeast eat all the sugar: a dry wine.":"Normalmente las levaduras se comen todo el azúcar: vino seco.","Alcohol stays in the wine; carbon dioxide usually escapes.":"El alcohol se queda; el dióxido de carbono suele escaparse.","10% abv = one tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"10 % vol. = una décima parte del líquido es alcohol.","How white wine is made":"Cómo se hace un vino blanco","White wine is usually made from white grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed, which releases some of the juice. Straight afterwards the crushed grapes are pressed, squeezing the skins to collect the rest of the juice. The key idea is that, for white wine, the juice is separated from the skins before fermentation begins.":"El vino blanco se suele hacer con uvas blancas. Tras la vendimia, la uva se estruja para liberar parte del zumo. Justo después, la uva estrujada pasa al prensado, que aprieta las pieles y recupera el zumo restante. La idea clave es que, en el blanco, el zumo se separa de las pieles antes de que empiece la fermentación.","Yeast are then added to the juice and fermentation starts. It can take place in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Once fermentation is over comes maturation, when the wine rests, again either in stainless steel or in oak. The final step is bottling, after which the wine is ready to reach the table.":"A continuación se añaden levaduras al zumo y empieza la fermentación. Puede hacerse en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble. Cuando termina la fermentación llega la crianza, en la que el vino reposa, de nuevo en acero o en roble. La última etapa es el embotellado, tras el cual el vino está listo para llegar a la mesa.","A useful point for the exam: white wine can also be made from black grapes. The colour of black grapes is all in the skin, and their juice is colourless. If black grapes are pressed gently before fermentation and the skins are removed straight away, the juice obtained is suitable for making a white wine.":"Un dato útil para el examen: también se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas. El color de las uvas tintas está todo en la piel y su zumo es incoloro. Si la uva tinta se prensa con suavidad antes de la fermentación y las pieles se retiran enseguida, se obtiene un zumo adecuado para elaborar un vino blanco.","White: crushing → pressing → fermentation → maturation → bottling.":"Blanco: estrujado → prensado → fermentación → crianza → embotellado.","For white wine, pressing comes before fermentation.":"En el blanco, el prensado va antes de la fermentación.","Fermentation and maturation: stainless steel or oak.":"Fermentación y crianza: en acero inoxidable o en roble.","Black grape juice is colourless, so it can make white wine.":"El zumo de uva tinta es incoloro: puede dar vino blanco.","How red wine is made":"Cómo se hace un vino tinto","Red wine is always made from black grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed and, unlike white wine, the juice is not separated: juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This is the big difference from white winemaking, because it is the skins that will provide the colour and the tannins.":"El vino tinto se hace siempre con uvas tintas. Tras la vendimia la uva se estruja y, a diferencia del blanco, el zumo no se separa: zumo y pieles van juntos al recipiente de fermentación. Esta es la gran diferencia con el vino blanco, porque son precisamente las pieles las que darán el color y los taninos.","Yeast are added and fermentation begins. During this stage the juice and skins are mixed thoroughly so that colour and tannin are drawn out of the skins. The more thorough the contact, the more colour and structure the wine gains. When fermentation has finished, the new red wine is drained off the skins.":"Se añaden levaduras y empieza la fermentación. Durante esta fase, el zumo y las pieles se mezclan a fondo para extraer de las pieles el color y los taninos. Cuanto más intenso es el contacto, más color y estructura gana el vino. Cuando termina la fermentación, el vino nuevo se escurre, es decir, se separa de las pieles.","The leftover skins still hold some wine, so they are pressed to release it: for red wine pressing comes after fermentation, whereas for white it comes before. Next is maturation, in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels, and finally bottling. The sequence to remember: crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing, maturation, bottling.":"Las pieles que quedan todavía retienen vino, así que se prensan para recuperarlo: en el tinto el prensado llega después de la fermentación, mientras que en el blanco va antes. Siguen la crianza, en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble, y por último el embotellado. Secuencia que hay que recordar: estrujado, fermentación, escurrido, prensado, crianza y embotellado.","Red wine: black grapes fermented with their skins.":"El tinto: uvas tintas fermentadas con sus pieles.","Mixing juice and skins extracts colour and tannin.":"Mezclar zumo y pieles extrae color y taninos.","After fermentation: draining, then pressing the skins.":"Tras la fermentación: escurrido y luego prensado de las pieles.","Red: crushing → fermentation → draining → pressing → maturation → bottling.":"Tinto: estrujado → fermentación → escurrido → prensado → crianza → embotellado.","How rosé wine is made":"Cómo se hace un vino rosado","Rosé is also made from black grapes, and at first the method is the same as for red: the grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the vessel together, yeast are added and fermentation starts. Colour begins to move from the skins into the juice, but rosé stands out for one clear choice: the contact is kept very short.":"El rosado también se hace con uvas tintas y, al principio, el método es el mismo que el del tinto: la uva se estruja, zumo y pieles van juntos al depósito, se añaden levaduras y empieza la fermentación. El color empieza a pasar de las pieles al zumo, pero el rosado se distingue por una decisión clara: el contacto dura muy poco.","After only a few hours the juice is drained off the skins. At that point it has picked up just a pink colour, and without the skins it cannot get any darker. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. It is the time spent in contact with the skins, a few hours rather than the whole fermentation, that explains why rosé is pink rather than red.":"Tras solo unas horas, el zumo se separa de las pieles. En ese momento solo ha tomado un color rosa y, sin las pieles, ya no puede oscurecerse más. La fermentación termina entonces sin las pieles. Es el tiempo de contacto con las pieles, unas horas en lugar de toda la fermentación, lo que explica por qué el rosado es rosa y no tinto.","After fermentation the rosé moves on to maturation, which can take place in stainless steel or oak, although oak is rarely used for rosé wines. Then it is bottled. Compared with red wine there is no pressing of the skins after fermentation, because the skins were removed early on. Sequence: crushing, fermentation, draining, maturation, bottling.":"Tras la fermentación, el rosado pasa a la crianza, que puede hacerse en acero inoxidable o en roble, aunque en los rosados el roble se usa poco. Después se embotella. Frente al tinto, no hay prensado de las pieles tras la fermentación, porque las pieles ya se retiraron al principio. Secuencia: estrujado, fermentación, escurrido, crianza y embotellado.","Rosé is made from black grapes.":"El rosado se hace con uvas tintas.","Only a few hours on the skins: the juice turns just pink.":"Unas horas con las pieles: el zumo solo se vuelve rosa.","Fermentation finishes without the skins.":"La fermentación termina sin las pieles.","Rosé is rarely matured in oak.":"El rosado rara vez se cría en roble.","Rosé: crushing → fermentation → draining → maturation → bottling.":"Rosado: estrujado → fermentación → escurrido → crianza → embotellado.","Storing wine":"Conservar el vino","A wine that is stored badly loses quality. At first it may simply lose some of its character; over time it can end up developing real faults. Three simple rules are enough to prevent this, covering temperature, light and the position of the bottle. They apply at home just as much as in a restaurant or a wine shop.":"Un vino mal conservado pierde calidad. Al principio puede simplemente perder parte de su carácter; con el tiempo puede llegar a desarrollar defectos de verdad. Para evitarlo bastan tres reglas sencillas, que tienen que ver con la temperatura, la luz y la posición de la botella. Sirven tanto en casa como en un restaurante o una tienda de vinos.","Rule one: for long-term storage, keep wine somewhere cool at a steady temperature. Extreme cold or heat, as well as big swings in temperature, can damage it. Rule two: keep bottles away from strong sunshine and bright artificial light. Light, and the heat that comes with it, can make a wine lose its fruity character.":"Primera regla: para guardarlo mucho tiempo, el vino debe estar en un lugar fresco y a temperatura constante. Tanto el frío o el calor extremos como los cambios bruscos de temperatura pueden estropearlo. Segunda regla: mantener las botellas lejos del sol fuerte y de la luz artificial intensa. La luz, y el calor que genera, pueden hacer que el vino pierda su carácter afrutado.","Rule three: bottles closed with a cork should be stored on their side. This keeps the cork in contact with the wine so that it stays moist. If the cork dries out, it can let air into the bottle and the wine loses its fruitiness. Bottles with a screwcap do not have this problem and can be stored standing up.":"Tercera regla: las botellas cerradas con corcho se guardan tumbadas. Así el corcho sigue en contacto con el vino y se mantiene húmedo. Si el corcho se seca, puede dejar entrar aire en la botella y el vino pierde su fruta. Las botellas con tapón de rosca no tienen este problema y pueden guardarse de pie.","Poor storage makes wine lose character and can cause faults.":"Guardar mal el vino le hace perder carácter y puede causar defectos.","Cool, constant temperature; no extremes or big swings.":"Temperatura fresca y constante; sin extremos ni cambios bruscos.","Away from sunshine and bright artificial light.":"Lejos del sol y de la luz artificial intensa.","Cork: store on its side. Screwcap: can stand up.":"Corcho: botella tumbada. Tapón de rosca: puede ir de pie.","Keeping opened wine fresh":"Conservar un vino abierto","Once a bottle is opened, the wine comes into contact with air and slowly starts to lose its freshness, eventually tasting stale. The first fix is simple: put the cork back in and keep the bottle in the fridge. The cold slows things down and helps the wine stay fresh for longer.":"Una vez abierta la botella, el vino entra en contacto con el aire y empieza poco a poco a perder frescura, hasta saber rancio. El primer remedio es sencillo: volver a poner el tapón y guardar la botella en el frigorífico. El frío frena el proceso y ayuda a que el vino se mantenga fresco más tiempo.","To keep a wine going for even longer, there are systems designed to keep it away from air. Vacuum systems use a small pump to draw the air out of the bottle. Blanket systems pump a gas into the bottle that pushes the air out and sits over the wine without harming it. Both share the same goal: limiting contact with air.":"Para alargar todavía más la vida del vino existen sistemas pensados para mantenerlo lejos del aire. Los sistemas de vacío usan una pequeña bomba que saca el aire de la botella. Los sistemas de «manta» de gas introducen en la botella un gas que empuja el aire hacia fuera y queda sobre el vino sin dañarlo. Los dos persiguen lo mismo: limitar el contacto con el aire.","The reasoning to remember is always the same: air is the enemy of opened wine, and it is also air that spoils wine when a cork dries out in storage. The fridge, a vacuum pump and an inert gas are three different ways to slow this down so that the wine is still enjoyable the next day.":"El razonamiento que hay que recordar es siempre el mismo: el aire es el enemigo del vino abierto, y también es el aire lo que estropea el vino cuando un corcho se seca en la bodega. El frigorífico, el vacío y el gas inerte son tres maneras distintas de frenar este proceso y servir al día siguiente un vino todavía agradable.","Opened wine goes stale as it reacts with air.":"El vino abierto se enrancia en contacto con el aire.","Cork back in and fridge keep it fresher for longer.":"Tapón y frigorífico lo mantienen fresco más tiempo.","Vacuum system: a pump removes the air.":"Vacío: una bomba saca el aire.","Blanket system: a harmless gas pushes the air out.":"Manta de gas: un gas inocuo expulsa el aire.","Service temperatures":"Las temperaturas de servicio","Temperature makes a big difference to how we experience a wine. In general, whites, rosés and sparkling wines are served chilled, while reds are served at room temperature or lightly chilled. These are guidelines, not laws: if a guest prefers a wine at a different temperature, the host should respect that preference.":"La temperatura cambia mucho la forma en que percibimos un vino. En general, blancos, rosados y espumosos se sirven fríos, mientras que los tintos se sirven a temperatura ambiente o ligeramente frescos. Son orientaciones, no leyes: si alguien prefiere un vino a otra temperatura, quien sirve debe respetar sus gustos.","The coldest wines are sweet wines such as Sauternes, served well chilled at 6–8°C (43–45°F), and sparkling wines such as Champagne, well chilled at 6–10°C (43–50°F). Light- and medium-bodied whites and rosés, such as Pinot Grigio, are served chilled at 7–10°C (45–50°F). Full-bodied whites, such as an oaked Chardonnay, are served lightly chilled at 10–13°C (50–55°F).":"Los vinos más fríos son los dulces, como el Sauternes, muy fríos a 6–8 °C, y los espumosos, como el Champagne, muy fríos a 6–10 °C. Los blancos ligeros o de cuerpo medio y los rosados, por ejemplo un Pinot Grigio, se sirven fríos a 7–10 °C. Los blancos con cuerpo, como una Chardonnay criada en roble, se sirven ligeramente frescos, a 10–13 °C.","Among reds, light ones such as Beaujolais are served lightly chilled, at around 13°C (55°F). Medium- and full-bodied reds, such as Shiraz, are served at room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F). Because central heating and air conditioning make 'room temperature' very variable, the range of degrees is a better guide than the room itself.":"Entre los tintos, los ligeros como el Beaujolais se sirven ligeramente frescos, alrededor de 13 °C. Los tintos de cuerpo medio o con cuerpo, como un Shiraz, se sirven a temperatura ambiente, entre 15 y 18 °C. Como la calefacción y el aire acondicionado hacen que la «temperatura ambiente» varíe mucho, es mejor fiarse del intervalo de grados que de la habitación.","To keep wine cool until the bottle is finished, you can use an insulated container or an ice bucket. If you use a bucket, fill it with ice and cold water: ice alone cools far less efficiently. On the other hand, a red that is too cold should never be warmed next to a radiator, because heat damages its flavours; instead, leave it in the room where it will be served and let it warm up naturally.":"Para mantener el vino frío hasta terminar la botella se puede usar un recipiente aislante o una cubitera. En ese caso, la cubitera se llena de hielo y también de agua fría: solo con hielo enfría mucho peor. Al contrario, un tinto demasiado frío nunca debe calentarse junto a un radiador, porque el calor estropea sus sabores; mejor dejarlo en la sala donde se va a servir hasta que se temple de forma natural.","Sweet and sparkling: well chilled (6–8°C / 6–10°C).":"Dulces y espumosos: muy fríos (6–8 °C / 6–10 °C).","Light/medium whites and rosés: chilled, 7–10°C.":"Blancos ligeros-medios y rosados: fríos, 7–10 °C.","Full whites: lightly chilled, 10–13°C; light reds: lightly chilled, 13°C.":"Blancos con cuerpo: ligeramente frescos, 10–13 °C; tintos ligeros: ligeramente frescos, 13 °C.","Medium/full reds: room temperature, 15–18°C.":"Tintos medios y con cuerpo: temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C.","Ice bucket with ice and water; never heat wine by a radiator.":"Cubitera con hielo y agua; nunca calentar el vino junto a un radiador.","Opening a bottle":"Abrir una botella","For a still wine sealed with a cork, the method is as follows. First remove the top of the capsule, using a foil cutter or the blade of a waiter's friend corkscrew, and wipe the neck of the bottle with a cloth. Then centre the corkscrew in the middle of the cork, screw it in and draw the cork out gently. Finally, wipe the neck again, both inside and outside.":"Para un vino tranquilo cerrado con corcho, se procede así. Primero se quita la parte superior de la cápsula, con un cortacápsulas o con la navaja de un sacacorchos de camarero, y se limpia el cuello de la botella con un paño. Después se centra el sacacorchos en medio del corcho, se enrosca y se saca el corcho con suavidad. Por último, se vuelve a limpiar el cuello, por dentro y por fuera.","Sparkling wine needs more care, because there is a lot of pressure inside the bottle. Chilling reduces it, but even when the wine is cold the cork can shoot out and injure someone. The golden rule: from the moment the wire cage is loosened, the cork must stay under your hand until it is completely out of the bottle.":"Con los espumosos hay que tener más cuidado, porque dentro de la botella hay mucha presión. Enfriar el vino la reduce, pero incluso frío el corcho puede salir disparado y herir a alguien. La regla de oro: desde que se afloja el morrión, el corcho debe quedar siempre bajo la mano hasta que esté totalmente fuera de la botella.","The steps are: remove the foil and loosen the cage while keeping the cork covered with your hand. Tilt the bottle at an angle, hold the cork in one hand and the base in the other, and turn the bottle, not the cork. Holding the cork firmly lets the pressure escape slowly, with a quiet sigh and no wine lost.":"Los pasos son: quitar el papel de aluminio y aflojar el morrión manteniendo el corcho cubierto con la mano. Inclinar la botella, sujetar el corcho con una mano y la base con la otra, y girar la botella, no el corcho. Al sujetar el corcho con firmeza, la presión sale despacio, con un leve suspiro y sin perder vino.","Still wine: remove capsule top, wipe, ease the cork out, wipe the neck.":"Vino tranquilo: quitar la cápsula, limpiar, sacar el corcho con suavidad, limpiar el cuello.","Sparkling: high pressure; the cork can injure.":"Espumoso: mucha presión; el corcho puede herir.","Once the cage is loosened, keep a hand on the cork.":"Tras aflojar el morrión, la mano siempre sobre el corcho.","Bottle at an angle; turn the bottle, not the cork.":"Botella inclinada; se gira la botella, no el corcho.","Glasses and checks before serving":"Copas y comprobaciones antes de servir","There are hundreds of glass shapes, but the best ones share one feature: the bowl narrows towards the rim. This shape holds and concentrates the aromas inside the glass, so they can be appreciated better. Red wine glasses are usually slightly larger than white wine glasses, and sparkling wines are served in flutes.":"Hay cientos de formas de copa, pero las mejores tienen algo en común: el cáliz se estrecha hacia el borde. Esta forma retiene y concentra los aromas dentro de la copa, así que se aprecian mejor. Normalmente las copas de tinto son algo más grandes que las de blanco, y los espumosos se sirven en copa flauta.","The glass must be perfectly clean. Dirt or traces of detergent can spoil a wine by changing its aromas and flavours. That is why glasses should always be polished before use, to remove any lingering dirt or finger marks. It is a simple habit that makes a real difference to what ends up in the glass.":"La copa tiene que estar perfectamente limpia. La suciedad o los restos de detergente pueden estropear el vino, alterando sus aromas y sabores. Por eso las copas siempre deben abrillantarse antes de usarlas, para quitar cualquier resto de suciedad o huellas de dedos. Es un gesto sencillo que marca una diferencia real en la copa.","Before serving, it is good practice to check the wine. Look at its appearance: haziness can point to a fault, and there should be no bits floating in it. Then smell it: the wine should not smell stale or have aromas of wet cardboard or vinegar. If something seems wrong, it is better not to serve it.":"Antes de servir, conviene comprobar el vino. Se observa su aspecto: si está turbio, puede indicar un defecto, y no debe haber trocitos flotando. Después se huele: el vino no debe oler a rancio ni tener aromas de cartón mojado o de vinagre. Si algo no va bien, es mejor no servirlo.","The best glasses narrow at the rim to concentrate aromas.":"La mejor copa se estrecha hacia el borde y concentra los aromas.","Red: slightly larger glass; sparkling: flute.":"Tinto: copa algo más grande; espumoso: flauta.","Clean, polished glasses: dirt and detergent spoil wine.":"Copas limpias y abrillantadas: suciedad y detergente estropean el vino.","Check: no haze or bits; no stale, wet cardboard or vinegar smells.":"Comprobar: sin turbidez ni trocitos; sin olor a rancio, cartón mojado o vinagre.","Food and wine: the basics":"Maridar comida y vino: lo básico","Food and wine pairing can look complicated, but at this level it comes down to two simple ideas: personal preference and a few predictable reactions between food and wine. The first idea matters most. When recommending a wine to a customer or a friend, what counts above all is what that person likes or dislikes.":"Maridar comida y vino parece complicado, pero a este nivel se reduce a dos ideas sencillas: los gustos personales y algunas reacciones previsibles entre comida y vino. La primera idea es la más importante. Cuando se recomienda un vino a un cliente o a un amigo, lo que cuenta ante todo es lo que esa persona disfruta o no.","A pairing may seem perfect to the person suggesting it, but if the other person does not enjoy that style of wine, there is no point recommending it. It also helps to remember that, for most people, most wines go acceptably with most foods. So there is not just one right wine for each dish.":"Un maridaje puede parecer perfecto a quien lo propone, pero si la otra persona no disfruta de ese estilo de vino, no tiene sentido recomendarlo. También conviene recordar que, para la mayoría de la gente, la mayoría de los vinos acompañan de forma aceptable a la mayoría de los platos. No existe, por tanto, un único vino correcto para cada plato.","Some features of food do, however, usually change how we perceive a wine: sweetness, umami, salt, acidity, flavour intensity, fat and chilli heat. Each one can make a wine seem better or worse. Knowing them lets you avoid the pairings most people dislike, and after that your options become almost limitless.":"Hay, sin embargo, algunas características de la comida que suelen cambiar cómo percibimos el vino: el dulzor, el umami, la sal, la acidez, la intensidad de sabor, la grasa y el picante de la guindilla. Cada una puede hacer que el vino parezca mejor o peor. Conocerlas permite evitar los maridajes que casi a todo el mundo le desagradan, y después las opciones son casi ilimitadas.","On the wine side, the elements that change are the ones you learn to spot when tasting: sweetness, acidity, bitterness, fruitiness, alcohol and body. Bitterness in wine, and the drying feel in the mouth, can come from the tannins in red wines or from oak. Keeping these words in mind makes the pairing table much easier to remember.":"Por el lado del vino, los elementos que cambian son los que se aprenden a reconocer en la cata: dulzor, acidez, amargor, fruta, alcohol y cuerpo. El amargor del vino, y la sensación que seca la boca, pueden venir de los taninos de los tintos o del roble. Tener presentes estas palabras hace que la tabla de maridajes sea mucho más fácil de recordar.","The person's own taste comes first.":"Los gustos de la persona van primero.","For most people, most wines suit most foods.":"Para casi todos, casi cualquier vino va con casi cualquier plato.","Food: sweet, umami, salt, acid, intense flavour, fat, chilli.":"Comida: dulce, umami, sal, ácido, sabor intenso, grasa, picante.","Wine: sweetness, acidity, bitterness, fruit, alcohol, body.":"Vino: dulzor, acidez, amargor, fruta, alcohol, cuerpo.","Bitterness in wine comes from tannin or oak.":"El amargor del vino viene de los taninos o del roble.","What food does to wine":"Qué le hace la comida al vino","Sweetness and umami are the two 'difficult' elements. Sweet or umami-rich food makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. A tannic red or a heavily oaked wine can therefore turn harsh. With a dessert, for example, a dry wine is likely to taste sour and lacking in fruit.":"El dulzor y el umami son los dos elementos «difíciles». Una comida dulce o rica en umami hace que el vino parezca más secante y amargo, más ácido, y menos dulce y afrutado. Un tinto tánico o un vino con mucho roble puede volverse duro. Con un postre, por ejemplo, un vino seco corre el riesgo de parecer agrio y sin fruta.","Salt and acidity, on the other hand, are wine-friendly. Salty food makes a wine seem less drying and bitter, less acidic, fruitier and fuller in body. Acidic food makes it seem less drying and bitter and less acidic, but also sweeter and fruitier. A dish with a sharp, acidic touch can therefore soften a very crisp wine.":"La sal y la acidez son, en cambio, aliadas del vino. Una comida salada hace que el vino parezca menos secante y amargo, menos ácido, más afrutado y con más cuerpo. Una comida ácida lo hace parecer menos secante y amargo y menos ácido, pero también más dulce y afrutado. Un plato con un toque ácido puede, por tanto, suavizar un vino muy vivo.","Three cases remain. A dish with very intense flavours can overwhelm a wine, which will seem to disappear, so a wine with enough flavour of its own works better. Fatty or oily food makes a wine seem less acidic. Finally, chilli heat makes the alcohol in a wine more noticeable, and the alcohol in turn increases the burning sensation of the chilli.":"Quedan tres casos. Un plato de sabores muy intensos puede tapar el vino, que parecerá desaparecer, así que conviene elegir un vino con sabor suficiente. Una comida grasa u oleosa hace que el vino parezca menos ácido. Por último, el picante de la guindilla hace que el alcohol del vino se note más, y el alcohol, a su vez, aumenta la sensación de ardor de la guindilla.","A way to remember it all: sweetness and umami 'take away' a wine's sweetness and fruit and boost its acidity and bitterness, while salt and acid do the opposite. Useful reasoning follows: with a sweet dish, choose a wine at least as sweet; with a spicy dish, a wine that is not too high in alcohol; with an umami-rich dish, a wine that is not too tannic.":"Un truco para recordarlo todo: el dulzor y el umami «quitan» al vino dulzor y fruta y aumentan su acidez y su amargor; la sal y el ácido hacen lo contrario. De ahí salen razonamientos útiles: con un plato dulce, un vino al menos igual de dulce; con un plato picante, un vino no demasiado alcohólico; con un plato rico en umami, un vino no demasiado tánico.","Sweet or umami → wine more drying, bitter, acidic; less sweet, fruity.":"Dulce o umami → vino más secante, amargo y ácido; menos dulce y afrutado.","Salty → wine less bitter and acidic; fruitier, fuller.":"Salado → vino menos amargo y ácido; más afrutado y con más cuerpo.","Acidic → wine less bitter and acidic; sweeter, fruitier.":"Ácido → vino menos amargo y ácido; más dulce y afrutado.","Intense flavours overwhelm wine; fat makes it seem less acidic.":"Los sabores intensos tapan el vino; la grasa lo hace parecer menos ácido.","Chilli + alcohol: more burn, alcohol more noticeable.":"Guindilla + alcohol: más ardor y alcohol más evidente.","Getting ready and looking at colour":"Prepararse y observar el color","Tasting well needs a method: approach every wine in the same order each time. This systematic approach to tasting lets you write accurate notes that you can look back on and compare in the future. At this level there are three stages: appearance, nose and palate. At each stage you look at only a few things, but always the same ones.":"Para catar bien hace falta un método: abordar cada vino siempre en el mismo orden. Este enfoque sistemático de la cata permite escribir notas precisas, que se pueden releer y comparar más adelante. A este nivel hay tres etapas: aspecto, nariz y boca. En cada una se observan pocas cosas, pero siempre las mismas.","Before starting, it is worth preparing your surroundings. There should be no distracting smells, such as strong perfume or cooking. You need a white surface to judge the colour properly. The ideal glass has a wide bowl that narrows at the top, to concentrate the aromas. Your palate should be clean too, with no lingering flavours such as toothpaste or coffee.":"Antes de empezar conviene preparar el entorno. No debe haber olores que distraigan, como perfumes fuertes o comida cocinándose. Hace falta una superficie blanca para juzgar bien el color. La copa ideal tiene un cáliz amplio que se estrecha arriba, para concentrar los aromas. La boca también debe estar limpia, sin sabores persistentes como pasta de dientes o café.","The first stage is appearance. At this level you look at just one thing: the colour, which can be white, rosé or red. Colour is already a clue to how the wine was made: a red fermented with its skins for a long time, a rosé for only a few hours.":"La primera etapa es el aspecto. A este nivel se observa una sola cosa: el color, que puede ser blanco, rosado o tinto. El color ya es una pista de cómo se hizo el vino: un tinto fermentó mucho tiempo con las pieles, un rosado solo unas horas.","Systematic approach: appearance, nose, palate, always in that order.":"Enfoque sistemático: aspecto, nariz, boca, siempre en ese orden.","No distracting smells; a white surface.":"Sin olores que distraigan; superficie blanca.","Wide glass narrowing at the top; a clean palate.":"Copa amplia que se estrecha arriba; boca limpia.","Appearance: colour white, rosé or red.":"Aspecto: color blanco, rosado o tinto.","The nose: fruit, oak and other":"La nariz: fruta, roble y otros","The second stage is the nose, meaning the wine's aromas. Bring the glass to your nose and try to recognise what the smells remind you of. Finding the words is hard at first, but it is a skill that improves with practice. To find your way, three broad families are used: fruit, oak and 'other'.":"La segunda etapa es la nariz, es decir, los aromas del vino. Se acerca la copa a la nariz y se intenta reconocer qué recuerdan los olores. Al principio cuesta encontrar las palabras, pero es una habilidad que mejora con la práctica. Para orientarse se usan tres grandes familias: fruta, roble y «otros».","Fruit is the most common family: nearly all wines smell of fruit. The type of fruit depends on the grape variety, for example Cabernet Sauvignon reminds you of blackcurrant, and on how ripe the grapes were. Cool-climate Chardonnay gives apple and lemon; warm-climate Chardonnay gives peach and pineapple. This is how climate shows up directly in the glass.":"La fruta es la familia más común: casi todos los vinos huelen a fruta. El tipo de fruta depende de la uva, por ejemplo la Cabernet Sauvignon recuerda a la grosella negra, y de lo madura que estaba la uva. Una Chardonnay de clima fresco da manzana y limón; de clima cálido, melocotón y piña. Así es como el clima aparece directamente en la copa.","Oak shows up when the wine has been fermented or matured in barrels. It brings aromas such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The 'other' family covers everything else: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. This variety is exactly what makes wine so interesting to smell.":"El roble aparece cuando el vino ha fermentado o se ha criado en barrica. Aporta aromas como vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro y humo. En la familia «otros» entra todo lo demás: hierba, flores, hierbas aromáticas, verduras, tierra, setas y cuero. Esta variedad es justo lo que hace que oler vino resulte tan interesante.","Nose: fruit, oak and 'other' aromas.":"Nariz: aromas de fruta, roble y «otros».","Fruit depends on grape variety and ripeness.":"La fruta depende de la uva y de su madurez.","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke.":"Roble: vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro, humo.","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather.":"Otros: hierba, flores, hierbas, verduras, tierra, setas, cuero.","The palate: structure and flavours":"La boca: estructura y sabores","The third stage is the palate: take a small sip and move it around your mouth. Here you assess five structural characteristics. Sweetness depends on how much sugar is left in the wine, and most wines are dry. Acidity makes your mouth water and gives freshness. Tannin, typical of red wines, dries the mouth.":"La tercera etapa es la boca: se toma un sorbo pequeño y se mueve por la boca. Aquí se valoran cinco características estructurales. El dulzor depende del azúcar que queda en el vino, y la mayoría de los vinos son secos. La acidez hace salivar y da frescura. El tanino, típico de los tintos, seca la boca.","The other two characteristics are alcohol and body. Many still and sparkling wines have between 11.5% and 14% abv, though some are as low as 8% and others reach 15%. Body is the overall feel of the wine in your mouth: simply ask yourself how mouth-filling it is. A light-bodied wine feels delicate, a full-bodied one feels dense and mouth-filling.":"Las otras dos características son el alcohol y el cuerpo. Muchos vinos tranquilos y espumosos tienen entre un 11,5 % y un 14 % vol., aunque algunos bajan hasta el 8 % y otros llegan al 15 %. El cuerpo es la sensación global del vino en la boca: basta con preguntarse cuánto «llena» la boca. Un vino ligero parece delicado, uno con cuerpo parece denso y envolvente.","Finally, on the palate you look for flavours, using the same families as on the nose: fruit, oak and other. You will often find the aromas you already smelled, and sometimes discover new ones. One last important note: in moderation alcohol is not regarded as harmful, but in excess it damages health and behaviour. Many countries publish official guidelines on low-risk drinking.":"Por último, en boca se buscan los sabores, con las mismas familias que en nariz: fruta, roble y otros. A menudo se reconocen los aromas ya percibidos y a veces se descubren otros nuevos. Una última nota importante: con moderación el alcohol no se considera perjudicial, pero en exceso daña la salud y el comportamiento. Muchos países publican pautas oficiales sobre un consumo de bajo riesgo.","Structure: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body.":"Estructura: dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol, cuerpo.","Acidity = mouth waters; tannin = mouth dries.":"Acidez = se saliva; tanino = la boca se seca.","Body = how mouth-filling the wine feels.":"Cuerpo = cuánto llena el vino la boca.","Flavours: fruit, oak, other.":"Sabores: fruta, roble, otros.","Which definition best describes wine?":"¿Qué definición describe mejor el vino?","Fermented grape juice":"Zumo de uva fermentado","Distilled grape juice":"Zumo de uva destilado","Concentrated grape juice":"Zumo de uva concentrado","Pasteurised grape juice":"Zumo de uva pasteurizado","Wine is made by fermenting the sweet juice of grapes.":"El vino se obtiene haciendo fermentar el zumo dulce de la uva.","To make wine, grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice. Alcoholic fermentation, carried out by yeast, then turns the sugar in that juice into alcohol. Without fermentation you would simply have grape juice; distilling or concentrating the juice is not part of the basic definition of wine.":"Para hacer vino se estrujan las uvas y se libera su zumo dulce. Después, la fermentación alcohólica, gracias a las levaduras, convierte el azúcar de ese zumo en alcohol. Sin fermentación solo quedaría zumo de uva; destilar o concentrar el zumo no forma parte de la definición básica del vino.","Which part of a black grape contains tannins?":"¿En qué parte de la uva tinta se encuentran los taninos?","The skin":"En la piel","The pulp":"En la pulpa","The juice":"En el zumo","The flower":"En la flor","Black grape skins hold both the colour and the tannins.":"La piel de las uvas tintas contiene tanto el color como los taninos.","The skin is what really sets black grapes apart from white ones: it is deeply coloured and contains tannins, which leave the mouth feeling dry. The pulp, by contrast, holds the juice, made of water, sugar and acid, and it is the same colour in all grapes.":"La piel es lo que distingue de verdad las uvas tintas de las blancas: tiene un color intenso y contiene taninos, que dejan sensación de sequedad en la boca. La pulpa, en cambio, contiene el zumo, formado por agua, azúcar y ácido, y tiene el mismo color en todas las uvas.","What is the juice in the pulp mainly made of?":"¿De qué está compuesto principalmente el zumo de la pulpa?","Water, sugar and acid":"Agua, azúcar y ácido","Water, tannin and colour":"Agua, taninos y color","Alcohol, sugar and yeast":"Alcohol, azúcar y levadura","Water, alcohol and carbon dioxide":"Agua, alcohol y dióxido de carbono","Grape juice is mostly water, sugar and acid.":"El zumo de uva es sobre todo agua, azúcar y ácido.","The pulp is the soft part of the grape and holds the juice, which is mostly water, sugar and acid. Tannin and colour are found in the skin instead. Alcohol and carbon dioxide only appear later, when yeast ferments the sugar in the juice.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda de la uva y contiene el zumo, formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Los taninos y el color están en la piel. El alcohol y el dióxido de carbono solo aparecen más tarde, cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar del zumo.","What do tannins do to your mouth?":"¿Qué sensación dejan los taninos en la boca?","Make it feel dry":"La dejan seca","Make it water":"La hacen salivar","Make it feel hot":"La calientan","Make it feel sweet":"La endulzan","Tannins from the skins leave the mouth feeling dry.":"Los taninos de la piel dejan sensación de sequedad en la boca.","Tannins come from black grape skins and are felt more than tasted: they dry out the mouth. When tasting, they should not be confused with acidity, which makes your mouth water instead; these are two opposite sensations worth learning to tell apart.":"Los taninos proceden de la piel de las uvas tintas y se notan más como una sensación que como un sabor: secan la boca. No hay que confundirlos con la acidez, que hace salivar: son dos sensaciones opuestas que conviene aprender a distinguir en la cata.","What colour is the pulp of a black grape?":"¿De qué color es la pulpa de una uva tinta?","The same as in a white grape":"El mismo que en una uva blanca","Deep red, like the skin":"Rojo intenso, como la piel","Purple, but only when fully ripe":"Morada, pero solo cuando está madura","Pink, paler than the skin":"Rosa, más clara que la piel","Pulp is the same colour in all grapes; the colour is in the skin.":"La pulpa tiene el mismo color en todas las uvas; el color está en la piel.","Inside, white and black grapes look very alike: the pulp is the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. This is exactly why a red wine gets its colour from the skins, and why a white wine can even be made from black grapes if the juice is separated from the skins straight away.":"Por dentro, las uvas blancas y tintas se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color sea cual sea el de la piel. Precisamente por eso el color de un vino tinto viene de las pieles, y por eso se puede hacer incluso un vino blanco con uvas tintas si se separa el zumo de las pieles enseguida.","In which season does the grape vine flower?":"¿En qué estación florece la vid?","Spring":"En primavera","Summer":"En verano","Autumn":"En otoño","Winter":"En invierno","Vines flower in spring; the grapes then ripen in summer.":"La vid florece en primavera; luego la uva madura en verano.","The vine's yearly cycle follows the seasons. In spring the clusters of flowers appear, and each flower will become a grape. During summer the grapes ripen, and they are picked towards the end of summer. In winter the vine rests, and it needs enough cold to do so.":"El ciclo anual de la vid sigue las estaciones. En primavera aparecen los racimos de flores, y cada flor se convertirá en una uva. En verano la uva madura y hacia el final del verano se vendimia. En invierno, en cambio, la vid descansa, y necesita suficiente frío para hacerlo.","What does each individual vine flower become?":"¿En qué se convierte cada flor de la vid?","One grape":"Una uva","A new shoot":"Un nuevo brote","A whole leaf":"Una hoja entera","A whole bunch":"Un racimo entero","After flowering, each single flower turns into a small grape.":"Tras la floración, cada flor se transforma en una uva pequeña.","Vine flowers come in clusters made up of many tiny flowers. After flowering, each one becomes a grape, so the cluster of flowers turns into a bunch of grapes. At first these grapes are small, hard and green; they only grow and ripen as the summer goes on.":"Las flores de la vid forman racimos compuestos por muchas flores diminutas. Tras la floración, cada una se convierte en una uva, así que el racimo de flores se transforma en un racimo de uvas. Al principio son pequeñas, duras y verdes; solo crecen y maduran a lo largo del verano.","What are grapes like just after flowering?":"¿Cómo son las uvas justo después de la floración?","Small, hard and green":"Pequeñas, duras y verdes","Small, soft and golden":"Pequeñas, blandas y doradas","Large, hard and purple":"Grandes, duras y moradas","Large, soft and sweet":"Grandes, blandas y dulces","All young grapes are small, hard and green, white or black.":"Todas las uvas jóvenes son pequeñas, duras y verdes, blancas o tintas.","Newly formed grapes are not ready yet: they are small, hard and green, and at this stage white and black grapes look the same. Only during summer ripening do they swell with water, become sweeter and change colour, towards golden for white grapes and purple for black ones.":"Recién formadas, las uvas aún no están listas: son pequeñas, duras y verdes, y en esta fase no se distinguen las blancas de las tintas. Solo con la maduración del verano se hinchan de agua, se vuelven más dulces y cambian de color, hacia el dorado las blancas y hacia el morado las tintas.","As grapes ripen, what happens to their sugar and acid levels?":"Durante la maduración, ¿qué ocurre con los niveles de azúcar y de ácido de la uva?","Sugar rises and acid falls":"El azúcar sube y el ácido baja","Sugar falls and acid rises":"El azúcar baja y el ácido sube","Both rise at the same rate":"Ambos suben al mismo ritmo","Both stay the same":"Ambos se mantienen igual","Ripening makes grapes sweeter and less acidic.":"Al madurar, la uva se vuelve más dulce y menos ácida.","While grapes ripen over the summer, several things change: they swell with water, sugar goes up, acid goes down and the flavours become riper. This balance between sugar and acid will later influence the alcohol and freshness of the wine.":"Mientras la uva madura en verano se producen varios cambios: las uvas se hinchan de agua, el azúcar aumenta, el ácido disminuye y los sabores se vuelven más maduros. Este equilibrio entre azúcar y ácido influirá más tarde en el alcohol y la frescura del vino.","What colour do white grapes turn as they ripen?":"¿De qué color se vuelven las uvas blancas al madurar?","From green to golden":"De verde a dorado","From green to purple":"De verde a morado","From yellow to green":"De amarillo a verde","From golden to pink":"De dorado a rosa","White grapes go from green to golden; black ones from green to purple.":"Las uvas blancas pasan de verde a dorado; las tintas, de verde a morado.","At first all grapes are green. As they ripen, the skin changes colour: it becomes golden in white grapes and purple in black grapes. This colour change goes hand in hand with the other signs of ripening, namely more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours.":"Al principio todas las uvas son verdes. Con la maduración, la piel cambia de color: se vuelve dorada en las uvas blancas y morada en las tintas. Este cambio acompaña a las demás señales de maduración: más agua, más azúcar, menos ácido y sabores más maduros.","Which of these does NOT happen as grapes ripen?":"¿Cuál de estos cambios NO ocurre cuando la uva madura?","Acidity increases":"La acidez aumenta","Grapes swell with water":"Las uvas se hinchan de agua","Sugar increases":"El azúcar aumenta","Flavours become riper":"Los sabores maduran","During ripening acidity falls, it does not rise.":"Durante la maduración la acidez baja, no sube.","Ripening brings more water into the grapes, more sugar and riper flavours, but acid moves the other way and drops. That is why an unripe grape tastes sour, while a ripe one is sweet and less acidic. Remembering this trend also helps you understand the effect of climate.":"La maduración aporta más agua a las uvas, más azúcar y sabores más maduros, pero el ácido va en sentido contrario y disminuye. Por eso una uva verde es agria y una madura es dulce y menos ácida. Recordar esta tendencia ayuda también a entender el efecto del clima.","In the vine's yearly cycle, when are the grapes usually picked?":"Según el ciclo de la vid, ¿cuándo se suele vendimiar?","In late summer":"A finales del verano","In early spring":"A principios de primavera","In midwinter":"En pleno invierno","Just after flowering":"Justo después de la floración","Grapes ripen through summer and are picked in late summer.":"La uva madura en verano y se recoge hacia el final del verano.","The vine flowers in spring, the flowers become grapes and these ripen during the summer. Once they are ripe enough, towards the end of summer, they are picked. Just after flowering the grapes are still small, hard and green, far too unripe to make wine.":"La vid florece en primavera, las flores se convierten en uvas y estas maduran durante el verano. Cuando están lo bastante maduras, hacia el final del verano, se recogen. Justo después de la floración las uvas son todavía pequeñas, duras y verdes, demasiado verdes para hacer vino.","Why do vines grow best where winters are cold?":"¿Por qué la vid crece mejor donde el invierno es frío?","The cold lets the vine rest":"Porque el frío le permite descansar","The cold raises sugar levels":"Porque el frío aumenta el azúcar","The cold makes the vine flower":"Porque el frío hace florecer la vid","The cold colours the skins":"Porque el frío colorea las pieles","A cold enough winter gives the vine a period of rest.":"Un invierno lo bastante frío da a la vid un periodo de descanso.","Besides the right amount of sunlight and heat during the growing season, a vine needs a winter cold enough to let it rest. This is why most vineyards are found in particular bands of latitude, neither too cold nor too hot.":"Además de la cantidad justa de sol y calor durante la temporada de crecimiento, la vid necesita un invierno lo bastante frío para poder descansar. Por eso la mayoría de los viñedos se encuentra en franjas de latitud concretas, ni demasiado frías ni demasiado cálidas.","Which of these is an example of a cool climate wine region?":"¿Cuál de estos es un ejemplo de región vitícola de clima fresco?","Germany":"Alemania","Parts of Australia":"Algunas zonas de Australia","Parts of California":"Algunas zonas de California","Areas on the Equator":"Las zonas del ecuador","Germany, like northern France, lies nearer the poles and has a cool climate.":"Alemania, como el norte de Francia, está más cerca de los polos y tiene clima fresco.","Cool climate regions are those closer to the poles, such as Germany and northern France. Parts of Australia and California are examples of warm climates instead. Right at the Equator it is too hot for vines to grow well and rest in winter.":"Las regiones de clima fresco son las más cercanas a los polos, como Alemania y el norte de Francia. Algunas partes de Australia y de California son, en cambio, ejemplos de clima cálido. Junto al ecuador hace demasiado calor para que la vid crezca bien y descanse en invierno.","Which type of grape is commonly grown in warm climate regions?":"¿Qué tipo de uva se cultiva con más frecuencia en las regiones cálidas?","Black grapes":"Las uvas tintas","White grapes":"Las uvas blancas","Unripe grapes":"Las uvas verdes","Skinless grapes":"Las uvas sin piel","Warm climates ripen grapes reliably, and black grapes are commonly grown.":"En clima cálido la uva madura con regularidad y es habitual cultivar uvas tintas.","Warm regions, closer to the Equator, have high average temperatures and more intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably. Growing black grapes is common there. In cool regions, closer to the poles, where grapes sometimes struggle to ripen at all, white grapes are more commonly grown.":"Las regiones cálidas, más cercanas al ecuador, tienen temperaturas medias altas y un sol más intenso, así que la uva madura con regularidad. Allí es habitual cultivar uvas tintas. En las regiones frescas, donde a veces a la uva le cuesta madurar, es más frecuente cultivar uvas blancas.","In a cool climate, grapes will usually have…":"En un clima fresco, ¿cómo suelen ser las uvas?","Less sugar and more acidity":"Menos azúcar y más acidez","More sugar and less acidity":"Más azúcar y menos acidez","More sugar and more acidity":"Más azúcar y más acidez","Less sugar and less acidity":"Menos azúcar y menos acidez","The cooler it is, the more acidic and less sugary the grapes stay.":"Cuanto más fresco, más ácida queda la uva y menos azúcar acumula.","With little heat and weaker sunshine, grapes ripen less: they build up less sugar and keep more acidity. In the glass this tends to give lighter, fresher wines. In a warm climate the opposite happens: more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours.":"Con poco calor y un sol más débil, la uva madura menos: acumula menos azúcar y conserva más acidez. En la copa, esto suele dar vinos más ligeros y frescos. En un clima cálido ocurre lo contrario: más azúcar, menos acidez y sabores más maduros.","Why does a warm-climate wine tend to show riper fruit flavours?":"¿Por qué un vino de clima cálido suele tener sabores de fruta más maduros?","Heat ripens the grapes further":"El calor hace madurar más la uva","Heat raises the grapes' acidity":"El calor aumenta la acidez de la uva","Heat removes colour from the skins":"El calor quita color a las pieles","Heat stops the vine flowering":"El calor detiene la floración","More heat and sun ripen grapes further: more sugar, riper flavours.":"Con más calor y sol la uva madura más: más azúcar y sabores más maduros.","In warm regions average temperatures are high and the sunshine is intense, so grapes ripen fully and reliably. This brings more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours. Chardonnay, for example, moves from apple and lemon aromas in a cool climate to peach and pineapple in a warm one.":"En las regiones cálidas las temperaturas medias son altas y el sol es intenso, así que la uva madura del todo y con regularidad. Esto aporta más azúcar, menos acidez y sabores más maduros. La Chardonnay, por ejemplo, pasa de aromas de manzana y limón en clima fresco a melocotón y piña en clima cálido.","A Chardonnay with apple and lemon aromas most likely comes from…":"Una Chardonnay con aromas de manzana y limón probablemente procede de…","A cool climate":"Un clima fresco","A warm climate":"Un clima cálido","A tropical climate":"Un clima tropical","A very dry climate":"Un clima muy seco","Green fruit and citrus point to less ripe, cool-climate grapes.":"La fruta verde y los cítricos indican uva menos madura, típica del clima fresco.","Climate changes the type of fruit you find in a wine. In a cool climate Chardonnay gives green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. In a warm climate, with riper grapes, it shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple.":"El clima cambia el tipo de fruta que se percibe en el vino. En clima fresco, la Chardonnay da fruta verde como la manzana y cítricos como el limón. En clima cálido, con uva más madura, muestra fruta de hueso como el melocotón y fruta tropical como la piña.","Why can grapes in cool regions struggle to ripen in some years?":"¿Por qué en las regiones frescas a la uva le cuesta a veces madurar?","Low temperatures and weaker sunlight":"Temperaturas bajas y sol más débil","High temperatures and stronger sunlight":"Temperaturas altas y sol más intenso","Winters too mild for the vine to rest":"Inviernos demasiado suaves para descansar","Vines too young to flower":"Vides demasiado jóvenes para florecer","Little heat and weaker light slow down ripening.":"Poco calor y una luz más débil frenan la maduración.","Cool regions lie closer to the poles: average temperatures are low and the sunlight can be less intense than near the Equator. In especially cool years the grapes may not ripen fully. This is one reason white grapes are commonly grown there.":"Las regiones frescas están más cerca de los polos: las temperaturas medias son bajas y la luz del sol puede ser menos intensa que cerca del ecuador. En los años especialmente frescos la uva puede no llegar a madurar del todo. Por eso allí se cultivan a menudo uvas blancas.","After planting, how long does a vine usually take before it gives a crop every year?":"Tras plantarla, ¿cuánto tarda normalmente una vid en dar cosecha cada año?","A couple of years":"Un par de años","A few months":"Unos meses","About twenty years":"Unos veinte años","Half a century":"Medio siglo","A vine matures a couple of years after planting, then crops every year.":"Una vid madura un par de años después de plantarla y luego da cosecha cada año.","The vine is a long-lived plant that can survive for several decades. After planting it needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year, always following the same cycle: flowering in spring, ripening in summer and harvest in late summer.":"La vid es una planta longeva que puede vivir varias décadas. Tras plantarla necesita un par de años para llegar a la madurez; desde entonces da una cosecha cada año, siguiendo siempre el mismo ciclo: floración en primavera, maduración en verano y vendimia al final del verano.","What is needed for alcoholic fermentation to take place?":"¿Qué hace falta para que se produzca la fermentación alcohólica?","Yeast":"Levaduras","Tannin":"Taninos","Oak":"Roble","Carbon dioxide":"Dióxido de carbono","Yeast are what turn the sugar in the juice into alcohol.":"Son las levaduras las que convierten el azúcar del zumo en alcohol.","Without yeast, grape juice would stay juice. Yeast are microscopic organisms that feed on sugar and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Oak can be used to ferment or mature wine but is not essential, and carbon dioxide is a product of fermentation, not an ingredient.":"Sin levaduras, el zumo de uva seguiría siendo zumo. Las levaduras son organismos microscópicos que se alimentan del azúcar y lo transforman en alcohol y dióxido de carbono. El roble puede usarse para fermentar o criar el vino, pero no es imprescindible; el dióxido de carbono es un producto de la fermentación, no un ingrediente.","What are the two products of alcoholic fermentation?":"¿Cuáles son los dos productos de la fermentación alcohólica?","Alcohol and carbon dioxide":"Alcohol y dióxido de carbono","Alcohol and sugar":"Alcohol y azúcar","Sugar and acid":"Azúcar y ácido","Water and tannin":"Agua y taninos","Yeast eat the sugar in the grape juice and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Sugar is therefore the starting point, not a product. The alcohol stays in the wine, while in most cases the carbon dioxide escapes into the atmosphere during fermentation.":"Las levaduras se comen el azúcar del zumo de uva y lo transforman en alcohol y dióxido de carbono. El azúcar es, por tanto, el punto de partida, no un producto. El alcohol se queda en el vino, mientras que el dióxido de carbono, en la mayoría de los casos, se escapa a la atmósfera durante la fermentación.","During the fermentation of a still wine, what usually happens to the carbon dioxide?":"¿Qué suele pasar con el dióxido de carbono producido al fermentar un vino tranquilo?","It escapes into the air":"Se escapa al aire","It stays in the wine":"Se queda en el vino","It turns back into sugar":"Se convierte en azúcar","It is absorbed by the skins":"Lo absorben las pieles","In most cases the gas escapes to the atmosphere; the alcohol stays.":"En la mayoría de los casos el gas se va a la atmósfera; el alcohol se queda.","During fermentation yeast produce alcohol and carbon dioxide. The alcohol remains in the new wine, while the gas normally escapes into the air, which gives a still wine with no bubbles. In sparkling wines, by contrast, some of this gas is trapped in the wine.":"Durante la fermentación, las levaduras producen alcohol y dióxido de carbono. El alcohol se queda en el vino recién hecho, mientras que el gas normalmente se escapa al aire, y así se obtiene un vino tranquilo, sin burbujas. En los espumosos, en cambio, parte de ese gas queda atrapado en el vino.","A label says 12% abv. What does this mean?":"Una etiqueta indica 12 % vol. ¿Qué significa?","12% of the liquid is alcohol":"El 12 % del líquido es alcohol","12% of the liquid is sugar":"El 12 % del líquido es azúcar","12% of the grapes were black":"El 12 % de la uva era tinta","12% of the wine was oak-aged":"El 12 % del vino se crió en roble","Alcohol by volume tells you what share of the liquid is alcohol.":"El porcentaje en volumen indica qué parte del líquido es alcohol.","Alcohol is expressed as a percentage of the volume. A wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol; one at 12% abv contains twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. The figure tells you nothing about sweetness, grape colour or the use of oak: it is only about alcohol.":"El grado alcohólico se expresa como porcentaje del volumen. Un vino de 10 % vol. tiene una décima parte de alcohol; uno de 12 % vol. tiene doce partes de alcohol de cada cien. La cifra no dice nada sobre el dulzor, el color de la uva o el uso de roble: solo habla del alcohol.","Why are most wines dry?":"¿Por qué la mayoría de los vinos son secos?","The yeast eat all the sugar":"Las levaduras consumen todo el azúcar","The skins absorb the sugar":"Las pieles absorben el azúcar","Oak removes the sugar":"El roble elimina el azúcar","Grapes contain no sugar":"La uva no contiene azúcar","Fermentation usually continues until no sugar is left.":"La fermentación suele seguir hasta que no queda azúcar.","Ripe grapes are full of sugar, but in most cases the yeast keep working until they have turned all of it into alcohol. The result is a dry wine, meaning one with no sugar or very little. To make sweet wines, some of the sugar has to remain in the wine.":"La uva madura es rica en azúcar, pero en la mayoría de los casos las levaduras siguen trabajando hasta convertirlo todo en alcohol. El resultado es un vino seco, es decir, sin azúcar o con muy poco. Para hacer vinos dulces hay que conseguir que parte del azúcar se quede en el vino.","In white winemaking, what happens straight after crushing?":"En la elaboración del vino blanco, ¿qué ocurre justo después del estrujado?","Pressing":"El prensado","Fermentation":"La fermentación","Draining":"El escurrido","Maturation":"La crianza","For white wine, crushed grapes are pressed before the juice ferments.":"En el blanco, la uva estrujada se prensa enseguida, antes de fermentar el zumo.","For white wine the order is: crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation and bottling. Pressing collects the juice left in the crushed grapes, so that only the juice, without the skins, goes on to ferment. Draining, by contrast, is a typical step in making red and rosé wines.":"En el blanco, el orden es: estrujado, prensado, fermentación, crianza y embotellado. El prensado recupera el zumo que queda en la uva estrujada, para que solo el zumo, sin pieles, fermente. El escurrido, en cambio, es un paso típico del tinto y del rosado.","Where can a white wine be fermented?":"¿Dónde puede fermentar un vino blanco?","Stainless steel tanks or oak barrels":"En depósitos de acero o barricas de roble","Only in oak barrels":"Solo en barricas de roble","Only in the bottle":"Solo en la botella","Only in stainless steel tanks":"Solo en depósitos de acero","White wine can ferment in either stainless steel or oak.":"El blanco puede fermentar tanto en acero inoxidable como en roble.","After crushing and pressing, yeast are added to the juice. Fermentation can happen in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels; it is the winemaker's choice. The maturation that follows can also take place in either of these two kinds of container.":"Tras el estrujado y el prensado, se añaden levaduras al zumo. La fermentación puede hacerse en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble: es una elección de quien elabora el vino. La crianza posterior también puede hacerse en cualquiera de estos dos tipos de recipiente.","Why is it possible to make white wine from black grapes?":"¿Por qué se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas?","Their juice is colourless":"Su zumo es incoloro","Their skins are golden":"Su piel es dorada","They contain no tannin":"No contienen taninos","They lose colour in oak":"Pierden color en roble","Colour is only in the skin; black grape juice has no colour.":"El color está solo en la piel; el zumo de la uva tinta es incoloro.","Black grapes have coloured skins but colourless juice, just like the pulp of white grapes. If they are pressed gently before fermentation and the juice is separated from the skins straight away, the colour does not pass into the juice and a white wine can be made.":"Las uvas tintas tienen la piel de color, pero su zumo es incoloro, igual que la pulpa de las uvas blancas. Si se prensan con suavidad antes de la fermentación y el zumo se separa enseguida de las pieles, el color no pasa al zumo y se puede elaborar un vino blanco.","In red winemaking, what goes into the fermentation vessel?":"En la elaboración del tinto, ¿qué va al recipiente de fermentación?","The juice together with the skins":"El zumo junto con las pieles","The juice alone, without skins":"Solo el zumo, sin pieles","The skins alone, without juice":"Solo las pieles, sin zumo","Wine that is already pressed":"Vino ya prensado","Red wine ferments with the skins, which give colour and tannin.":"El tinto fermenta con las pieles, que aportan color y taninos.","After black grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This long contact is what draws colour and tannin out of the skins. For white wine, by contrast, the juice is separated from the skins by pressing before it ferments.":"Tras estrujar las uvas tintas, el zumo y las pieles van juntos al recipiente de fermentación. Este contacto prolongado es lo que permite extraer el color y los taninos de las pieles. En el blanco, por el contrario, el zumo se separa de las pieles con el prensado antes de fermentar.","Why are juice and skins mixed thoroughly during red wine fermentation?":"¿Por qué se mezclan a fondo zumo y pieles al fermentar el tinto?","To extract colour and tannin":"Para extraer color y taninos","To add oak flavours":"Para añadir sabor a roble","To remove sugar from the skins":"Para quitar azúcar a las pieles","To release carbon dioxide":"Para liberar el dióxido de carbono","Mixing helps colour and tannin pass from the skins into the wine.":"Mezclar ayuda a que color y taninos pasen de las pieles al vino.","The colour and tannin of red wine are found in the skins of black grapes. By mixing the skins well with the juice during fermentation, these substances pass into the wine. That is why a red wine has deep colour and a structure that dries the mouth, while a white does not.":"El color y los taninos del vino tinto están en la piel de las uvas tintas. Al mezclar bien las pieles con el zumo durante la fermentación, estas sustancias pasan al vino. Por eso un tinto tiene un color intenso y una estructura que seca la boca, y un blanco no.","In red winemaking, when is the wine drained off the skins?":"En el tinto, ¿cuándo se escurre el vino de las pieles?","Once fermentation has finished":"Al terminar la fermentación","Straight after crushing":"Justo después del estrujado","After a few hours of fermentation":"Tras unas horas de fermentación","After bottling":"Después del embotellado","Red wine stays on the skins for the whole fermentation, then is drained.":"El tinto se queda con las pieles toda la fermentación y luego se escurre.","For red wine the skins stay in contact with the juice for the whole fermentation, so they give plenty of colour and tannin. Only when fermentation is over is the new wine drained off the skins. Draining after just a few hours is, by contrast, the typical technique for rosé.":"En el tinto, las pieles se quedan en contacto con el zumo durante toda la fermentación, para que cedan mucho color y tanino. Solo cuando la fermentación ha terminado se escurre el vino nuevo de las pieles. Escurrir tras unas pocas horas es, en cambio, la técnica típica del rosado.","Why are the skins pressed after a red wine is drained?":"¿Por qué se prensan las pieles después de escurrir el tinto?","To release the remaining wine":"Para recuperar el vino restante","To extract more sugar":"Para extraer más azúcar","To start fermentation":"Para iniciar la fermentación","To turn the wine rosé":"Para volver rosado el vino","The skins still hold wine, which pressing recovers.":"Las pieles todavía retienen vino, que se recupera al prensar.","After draining, the skins are still soaked with wine. Pressing them recovers this wine, which would otherwise be lost. So in red winemaking pressing comes after fermentation, the opposite of white winemaking, where the grapes are pressed before fermenting. Maturation and bottling then follow.":"Después del escurrido, las pieles siguen empapadas de vino. Al prensarlas se recupera ese vino, que de otro modo se perdería. En el tinto, por tanto, el prensado va después de la fermentación, al contrario que en el blanco, donde la uva se prensa antes de fermentar. Luego vienen la crianza y el embotellado.","Which is the correct order of steps for a red wine?":"¿Cuál es el orden correcto de las fases de un vino tinto?","Crushing, fermentation, draining, pressing":"Estrujado, fermentación, escurrido, prensado","Crushing, pressing, fermentation, draining":"Estrujado, prensado, fermentación, escurrido","Pressing, crushing, draining, fermentation":"Prensado, estrujado, escurrido, fermentación","Crushing, draining, fermentation, pressing":"Estrujado, escurrido, fermentación, prensado","Red ferments on the skins, then is drained and the skins pressed.":"El tinto fermenta con las pieles y después se escurre y se prensa.","Red wine follows this sequence: crushing the black grapes, fermenting juice and skins together, draining the new wine, pressing the skins, maturation and bottling. Starting with crushing then pressing describes white winemaking instead, where pressing happens before fermentation and only the juice is fermented.":"El tinto sigue esta secuencia: estrujado de las uvas tintas, fermentación del zumo con las pieles, escurrido del vino nuevo, prensado de las pieles, crianza y embotellado. Empezar con estrujado y luego prensado describe el blanco, en el que el prensado va antes de la fermentación.","Which type of grape is used to make rosé wine?":"¿Con qué tipo de uva se hace el vino rosado?","Dried grapes":"Uvas pasas","Rosé comes from black grapes with brief skin contact.":"El rosado se hace con uvas tintas y un contacto breve con las pieles.","The pink colour comes from the skins of black grapes. The juice stays in contact with the skins for only a few hours, so it picks up just a little colour; it is then separated and finishes fermenting without the skins. White grapes do not have skins coloured enough to do this.":"El color rosa viene de la piel de las uvas tintas. El zumo está en contacto con las pieles solo unas horas, así que toma muy poco color; después se separa y termina de fermentar sin las pieles. Las uvas blancas no tienen la piel lo bastante coloreada para esto.","For a rosé, when is the juice drained from the skins?":"En un rosado, ¿cuándo se separa el zumo de las pieles?","After only a few hours":"Tras unas pocas horas","After fermentation is complete":"Tras toda la fermentación","After oak maturation":"Tras la crianza en roble","Before crushing":"Antes del estrujado","For rosé, skin contact lasts only a few hours.":"En el rosado, el contacto con las pieles dura solo unas horas.","Rosé starts out like a red: black grapes are crushed and fermentation begins with the skins. After only a few hours, though, the juice is drained off while it is still just pink. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. Draining at the end of fermentation would give a red wine instead.":"El rosado empieza como un tinto: uvas tintas estrujadas y fermentación con las pieles. Pero tras solo unas horas el zumo se separa, cuando todavía es solo rosa. La fermentación termina sin las pieles. Separarlo al final de la fermentación daría, en cambio, un vino tinto.","What mainly explains the colour difference between a rosé and a red?":"¿Qué explica sobre todo la diferencia de color entre un rosado y un tinto?","How long the juice stays on the skins":"El tiempo de contacto con las pieles","The colour of the grape pulp":"El color de la pulpa de la uva","The use of oak barrels":"El uso de barricas de roble","The amount of yeast added":"La cantidad de levadura añadida","A few hours on the skins gives pink; the whole fermentation gives red.":"Unas horas con las pieles dan rosa; toda la fermentación da tinto.","Rosé and red are both made from black grapes, whose pulp is the same colour as that of white grapes. The colour comes from the skins: for red they stay in the juice for the whole fermentation, for rosé only for a few hours. That is why rosé stays pink.":"El rosado y el tinto se hacen con uvas tintas, cuya pulpa tiene el mismo color que la de las uvas blancas. El color viene de las pieles: en el tinto se quedan en el zumo durante toda la fermentación; en el rosado, solo unas horas. Por eso el rosado se queda rosa.","Which statement about the maturation of rosé wines is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre la crianza de los rosados es correcta?","They are rarely matured in oak":"Rara vez se crían en roble","They are always matured in oak":"Siempre se crían en roble","They are matured on their skins":"Se crían con las pieles","They are matured only in bottle":"Solo se crían en botella","Rosé can mature in steel or oak, but oak is rarely used.":"El rosado puede criarse en acero o en roble, pero el roble es poco habitual.","After fermentation, both reds and rosés can be matured in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels. For rosé, however, oak is rarely used. The skins were already removed after a few hours, so maturation never takes place on the skins. The wine is then bottled.":"Tras la fermentación, tintos y rosados pueden criarse en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble. En los rosados, sin embargo, el roble se usa poco. Las pieles ya se retiraron tras unas horas, así que la crianza nunca se hace con las pieles. Después el vino se embotella.","Which step is part of red winemaking but NOT rosé?":"¿Qué fase existe en el tinto pero NO en el rosado?","Pressing the skins after fermentation":"Prensado de las pieles tras la fermentación","Crushing the black grapes":"Estrujado de las uvas tintas","Adding yeast":"Adición de levaduras","Bottling":"Embotellado","Rosé skins are removed early, so there is nothing to press afterwards.":"En el rosado las pieles se retiran pronto, así que no hay que prensarlas después.","Both wines go through crushing, adding yeast, fermentation, draining, maturation and bottling. For red, however, the skins stay until fermentation ends and are then pressed to recover the wine. For rosé the juice leaves the skins after a few hours, so this final pressing does not happen.":"Ambos vinos pasan por el estrujado, las levaduras, la fermentación, el escurrido, la crianza y el embotellado. En el tinto, sin embargo, las pieles se quedan hasta el final de la fermentación y después se prensan para recuperar el vino. En el rosado el zumo deja las pieles tras unas horas, así que ese prensado final no existe.","In which wine is pressing done BEFORE fermentation?":"¿En qué tipo de vino el prensado se hace ANTES de la fermentación?","White wine":"En el vino blanco","Red wine":"En el vino tinto","Rosé wine":"En el vino rosado","None of them":"En ninguno","White grapes are pressed first so only the juice ferments.":"En el blanco se prensa enseguida para fermentar solo el zumo.","For white wine the grapes are crushed and then pressed, so the juice is separated from the skins and ferments on its own. For red, fermentation happens with the skins, which are only pressed after draining. For rosé the juice is drained off the skins after a few hours, with no final pressing.":"En el blanco, la uva se estruja y luego se prensa, de modo que el zumo se separa de las pieles y fermenta solo. En el tinto, la fermentación se hace con las pieles, que solo se prensan tras el escurrido. En el rosado, el zumo se escurre de las pieles tras unas horas, sin prensado final.","Where can wines be matured after fermentation?":"¿Dónde pueden criarse los vinos tras la fermentación?","In stainless steel tanks or oak barrels":"En depósitos de acero o en barricas de roble","Only among the pressed skins":"Solo entre las pieles prensadas","Only on the vine":"Solo en la vid","Only in an ice bucket":"Solo en una cubitera con hielo","Maturation uses stainless steel or oak, for whites, reds and rosés.":"La crianza se hace en acero o en roble, para blancos, tintos y rosados.","Once fermentation is over, the wine can rest in stainless steel tanks or oak barrels. This applies to whites, reds and rosés, although oak is rare for rosé. Oak, as you will see later, can give the wine aromas of its own. After maturation the wine is bottled.":"Una vez terminada la fermentación, el vino puede reposar en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble. Vale para blancos, tintos y rosados, aunque en los rosados el roble es raro. El roble, como se verá más adelante, puede dar al vino aromas propios. Tras la crianza, el vino se embotella.","How should wine be kept for long-term storage?":"¿Cómo debe guardarse un vino durante mucho tiempo?","Cool, at a constant temperature":"En fresco, a temperatura constante","Warm, at a constant temperature":"En calor, a temperatura constante","Cool at night, warm by day":"En fresco de noche, en calor de día","Next to a bright window":"Junto a una ventana luminosa","Cool and steady: extremes and swings in temperature damage wine.":"Fresco y constante: los extremos y cambios de temperatura dañan el vino.","For long-term storage, wine needs a cool place with a stable temperature. Extreme heat or cold, as well as big swings, can damage it, making it lose character and eventually causing faults. Bright light should also be avoided, because it makes the wine lose its fruitiness.":"Para guardarlo mucho tiempo, el vino necesita un lugar fresco y con temperatura estable. El calor o el frío extremos, igual que los cambios bruscos, pueden estropearlo, hacerle perder carácter y, a la larga, provocar defectos. También hay que evitar la luz intensa, que le hace perder la fruta.","What can strong sunshine and bright artificial light do to wine?":"¿Qué efecto pueden tener el sol fuerte y la luz artificial intensa en el vino?","Make it lose its fruity character":"Hacerle perder su carácter afrutado","Raise its alcohol level":"Aumentar su grado alcohólico","Make it sweeter":"Hacerlo más dulce","Increase its tannins":"Aumentar sus taninos","Light, and the heat it brings, strip wine of its fruitiness.":"La luz y el calor que genera quitan al vino su fruta.","Bottles should be kept away from strong sunshine and bright artificial light. Both the light and the heat it gives off can make a wine lose its fruity character. They do not change the alcohol, sugar or tannin: the damage is mainly to the fruit aromas and flavours.":"Las botellas deben mantenerse lejos del sol fuerte y de la luz artificial intensa. Tanto la luz como el calor que produce pueden hacer que el vino pierda su carácter afrutado. No cambian el alcohol, el azúcar ni los taninos: el daño afecta sobre todo a los aromas y sabores de fruta.","Why should a bottle sealed with a cork be stored on its side?":"¿Por qué una botella con corcho se guarda tumbada?","The cork stays moist and keeps air out":"El corcho sigue húmedo y no deja entrar aire","The wine matures faster":"El vino madura más rápido","The wine becomes sweeter":"El vino se vuelve más dulce","It saves space in the cellar":"Se ahorra espacio en la bodega","Lying down, the cork touches the wine and does not dry out.":"Tumbada, el corcho toca el vino y no se seca.","With the bottle on its side, the cork stays in contact with the wine and remains moist. A dried-out cork can let air into the bottle, and air makes the wine lose its fruity character. Screwcap bottles do not run this risk and can be stored upright.":"Con la botella tumbada, el corcho sigue en contacto con el vino y se mantiene húmedo. Un corcho seco puede dejar entrar aire en la botella, y el aire hace que el vino pierda su carácter afrutado. Las botellas con tapón de rosca no corren este riesgo y pueden guardarse de pie.","How can screwcap bottles be stored?":"¿Cómo pueden guardarse las botellas con tapón de rosca?","Standing up":"De pie, sin problema","Only on their side":"Solo tumbadas","Only upside down":"Solo boca abajo","Only near a heat source":"Solo cerca de una fuente de calor","With no cork to keep moist, the bottle can stand up.":"Sin corcho que mantener húmedo, la botella puede estar de pie.","Lying a bottle down only serves to keep a cork moist, so it does not dry out and let air in. A screwcap has no such problem, so the bottle can be stored standing up. The other rules, a cool and constant temperature and no bright light, still apply.":"Tumbar la botella solo sirve para mantener húmedo el corcho, de modo que no se seque y no deje entrar aire. El tapón de rosca no tiene ese problema, así que la botella puede guardarse de pie. Las demás reglas, fresco, temperatura constante y sin luz intensa, siguen valiendo.","How does a vacuum system keep opened wine fresh?":"¿Cómo funciona un sistema de vacío para el vino abierto?","A pump removes air from the bottle":"Una bomba saca el aire de la botella","A gas pushes the air out":"Un gas expulsa el aire","Ice chills the bottle neck":"El hielo enfría el cuello","The cork is sealed with wax":"El corcho se sella con cera","A vacuum pumps air out; a blanket system pushes it out with gas.":"El vacío saca el aire; el sistema de gas lo expulsa.","Opened wine goes stale because it reacts with air. Vacuum systems use a pump to draw the air out of the bottle, reducing this contact. They should not be confused with blanket systems, which instead pump in a harmless gas to push the air out.":"El vino abierto se enrancia porque reacciona con el aire. Los sistemas de vacío usan una bomba para extraer el aire de la botella y reducir ese contacto. No hay que confundirlos con los sistemas de manta de gas, que introducen un gas inocuo para expulsar el aire.","How does a blanket system work?":"¿Cómo funciona un sistema de «manta» de gas?","A harmless gas pushes the air out":"Un gas inocuo expulsa el aire","A pump draws out the wine":"Una bomba saca el vino","A cloth covers the bottle":"Un paño cubre la botella","Fresh wine is added daily":"Se añade vino nuevo cada día","The gas takes the air's place and does not harm the wine.":"El gas ocupa el lugar del aire y no daña el vino.","In blanket systems a gas is pumped into the bottle, pushing the air out. The gas does not harm the wine and shields it from contact with air, which would otherwise make it stale. It is an alternative to a vacuum system, which removes the air with a pump.":"En los sistemas de manta se introduce en la botella un gas que expulsa el aire. El gas no daña el vino y lo protege del contacto con el aire, que de otro modo lo enranciaría. Es una alternativa al sistema de vacío, que saca el aire con una bomba.","What is the simplest way to keep an opened wine fresher?":"¿Cuál es la forma más sencilla de mantener fresco un vino abierto?","Recork it and keep it in the fridge":"Taparlo y meterlo en el frigorífico","Leave it open on the table":"Dejarlo abierto en la mesa","Warm it near a radiator":"Calentarlo junto a un radiador","Put it in sunlight":"Ponerlo al sol","Cork and fridge slow down the wine going stale.":"Tapón y frigorífico frenan que el vino se enrancie.","After opening, wine reacts with air and slowly loses its freshness. Putting the cork back and keeping it in the fridge helps it last longer. For even longer, vacuum or blanket systems can be used. Heat and light, on the other hand, only make things worse.":"Tras abrirlo, el vino reacciona con el aire y poco a poco pierde frescura. Volver a taparlo y guardarlo en el frigorífico ayuda a que dure más. Para más tiempo aún, se pueden usar sistemas de vacío o de manta de gas. El calor y la luz, en cambio, empeoran las cosas.","At what temperature should a sweet wine such as Sauternes be served?":"¿A qué temperatura se sirve un vino dulce como el Sauternes?","Well chilled, 6–8°C (43–45°F)":"Muy frío, 6–8 °C","Lightly chilled, 10–13°C (50–55°F)":"Ligeramente fresco, 10–13 °C","Lightly chilled, about 13°C (55°F)":"Ligeramente fresco, unos 13 °C","Room temperature, 15–18°C (59–64°F)":"Temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C","Sweet wines such as Sauternes are served well chilled, at 6–8°C.":"Los vinos dulces, como el Sauternes, se sirven muy fríos, a 6–8 °C.","Sweet wines are among the coldest-served wines, together with sparkling wines. The recommended range for a sweet wine such as Sauternes is 6–8°C. By contrast, 10–13°C suits full-bodied whites, around 13°C suits light reds, and 15–18°C suits medium- and full-bodied reds.":"Los vinos dulces están entre los que se sirven más fríos, junto con los espumosos. El intervalo recomendado para un dulce como el Sauternes es de 6 a 8 °C. En cambio, 10–13 °C corresponde a los blancos con cuerpo, unos 13 °C a los tintos ligeros y 15–18 °C a los tintos medios o con cuerpo.","How should a sparkling wine such as Champagne be served?":"¿Cómo se sirve un espumoso como el Champagne?","Well chilled, 6–10°C (43–50°F)":"Muy frío, 6–10 °C","Slightly warmed":"Ligeramente templado","Sparkling wines are served well chilled, between 6 and 10°C.":"Los espumosos se sirven muy fríos, entre 6 y 10 °C.","Champagne and other sparkling wines should be served well chilled, in the 6–10°C range. Cold also has a practical benefit: it reduces the pressure in the bottle and makes opening safer. To keep it cool, use an ice bucket with ice and cold water or an insulated container.":"El Champagne y los demás espumosos se sirven muy fríos, entre 6 y 10 °C. El frío tiene además una ventaja práctica: reduce la presión de la botella y hace que abrirla sea más seguro. Para mantenerlo frío se puede usar una cubitera con hielo y agua fría o un recipiente aislante.","At what temperature should a light white such as Pinot Grigio be served?":"¿A qué temperatura se sirve un blanco ligero como el Pinot Grigio?","Chilled, 7–10°C (45–50°F)":"Frío, 7–10 °C","Light and medium whites and rosés: chilled, at 7–10°C.":"Blancos ligeros o medios y rosados: fríos, a 7–10 °C.","Light- and medium-bodied whites such as Pinot Grigio, and rosés, are served chilled at 7–10°C. Only fuller whites, such as an oaked Chardonnay, are served a little warmer, at 10–13°C. The remaining ranges, from lightly chilled to room temperature, apply to red wines.":"Los blancos ligeros o de cuerpo medio, como el Pinot Grigio, y los rosados se sirven fríos, entre 7 y 10 °C. Solo los blancos con más cuerpo, como una Chardonnay criada en roble, se sirven algo menos fríos, a 10–13 °C. Los demás valores corresponden a los tintos.","Which wine is served lightly chilled at 10–13°C (50–55°F)?":"¿Qué vino se sirve «ligeramente fresco» a 10–13 °C?","An oaked Chardonnay":"Una Chardonnay criada en roble","A Champagne":"Un Champagne","A Sauternes":"Un Sauternes","A Shiraz":"Un Shiraz","Full-bodied whites, like oaked Chardonnay, are served lightly chilled.":"Los blancos con cuerpo, como la Chardonnay con roble, se sirven ligeramente frescos.","A full-bodied white, such as an oaked Chardonnay, is served a little less cold than other whites, at 10–13°C. Champagne and Sauternes are served well chilled, while a Shiraz, a medium- to full-bodied red, is served at room temperature, 15–18°C.":"Un blanco con cuerpo, como una Chardonnay criada en roble, se sirve algo menos frío que los demás blancos, a 10–13 °C. El Champagne y el Sauternes se sirven muy fríos, mientras que un Shiraz, tinto de cuerpo medio a alto, se sirve a temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C.","How should a light-bodied red such as Beaujolais be served?":"¿Cómo se sirve un tinto ligero como el Beaujolais?","Warmed above 20°C (68°F)":"Calentado por encima de 20 °C","Light reds are served lightly chilled, at around 13°C.":"Los tintos ligeros se sirven ligeramente frescos, hacia 13 °C.","Not all reds are served at room temperature. Light-bodied ones such as Beaujolais are more enjoyable lightly chilled, at around 13°C. Medium- and full-bodied reds such as Shiraz, on the other hand, are served at room temperature, between 15 and 18°C.":"No todos los tintos se sirven a temperatura ambiente. Los de cuerpo ligero, como el Beaujolais, resultan más agradables ligeramente frescos, hacia 13 °C. Los tintos de cuerpo medio o con cuerpo, como el Shiraz, se sirven en cambio a temperatura ambiente, entre 15 y 18 °C.","Which range is recommended for a full-bodied red such as Shiraz?":"¿Qué intervalo se recomienda para un tinto con cuerpo como el Shiraz?","15–18°C (59–64°F)":"15–18 °C","6–8°C (43–45°F)":"6–8 °C","7–10°C (45–50°F)":"7–10 °C","10–13°C (50–55°F)":"10–13 °C","Medium and full reds are served at room temperature, 15–18°C.":"Los tintos medios y con cuerpo se sirven a temperatura ambiente, 15–18 °C.","For medium- and full-bodied reds, 'room temperature' means 15–18°C. Because heating and air conditioning make room temperatures vary a lot, it is safer to rely on this range. The colder ranges are for whites, rosés, sparkling wines and sweet wines.":"Para los tintos de cuerpo medio o con cuerpo, la «temperatura ambiente» equivale a 15–18 °C. Como la calefacción y el aire acondicionado hacen variar mucho la temperatura de las salas, es más seguro guiarse por este intervalo. Los intervalos más fríos son para blancos, rosados, espumosos y vinos dulces.","How should an ice bucket be filled to keep wine cool?":"¿Cómo se llena una cubitera para mantener frío el vino?","With ice and cold water":"Con hielo y agua fría","With ice only":"Solo con hielo","With room-temperature water only":"Solo con agua del tiempo","With salt and dry ice":"Con sal y hielo seco","Ice alone cools much less efficiently.":"Solo con hielo, la cubitera enfría mucho peor.","To keep a wine cool until the bottle is finished, you can use an insulated container or an ice bucket. If you choose a bucket, fill it with ice and cold water together: the water surrounds the bottle and chills it far more effectively than ice on its own.":"Para mantener frío un vino hasta terminar la botella se puede usar un recipiente aislante o una cubitera. Si se elige la cubitera, hay que llenarla de hielo y agua fría a la vez: el agua rodea la botella y la enfría mucho mejor que el hielo solo.","A red wine is too cold. What should you do?":"Un tinto está demasiado frío. ¿Qué conviene hacer?","Let it warm up naturally in the room":"Dejar que se temple solo en la sala","Place it next to a radiator":"Ponerlo junto a un radiador","Stand it in boiling water":"Meterlo en agua hirviendo","Heat it in a microwave":"Calentarlo en el microondas","Heating damages the flavours; let the wine warm up by itself.":"Calentar el vino estropea sus sabores; mejor dejar que se temple solo.","Putting wine near a heat source such as a radiator can damage its flavours. The right approach is to take the bottle into the room where it will be served and let its temperature rise naturally. With a little advance planning, the wine will reach the right temperature.":"Acercar el vino a una fuente de calor, como un radiador, puede estropear sus sabores. Lo correcto es llevar la botella a la sala donde se va a servir y dejar que la temperatura suba de forma natural. Con un poco de antelación, el vino llegará a la temperatura adecuada.","When opening sparkling wine, from when must your hand stay on the cork?":"Al abrir un espumoso, ¿desde cuándo hay que tener siempre la mano sobre el corcho?","From loosening the wire cage":"Desde que se afloja el morrión","Only once the cork is out":"Solo cuando ha salido el corcho","Only when pouring the wine":"Solo al servir el vino","From when it goes in the fridge":"Desde que está en el frigorífico","Once the cage is loose, pressure can shoot the cork out.":"Aflojado el morrión, la presión puede hacer saltar el corcho.","A bottle of sparkling wine holds a lot of pressure, and even when chilled the cork can fly out and hurt someone. That is why, as soon as the wire cage is loosened, the cork must be covered by your hand and kept under control until it is fully out of the bottle.":"Una botella de espumoso tiene mucha presión y, aunque esté fría, el corcho puede salir volando y herir a alguien. Por eso, en cuanto se afloja el morrión, hay que cubrir el corcho con la mano y mantenerlo controlado hasta que esté completamente fuera de la botella.","What is the correct technique for opening sparkling wine?":"¿Cuál es la técnica correcta para abrir un espumoso?","Hold the bottle at an angle and turn the bottle":"Botella inclinada y se gira la botella","Hold the bottle upright and twist the cork":"Botella recta y se gira el corcho","Shake the bottle and push the cork":"Se agita la botella y se empuja el corcho","Use a screw corkscrew":"Se usa un sacacorchos de rosca","Hold the cork still and turn the tilted bottle.":"Se sujeta el corcho y se gira la botella inclinada.","After removing the foil and loosening the cage, tilt the bottle, hold the cork in one hand and the base in the other, and turn the bottle. Holding the cork firmly lets the pressure escape gently, with a quiet sigh and without losing any wine.":"Tras quitar el papel de aluminio y aflojar el morrión, se inclina la botella, se sujeta el corcho con una mano y la base con la otra, y se gira la botella. Al sujetar el corcho con firmeza, la presión sale despacio, con un leve suspiro y sin perder vino.","What should you do right after pulling the cork from a still wine?":"¿Qué se hace justo después de sacar el corcho de un vino tranquilo?","Wipe the neck inside and out with a cloth":"Limpiar el cuello por dentro y por fuera","Put the capsule back on at once":"Volver a poner la cápsula","Shake the bottle":"Agitar la botella","Warm the bottle neck":"Calentar el cuello de la botella","Once the cork is out, wipe the neck inside and out.":"Tras sacar el corcho, se limpia el cuello por dentro y por fuera.","To open a still wine with a cork, remove the top of the capsule and wipe the neck; then centre the corkscrew, screw it in and draw the cork out gently. Finally, run a cloth round the neck, both inside and outside, before serving.":"Para abrir un vino tranquilo con corcho, se quita la parte superior de la cápsula y se limpia el cuello; después se centra el sacacorchos, se enrosca y se saca el corcho con suavidad. Por último, se pasa un paño por el cuello, por dentro y por fuera, antes de servir.","Why do the best wine glasses narrow at the rim?":"¿Por qué las mejores copas se estrechan hacia el borde?","To concentrate the wine's aromas":"Para concentrar los aromas del vino","To keep the wine warmer":"Para mantener el vino más caliente","To reduce the amount poured":"Para reducir la cantidad servida","To make bubbles last longer":"Para que las burbujas duren más","The shape keeps aromas in the glass so they are easier to appreciate.":"La forma retiene los aromas en la copa para apreciarlos mejor.","There are many glass shapes, but the best have a bowl that narrows towards the top. This keeps the aromas concentrated inside so they can be appreciated better. It is the same reason a wide glass narrowing at the top is chosen for tasting.":"Hay muchísimas formas de copa, pero las mejores tienen un cáliz que se estrecha hacia arriba. Así los aromas se quedan concentrados dentro y se aprecian mejor. Por el mismo motivo, en una cata se elige una copa amplia que se estrecha en la parte superior.","In which glass is sparkling wine usually served?":"¿En qué copa se suele servir un espumoso?","A flute":"En copa flauta","A red wine glass":"En copa de tinto","A white wine glass":"En copa de blanco","A tumbler":"En un vaso","Sparkling wines go in flutes; reds in glasses slightly larger than whites.":"Los espumosos van en copa flauta; los tintos, en copas algo más grandes que los blancos.","Sparkling wines are usually served in flutes, while red wine glasses are slightly larger than white wine glasses. Whatever the shape, the glass must be completely clean and polished before use, because dirt and traces of detergent can spoil the wine.":"Normalmente los espumosos se sirven en copa flauta, mientras que las copas de tinto son algo más grandes que las de blanco. Sea cual sea la forma, la copa debe estar limpia y abrillantada, porque la suciedad y los restos de detergente pueden estropear el vino.","Before serving, which smell suggests a wine may be faulty?":"Antes de servir, ¿qué olor puede indicar un defecto?","A wet cardboard smell":"Olor a cartón mojado","A fresh fruit aroma":"Aroma de fruta fresca","Vanilla notes from oak":"Notas de vainilla del roble","Delicate floral aromas":"Aromas florales delicados","Stale, wet cardboard or vinegar smells can signal a fault.":"Olores a rancio, cartón mojado o vinagre pueden indicar un defecto.","Before serving, check the appearance for haziness or floating bits, then the nose. A sound wine should not smell stale or of wet cardboard or vinegar. Fruit, flowers and vanilla from oak, on the other hand, are normal and pleasant aromas.":"Antes de servir se comprueba el aspecto, buscando turbidez o trocitos, y después la nariz. Un vino en buen estado no debe oler a rancio ni tener olores de cartón mojado o de vinagre. La fruta, las flores y la vainilla del roble son, en cambio, aromas normales y agradables.","When checking a wine's appearance before serving, what may indicate a fault?":"Al mirar el vino antes de servirlo, ¿qué puede indicar un defecto?","Haziness":"Un aspecto turbio","A pink colour":"Un color rosa","A golden colour":"Un color dorado","A deep red colour":"Un color rojo intenso","A hazy wine may be faulty; floating bits should also be avoided.":"Un vino turbio puede tener un defecto; tampoco debe haber trocitos flotando.","Pink, golden or deep red are simply the colours of different types of wine. A hazy wine, however, may point to a fault. Before serving you should also check that nothing is floating in the wine and that it does not smell stale or of vinegar.":"El rosa, el dorado o el rojo intenso son simplemente los colores de distintos tipos de vino. Un vino turbio, en cambio, puede indicar un defecto. Antes de servir también se comprueba que no haya trocitos flotando y que no huela a rancio ni a vinagre.","When recommending a wine with food, what matters most?":"Al recomendar un vino para un plato, ¿qué es lo más importante?","The person's own preferences":"Los gustos de la persona","The price of the bottle":"El precio de la botella","The vintage of the wine":"La añada del vino","The colour of the dish":"El color del plato","If someone dislikes that style of wine, there is no point suggesting it.":"Si a alguien no le gusta ese estilo de vino, no tiene sentido recomendarlo.","A pairing may seem exceptional to the person suggesting it, but the first criterion is always what the person drinking the wine likes or dislikes. Only after that do the food and wine interactions come in, helping you avoid the combinations that most people find unpleasant.":"Un maridaje puede parecer excepcional a quien lo propone, pero el primer criterio es siempre lo que le gusta o no a quien va a beber el vino. Solo después entran en juego las reacciones entre comida y vino, que ayudan a evitar las combinaciones que a la mayoría de la gente le resultan desagradables.","Sweet food makes a wine seem…":"Una comida dulce hace que el vino parezca…","More acidic and less fruity":"Más ácido y menos afrutado","Less acidic and more fruity":"Menos ácido y más afrutado","Sweeter and fuller-bodied":"Más dulce y con más cuerpo","Less bitter and sweeter":"Menos amargo y más dulce","Sweetness in food makes wine more acidic, bitter and less fruity.":"El dulzor de la comida hace el vino más ácido, amargo y menos afrutado.","Sweetness is one of the hardest elements to pair. It makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. That is why a dry wine served with a dessert can taste sour and dull. With sweet dishes, a wine with at least as much sweetness works better.":"El dulzor es uno de los elementos más difíciles de maridar. Hace que el vino parezca más secante y amargo, más ácido, y menos dulce y afrutado. Por eso un vino seco servido con un postre puede resultar agrio y apagado. Con platos dulces funciona mejor un vino que tenga al menos el mismo dulzor.","Which food component has the same effect on wine as sweetness?":"¿Qué componente de la comida tiene sobre el vino el mismo efecto que el dulzor?","Umami":"El umami","Salt":"La sal","Acidity":"La acidez","Fat":"La grasa","Umami and sweetness both make wine more bitter, acidic and less fruity.":"El umami y el dulzor hacen el vino más amargo, ácido y menos afrutado.","Umami and sweetness act on wine in the same way: they make it seem more drying and bitter, more acidic, and less sweet and fruity. Salt and acidity have the opposite effect, while fat only changes how acidic the wine seems, making it taste less acidic.":"El umami y el dulzor actúan sobre el vino de la misma manera: lo hacen parecer más secante y amargo, más ácido, y menos dulce y afrutado. La sal y la acidez tienen el efecto contrario, mientras que la grasa solo cambia la percepción de la acidez, que disminuye.","With an umami-rich dish, which wine is most likely to taste harsh?":"Con un plato rico en umami, ¿qué vino tiene más riesgo de resultar duro?","A very tannic red":"Un tinto muy tánico","A fruity rosé":"Un rosado afrutado","A sweet white":"Un blanco dulce","A light, low-tannin red":"Un tinto ligero poco tánico","Umami boosts bitterness and dryness, already strong in a tannic red.":"El umami aumenta amargor y sequedad, ya fuertes en un tinto tánico.","Umami makes a wine seem more drying and bitter, more acidic and less fruity. In a very tannic red, which already dries the mouth and can taste bitter, this effect adds up and the wine can turn harsh. A light, low-tannin red suffers much less.":"El umami hace que el vino parezca más secante y amargo, más ácido y menos afrutado. En un tinto muy tánico, que ya seca la boca y puede tener amargor, este efecto se suma y el vino puede volverse duro. Un tinto ligero y poco tánico lo sufre mucho menos.","What effect does salty food have on wine?":"¿Qué efecto tiene una comida salada sobre el vino?","It seems fruitier and fuller-bodied":"Lo hace parecer más afrutado y con cuerpo","It seems more bitter and acidic":"Lo hace parecer más amargo y ácido","It seems less fruity":"Lo hace parecer menos afrutado","It makes the alcohol stand out":"Hace que se note más el alcohol","Salt makes wine less bitter and acidic, fruitier and fuller.":"La sal hace el vino menos amargo y ácido, más afrutado y con cuerpo.","Salt is wine-friendly. Salty food makes a wine seem less drying and bitter, less acidic, fruitier and fuller-bodied. That is why salty dishes are generally easy to pair. Making the alcohol more noticeable, on the other hand, is the effect of chilli heat.":"La sal es una aliada del vino. Una comida salada lo hace parecer menos secante y amargo, menos ácido, más afrutado y con más cuerpo. Por eso los platos salados suelen ser fáciles de maridar. Que el alcohol se note más es, en cambio, el efecto del picante.","Acidic food makes a wine seem…":"Una comida ácida hace que el vino parezca…","Sweeter and fruitier":"Más dulce y afrutado","More acidic and bitter":"Más ácido y amargo","Less sweet and fruity":"Menos dulce y afrutado","More alcoholic and hot":"Más alcohólico y cálido","Acid in food makes wine less acidic, sweeter and fruitier.":"La acidez de la comida hace el vino menos ácido, más dulce y afrutado.","It may sound surprising, but acidic food makes a wine taste less acidic. It also makes it seem less drying and bitter, sweeter and fruitier. That is why a dish with a sharp, acidic note can soften a very crisp wine that might seem sharp on its own.":"Puede sorprender, pero una comida ácida hace que el vino se perciba menos ácido. También lo hace parecer menos secante y amargo, más dulce y más afrutado. Por eso un plato con un toque ácido puede suavizar un vino muy vivo que, solo, parecería punzante.","What happens to a delicate wine served with a very highly flavoured dish?":"¿Qué le pasa a un vino delicado servido con un plato de sabores muy intensos?","It is overwhelmed by the food":"La comida lo tapa","It seems fuller-bodied":"Parece tener más cuerpo","It seems sweeter":"Parece más dulce","It seems more tannic":"Parece más tánico","Very intense flavours cover the wine, which seems to vanish.":"Los sabores muy intensos cubren el vino, que parece desaparecer.","When food is very highly flavoured, the wine can be overwhelmed: its aromas and flavours can hardly be noticed. This is mainly a risk for delicate or light wines. With strongly flavoured dishes, it is better to choose a wine with enough flavour intensity to hold its own.":"Cuando la comida tiene sabores muy intensos, puede tapar el vino: sus aromas y sabores apenas se notan. Es sobre todo un riesgo para los vinos delicados o ligeros. Con platos muy sabrosos conviene, por tanto, un vino con suficiente intensidad de sabor para estar a la altura.","What effect does fatty or oily food have on wine?":"¿Qué efecto tiene una comida grasa u oleosa sobre el vino?","It makes it seem less acidic":"Lo hace parecer menos ácido","It makes it seem more acidic":"Lo hace parecer más ácido","It makes it seem more alcoholic":"Lo hace parecer más alcohólico","It makes it seem more bitter":"Lo hace parecer más amargo","Fat softens how acidic the wine seems.":"La grasa suaviza la percepción de la acidez del vino.","Fatty or oily food makes a wine seem less acidic. This is a useful effect to remember: a wine with high acidity can be pleasant alongside a rich, fatty dish. A stronger feel of alcohol comes from chilli instead, while extra bitterness comes from sweetness and umami.":"Una comida grasa u oleosa hace que el vino parezca menos ácido. Es un efecto útil de recordar: un vino de acidez alta puede resultar agradable junto a un plato rico en grasa. Que el alcohol se note más depende, en cambio, del picante, y el mayor amargor, del dulzor y del umami.","What happens when a high-alcohol wine is drunk with a chilli-hot dish?":"¿Qué ocurre al beber un vino muy alcohólico con un plato picante?","The chilli burn increases":"El ardor de la guindilla aumenta","The chilli burn disappears":"El ardor de la guindilla desaparece","The wine seems sweeter":"El vino parece más dulce","The wine seems less alcoholic":"El vino parece menos alcohólico","Alcohol boosts chilli heat, and chilli makes alcohol more noticeable.":"El alcohol aumenta el picante y el picante hace notar más el alcohol.","With chilli heat, the alcohol in the wine becomes more noticeable, and the alcohol in turn increases the burning sensation. The result is a pairing many people find uncomfortable. With chilli-hot dishes, it is therefore better to choose a wine that is not too high in alcohol.":"Con el picante, el alcohol del vino se nota más, y el alcohol, a su vez, aumenta la sensación de ardor. El resultado es un maridaje que mucha gente encuentra incómodo. Con platos picantes conviene, por tanto, elegir un vino no demasiado alcohólico.","Where can bitterness in a wine come from?":"¿De dónde puede venir el amargor de un vino?","Tannin or oak":"De los taninos o del roble","Leftover sugar":"Del azúcar residual","The grape pulp":"De la pulpa de la uva","Bitterness comes from skin tannins or from oak.":"El amargor viene de los taninos de las pieles o del roble.","In food pairing you often hear that a wine becomes 'more bitter'. This bitterness can come from tannins, found mainly in reds because they come from black grape skins, or from oak used to ferment or mature the wine. Sweetness and umami in food make it stronger.":"En los maridajes se suele decir que el vino se vuelve «más amargo». Ese amargor puede venir de los taninos, presentes sobre todo en los tintos porque proceden de la piel de las uvas tintas, o del roble usado para fermentar o criar el vino. El dulzor y el umami lo acentúan.","Which pair of food components makes wine seem less bitter and less acidic?":"¿Qué pareja de componentes de la comida hace el vino menos amargo y menos ácido?","Salt and acidity":"Sal y acidez","Sweetness and umami":"Dulzor y umami","Sweetness and chilli":"Dulzor y picante","Umami and chilli":"Umami y picante","Salt and acidity are the wine-friendly components that soften it.":"La sal y la acidez son los componentes aliados que suavizan el vino.","Salt and acidity make a wine seem less drying and bitter and less acidic; salt also makes it fruitier and fuller, acidity sweeter and fruitier. Sweetness and umami do the opposite, while chilli heat makes alcohol more noticeable and is boosted by it in turn.":"La sal y la acidez hacen que el vino parezca menos secante y amargo y menos ácido; la sal lo hace además más afrutado y con más cuerpo, y la acidez, más dulce y afrutado. El dulzor y el umami hacen lo contrario, y el picante hace notar más el alcohol y a su vez se intensifica con él.","With a very sweet dessert, which wine is the safest choice?":"Con un postre muy dulce, ¿qué vino es la elección más segura?","A wine at least as sweet":"Un vino al menos igual de dulce","A dry, tannic red":"Un tinto seco y tánico","A dry, high-acid white":"Un blanco seco y ácido","A dry, light rosé":"Un rosado seco y ligero","Sweet food strips sweetness and fruit from wine, so pick a sweet wine.":"El dulzor de la comida quita dulzor y fruta al vino: hace falta un vino dulce.","Sweet food makes a wine seem less sweet and fruity, more acidic and more bitter. A dry wine, especially a tannic or very acidic one, is likely to taste sour and harsh. A wine with at least as much sweetness as the dish keeps its balance instead.":"Una comida dulce hace que el vino parezca menos dulce y afrutado, más ácido y más amargo. Un vino seco, sobre todo si es tánico o muy ácido, puede resultar agrio y duro. Un vino con al menos el mismo dulzor que el plato, en cambio, mantiene su equilibrio.","With a chilli-hot dish, which wine is generally best avoided?":"Con un plato picante, ¿qué vino conviene evitar en general?","A high-alcohol wine":"Un vino muy alcohólico","A low-alcohol wine":"Un vino poco alcohólico","A fruity wine":"Un vino afrutado","A wine with some sweetness":"Un vino con algo de dulzor","Chilli brings out alcohol, which in turn increases the burn.":"El picante resalta el alcohol, que a su vez aumenta el ardor.","The interaction between chilli and alcohol works both ways: chilli heat makes the wine's alcohol more noticeable, and the alcohol makes the dish burn more. A high-alcohol wine is therefore likely to create an unpleasant pairing, while a wine with less alcohol accompanies the dish in better balance.":"La interacción entre picante y alcohol funciona en los dos sentidos: el picante hace que el alcohol del vino se note más, y el alcohol hace que el plato queme más. Un vino muy alcohólico puede crear, por tanto, un maridaje desagradable, mientras que uno con menos alcohol acompaña el plato con más equilibrio.","Which statement about food and wine pairing is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre el maridaje es correcta?","Most wines suit most foods for most people":"Casi cualquier vino va con casi cualquier plato","Every dish has only one right wine":"Cada plato tiene un único vino correcto","Red wine only suits meat":"El tinto solo va con carne","White wine only suits fish":"El blanco solo va con pescado","For most people, most wines are an acceptable match for most foods.":"Para la mayoría, la mayoría de los vinos acompañan bien a la mayoría de los platos.","Pairing is not a matter of rigid rules. For most people, most wines are an acceptable partner for most foods. You only need to know the few interactions that usually cause trouble, such as sweetness, umami and chilli, and your choices then become almost limitless.":"El maridaje no está hecho de reglas rígidas. Para casi todo el mundo, casi cualquier vino acompaña de forma aceptable a casi cualquier plato. Basta con conocer las pocas interacciones que suelen dar problemas, como el dulzor, el umami y el picante, para tener después una libertad casi ilimitada.","A very high-acid white tastes too sharp. Which dish will make it seem softer?":"Un blanco muy ácido parece demasiado punzante. ¿Qué plato lo hará parecer más suave?","A dish with an acidic touch":"Un plato con un toque ácido","A very sweet dessert":"Un postre muy dulce","An umami-rich dish":"Un plato rico en umami","A very hot chilli dish":"Un plato muy picante","Acidic food makes a wine seem less acidic, sweeter and fruitier.":"La comida ácida hace que el vino parezca menos ácido, más dulce y afrutado.","Acidic food 'absorbs' some of the perceived acidity: the wine seems less acidic, sweeter and fruitier. Sweetness and umami would do the opposite, making it even more acidic. Chilli does not reduce acidity but brings out alcohol. Salt or fat can also help.":"La comida ácida «absorbe» parte de la acidez percibida: el vino parece menos ácido, más dulce y más afrutado. El dulzor y el umami harían lo contrario, volviéndolo aún más ácido. El picante no reduce la acidez, sino que hace notar más el alcohol. La sal o la grasa también pueden ayudar.","Which type of food makes a wine seem fuller-bodied?":"¿Qué tipo de comida hace que un vino parezca con más cuerpo?","Salty food":"Una comida salada","Sweet food":"Una comida dulce","Umami-rich food":"Una comida rica en umami","Chilli-hot food":"Una comida picante","Salt makes wine seem fruitier and fuller-bodied.":"La sal hace que el vino parezca más afrutado y con más cuerpo.","Among the food components, salt is the one that adds perceived body to a wine, as well as making it fruitier, less bitter and less acidic. Sweetness and umami make it seem harsher and less fruity, while chilli heat mainly makes its alcohol stand out.":"Entre los componentes de la comida, la sal es la que aporta cuerpo percibido al vino, además de hacerlo más afrutado, menos amargo y menos ácido. El dulzor y el umami lo hacen parecer más duro y menos afrutado, mientras que el picante hace destacar sobre todo su alcohol.","Which wine is most at risk with a sweet dish?":"¿Qué vino corre más riesgo con un plato dulce?","A dry red with high tannin":"Un tinto seco con muchos taninos","A sweet white with good acidity":"Un blanco dulce con buena acidez","A medium-sweet, fruity white":"Un blanco semidulce y afrutado","A sweet, fruity rosé":"Un rosado dulce y afrutado","Sweet food boosts bitterness and dryness and removes fruit: a tannic red suffers.":"El dulzor aumenta amargor y sequedad y quita fruta: un tinto tánico sufre.","Sweet food makes a wine more drying and bitter, more acidic and less fruity. A dry, tannic red already has a strong drying feel and no sweetness to push back, so it becomes harsh. Sweet wines, by contrast, keep their balance better next to a sweet dish.":"Una comida dulce hace que el vino sea más secante y amargo, más ácido y menos afrutado. Un tinto seco y tánico ya tiene una fuerte sensación de sequedad y ningún dulzor que oponer, así que se vuelve duro. Los vinos dulces, en cambio, mantienen mejor su equilibrio junto a un plato dulce.","A red wine tastes fruitier and less bitter with a dish. Which food component is most likely responsible?":"Un tinto parece más afrutado y menos amargo con un plato. ¿Qué componente del plato es el más probable?","Sweetness":"El dulzor","Chilli heat":"El picante","Salt makes wine fruitier and less bitter.":"La sal hace el vino más afrutado y menos amargo.","Of the options given, only salt makes a wine fruitier and less bitter, as well as less acidic and fuller-bodied. Sweetness and umami have the opposite effect: more bitterness, less fruit. Chilli heat does not act on fruit and bitterness, but it makes the wine's alcohol stand out.":"De las opciones, solo la sal hace que el vino sea más afrutado y menos amargo, además de menos ácido y con más cuerpo. El dulzor y el umami tienen el efecto contrario: más amargor y menos fruta. El picante no actúa sobre la fruta ni el amargor, sino que hace destacar el alcohol.","Why is it useful to know the common food and wine interactions?":"¿Por qué es útil conocer las interacciones entre comida y vino?","To avoid what most people find unpleasant":"Para evitar lo que a casi todos les desagrada","To impose your taste on others":"Para imponer tu gusto a los demás","To always choose the same wine":"Para elegir siempre el mismo vino","To pair only expensive wines":"Para maridar solo vinos caros","Knowing what to avoid makes your pairing options almost limitless.":"Sabiendo qué evitar, las opciones de maridaje se vuelven casi ilimitadas.","Knowing the typical reactions, from sweetness, umami, salt and acid to intense flavour, fat and chilli, is not about finding the one right wine. It is about knowing what most people would want to avoid. That way you are never tied to one pairing and can always start from the person's own taste.":"Conocer las reacciones típicas, es decir, dulzor, umami, sal, ácido, sabores intensos, grasa y picante, no sirve para encontrar el único vino correcto, sino para saber qué querría evitar la mayoría de la gente. Así nunca se depende de un solo maridaje y siempre se puede partir de los gustos de la persona.","Which food component makes a medium-sweet wine seem LESS sweet?":"¿Qué componente de la comida hace que un vino semidulce parezca MENOS dulce?","Umami takes away sweetness and fruit, just as sweet food does.":"El umami quita dulzor y fruta al vino, igual que la comida dulce.","Umami works like sweetness in food: the wine seems less sweet and less fruity, more bitter and more acidic. Acidity in food does the opposite and makes the wine seem sweeter and fruitier; salt makes it fruitier and fuller, while fat only reduces the perceived acidity.":"El umami actúa como el dulzor de la comida: el vino parece menos dulce y menos afrutado, más amargo y más ácido. La acidez de la comida hace lo contrario y lo vuelve más dulce y afrutado; la sal lo hace más afrutado y con cuerpo, y la grasa solo reduce la acidez percibida.","In what order does the systematic approach to tasting run?":"¿En qué orden se sigue el enfoque sistemático de la cata?","Appearance, nose, palate":"Aspecto, nariz, boca","Nose, appearance, palate":"Nariz, aspecto, boca","Palate, nose, appearance":"Boca, nariz, aspecto","Appearance, palate, nose":"Aspecto, boca, nariz","First look, then smell, then taste.":"Primero se mira, luego se huele y por último se prueba.","The systematic approach always follows the same order: appearance (colour), nose (fruit, oak and other aromas) and palate (structure and flavours). Repeating the same route for every wine lets you write consistent, accurate notes that you can compare over time.":"El enfoque sistemático sigue siempre el mismo orden: aspecto (el color), nariz (aromas de fruta, roble y otros) y boca (estructura y sabores). Repetir el mismo recorrido con cada vino permite escribir notas coherentes y precisas, que se pueden comparar con el tiempo.","Why is it useful to take the same approach with every wine you taste?":"¿Por qué es útil seguir siempre el mismo método de cata?","To write accurate notes you can compare":"Para escribir notas precisas y comparables","To drink more wine in less time":"Para beber más vino en menos tiempo","To warm the wine in the glass":"Para calentar el vino en la copa","To avoid looking at the colour":"Para no tener que mirar el color","A consistent method gives accurate notes to refer back to.":"Un método constante da notas precisas para consultar después.","Approaching every sample the same way helps you not to miss anything and to describe wines with the same words. Your tasting notes are then accurate and can be read again and compared later, for example to remember the differences between two grape varieties.":"Abordar cada muestra de la misma forma ayuda a no olvidar nada y a describir los vinos con las mismas palabras. Así las notas de cata resultan precisas y se pueden releer y comparar más adelante, por ejemplo para recordar las diferencias entre dos uvas.","Why do you need a white surface when tasting?":"¿Por qué hace falta una superficie blanca en la cata?","To judge the colour better":"Para juzgar mejor el color","To smell the aromas better":"Para oler mejor los aromas","To keep the wine cool":"Para mantener fresco el vino","To measure the alcohol":"Para medir el alcohol","A white background helps you assess the wine's appearance.":"El fondo blanco ayuda a valorar el aspecto del vino.","Colour is what you look at during the appearance stage, and a white background lets you see it without interference. The other preparations are for the nose and palate: no distracting smells, a glass that concentrates the aromas, and a palate free of flavours such as coffee or toothpaste.":"El color es lo que se observa en la fase de aspecto, y un fondo blanco permite verlo sin interferencias. Los demás preparativos son para la nariz y la boca: sin olores que distraigan, una copa que concentre los aromas y una boca libre de sabores como el café o la pasta de dientes.","Which of these could spoil a tasting?":"¿Cuál de estos puede estropear una cata?","Having just brushed your teeth":"Acabar de lavarse los dientes","Using a white surface":"Usar una superficie blanca","Using a glass that narrows at the top":"Usar una copa que se estrecha arriba","Tasting in a room with no smells":"Catar en una sala sin olores","Lingering flavours like toothpaste or coffee distort the wine.":"Sabores persistentes como pasta de dientes o café alteran el vino.","Tasting needs a clean palate, without flavours lingering in the mouth such as toothpaste or coffee, which would change how the wine tastes. A white surface, a glass that concentrates the aromas and a room free of smells are, on the other hand, ideal conditions for a good tasting.":"Para catar hace falta una boca limpia, sin sabores persistentes como los de la pasta de dientes o el café, que cambiarían la percepción del vino. Una superficie blanca, una copa que concentre los aromas y una sala sin olores son, en cambio, condiciones ideales para catar bien.","At this level, what do you assess at the appearance stage?":"A este nivel, ¿qué se observa en la fase de aspecto?","Colour: white, rosé or red":"El color: blanco, rosado o tinto","The wine's body":"El cuerpo del vino","The fruit aromas":"Los aromas de fruta","The tannin level":"El nivel de tanino","At appearance you look only at the wine's colour.":"En el aspecto solo se mira el color del vino.","In the basic systematic approach, appearance is only about colour: white, rosé or red. Aromas are assessed on the nose, while body, tannin and the other structural characteristics are judged on the palate, meaning when you actually taste the wine.":"En el enfoque sistemático básico, el aspecto solo se refiere al color: blanco, rosado o tinto. Los aromas se valoran en nariz, mientras que el cuerpo, el tanino y las demás características estructurales se juzgan en boca, es decir, al probar el vino.","Which three aroma families are used on the nose?":"¿Cuáles son las tres familias de aromas que se usan en nariz?","Fruit, oak, other":"Fruta, roble, otros","Sweet, sour, bitter":"Dulce, ácido, amargo","White, rosé, red":"Blanco, rosado, tinto","Light, medium, full":"Ligero, medio, con cuerpo","Aromas are grouped into fruit, oak and other.":"Los aromas se agrupan en fruta, roble y otros.","On the nose, aromas are described by grouping them into three families: fruit, which depends on grape variety and ripeness; oak, which gives notes such as vanilla or cedar; and other, which covers grass, flowers, earth, mushroom, leather and so on. The same families are then used for flavours on the palate.":"En nariz, los aromas se describen agrupándolos en tres familias: fruta, que depende de la uva y de su madurez; roble, que da notas como vainilla o cedro; y otros, que incluye hierba, flores, tierra, setas, cuero, etc. Las mismas familias sirven después para los sabores en boca.","Which of these aromas usually comes from oak?":"¿Cuál de estos aromas suele venir del roble?","Vanilla":"Vainilla","Lemon":"Limón","Grass":"Hierba","Strawberry":"Fresa","Oak gives notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke.":"El roble da notas de vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro y humo.","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, it can pick up aromas such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. Lemon and strawberry belong to the fruit family instead, while grass falls into the 'other' family, along with flowers, earth and leather.":"Cuando un vino fermenta o se cría en barricas de roble, puede adquirir aromas como vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro y humo. El limón y la fresa pertenecen, en cambio, a la familia de la fruta, mientras que la hierba entra en la familia «otros», junto con las flores, la tierra y el cuero.","Which aroma family do mushroom and leather belong to?":"¿En qué familia de aromas entran las setas y el cuero?","Other":"Otros","Fruit":"Fruta","Structure":"Estructura","Mushroom and leather are neither fruit nor oak, so they are 'other'.":"Las setas y el cuero no son fruta ni roble: entran en «otros».","The 'other' family gathers all aromas that are neither fruit nor oak: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. This wide variety is what makes wine so interesting. Structure, by contrast, is not an aroma family at all; it covers sensations such as acidity and tannin.":"La familia «otros» reúne todos los aromas que no son ni fruta ni roble: hierba, flores, hierbas aromáticas, verduras, tierra, setas y cuero. Esta gran variedad es lo que hace el vino tan interesante. La estructura, en cambio, no es una familia de aromas: se refiere a sensaciones como la acidez y el tanino.","Which structural characteristic makes your mouth water?":"¿Qué característica estructural hace salivar?","Body":"El cuerpo","Acidity makes your mouth water and gives freshness.":"La acidez hace salivar y da frescura al vino.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice and is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. It gives wine a refreshing character: too much makes it unpleasantly sharp, too little makes it lose freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth, while body describes how much the wine fills it.":"La acidez procede directamente del zumo de uva y se reconoce con facilidad porque hace salivar. Da al vino un carácter refrescante: demasiada lo vuelve agrio y demasiado poca le quita frescura. El tanino, en cambio, seca la boca, y el cuerpo describe cuánto la llena el vino.","What does the 'body' of a wine describe?":"¿Qué describe el «cuerpo» de un vino?","How mouth-filling the wine feels":"Cuánto llena el vino la boca","How deep the colour is":"Lo intenso que es el color","How much sugar it contains":"Cuánto azúcar contiene","How fruity it smells":"Cuánto huele a fruta","Body is the overall sense of fullness in the mouth.":"El cuerpo es la sensación global de plenitud en la boca.","Many factors contribute to body, so the easiest way to judge it is to ask how mouth-filling the wine is. Full-bodied wines feel dense and mouth-filling, light-bodied wines more delicate. Body is assessed on the palate, not by looking at the colour or smelling the wine.":"Muchos factores influyen en el cuerpo, así que la forma más sencilla de valorarlo es preguntarse cuánto llena el vino la boca. Los vinos con cuerpo parecen densos y envolventes; los ligeros, más delicados. El cuerpo se valora en boca, no mirando el color ni oliendo el vino.","Which list shows the structural characteristics assessed on the palate?":"¿Qué lista recoge las características estructurales que se valoran en boca?","Sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body":"Dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol, cuerpo","Colour, fruit, oak, alcohol, body":"Color, fruta, roble, alcohol, cuerpo","Fruit, oak, other, acidity, tannin":"Fruta, roble, otros, acidez, tanino","Sweetness, colour, fruit, alcohol, body":"Dulzor, color, fruta, alcohol, cuerpo","The five structural characteristics are sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body.":"Las cinco características estructurales son dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol y cuerpo.","On the palate you assess two things: structure and flavours. Structure covers sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body. Fruit, oak and other, on the other hand, are families of aromas and flavours, while colour belongs to the appearance stage. Keeping these categories apart makes your notes clearer.":"En boca se valoran dos cosas: la estructura y los sabores. La estructura abarca dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol y cuerpo. Fruta, roble y otros son, en cambio, familias de aromas y sabores, y el color pertenece a la fase de aspecto. Mantener separadas estas categorías hace que las notas sean más claras.","Tasting a red wine, your mouth feels dry. Which characteristic are you noticing?":"Al probar un tinto notas que la boca se seca. ¿Qué característica percibes?","Fruitiness":"La fruta","Tannin, from the grape skins, dries the mouth.":"El tanino, que viene de las pieles, seca la boca.","Tannin is typical of red wines because it comes from the skins of black grapes, which stay in contact with the juice during fermentation. It is felt more than tasted: the mouth dries out. Acidity, by contrast, makes your mouth water.":"El tanino es típico de los tintos porque procede de la piel de las uvas tintas, que se quedan en contacto con el zumo durante la fermentación. Se nota más como una sensación que como un sabor: la boca se seca. La acidez, en cambio, hace salivar.","Black grape skin":"Piel de la uva tinta","Deep colour and tannins, which make the mouth feel dry.":"Color intenso y taninos, que dejan la boca seca.","Grape pulp":"Pulpa de la uva","Soft part holding the juice: water, sugar and acid. Same colour in all grapes.":"Parte blanda con el zumo: agua, azúcar y ácido. Mismo color en todas las uvas.","Tannins":"Taninos","Substances in black grape skins that dry out the mouth.":"Sustancias de la piel de las uvas tintas que secan la boca.","The vine's yearly cycle":"Ciclo anual de la vid","Flowering in spring, ripening in summer, picking in late summer.":"Floración en primavera, maduración en verano, vendimia a finales de verano.","What changes as grapes ripen?":"¿Qué cambia cuando la uva madura?","More water and sugar, less acid, riper flavours, colour change.":"Más agua y azúcar, menos ácido, sabores más maduros, cambio de color.","Cool climate":"Clima fresco","Nearer the poles (Germany, northern France): less sugar, more acidity; often white grapes.":"Cerca de los polos (Alemania, norte de Francia): menos azúcar, más acidez; a menudo uvas blancas.","Warm climate":"Clima cálido","Nearer the Equator (parts of Australia and California): more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours; often black grapes.":"Cerca del ecuador (partes de Australia y California): más azúcar, menos acidez, sabores maduros; a menudo uvas tintas.","Chardonnay: cool or warm climate?":"Chardonnay: ¿clima fresco o cálido?","Cool: apple and lemon. Warm: peach and pineapple.":"Fresco: manzana y limón. Cálido: melocotón y piña.","Microscopic organisms that eat sugar and make alcohol and carbon dioxide.":"Organismos microscópicos que comen azúcar y producen alcohol y dióxido de carbono.","abv":"% vol.","Alcohol by volume: 10% abv = one tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"Parte de alcohol en el volumen del vino: 10 % = una décima parte es alcohol.","White wine steps":"Fases del vino blanco","Crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation, bottling.":"Estrujado, prensado, fermentación, crianza, embotellado.","Red wine steps":"Fases del vino tinto","Crushing, fermentation on skins, draining, pressing, maturation, bottling.":"Estrujado, fermentación con pieles, escurrido, prensado, crianza, embotellado.","Rosé wine steps":"Fases del vino rosado","Crushing, fermentation, draining after a few hours, maturation, bottling.":"Estrujado, fermentación, escurrido a las pocas horas, crianza, embotellado.","White wine from black grapes?":"¿Blanco con uvas tintas?","Yes: the juice is colourless; press gently before fermentation.":"Sí: el zumo es incoloro; se prensa con suavidad antes de fermentar.","Stainless steel or oak":"Acero inoxidable o roble","Vessels for fermenting and maturing wine; oak is rare for rosé.":"Recipientes para fermentar y criar el vino; en los rosados el roble es raro.","3 storage rules":"3 reglas para guardar el vino","Cool and constant; away from light; cork = bottle on its side.":"Fresco y constante; lejos de la luz; corcho = botella tumbada.","Why lay corked bottles down?":"¿Por qué tumbar las botellas con corcho?","The cork stays moist; a dry cork lets air in and the wine loses fruit.":"El corcho sigue húmedo; si se seca entra aire y el vino pierde fruta.","Vacuum system":"Sistema de vacío","A pump removes air from the opened bottle.":"Una bomba saca el aire de la botella abierta.","Blanket system":"Sistema de manta de gas","A harmless gas is pumped in to push the air out.":"Un gas inocuo expulsa el aire de la botella.","Sauternes and Champagne":"Sauternes y Champagne","Well chilled: 6–8°C (sweet) and 6–10°C (sparkling).":"Muy fríos: 6–8 °C (dulce) y 6–10 °C (espumoso).","Pinot Grigio and oaked Chardonnay":"Pinot Grigio y Chardonnay con roble","Chilled 7–10°C (light white); lightly chilled 10–13°C (full white).":"Fríos 7–10 °C (blanco ligero); ligeramente frescos 10–13 °C (blanco con cuerpo).","Beaujolais and Shiraz":"Beaujolais y Shiraz","Lightly chilled 13°C (light red); room temperature 15–18°C (full red).":"Ligeramente fresco 13 °C (tinto ligero); ambiente 15–18 °C (tinto con cuerpo).","Opening sparkling wine":"Abrir un espumoso","Hand on the cork once the cage is loose; bottle tilted; turn the bottle.":"Mano sobre el corcho tras el morrión; botella inclinada; se gira la botella.","Pairing rule no. 1":"Regla n.º 1 del maridaje","Start with the person's taste: never push a style they dislike.":"Partir de los gustos de la persona: no recomendar un estilo que no le guste.","Wine more drying, bitter and acidic; less sweet and fruity.":"Vino más secante, amargo y ácido; menos dulce y afrutado.","Same as sweetness: wine more bitter and acidic, less fruity.":"Igual que el dulzor: vino más amargo y ácido, menos afrutado.","Wine less bitter and acidic; fruitier and fuller.":"Vino menos amargo y ácido; más afrutado y con cuerpo.","Acidic food":"Comida ácida","Wine less bitter and acidic; sweeter and fruitier.":"Vino menos amargo y ácido; más dulce y afrutado.","Highly flavoured food":"Sabores muy intensos","Can overwhelm the wine.":"Pueden tapar el vino.","Fatty or oily food":"Comida grasa u oleosa","Makes the wine seem less acidic.":"Hace que el vino parezca menos ácido.","Alcohol increases the burn; the wine's alcohol stands out more.":"El alcohol aumenta el ardor; el alcohol del vino se nota más.","Systematic approach to tasting":"Enfoque sistemático de la cata","Appearance (colour) → nose (aromas) → palate (structure and flavours).":"Aspecto (color) → nariz (aromas) → boca (estructura y sabores).","Preparing to taste":"Prepararse para catar","No smells, white surface, wide glass narrowing at the top, clean palate.":"Sin olores, superficie blanca, copa amplia que se estrecha, boca limpia.","Oak aromas":"Aromas del roble","Vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke.":"Vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro, humo.","'Other' aromas":"Aromas «otros»","Grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather.":"Hierba, flores, hierbas, verduras, tierra, setas, cuero.","Structure on the palate":"Estructura en boca","Sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body.":"Dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol, cuerpo.","How mouth-filling the wine is: light = delicate, full = dense.":"Cuánto llena la boca: ligero = delicado, con cuerpo = denso.","Three types of wine: still, sparkling, fortified":"Tres tipos de vino: tranquilo, espumoso, fortificado","When people simply say «wine», they usually mean a still wine: one without bubbles. This is by far the biggest category. Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, though most sit between 11.5% and 14%. The abv figure (alcohol by volume) tells you how much of the liquid is alcohol, so a wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol.":"Cuando alguien dice simplemente «vino», casi siempre piensa en un vino tranquilo, es decir, sin burbujas. Es la categoría más amplia con diferencia. Los vinos tranquilos tienen entre un 8 % y un 15 % vol., aunque la mayoría se mueve entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %. La cifra «% vol.» (abv en inglés) indica qué parte del líquido es alcohol: un vino de 10 % vol. es una décima parte alcohol.","Many still wines take their name from the place where they are made: Sancerre and Burgundy in France, Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy. Others carry the name of the grape variety instead, such as a Pinot Grigio. Spotting which of the two naming logics a label uses is a quick first step towards knowing what will be in the glass.":"Muchos vinos tranquilos llevan el nombre de la zona donde se elaboran: Sancerre y Burgundy (Borgoña) en Francia, Rioja en España, Chianti en Italia. Otros, en cambio, indican el nombre de la variedad de uva, como un Pinot Grigio. Reconocer cuál de las dos lógicas sigue una etiqueta ayuda enseguida a saber qué esperar de la copa.","Sparkling wines are fizzy. Fermentation creates carbon dioxide gas, and if that gas is kept trapped inside the wine, it is released as bubbles once the bottle is opened. Champagne from France is the most famous example; Cava from Spain and Prosecco from Italy are also very well known. Sparkling wine is now made all around the world.":"Los vinos espumosos tienen burbujas. La fermentación genera dióxido de carbono y, si ese gas queda atrapado en el vino, sale en forma de burbujas al abrir la botella. El ejemplo más famoso es el Champagne francés; el Cava español y el Prosecco italiano también son muy conocidos. Hoy se elaboran espumosos en todo el mundo.","Fortified wines have had extra alcohol added to them. That is why they are stronger than still wines, usually somewhere between 15% and 22% abv. Two classic examples to remember are Sherry, from Spain, and Port, from Portugal. You will meet both again in the chapter on other wines to know.":"Los vinos fortificados son vinos a los que se ha añadido alcohol. Por eso tienen más graduación que los tranquilos: normalmente entre un 15 % y un 22 % vol. Dos ejemplos clásicos que conviene recordar son el Sherry (Jerez), de España, y el Port (Oporto), de Portugal. Volveremos a ellos en el capítulo de otros vinos que conocer.","Still: no bubbles, 8–15% abv (mostly 11.5–14%)":"Tranquilo: sin burbujas, 8–15 % vol. (casi siempre 11,5–14 %)","Sparkling: carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine":"Espumoso: dióxido de carbono de la fermentación atrapado en el vino","Fortified: extra alcohol added, 15–22% abv (Sherry, Port)":"Fortificado: alcohol añadido, 15–22 % vol. (Sherry, Port)","A wine may be named after its region or its grape":"Un vino puede llamarse como su zona o como su uva","Colour: white, red, rosé":"El color: blanco, tinto, rosado","A wine's colour depends on two things: the grape variety and the way the wine is made. There are white grapes and black grapes, but inside they look very alike: the pulp is the same colour in both and the juice has no colour. All the colour of a black grape sits in its skin, which also holds the tannins.":"El color de un vino depende de dos cosas: la variedad de uva y la forma de elaborarlo. Hay uvas blancas y uvas tintas, pero por dentro se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color en ambas y el zumo es incoloro. Todo el color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo (la piel), que además contiene los taninos.","White wines are usually made from white grapes, as in Chablis or a Riesling. Yet black grapes can also give a white wine. The trick is to separate the skins from the juice before fermentation, for example by pressing gently: since the colour lives in the skins, the juice stays pale and the finished wine is white.":"Los vinos blancos suelen elaborarse con uvas blancas, como un Chablis o un Riesling. Sin embargo, también se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas. Basta con separar los hollejos del zumo antes de la fermentación, por ejemplo con un prensado suave: como el color está en la piel, el zumo sigue claro y el vino resulta blanco.","A red wine, on the other hand, must come from black grapes. During fermentation the skins stay in the juice and are mixed in thoroughly, so they pass colour and tannin into the wine. Once fermentation is over, the new wine is drained off the skins. Rioja from Spain and Cabernet Sauvignon wines are red examples.":"Un vino tinto, en cambio, tiene que hacerse con uvas tintas. Durante la fermentación los hollejos permanecen en el zumo y se mezclan bien con él, de modo que le ceden color y tanino. Cuando termina la fermentación, el vino se separa de los hollejos. El Rioja español y los vinos de Cabernet Sauvignon son ejemplos de tintos.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, but the skin contact is short: just a few hours. The juice, by then only pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins, giving a lightly coloured wine. White Zinfandel from California is a rosé example. Rosé wines are also only rarely aged in oak.":"El rosado también procede de uvas tintas, pero el contacto con los hollejos es breve: apenas unas horas. Después el zumo, solo ligeramente rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. El resultado es un vino de color suave. El White Zinfandel de California es un ejemplo de rosado. Además, los rosados rara vez se crían en roble.","Black grape colour is in the skin; the juice is colourless":"El color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo; el zumo es incoloro","White: usually white grapes, possible from black grapes without skins":"Blanco: normalmente uvas blancas, también tintas sin hollejos","Red: black grapes only, skins kept through fermentation":"Tinto: solo uvas tintas, con hollejos durante toda la fermentación","Rosé: black grapes, a few hours of skin contact":"Rosado: uvas tintas, pocas horas de contacto con los hollejos","Structure (1): sweetness and acidity":"Estructura (1): dulzor y acidez","Sweetness comes from sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry: to make one, the yeast must turn all the sugar in the juice into alcohol, leaving little or none behind. Dry examples include Chablis and Sauvignon Blanc wines among whites, and Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon wines among reds.":"El dulzor depende del azúcar que queda en el vino. La mayoría de los vinos son secos: para lograrlo, las levaduras tienen que convertir en alcohol todo el azúcar del zumo, de modo que queda muy poco o nada. Son secos, por ejemplo, el Chablis y los Sauvignon Blanc entre los blancos, y el Côtes du Rhône, el Chianti y los Cabernet Sauvignon entre los tintos.","Medium-sweet wines are mostly white or rosé. There are two main ways to make them: remove the yeast before it has turned all the sugar into alcohol, or blend some unfermented grape juice into a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, are good examples.":"Los vinos de dulzor medio son sobre todo blancos o rosados. Se elaboran de dos maneras: retirando las levaduras antes de que hayan transformado todo el azúcar, o añadiendo zumo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Algunos Riesling alemanes y el White Zinfandel, el rosado californiano, son buenos ejemplos.","Sweet wines hold so much sugar that they can feel thick, almost syrupy. They can come from grapes so rich in sugar that the yeast stop before eating it all, as in Sauternes or some German Rieslings. In fortified wines, strong distilled alcohol is added, killing the yeast early; the sugar left behind makes Port and some Sherries sweet.":"Los vinos dulces tienen tanto azúcar que pueden resultar espesos, casi como un almíbar. Pueden proceder de uvas tan azucaradas que las levaduras se detienen antes de consumirlo todo, como en el Sauternes o en algunos Riesling alemanes. En los fortificados, en cambio, se añade alcohol destilado de alta graduación que mata las levaduras: el azúcar restante hace dulces el Port y algunos Sherry.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. Too much tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its freshness. Chablis, Chianti and wines from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir all have high acidity.":"La acidez procede directamente del zumo de uva y es lo que hace que un vino resulte refrescante. Es fácil de reconocer porque hace salivar. Demasiada acidez hace que el vino sea desagradablemente ácido; demasiado poca y pierde su frescura. El Chablis, el Chianti y los vinos de Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon y Pinot Noir tienen acidez alta.","In sweet wines, acidity is vital. It acts as a counterweight to the sugar and stops the wine from tasting cloying. That is why a good Sauternes or a sweet Riesling always has high acidity: sweetness and freshness balance each other, and every sip stays enjoyable to the end.":"En los vinos dulces, la acidez es esencial. Hace de contrapeso al azúcar y evita que el vino resulte empalagoso. Por eso un buen Sauternes o un Riesling dulce siempre tienen una acidez alta: dulzor y frescura se equilibran y cada sorbo sigue siendo agradable hasta el final.","Dry: yeast turn all the sugar into alcohol":"Seco: las levaduras convierten todo el azúcar en alcohol","Medium: yeast removed early, or unfermented juice added":"Medio: levaduras retiradas antes, o zumo sin fermentar añadido","Sweet: very sugary grapes, or added alcohol killing the yeast":"Dulce: uvas muy azucaradas, o alcohol añadido que mata las levaduras","Acidity: from the juice, makes the mouth water, balances sweetness":"Acidez: viene del zumo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor","Structure (2): tannin, alcohol and body":"Estructura (2): tanino, alcohol y cuerpo","Tannin belongs to red wines and comes from the skins of black grapes. How much a wine has depends on the grape variety and on the winemaking. It can taste a little bitter, but mostly it is something you feel: it leaves your mouth dry. Red Bordeaux and Chianti are high in tannin; Beaujolais and some Pinot Noir wines are low.":"El tanino es propio de los vinos tintos y procede de los hollejos de las uvas tintas. Su cantidad depende de la variedad y de la elaboración. Puede resultar algo amargo, pero sobre todo se nota como una sensación: deja la boca seca. El Bordeaux tinto y el Chianti tienen mucho tanino; el Beaujolais y algunos Pinot Noir, poco.","Nearly all still and sparkling wines sit between 11.5% and 14% abv. A few reach 15%, while others go as low as 8%. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a French red, is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. Remember that alcohol is produced when yeast ferment sugar.":"Casi todos los vinos tranquilos y espumosos tienen entre un 11,5 % y un 14 % vol. Algunos llegan al 15 % y otros bajan hasta el 8 %. El Châteauneuf-du-Pape, tinto francés, es un ejemplo de vino con mucho alcohol; el White Zinfandel californiano, de vino con poco. Recuerda que el alcohol se forma cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar.","Body describes the overall feel of a wine in your mouth. Many things contribute to it, so the easiest question to ask is: how mouth-filling is it? Full-bodied wines feel dense and rich, while light-bodied ones feel more delicate. Light: Pinot Grigio, Beaujolais. Medium: Sancerre, Côtes du Rhône. Full: Californian Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauternes.":"El cuerpo describe la sensación general del vino en la boca. Influyen muchos factores, así que la pregunta más sencilla es: ¿cuánto llena la boca? Un vino con cuerpo parece denso y envolvente; uno ligero, más delicado. Ligeros: Pinot Grigio y Beaujolais. Medios: Sancerre y Côtes du Rhône. Con mucho cuerpo: Cabernet Sauvignon de California y Sauternes.","Tannin: from skins, dries the mouth, a red-wine feature":"Tanino: de los hollejos, seca la boca, propio de los tintos","Alcohol: usually 11.5–14% abv, 8–15% for still and sparkling":"Alcohol: normalmente 11,5–14 % vol., entre 8 y 15 % en tranquilos y espumosos","Body: how mouth-filling the wine is (light, medium, full)":"Cuerpo: cuánto llena la boca el vino (ligero, medio, con cuerpo)","Aromas and flavours: fruit, oak, other":"Aromas y sabores: fruta, roble, otros","A wine's aromas and flavours come from different places. Some come straight from the grapes, while others develop during winemaking and maturation. Putting them into words feels hard at first, but it is a skill that grows with practice. A simple method is to ask three questions: do I notice fruit? Oak? Something else?":"Los aromas y sabores de un vino tienen orígenes distintos. Algunos proceden directamente de la uva y otros aparecen durante la elaboración y la crianza. Al principio cuesta describirlos, pero es una habilidad que mejora con la práctica. Un método sencillo es preguntarse: ¿noto fruta? ¿Noto roble? ¿Noto otra cosa?","Almost every wine smells of fruit. The kind of fruit depends first on the grape variety: Cabernet Sauvignon, for instance, smells of blackcurrant. Ripeness matters too. A Chardonnay from a cool climate shows green apple and lemon, whereas one from a warm climate leans towards peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple.":"Casi todos los vinos huelen a fruta. El tipo de fruta depende ante todo de la variedad: el Cabernet Sauvignon, por ejemplo, recuerda a la grosella negra. También influye la madurez de la uva: un Chardonnay de clima fresco recuerda a la manzana verde y al limón, mientras que uno de clima cálido tira hacia el melocotón y frutas tropicales como la piña.","Wine can be fermented and/or matured in oak barrels. When it is, the wood adds notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The use of oak is sometimes mentioned on the label. If you pick up these aromas alongside the fruit, it is a good clue that the wine has spent time in barrel.":"El vino puede fermentar y/o criarse en barricas de roble. En ese caso la madera aporta notas de vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro y ahumado. A veces el uso de roble aparece en la etiqueta. Si notas estos aromas junto a la fruta, es una buena pista de que el vino ha pasado por barrica.","Finally, there are the «other» aromas that make wine so varied and interesting: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. A Sauvignon Blanc, for example, can bring cut grass to mind, while Chianti can show dried herbs. Keeping them in a family of their own stops you confusing them with fruit.":"Por último están los «otros» aromas, que hacen el vino tan variado e interesante: hierba, flores, hierbas aromáticas, verduras, tierra, champiñón y cuero. Un Sauvignon Blanc, por ejemplo, puede recordar a hierba recién cortada, y el Chianti a hierbas secas. Agruparlos en una familia aparte ayuda a no confundirlos con la fruta.","Fruit: depends on the grape variety and its ripeness":"Fruta: depende de la variedad y de la madurez de la uva","Cool climate = apple, lemon; warm climate = peach, pineapple":"Clima fresco = manzana, limón; clima cálido = melocotón, piña","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke":"Roble: vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro, ahumado","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather":"Otros: hierba, flores, hierbas, verduras, tierra, champiñón, cuero","Style: the sum of the characteristics":"El estilo: la suma de las características","Each of the three types of wine, still, sparkling or fortified, can come in many different styles. A style brings together three elements: colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. Describing a style means putting these pieces together into one complete portrait of the wine.":"Cada uno de los tres tipos de vino, tranquilo, espumoso o fortificado, puede presentarse en muchos estilos. El estilo reúne tres elementos: el color, la estructura (dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol, cuerpo) y los aromas y sabores. Describir un estilo es juntar estas piezas en un retrato completo del vino.","A comparison makes this clear. Chablis and Sauternes are both French white wines, yet their styles are opposites. Chablis is dry, high in acidity, light to medium in body, with green apple and lemon and no oak. Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla from oak, held up by high acidity.":"Una comparación lo deja claro. El Chablis y el Sauternes son ambos blancos franceses y, sin embargo, sus estilos son opuestos. El Chablis es seco, de acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio, con manzana verde y limón y sin roble. El Sauternes es dulce y con cuerpo, con albaricoque, miel y vainilla del roble, sostenido por una acidez alta.","Style depends a lot on the climate where the grapes grow. The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have, giving fresher, lighter wines with green fruit and citrus. The warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity: flavours taste riper and, since sugar becomes alcohol, wines tend to be stronger and fuller.":"El estilo depende mucho del clima en que crece la uva. Cuanto más fresco, menos azúcar y más acidez tiene la uva: salen vinos más frescos y ligeros, con fruta verde y cítricos. Cuanto más cálido, más azúcar y menos acidez: los sabores son más maduros y, como el azúcar se convierte en alcohol, los vinos suelen tener más graduación y más cuerpo.","To describe a style, you follow a systematic approach to tasting. First the appearance: the colour (white, red, rosé). Then the nose: aromas of fruit, oak or other. Finally the palate: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body, plus the flavours. Always using the same order makes it easier to compare wines and remember them.":"Para describir un estilo se sigue un enfoque sistemático de la cata. Primero la vista: el color (blanco, tinto, rosado). Después la nariz: aromas de fruta, de roble u otros. Por último la boca: dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol y cuerpo, además de los sabores. Seguir siempre el mismo orden ayuda a quien estudia a comparar vinos y recordarlos.","Style = colour + structure + aromas and flavours":"Estilo = color + estructura + aromas y sabores","Cool climate: more acid, less sugar, lighter and fresher wines":"Clima fresco: más acidez, menos azúcar, vinos más ligeros y frescos","Warm climate: more sugar, less acid, riper flavours":"Clima cálido: más azúcar, menos acidez, sabores más maduros","Tasting: appearance, nose, palate, always in the same order":"Cata: vista, nariz, boca, siempre en el mismo orden","Chardonnay":"Chardonnay","Chardonnay is one of the most popular and widely planted grape varieties in the world. It makes dry wines, but in very different styles. The main reason is that it does well in both cool and warm climates and changes character with the ripeness of the grapes. Choices in the winery, above all the use of oak, also shape its style.":"La Chardonnay es una de las variedades más apreciadas y plantadas del mundo. Da vinos secos, pero en estilos muy distintos. La razón principal es que se adapta tanto a climas frescos como cálidos y cambia de carácter según lo madura que esté la uva. Las decisiones en bodega, sobre todo el uso del roble, también modifican su estilo.","In a cool climate the grapes ripen less, so they stay more acidic and less sugary. The result is a Chardonnay with high acidity, a light to medium body and aromas of green fruit (apple) and citrus (lemon). In a warm climate the grapes ripen further: the wine has medium acidity, a medium to full body and flavours of stone fruit (peach) and tropical fruit (pineapple, banana).":"En clima fresco la uva madura menos y se mantiene más ácida y menos azucarada. El resultado es un Chardonnay de acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio y aromas de fruta verde (manzana) y cítricos (limón). En clima cálido la uva madura más: el vino tiene acidez media, cuerpo medio a alto y sabores de fruta de hueso (melocotón) y tropical (piña, plátano).","Chardonnay can be fermented and matured in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Without oak it keeps pure, fresh fruit. With oak it picks up vanilla notes and often a richer character. A typical example of the warm, oaked style is a full-bodied Californian Chardonnay with ripe tropical fruit and vanilla.":"La Chardonnay puede fermentar y criarse en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble. Sin madera conserva una fruta pura y fresca. Con roble adquiere notas de vainilla y a menudo un carácter más rico. Un ejemplo típico del estilo cálido y con madera es un Chardonnay californiano con cuerpo, fruta tropical madura y vainilla.","Chardonnay is the grape behind white Burgundy (Bourgogne) in France: medium-bodied, high-acid wines with lemon and peach, sometimes with vanilla from oak. Chablis comes from the coolest part of Burgundy: high acidity, light to medium body, apple and lemon, and usually no oak. Outside France, Australia and California are well known for Chardonnay.":"La Chardonnay es la uva de los blancos de Burgundy (Borgoña), en Francia: vinos de cuerpo medio y acidez alta, con limón y melocotón y a veces vainilla del roble. El Chablis procede de la parte más fresca de Borgoña: acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio, manzana y limón y normalmente sin madera. Fuera de Francia destacan Australia y California.","Chardonnay is also used to make Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir. In short, when you meet a Chardonnay, ask two questions: was the climate cool or warm (apple and lemon, or peach and pineapple)? And did the wine see oak (vanilla or not)? The answers tell you almost everything about its style.":"La Chardonnay también se utiliza para elaborar Champagne, donde a menudo se mezcla con Pinot Noir. En resumen, ante un Chardonnay hazte dos preguntas: ¿clima fresco o cálido (manzana y limón, o melocotón y piña)? ¿Ha pasado por roble (vainilla o no)? Las respuestas te dicen casi todo sobre su estilo.","Dry wines in many styles; one of the most planted grapes":"Vinos secos de muchos estilos; una de las uvas más plantadas","Cool: high acidity, apple and lemon; warm: peach, pineapple, banana":"Fresco: acidez alta, manzana y limón; cálido: melocotón, piña, plátano","Oak adds vanilla":"El roble aporta vainilla","White Burgundy and Chablis (unoaked); also Australia and California":"Burgundy blanco y Chablis (sin madera); también Australia y California","In Champagne with Pinot Noir":"En el Champagne junto a la Pinot Noir","Sauvignon Blanc":"Sauvignon Blanc","Sauvignon Blanc makes dry wines with intense aromas and refreshingly high acidity. The body ranges from light to medium. It is an easy grape to spot by its nose: as soon as you lift the glass, you notice sharp, lively aromas that set it apart from more delicate whites such as Pinot Grigio.":"La Sauvignon Blanc da vinos secos de aromas intensos y con una acidez alta y refrescante. El cuerpo va de ligero a medio. Es una uva fácil de reconocer por la nariz: en cuanto acercas la copa, notas aromas nítidos y vivos que la distinguen de blancos más delicados como el Pinot Grigio.","The fruit ranges from green apple to citrus such as grapefruit, and on to tropical fruit such as passion fruit. Alongside the fruit there are often herbaceous notes: asparagus, green bell pepper and freshly cut grass. This mix of fresh fruit and «green» notes is Sauvignon Blanc's signature.":"La fruta va de la manzana verde a los cítricos, como el pomelo, hasta las frutas tropicales, como la fruta de la pasión. Junto a la fruta aparecen a menudo notas herbáceas: espárrago, pimiento verde, hierba recién cortada. Esta mezcla de fruta fresca y notas «verdes» es la firma de la Sauvignon Blanc.","In the winery the aim is to protect those aromas. So Sauvignon Blanc is often fermented in stainless steel tanks and usually not matured in oak: wood would add vanilla and toasty notes that would hide the grape's typical aromas. The result is a fresh, direct and very aromatic wine.":"En bodega el objetivo es proteger esos aromas. Por eso la Sauvignon Blanc fermenta a menudo en depósitos de acero inoxidable y normalmente no se cría en roble: la madera añadiría vainilla y notas tostadas que taparían los aromas típicos de la uva. El resultado es un vino fresco, directo y muy aromático.","Two very popular wines to remember: New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc (from Marlborough, for example), often showing grapefruit, lemon and grass, and Sancerre, a dry, medium-bodied white from France's Loire Valley with green apple and herbaceous notes. Sancerre labels usually do not name the grape, so you need to know it is Sauvignon Blanc.":"Dos vinos muy populares que conviene recordar: el Sauvignon Blanc de Nueva Zelanda (por ejemplo, de Marlborough), a menudo con pomelo, limón e hierba, y el Sancerre, blanco seco del valle del Loira, en Francia, de cuerpo medio, con manzana verde y notas herbáceas. En la etiqueta del Sancerre no suele aparecer la uva: hay que saber que es Sauvignon Blanc.","Dry, pronounced aromas, high acidity, light to medium body":"Seco, aromas intensos, acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio","Apple, grapefruit, passion fruit + asparagus, green pepper, grass":"Manzana, pomelo, fruta de la pasión + espárrago, pimiento verde, hierba","Stainless steel, usually no oak, to keep its aromas":"Acero inoxidable, normalmente sin roble, para conservar los aromas","Key wines: New Zealand and Sancerre (Loire)":"Vinos clave: Nueva Zelanda y Sancerre (Loira)","Pinot Grigio":"Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio is a hugely popular grape variety. Its wines are usually dry and light-bodied, with medium to high acidity. The flavours are simple and delicate: mostly pear and lemon. It is not about power or complexity; it is an easy, fresh and straightforward white made to be enjoyed without fuss.":"El Pinot Grigio es una variedad muy popular. Sus vinos suelen ser secos, de cuerpo ligero y con una acidez media a alta. Los sabores son sencillos y delicados: sobre todo pera y limón. No busca potencia ni complejidad: es un blanco fácil, fresco y directo, pensado para disfrutarlo sin complicaciones.","Here too, winemaking choices are about protecting the fruit. Pinot Grigio is usually fermented in stainless steel tanks and not matured in oak. That way it keeps its fruity flavours and its lightness: oak, with its vanilla and toasty notes, would easily cover such delicate fruit.":"También aquí las decisiones de bodega sirven para proteger la fruta. El Pinot Grigio suele fermentar en depósitos de acero inoxidable y no pasa por roble. Así conserva sus sabores afrutados y su ligereza: la madera, con su vainilla y sus notas tostadas, taparía una fruta tan delicada.","Pinot Grigio is linked above all with Italy, for example areas such as Veneto or Trentino, but it is grown in other countries too. The name on the label is the grape's name, making it the classic example of a wine named after its variety. Being light, it is served chilled, like other light and medium-bodied whites.":"El Pinot Grigio se asocia sobre todo con Italia, por ejemplo con zonas como el Véneto o el Trentino, aunque también se cultiva en otros países. El nombre de la etiqueta es el de la uva: es el ejemplo típico de vino que se llama como su variedad. Al ser ligero, se sirve frío, como los demás blancos ligeros o de cuerpo medio.","Usually dry, light body, medium to high acidity":"Normalmente seco, cuerpo ligero, acidez media a alta","Simple pear and lemon flavours":"Sabores sencillos de pera y limón","Stainless steel, no oak, to keep the fruit":"Acero inoxidable, sin roble, para conservar la fruta","Mainly associated with Italy":"Asociado sobre todo con Italia","Riesling":"Riesling","Riesling is a versatile grape: it makes wines from dry through medium to sweet. One thing never changes, though: every Riesling has high acidity. That acidity balances any sugar, so even a sweet Riesling stays fresh rather than cloying. The body ranges from light to medium.":"La Riesling es una uva versátil: da vinos secos, de dulzor medio o dulces. Pero hay algo que no cambia: todos los Riesling tienen una acidez alta. Esa acidez equilibra el azúcar que pueda haber, de modo que incluso un Riesling dulce sigue siendo fresco y no empalaga. El cuerpo va de ligero a medio.","The aromas are pronounced and can range from flowers and green apple to citrus (lime, lemon) and on to stone fruit (peach, apricot). Like Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Grigio, Riesling is often fermented in stainless steel and not matured in oak, so that the grape's pure aromas take centre stage.":"Los aromas son intensos y pueden ir de las flores y la manzana verde a los cítricos (lima, limón) y hasta la fruta de hueso (melocotón, albaricoque). Como la Sauvignon Blanc y el Pinot Grigio, la Riesling fermenta a menudo en acero inoxidable y no pasa por roble: se busca poner en primer plano los aromas puros de la uva.","Riesling is the classic grape of Germany, where it is made across the whole range from dry to sweet; some German Rieslings, from the Mosel for example, are medium-sweet, balanced by acidity and low in alcohol. Alsace in France and Australia, on the other hand, make Riesling in a dry style, often with lime, lemon and floral notes.":"La Riesling es la uva clásica de Alemania, donde se elabora en toda la gama, de seco a dulce; algunos Riesling alemanes, por ejemplo del Mosela, tienen un dulzor medio equilibrado por la acidez y poca graduación. Alsacia, en Francia, y Australia elaboran en cambio Riesling de estilo seco, a menudo con lima, limón y notas florales.","Watch the label: because the same grape can make dry, medium or sweet wines, the word «Riesling» alone does not tell you how sweet the wine will be. The origin helps: Alsace and Australia point to a dry style, while Germany covers the whole range. It is also worth reading the wine's description.":"Ojo con la etiqueta: como la misma uva puede dar vinos secos, de dulzor medio o dulces, la palabra «Riesling» por sí sola no indica cuánto dulzor tendrá el vino. El origen ayuda: Alsacia y Australia hacen pensar en un estilo seco, mientras que Alemania abarca toda la gama. Conviene leer también la descripción del vino.","Dry to sweet, but always high in acidity":"De seco a dulce, pero siempre con acidez alta","Floral, apple, lime, lemon, peach, apricot":"Flores, manzana, lima, limón, melocotón, albaricoque","Stainless steel, no oak":"Acero inoxidable, sin roble","Germany: full range; Alsace and Australia: dry style":"Alemania: toda la gama; Alsacia y Australia: estilo seco","Cabernet Sauvignon":"Cabernet Sauvignon","Cabernet Sauvignon is a black grape planted all over the world. It makes dry red wines with high tannin and high acidity: you notice both the drying grip and the mouth-watering freshness straight away. The body ranges from medium to full. Like other black grapes, it does well in warm regions, where the grapes ripen reliably.":"El Cabernet Sauvignon es una uva tinta plantada en todo el mundo. Da tintos secos con mucho tanino y acidez alta: enseguida se nota cómo se seca la boca y la frescura que hace salivar. El cuerpo va de medio a alto. Como otras uvas tintas, se da bien en regiones cálidas, donde la uva madura con regularidad.","Its signature aroma is blackcurrant, often with black cherry. Alongside the fruit there are herbaceous notes such as green bell pepper and mint. Many Cabernet Sauvignons are matured in oak, which adds cedar and vanilla. A Californian Cabernet, for example, can be full-bodied, with intense blackcurrant and cedar notes.":"Su aroma más típico es la grosella negra, a menudo con cereza negra. Junto a la fruta aparecen notas herbáceas como pimiento verde y menta. Muchos Cabernet Sauvignon se crían en roble, que añade cedro y vainilla. Un Cabernet californiano, por ejemplo, puede tener mucho cuerpo, con grosella negra intensa y notas de cedro.","Because its tannin is so high, Cabernet Sauvignon is often blended with other grapes. In Bordeaux it is paired with Merlot, which softens the wine and adds body. In Australia it is sometimes blended with Shiraz, which brings spicy aromas. Blending is therefore a way to round out or enrich the style.":"Como su tanino es tan alto, el Cabernet Sauvignon se mezcla a menudo con otras uvas. En Burdeos se une al Merlot, que suaviza el vino y le da más cuerpo. En Australia a veces se mezcla con Shiraz, que aporta notas especiadas. El ensamblaje sirve, por tanto, para pulir o enriquecer el estilo.","Beyond Bordeaux, Cabernet Sauvignon is widely grown in California, Australia, Chile and South Africa. In these countries it often appears on its own on the label, under the grape's name. In Bordeaux, by contrast, the label shows the region and the wine is usually a blend, so you need to know it contains Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot.":"Además de en Burdeos, el Cabernet Sauvignon se cultiva mucho en California, Australia, Chile y Sudáfrica. En estos países suele aparecer solo en la etiqueta, con el nombre de la uva. En Burdeos, en cambio, la etiqueta indica la zona y el vino suele ser un ensamblaje: hay que saber que lleva Cabernet Sauvignon y Merlot.","Dry, high tannin, high acidity, medium to full body":"Seco, tanino alto, acidez alta, cuerpo medio a alto","Blackcurrant, black cherry, green pepper, mint; oak: cedar, vanilla":"Grosella negra, cereza negra, pimiento verde, menta; roble: cedro, vainilla","Bordeaux: blended with Merlot (softness and body)":"Burdeos: con Merlot (suavidad y cuerpo)","Also California, Australia (sometimes with Shiraz), Chile, South Africa":"También California, Australia (a veces con Shiraz), Chile, Sudáfrica","Merlot":"Merlot","Merlot makes wines that are generally dry and medium- to full-bodied, with medium acidity and medium tannin. That makes it softer and rounder than Cabernet Sauvignon. Its fruit ranges from red fruit such as strawberry and red plum to black fruit such as blackberry and black plum.":"El Merlot da vinos generalmente secos, de cuerpo medio a alto, con acidez y tanino medios. Por eso es más suave y redondo que el Cabernet Sauvignon. Su fruta va de las frutas rojas, como la fresa y la ciruela roja, a las negras, como la mora y la ciruela negra.","Merlot is often matured in oak, which adds vanilla notes to the fruit. Chile and California use it to make soft, fruity, easy-drinking wines: on a wine list, a Chilean Merlot might be described as «smooth, with black plum and blackberry». It is one of the most approachable reds for beginners.":"El Merlot se cría a menudo en roble, que añade notas de vainilla a la fruta. En Chile y California se elaboran con él vinos suaves y afrutados, fáciles de beber: en una carta, un Merlot chileno puede describirse como «suave, con ciruela negra y mora». Es uno de los tintos más accesibles para empezar.","Merlot is Cabernet Sauvignon's classic partner. In a blend the two complete each other: Merlot brings softness and body, while Cabernet Sauvignon adds tannin and acidity. Bordeaux is the most famous region for this blend; in some parts of Bordeaux, such as Saint-Émilion, Merlot is often the main grape. The blend is now common in many other countries.":"El Merlot es el compañero clásico del Cabernet Sauvignon. En el ensamblaje se complementan: el Merlot aporta suavidad y cuerpo, y el Cabernet Sauvignon añade tanino y acidez. La región más famosa por esta mezcla es Burdeos; en algunas zonas, como Saint-Émilion, el Merlot suele ser la uva principal. Hoy esta mezcla es habitual en muchos otros países.","Dry, medium to full body, medium acidity and tannin":"Seco, cuerpo medio a alto, acidez y tanino medios","From strawberry and red plum to blackberry and black plum; oak: vanilla":"De fresa y ciruela roja a mora y ciruela negra; roble: vainilla","Chile and California: soft, fruity wines":"Chile y California: vinos suaves y afrutados","Bordeaux: blend with Cabernet Sauvignon (which adds tannin and acidity)":"Burdeos: mezcla con Cabernet Sauvignon (que añade tanino y acidez)","Pinot Noir":"Pinot Noir","Pinot Noir makes reds that are usually dry and light- to medium-bodied, with high acidity and low to medium tannin. It is an elegant, delicate red, very different from Cabernet Sauvignon. Its aromas are of red fruit: strawberry, red cherry and raspberry. It is often matured in oak, which adds notes of vanilla and smoke.":"La Pinot Noir da tintos normalmente secos, de cuerpo ligero a medio, con acidez alta y tanino bajo a medio. Es, por tanto, un tinto elegante y delicado, muy distinto del Cabernet Sauvignon. Sus aromas son de frutas rojas: fresa, cereza roja y frambuesa. Si pasa por roble, algo frecuente, suma notas de vainilla y ahumado.","Pinot Noir is the grape of red Burgundy (Bourgogne) in France: dry, light to medium-bodied, very fresh wines with raspberry and red cherry, and sometimes vanilla and smoke from oak. It is also the main black grape of New Zealand, for example in the Central Otago region.":"La Pinot Noir es la uva de los tintos de Borgoña (Burgundy, Bourgogne), en Francia: vinos secos, ligeros a medios, muy frescos, con frambuesa y cereza roja y a veces vainilla y ahumado del roble. También es la principal uva tinta de Nueva Zelanda, por ejemplo en la zona de Central Otago.","Unlike Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, Pinot Noir is not usually blended with other grapes when making red wine; producers prefer to show its pure character. There is one important exception: in Champagne, Pinot Noir is often blended with Chardonnay. There the skins are removed straight away, so the juice stays pale.":"A diferencia del Cabernet Sauvignon y del Merlot, la Pinot Noir no suele mezclarse con otras uvas cuando se hace vino tinto: se prefiere mostrar su carácter puro. Hay, sin embargo, una excepción importante: en el Champagne, la Pinot Noir se mezcla a menudo con Chardonnay. Allí los hollejos se separan enseguida y el zumo se mantiene claro.","Dry, light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin":"Seco, cuerpo ligero a medio, acidez alta, tanino bajo a medio","Strawberry, red cherry, raspberry; oak: vanilla, smoke":"Fresa, cereza roja, frambuesa; roble: vainilla, ahumado","Red Burgundy; New Zealand's main black grape":"Borgoña tinto; principal uva tinta de Nueva Zelanda","Not usually blended for reds; in Champagne with Chardonnay":"Normalmente sin mezclar en tintos; en el Champagne con Chardonnay","Syrah / Shiraz":"Syrah / Shiraz","This is one grape with two names: it is called Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia, so the name on the label also hints at the origin and often the style. It makes dry wines with medium to full body, medium to high tannin and medium acidity. Typical flavours are black fruit (blackberry, black cherry) and spice (black pepper, liquorice).":"Es una misma uva con dos nombres: en Francia se llama Syrah y en Australia, Shiraz. Por eso el nombre de la etiqueta también sugiere el origen y, a menudo, el estilo. Da vinos secos, de cuerpo medio a alto, con tanino medio a alto y acidez media. Los sabores típicos son fruta negra (mora, cereza negra) y especias (pimienta negra, regaliz).","Many Syrahs and Shirazes are matured in oak, which adds vanilla or coconut notes. Alongside the black fruit and spice, these oak aromas make the wine richer. For anyone studying, the pairing «black fruit + black pepper» is an excellent clue for recognising this grape.":"Muchos Syrah y Shiraz se crían en roble, que añade notas de vainilla o de coco. Junto a la fruta negra y las especias, estos aromas de la madera hacen el vino más rico. Para quien estudia, la pareja «fruta negra + pimienta negra» es una pista excelente para reconocer esta uva.","Climate changes the style a great deal. In France's Northern Rhône, Syrah can make medium-bodied wines with fresh blackberry and black pepper. In warm parts of Australia, such as the Barossa Valley, the grapes ripen further, and Shiraz becomes full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice.":"El clima cambia mucho el estilo. En el norte del Ródano, en Francia, la Syrah puede dar vinos de cuerpo medio, con mora fresca y pimienta negra. En las zonas cálidas de Australia, como el Barossa Valley, la uva madura más: la Shiraz se vuelve de cuerpo alto, con cereza negra casi confitada y regaliz.","Australian Shiraz is also blended with Cabernet Sauvignon, and in that blend it contributes spicy aromas. To sum up: France and the Northern Rhône = fresher, peppery Syrah; warm Australia = full, ripe Shiraz. Same grape, two climates, two different styles.":"La Shiraz australiana también se mezcla con Cabernet Sauvignon, y en esa mezcla aporta aromas especiados. En resumen: Francia y norte del Ródano = Syrah más fresca y con pimienta; Australia cálida = Shiraz con cuerpo y madura. La misma uva, dos climas, dos estilos distintos.","Syrah in France, Shiraz in Australia: the same grape":"Syrah en Francia, Shiraz en Australia: la misma uva","Dry, medium to full body, medium to high tannin, medium acidity":"Seco, cuerpo medio a alto, tanino medio a alto, acidez media","Blackberry, black cherry, black pepper, liquorice; oak: vanilla, coconut":"Mora, cereza negra, pimienta negra, regaliz; roble: vainilla, coco","Northern Rhône: medium, peppery; warm Australia: full, jammy, liquorice":"Norte del Ródano: medio y con pimienta; Australia cálida: con cuerpo, confitado, regaliz","Which type of wine has had extra alcohol added?":"¿A qué tipo de vino se le ha añadido alcohol?","Fortified":"Fortificado","Sparkling":"Espumoso","Still":"Tranquilo","Rosé":"Rosado","Fortified wines have alcohol added, which makes them stronger.":"A los fortificados se les añade alcohol, por eso son más fuertes.","There are three types of wine: still, sparkling and fortified. Only fortified wine has extra alcohol added, which lifts it to between 15% and 22% abv. Sparkling wine owes its bubbles to carbon dioxide from fermentation, and rosé is a colour, not a type of wine.":"Hay tres tipos de vino: tranquilo, espumoso y fortificado. Solo al fortificado se le añade alcohol, lo que eleva su graduación a entre el 15 % y el 22 % vol. El espumoso debe sus burbujas al dióxido de carbono de la fermentación, y el rosado es un color, no un tipo de vino.","What is the usual alcohol range of fortified wines?":"¿Cuál es la graduación habitual de los vinos fortificados?","15–22% abv":"15–22 % vol.","8–11% abv":"8–11 % vol.","11.5–14% abv":"11,5–14 % vol.","4–7% abv":"4–7 % vol.","The added alcohol puts fortified wines between 15% and 22% abv.":"El alcohol añadido sitúa a los fortificados entre el 15 % y el 22 % vol.","Still and sparkling wines almost always sit between 11.5% and 14% abv, with extremes from 8% to 15%. Fortified wines such as Sherry and Port have extra alcohol added, so they move up into a higher band of 15% to 22% abv.":"Los vinos tranquilos y espumosos casi siempre están entre el 11,5 % y el 14 % vol., con extremos del 8 % al 15 %. Los fortificados, como el Sherry y el Port, reciben alcohol adicional y suben a una franja más alta, del 15 % al 22 % vol.","Where do the bubbles in sparkling wine come from?":"¿De dónde salen las burbujas del vino espumoso?","Carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine":"Dióxido de carbono de la fermentación atrapado en el vino","Distilled alcohol added after fermentation":"Alcohol destilado añadido tras la fermentación","Sugar left in the wine after fermentation":"Azúcar que queda en el vino tras fermentar","Air entering through the oak barrel staves":"Aire que entra por las duelas de la barrica","Fermentation makes carbon dioxide; when it is trapped, it becomes the bubbles.":"La fermentación produce dióxido de carbono; si queda atrapado, forma las burbujas.","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol and carbon dioxide. In still wines the gas escapes into the air, but in sparkling wines it is kept inside the wine. When the bottle is opened, the gas is released as bubbles, as in Champagne, Cava or Prosecco.":"Las levaduras convierten el azúcar en alcohol y dióxido de carbono. En los vinos tranquilos el gas se escapa al aire, pero en los espumosos se retiene dentro del vino. Al abrir la botella, el gas se libera en forma de burbujas, como en el Champagne, el Cava o el Prosecco.","Between which values do most still wines fall?":"¿Entre qué valores se sitúan la mayoría de los vinos tranquilos?","11.5% and 14% abv":"11,5 % y 14 % vol.","15% and 22% abv":"15 % y 22 % vol.","5% and 8% abv":"5 % y 8 % vol.","16% and 20% abv":"16 % y 20 % vol.","Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, but most sit between 11.5% and 14%.":"Los tranquilos van del 8 % al 15 % vol., pero casi todos entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %.","The full range for still wines runs from 8% to 15% abv, but the great majority sit between 11.5% and 14%. Figures of 15% to 22% are typical of fortified wines, which have alcohol added. White Zinfandel is an example of a still wine at the low end.":"La franja completa de los vinos tranquilos va del 8 % al 15 % vol., pero la gran mayoría se sitúa entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %. Las cifras del 15 % al 22 % son típicas de los fortificados, a los que se añade alcohol. El White Zinfandel es un ejemplo de vino con poca graduación.","Which of these wines is named after its grape variety?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos lleva el nombre de su variedad de uva?","Rioja":"Rioja","Chianti":"Chianti","Sancerre":"Sancerre","Pinot Grigio is a grape; Rioja, Chianti and Sancerre are places.":"Pinot Grigio es una uva; Rioja, Chianti y Sancerre son zonas.","Many European wines take the name of the area where they are made: Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy, Sancerre in France. Other wines show the grape variety on the label instead. Pinot Grigio is a typical example of a wine named after its grape.":"Muchos vinos europeos llevan el nombre de la zona donde se elaboran: Rioja en España, Chianti en Italia, Sancerre en Francia. Otros, en cambio, indican la variedad de uva en la etiqueta. El Pinot Grigio es precisamente un ejemplo de vino que se llama como su uva.","Which of these is a Spanish sparkling wine?":"¿Cuál de estos es un espumoso español?","Cava":"Cava","Prosecco":"Prosecco","Champagne":"Champagne","Sherry":"Sherry","Cava is the sparkling wine from Spain.":"El Cava es el espumoso de España.","Three famous sparkling wines to remember: Champagne from France, Prosecco from Italy and Cava from Spain. Sherry is also Spanish, but it is a fortified wine, not a sparkling one: it has had alcohol added and has no bubbles. Sparkling wines are, in fact, now made in almost every wine-producing country.":"Tres espumosos famosos que conviene recordar: Champagne de Francia, Prosecco de Italia y Cava de España. El Sherry también es español, pero es un vino fortificado, no un espumoso: lleva alcohol añadido y no tiene burbujas. De hecho, hoy se elaboran espumosos en casi todos los países productores de vino.","Why is a red wine red?":"¿Por qué un vino tinto es tinto?","The skins stay in the juice during fermentation":"Los hollejos se quedan en el zumo durante la fermentación","The pulp of black grapes is red in colour":"La pulpa de las uvas tintas es de color rojo","The oak barrels give their colour to the wine":"Las barricas de roble ceden color al vino","Unfermented black grape juice is added":"Se añade zumo de uva tinta sin fermentar","The colour is in the skins, which release it during fermentation.":"El color está en los hollejos, que lo ceden durante la fermentación.","The pulp of white and black grapes is the same colour and the juice is colourless. To make a red wine, black grapes are used and the skins are kept in contact with the juice throughout fermentation, mixed in well, so colour and tannin pass into the wine.":"La pulpa de las uvas blancas y tintas tiene el mismo color y el zumo es incoloro. Para hacer un tinto se usan uvas tintas y se dejan los hollejos en contacto con el zumo durante toda la fermentación, mezclándolos bien: así pasan al vino el color y el tanino.","Can a white wine be made from black grapes?":"¿Se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas?","Yes, by separating skins and juice before fermentation":"Sí, separando hollejos y zumo antes de fermentar","Yes, but only if the wine is then aged in oak":"Sí, pero solo si después se cría en roble","No, black grapes always give a red wine":"No, las uvas tintas siempre dan vino tinto","No, black grapes can only make rosé wine":"No, las uvas tintas solo dan vino rosado","Black grape juice is colourless, so without the skins the wine stays white.":"El zumo de la uva tinta es incoloro: sin hollejos, el vino queda blanco.","All the colour of a black grape is in its skin. If the grapes are pressed gently and the skins are separated from the juice before fermentation, the juice stays pale and makes a white wine. This same idea is what allows Pinot Noir to be used in Champagne.":"Todo el color de la uva tinta está en su piel. Si las uvas se prensan con suavidad y los hollejos se separan del zumo antes de la fermentación, el zumo sigue claro y da un vino blanco. Es la misma idea que permite usar Pinot Noir en el Champagne.","How is a rosé wine made?":"¿Cómo se elabora un vino rosado?","Black grapes with only a few hours of skin contact":"Uvas tintas con pocas horas de contacto con los hollejos","White grapes fermented together with their skins":"Uvas blancas fermentadas junto con sus hollejos","Black grapes kept on skins until fermentation ends":"Uvas tintas con hollejos hasta el final de la fermentación","White grapes aged for a long time in oak barrels":"Uvas blancas criadas largo tiempo en barricas de roble","The juice sits with black grape skins for a few hours, then is drained off.":"El zumo pasa unas horas con los hollejos de uva tinta y luego se separa.","Rosé comes from black grapes, like red wine, but the skin contact lasts only a few hours. The juice, now just pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins. If the skins stayed in until the end, the result would be a red wine instead.":"El rosado procede de uvas tintas, como el tinto, pero el contacto con los hollejos dura solo unas horas. El zumo, apenas rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. Si los hollejos se quedaran hasta el final, se obtendría un vino tinto.","Which of these wines is a rosé?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos es un rosado?","White Zinfandel":"White Zinfandel","Chablis":"Chablis","Beaujolais":"Beaujolais","Sauternes":"Sauternes","Despite its name, White Zinfandel from California is a rosé.":"Pese a su nombre, el White Zinfandel de California es un rosado.","The name can mislead you: White Zinfandel is a Californian rosé, medium-sweet, low in alcohol, with strawberry and raspberry flavours. Chablis and Sauternes are French white wines, while Beaujolais is a light red with low tannin. So never judge a wine by its name alone.":"El nombre puede despistar: el White Zinfandel es un rosado californiano, de dulzor medio, con poco alcohol y sabores de fresa y frambuesa. El Chablis y el Sauternes son blancos franceses, y el Beaujolais es un tinto ligero y con poco tanino. Así que conviene no juzgar nunca un vino solo por su nombre.","What happens when a dry wine is made?":"¿Qué ocurre cuando se elabora un vino seco?","The yeast turn all of the sugar into alcohol":"Las levaduras convierten todo el azúcar en alcohol","Distilled alcohol is added before fermentation ends":"Se añade alcohol destilado antes del final","Unfermented grape juice is added to the wine":"Se añade zumo de uva sin fermentar","The yeast are removed before they finish":"Se retiran las levaduras antes de terminar","A wine is dry when the yeast have eaten all the sugar.":"Un vino es seco cuando las levaduras se han comido todo el azúcar.","Most wines are dry: the yeast keep working until they have turned all the sugar into alcohol. The other answers describe ways of keeping sugar in the wine: removing yeast or adding juice for medium wines, and adding alcohol for sweet fortified wines.":"La mayoría de los vinos son secos: las levaduras trabajan hasta convertir todo el azúcar en alcohol. Las demás respuestas describen formas de conservar azúcar: retirar las levaduras o añadir zumo en los vinos de dulzor medio, y añadir alcohol en los fortificados dulces.","Which method is used to make a medium-sweet wine?":"¿Qué método sirve para obtener un vino de dulzor medio?","Adding unfermented grape juice to a dry wine":"Añadir zumo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco","Leaving the skins in the juice for longer":"Dejar los hollejos más tiempo en el zumo","Maturing the wine in oak barrels":"Criar el vino en barricas de roble","Picking the grapes before they ripen":"Vendimiar la uva antes de que madure","Unfermented juice brings sugar back into an already dry wine.":"El zumo sin fermentar aporta azúcar a un vino ya seco.","There are two routes to a medium-sweet wine: remove the yeast before they have eaten all the sugar, or add unfermented grape juice to a dry wine. Skins and oak affect colour, tannin and aromas, not the level of sweetness.":"Hay dos caminos para un vino de dulzor medio: retirar las levaduras antes de que consuman todo el azúcar, o añadir zumo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Los hollejos y el roble influyen en el color, el tanino y los aromas, no en el dulzor.","In a sweet fortified wine, what stops the fermentation?":"En un vino fortificado dulce, ¿qué detiene la fermentación?","Adding distilled alcohol, which kills the yeast":"Añadir alcohol destilado, que mata las levaduras","Adding unfermented grape juice to the wine":"Añadir zumo de uva sin fermentar","Moving the wine into oak barrels":"Pasar el vino a barricas de roble","Draining the wine off the skins":"Separar el vino de los hollejos","The strong added alcohol kills the yeast, leaving sugar in the wine.":"El alcohol fuerte añadido mata las levaduras y deja azúcar en el vino.","In sweet fortified wines, high-strength distilled alcohol is added before the yeast have eaten all the sugar. The yeast die, the leftover sugar makes the wine sweet and the added alcohol makes it stronger. Port and some Sherries are made this way.":"En los fortificados dulces se añade alcohol destilado de alta graduación antes de que las levaduras se coman todo el azúcar. Las levaduras mueren, el azúcar que queda hace dulce el vino y el alcohol añadido lo hace más fuerte. Así se elaboran el Port y algunos Sherry.","Which sensation tells you a wine has high acidity?":"¿Qué sensación indica una acidez alta?","It makes your mouth water":"Hace salivar","It makes your mouth feel dry":"Deja la boca seca","It warms the back of your throat":"Da calor en la garganta","It feels thick and syrupy":"Parece espesa y almibarada","Acidity is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water.":"La acidez se reconoce porque hace salivar.","Each part of a wine's structure has its own sensation. Acidity makes your mouth water and brings freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth; alcohol is felt as warmth; and a very sweet wine can feel thick and syrupy. Too much acidity, however, makes a wine taste unpleasantly sharp.":"Cada elemento de la estructura se reconoce por una sensación distinta. La acidez hace salivar y aporta frescura. El tanino, en cambio, seca la boca; el alcohol se nota como calor; y un vino muy dulce puede resultar espeso y almibarado. Eso sí, demasiada acidez hace que el vino resulte desagradablemente ácido.","Why is acidity important in sweet wines?":"¿Por qué es importante la acidez en los vinos dulces?","It balances the sweetness so the wine is not cloying":"Equilibra el dulzor y evita que empalague","It raises the alcohol level of the wine":"Aumenta la graduación del vino","It gives the wine a deeper colour":"Da al vino un color más intenso","It adds tannin and therefore more body":"Añade tanino y, por tanto, más cuerpo","Without acidity, a sweet wine would taste cloying.":"Sin acidez, un vino dulce resultaría empalagoso.","Acidity comes from the grape juice and refreshes the wine. In sweet wines it acts as a counterweight to the sugar, which is why Sauternes and sweet Rieslings have high acidity. It does not change the colour, the tannin or the alcohol level. Without it, the wine would feel heavy.":"La acidez procede del zumo de uva y refresca el vino. En los dulces hace de contrapeso al azúcar: por eso el Sauternes y los Riesling dulces tienen acidez alta. No influye en el color, el tanino ni la graduación. Sin ella, el vino resultaría pesado.","Where does tannin in wine come from?":"¿De dónde procede el tanino del vino?","The skins of black grapes":"Los hollejos de la uva tinta","The pulp of white grapes":"La pulpa de la uva blanca","The sugar in the juice":"El azúcar del zumo","The yeast used in fermentation":"Las levaduras de la fermentación","Tannin sits in black grape skins, which is why it is a red-wine feature.":"El tanino está en el hollejo de la uva tinta; por eso es propio de los tintos.","Black grapes have coloured skins that contain tannins. When red wine ferments, the skins stay in the juice and release colour and tannin. How much tannin the wine ends up with depends on the grape and the winemaking: red Bordeaux has a lot, Beaujolais very little.":"Las uvas tintas tienen hollejos coloreados que contienen taninos. Al fermentar un tinto, los hollejos permanecen en el zumo y le ceden color y tanino. La cantidad final depende de la variedad y de la elaboración: el Bordeaux tinto tiene mucho; el Beaujolais, poco.","Which of these reds is low in tannin?":"¿Cuál de estos tintos tiene poco tanino?","Red Bordeaux":"Bordeaux tinto","Port":"Port","Beaujolais is a light, fresh red with low tannin.":"El Beaujolais es un tinto ligero, fresco y con poco tanino.","Beaujolais is a classic example of a low-tannin red, along with some Pinot Noir wines. Red Bordeaux and Chianti, by contrast, are standard examples of high-tannin reds, and Port, a sweet red fortified wine, also has high tannins. Remember that tannin leaves the mouth feeling dry.":"El Beaujolais es un ejemplo clásico de tinto con poco tanino, como algunos Pinot Noir. El Bordeaux tinto y el Chianti, en cambio, son ejemplos típicos de tintos muy tánicos, y el Port, vino fortificado tinto y dulce, también tiene taninos altos. Recuerda que el tanino deja la boca seca.","Which of these is an example of a high-alcohol wine?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos es un ejemplo de vino con mucho alcohol?","Châteauneuf-du-Pape":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is a full-bodied French red with high alcohol.":"El Châteauneuf-du-Pape es un tinto francés con cuerpo y mucho alcohol.","Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a red from the Rhône, is the textbook example of a high-alcohol wine: dry and full-bodied, with strawberry and clove. At the other end, White Zinfandel is the standard low-alcohol example, while Beaujolais and Pinot Grigio are light-bodied wines.":"El Châteauneuf-du-Pape, tinto del Ródano, es el ejemplo típico de vino con mucho alcohol: seco, con cuerpo, con fresa y clavo. En el extremo opuesto, el White Zinfandel es el ejemplo de vino con poco alcohol, y el Beaujolais y el Pinot Grigio son vinos ligeros.","What does «12% abv» on a label mean?":"¿Qué significa «12 % vol.» en la etiqueta?","The wine contains 12% sugar":"El vino contiene un 12 % de azúcar","The wine spent 12 months in oak":"El vino pasó 12 meses en barrica","Alcohol by volume shows what share of the wine is alcohol.":"El porcentaje en volumen indica qué parte del vino es alcohol.","Alcohol is measured as a percentage of the total volume, called alcohol by volume or abv. A wine at 12% abv has twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. That is a typical figure for a still wine, as most sit between 11.5% and 14%.":"El alcohol se mide como porcentaje del volumen total (abv en inglés). Un vino de 12 % vol. contiene doce partes de alcohol de cada cien. Es una cifra típica de un vino tranquilo: la mayoría se sitúa entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %.","What does the body of a wine describe?":"¿Qué describe el cuerpo de un vino?","How much acidity the wine contains":"Cuánta acidez contiene el vino","How deep the colour of the wine is":"Lo intenso que es el color del vino","How long the wine stayed in oak":"Cuánto tiempo pasó en barrica","Body is the overall feel in the mouth: light, medium or full.":"El cuerpo es la sensación general en boca: ligero, medio o con cuerpo.","Many factors shape body, so the practical question is: how much does this wine fill my mouth? Full-bodied wines such as Sauternes or a Californian Cabernet Sauvignon feel dense and rich, while light ones such as Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais feel more delicate.":"El cuerpo depende de muchos factores, así que la pregunta práctica es: ¿cuánto me llena la boca este vino? Los vinos con cuerpo, como el Sauternes o un Cabernet Sauvignon californiano, resultan densos; los ligeros, como el Pinot Grigio o el Beaujolais, más delicados.","Which of these wines is full-bodied?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos tiene mucho cuerpo?","Sauternes, the sweet white from Bordeaux, is full-bodied.":"El Sauternes, blanco dulce de Burdeos, tiene mucho cuerpo.","Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla. Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais are examples of light-bodied wines, and Sancerre is a dry white with medium body. A Californian Cabernet Sauvignon would also be a good example of a full-bodied wine.":"El Sauternes es dulce y con mucho cuerpo, con albaricoque, miel y vainilla. El Pinot Grigio y el Beaujolais son ejemplos de vinos ligeros, y el Sancerre es un blanco seco de cuerpo medio. Un Cabernet Sauvignon de California también sería un buen ejemplo de vino con cuerpo.","Which group of aromas typically comes from oak?":"¿Qué grupo de aromas procede normalmente del roble?","Vanilla, cedar, smoke":"Vainilla, cedro, ahumado","Apple, lemon, pear":"Manzana, limón, pera","Grass, asparagus, bell pepper":"Hierba, espárrago, pimiento","Strawberry, raspberry, cherry":"Fresa, frambuesa, cereza","Oak gives vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves.":"El roble aporta vainilla, cedro, ahumado, coco y clavo.","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, the wood adds notes of vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves. Apple, lemon and pear are fruit aromas, while grass, asparagus and bell pepper are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc, for example.":"Cuando un vino fermenta o se cría en barricas de roble, la madera aporta notas de vainilla, cedro, ahumado, coco y clavo. Manzana, limón y pera son aromas de fruta; hierba, espárrago y pimiento son notas herbáceas típicas, por ejemplo, del Sauvignon Blanc.","Which aromas does a cool-climate Chardonnay usually show?":"¿Qué aromas suele tener un Chardonnay de clima fresco?","Green apple and lemon":"Manzana verde y limón","Peach and pineapple":"Melocotón y piña","Blackcurrant and mint":"Grosella negra y menta","Strawberry and cherry":"Fresa y cereza","In a cool climate grapes ripen less, giving green fruit and citrus.":"En clima fresco la uva madura menos: fruta verde y cítricos.","How ripe the grapes are changes the fruit you notice. A cool-climate Chardonnay smells of green apple and lemon; a warm-climate one of peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple. Blackcurrant and mint are typical of Cabernet Sauvignon, and strawberry and cherry of Pinot Noir.":"La madurez de la uva cambia la fruta que se percibe. Un Chardonnay de clima fresco huele a manzana verde y limón; uno de clima cálido, a melocotón y frutas tropicales como la piña. Grosella negra y menta son típicas del Cabernet Sauvignon, y fresa y cereza del Pinot Noir.","Which of these aromas belongs to the «other» family?":"¿Cuál de estos aromas pertenece a la familia «otros»?","Mushroom":"Champiñón","Pineapple":"Piña","Blackcurrant":"Grosella negra","Mushroom, earth, leather, grass and flowers are «other» aromas.":"Champiñón, tierra, cuero, hierba y flores son «otros» aromas.","Aromas fall into three families: fruit, oak and other. Pineapple and blackcurrant are fruit, and vanilla comes from oak. The «other» family covers grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. These are the aromas that make wine so varied and interesting to explore.":"Los aromas se reparten en tres familias: fruta, roble y otros. La piña y la grosella negra son fruta, y la vainilla procede del roble. La familia «otros» agrupa hierba, flores, hierbas aromáticas, verduras, tierra, champiñón y cuero. Son precisamente estos aromas los que hacen el vino tan variado e interesante.","What is the style of a wine?":"¿Qué es el estilo de un vino?","Its colour, structure and aromas combined":"El conjunto de color, estructura y aromas","Only the grape variety it is made from":"Solo la variedad con la que se elabora","Only the region where it is produced":"Solo la zona donde se produce","Only its level of alcohol":"Solo su graduación alcohólica","Style combines colour, structure, and aromas and flavours.":"El estilo combina color, estructura y aromas y sabores.","Grape, region and alcohol all influence style, but none of them describes it alone. Style is the sum of colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. That is how two French whites such as Chablis and Sauternes can be complete opposites.":"La uva, la zona y el alcohol influyen en el estilo, pero ninguno lo describe por sí solo. El estilo es la suma del color, la estructura (dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol, cuerpo) y los aromas y sabores. Por eso dos blancos franceses como el Chablis y el Sauternes pueden ser opuestos.","What effect does a cool climate have on the grapes?":"¿Qué efecto tiene un clima fresco en la uva?","More tannin and more colour":"Más tanino y más color","Riper, more tropical flavours":"Sabores más maduros y tropicales","The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acid the grapes have.":"Cuanto más fresco, menos azúcar y más acidez tiene la uva.","As a rule, the cooler the climate, the more acidic and the less sugary the grapes stay; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, with riper flavours. That is why cool-climate wines tend to be fresher and lighter, with green fruit and citrus.":"En general, cuanto más fresco es el clima, más ácida y menos dulce se queda la uva; cuanto más cálido, más azúcar, menos acidez y sabores más maduros. Por eso los vinos de clima fresco suelen ser más frescos y ligeros, con fruta verde y cítricos.","What is a cool-climate Chardonnay usually like?":"¿Cómo suele ser un Chardonnay de clima fresco?","High acidity, light to medium body, apple and lemon":"Acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio, manzana y limón","Medium acidity, full body, pineapple and banana":"Acidez media, mucho cuerpo, piña y plátano","Low acidity, full body, honey and apricot":"Acidez baja, mucho cuerpo, miel y albaricoque","Medium acidity, light body, pear and flowers":"Acidez media, cuerpo ligero, pera y flores","A cool climate keeps acidity high and gives green fruit and citrus.":"El clima fresco mantiene la acidez alta y da fruta verde y cítricos.","In cool climates the grapes ripen less, so they keep more acidity and less sugar. The resulting Chardonnay has high acidity, a light to medium body and aromas of apple and lemon. Chablis, from the coolest part of Burgundy, is the classic example of this style.":"En climas frescos la uva madura menos, así que conserva más acidez y menos azúcar. El Chardonnay resultante tiene acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio y aromas de manzana y limón. El Chablis, de la parte más fresca de Borgoña, es el ejemplo clásico de este estilo.","Which flavours does a warm-climate Chardonnay show?":"¿Qué sabores muestra un Chardonnay de clima cálido?","Peach, pineapple and banana":"Melocotón, piña y plátano","Grapefruit, asparagus and grass":"Pomelo, espárrago e hierba","Blackcurrant, mint and cedar":"Grosella negra, menta y cedro","Warmth ripens the grapes further, giving stone and tropical fruit.":"Con el calor la uva madura más: fruta de hueso y tropical.","Warm-climate Chardonnay comes from riper grapes: medium acidity, medium to full body, and flavours of peach, pineapple and banana. Green apple and lemon point instead to a cool climate. Grapefruit and asparagus suggest Sauvignon Blanc, while blackcurrant and mint suggest Cabernet Sauvignon.":"El Chardonnay de clima cálido procede de uvas más maduras: acidez media, cuerpo medio a alto y sabores de melocotón, piña y plátano. La manzana verde y el limón indican, en cambio, un clima fresco. Pomelo y espárrago apuntan a la Sauvignon Blanc; grosella negra y menta, al Cabernet Sauvignon.","Which grape is used for white Burgundy?":"¿Con qué uva se elaboran los blancos de Borgoña?","White Burgundy, including Chablis, is made from Chardonnay.":"Los blancos de Borgoña, Chablis incluido, se hacen con Chardonnay.","Burgundy (Bourgogne) is France's benchmark region for Chardonnay. Its whites are medium-bodied with high acidity, lemon and peach, and sometimes vanilla from oak. Chablis, from the coolest part of the region, is also Chardonnay. Sauvignon Blanc, by contrast, is the grape of Sancerre.":"Borgoña (Burgundy, Bourgogne) es la región francesa de referencia para la Chardonnay. Sus blancos tienen cuerpo medio, acidez alta, limón y melocotón y a veces vainilla del roble. El Chablis, de la parte más fresca, también es Chardonnay. La Sauvignon Blanc, en cambio, es la uva del Sancerre.","Why does Chablis have high acidity?":"¿Por qué el Chablis tiene una acidez alta?","It comes from the coolest part of Burgundy":"Procede de la parte más fresca de Borgoña","It is aged for a long time in new oak":"Se cría mucho tiempo en roble nuevo","It is made from pressed black grapes":"Se elabora con uvas tintas prensadas","The grapes are picked very ripe":"La uva se vendimia muy madura","A cool climate limits ripening, so the grapes stay more acidic.":"El clima fresco limita la maduración y la uva se mantiene más ácida.","Chablis comes from the coolest area of Burgundy. There the grapes ripen less, so they stay more acidic and give green apple and lemon flavours. The result is a dry white, light to medium in body, usually with no oak. Very ripe grapes would do the opposite and give lower acidity.":"El Chablis procede de la zona más fresca de Borgoña. Allí la uva madura menos, conserva más acidez y da sabores de manzana verde y limón. El resultado es un blanco seco, de cuerpo ligero a medio, normalmente sin roble. Una uva muy madura haría lo contrario y daría menos acidez.","Where do vanilla notes in some white Burgundies come from?":"¿De dónde vienen las notas de vainilla de algunos Borgoña blancos?","Maturation in oak":"La crianza en roble","The region's cool climate":"El clima fresco de la región","The grape skins":"Los hollejos de la uva","Stainless steel tanks":"Los depósitos de acero","Vanilla is a typical aroma from time in oak.":"La vainilla es un aroma típico del paso por roble.","White Burgundy can be matured in oak or not. When it spends time in barrel, the wood adds vanilla notes to the lemon and peach aromas. Stainless steel, by contrast, adds no aromas, and the cool climate affects acidity and the type of fruit rather than vanilla.":"Los Borgoña blancos pueden criarse en roble o no. Cuando pasan por barrica, la madera añade notas de vainilla a los aromas de limón y melocotón. El acero inoxidable, en cambio, no aporta aromas, y el clima fresco influye en la acidez y en el tipo de fruta, no en la vainilla.","In Champagne, Chardonnay is often blended with which grape?":"En el Champagne, ¿con qué uva se mezcla a menudo la Chardonnay?","Champagne is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir.":"El Champagne se elabora con Chardonnay y Pinot Noir.","Champagne, the famous French sparkling wine, is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, often blended together. Pinot Noir is a black grape, but its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a white wine. Merlot and Riesling are not Champagne grapes.":"El Champagne, el famoso espumoso francés, se elabora con Chardonnay y Pinot Noir, a menudo mezcladas. La Pinot Noir es una uva tinta, pero su zumo es incoloro: si se separan enseguida los hollejos, se obtiene vino blanco. Merlot y Riesling no son uvas del Champagne.","Besides Burgundy, which places are well known for Chardonnay?":"Además de Borgoña, ¿qué lugares son famosos por la Chardonnay?","Australia and California":"Australia y California","Germany and Alsace":"Alemania y Alsacia","Spain and Portugal":"España y Portugal","New Zealand and the Loire":"Nueva Zelanda y el Loira","Australia and California are well known for their Chardonnay.":"Australia y California son conocidas por sus Chardonnay.","Chardonnay is grown in many countries, but besides Burgundy, Australia and California are especially well known, often for warmer, fruitier styles. Germany and Alsace are famous for Riesling, while New Zealand and the Loire (Sancerre) are famous for Sauvignon Blanc.":"La Chardonnay se cultiva en muchos países, pero además de Borgoña destacan Australia y California, a menudo con estilos más cálidos y afrutados. Alemania y Alsacia son famosas por la Riesling, y Nueva Zelanda y el Loira (Sancerre) por la Sauvignon Blanc.","Which herbaceous notes are typical of Sauvignon Blanc?":"¿Qué notas herbáceas son típicas de la Sauvignon Blanc?","Asparagus, green bell pepper, grass":"Espárrago, pimiento verde, hierba","Vanilla, coconut, smoke":"Vainilla, coco, ahumado","Honey, apricot, peach":"Miel, albaricoque, melocotón","Black pepper, liquorice, blackberry":"Pimienta negra, regaliz, mora","Sauvignon Blanc pairs fresh fruit with asparagus, green pepper and grass.":"La Sauvignon Blanc une fruta fresca a notas de espárrago, pimiento e hierba.","Besides fruit (apple, grapefruit, passion fruit), Sauvignon Blanc often shows herbaceous notes: asparagus, green bell pepper and cut grass. Vanilla, coconut and smoke come from oak; black pepper and liquorice are typical of Syrah/Shiraz; and honey and apricot belong to Sauternes.":"Además de fruta (manzana, pomelo, fruta de la pasión), la Sauvignon Blanc muestra a menudo notas herbáceas: espárrago, pimiento verde e hierba cortada. Vainilla, coco y ahumado vienen del roble; pimienta negra y regaliz son típicos de la Syrah/Shiraz; miel y albaricoque, del Sauternes.","Why is Sauvignon Blanc usually not matured in oak?":"¿Por qué la Sauvignon Blanc no suele criarse en roble?","To keep its characteristic aromas":"Para conservar sus aromas típicos","To increase the wine's tannin":"Para aumentar el tanino del vino","To make the wine sweeter":"Para hacerlo más dulce","To give it a darker colour":"Para darle un color más oscuro","Without oak, the grape's intense aromas stay in the spotlight.":"Sin madera, los aromas intensos de la uva siguen en primer plano.","Sauvignon Blanc is loved precisely for its intense fruity and herbaceous aromas. To protect them, it is often fermented in stainless steel and usually not matured in oak, which would add vanilla and toasty notes. Oak is not used to make it sweeter or darker.":"La Sauvignon Blanc se aprecia precisamente por sus intensos aromas de fruta e hierba. Para protegerlos, suele fermentar en acero inoxidable y normalmente no se cría en roble, que añadiría vainilla y notas tostadas. La madera no se usa para hacerla más dulce ni más oscura.","Which French wine is made from Sauvignon Blanc?":"¿Qué vino francés se elabora con Sauvignon Blanc?","Côtes du Rhône":"Côtes du Rhône","Sancerre, a white from the Loire, is made from Sauvignon Blanc.":"El Sancerre, blanco del Loira, se elabora con Sauvignon Blanc.","Sancerre is a dry, medium-bodied white from the Loire Valley with green apple, grass and high acidity. It is Sauvignon Blanc, even though the label usually does not say so. Chablis is made from Chardonnay, while Beaujolais and Côtes du Rhône are red wines.":"El Sancerre es un blanco seco del valle del Loira, de cuerpo medio, con manzana verde, hierba y acidez alta: es Sauvignon Blanc, aunque la etiqueta no suela decirlo. El Chablis se elabora con Chardonnay, mientras que el Beaujolais y el Côtes du Rhône son tintos.","Which pair of wines are classic Sauvignon Blanc wines?":"¿Qué pareja de vinos es un clásico de la Sauvignon Blanc?","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre":"Sauvignon Blanc de Nueva Zelanda y Sancerre","Chablis and white Burgundy":"Chablis y Borgoña blanco","Alsace and Mosel Riesling":"Riesling de Alsacia y del Mosela","Prosecco and Cava":"Prosecco y Cava","They are the two most popular Sauvignon Blanc wines to know.":"Son los dos vinos de Sauvignon Blanc más populares.","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc, from Marlborough for example, and Sancerre from the Loire are the two most popular examples of the grape: dry, aromatic and high in acidity. Chablis and white Burgundy are Chardonnay, while Prosecco and Cava are sparkling wines made from other grapes.":"El Sauvignon Blanc de Nueva Zelanda, por ejemplo de Marlborough, y el Sancerre del Loira son los dos ejemplos más populares de esta uva: secos, aromáticos y de acidez alta. Chablis y Borgoña blanco son Chardonnay; Prosecco y Cava son espumosos de otras variedades.","What acidity and body are typical of Sauvignon Blanc?":"¿Qué acidez y cuerpo son típicos de la Sauvignon Blanc?","High acidity, light to medium body":"Acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio","Low acidity, full body":"Acidez baja, mucho cuerpo","Medium acidity, full body":"Acidez media, mucho cuerpo","Low acidity, light body":"Acidez baja, cuerpo ligero","Sauvignon Blanc is crisp: high acidity with a light to medium body.":"La Sauvignon Blanc es viva: acidez alta y cuerpo ligero a medio.","Sauvignon Blanc makes dry wines with refreshingly high acidity and a light to medium body. Together with its intense fruity and herbaceous aromas, that freshness defines its style. A full body with medium acidity would point more towards a warm-climate Chardonnay.":"La Sauvignon Blanc da vinos secos de acidez alta y refrescante, con cuerpo ligero a medio. Junto con sus intensos aromas de fruta e hierba, esa frescura define su estilo. Un cuerpo alto con acidez media haría pensar más bien en un Chardonnay de clima cálido.","Which range of fruit is found in Sauvignon Blanc?":"¿Qué gama de frutas se encuentra en la Sauvignon Blanc?","Apple, grapefruit, passion fruit":"Manzana, pomelo, fruta de la pasión","Blackcurrant, black cherry, blackberry":"Grosella negra, cereza negra, mora","Strawberry, raspberry, red cherry":"Fresa, frambuesa, cereza roja","Apricot, honey, ripe peach":"Albaricoque, miel, melocotón maduro","Sauvignon Blanc ranges from green fruit to citrus to tropical fruit.":"La Sauvignon Blanc va de la fruta verde a los cítricos y los tropicales.","Sauvignon Blanc's fruit aromas run from green apple through grapefruit to passion fruit, often with herbaceous notes. Black fruit is typical of reds like Cabernet Sauvignon, red fruit of Pinot Noir, while apricot and honey bring Sauternes to mind. Recognising the family of fruit is the first step towards naming the grape.":"Los aromas de fruta de la Sauvignon Blanc van de la manzana verde al pomelo y hasta la fruta de la pasión, a menudo con notas herbáceas. La fruta negra es típica de tintos como el Cabernet Sauvignon, la roja de la Pinot Noir, y el albaricoque y la miel recuerdan al Sauternes. Reconocer la familia de fruta es el primer paso para adivinar la uva.","Which description matches a Pinot Grigio?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a un Pinot Grigio?","Dry, light-bodied, pear and lemon":"Seco, ligero, pera y limón","Sweet, full-bodied, apricot and honey":"Dulce, con cuerpo, albaricoque y miel","Dry, full-bodied, pineapple and vanilla":"Seco, con cuerpo, piña y vainilla","Medium, light, strawberry and raspberry":"Semiseco, ligero, fresa y frambuesa","Pinot Grigio is usually dry and light, with pear and lemon.":"El Pinot Grigio suele ser seco y ligero, con pera y limón.","Pinot Grigio usually makes dry, light-bodied wines with medium to high acidity and simple pear and lemon flavours. The other descriptions fit other wines: Sauternes (sweet, apricot and honey), an oaked warm-climate Chardonnay, and White Zinfandel. Think of it as a simple, fresh and easy white.":"El Pinot Grigio suele dar vinos secos, de cuerpo ligero, con acidez media a alta y sabores sencillos de pera y limón. Las otras descripciones encajan con otros vinos: el Sauternes (dulce, albaricoque y miel), un Chardonnay cálido con roble y el White Zinfandel. Piensa en un blanco sencillo y fresco.","Which country is Pinot Grigio mainly associated with?":"¿Con qué país se asocia sobre todo el Pinot Grigio?","Italy":"Italia","Spain":"España","New Zealand":"Nueva Zelanda","Pinot Grigio is mainly linked with Italy, though grown elsewhere too.":"El Pinot Grigio se asocia sobre todo con Italia, aunque se cultiva en otros lugares.","Pinot Grigio is a hugely popular grape mainly associated with Italy, in areas such as Veneto or Trentino, although it is grown in several other countries too. Germany is the classic home of Riesling, and New Zealand is known for Sauvignon Blanc and Pinot Noir.":"El Pinot Grigio es una uva muy popular asociada sobre todo con Italia, con zonas como el Véneto o el Trentino, aunque se cultiva en otros países. Alemania es la patria clásica de la Riesling, y Nueva Zelanda es conocida por la Sauvignon Blanc y la Pinot Noir.","Why is Pinot Grigio usually made in stainless steel without oak?":"¿Por qué el Pinot Grigio suele hacerse en acero y sin roble?","To keep its fruity flavours":"Para conservar sus sabores afrutados","To add notes of vanilla":"Para añadir notas de vainilla","To increase its tannin":"Para aumentar su tanino","To make it higher in alcohol":"Para darle más alcohol","Steel adds no aromas, so the delicate fruit stays intact.":"El acero no aporta aromas y deja intacta la fruta delicada.","Pinot Grigio has delicate pear and lemon flavours. Fermenting it in stainless steel and skipping oak maturation protects that fruit and lightness. Oak would add exactly the vanilla notes the style avoids, while tannin and alcohol do not depend on the vessel used.":"El Pinot Grigio tiene sabores delicados de pera y limón. Al fermentarlo en acero inoxidable y sin crianza en roble, la bodega protege su fruta y su ligereza. El roble añadiría precisamente la vainilla, mientras que el tanino y el alcohol no dependen del recipiente.","What range of sweetness can Riesling have?":"¿Qué gama de dulzor puede tener la Riesling?","Dry to sweet, always with high acidity":"De seco a dulce, siempre muy ácido","Always sweet, with low acidity":"Siempre dulce, con acidez baja","Always dry, with low acidity":"Siempre seco, con acidez baja","Only medium, with medium acidity":"Solo semiseco, con acidez media","Riesling can be dry, medium or sweet, but always has high acidity.":"La Riesling puede ser seca, semiseca o dulce, pero siempre muy ácida.","Riesling is versatile: it makes dry, medium and sweet wines. What does not change is its high acidity, which balances the sugar and keeps the wine fresh. So when you see «Riesling» on a label, check the origin or the description to work out how sweet it will be.":"La Riesling es versátil: da vinos secos, de dulzor medio y dulces. Lo que no cambia es su acidez alta, que equilibra el azúcar y mantiene el vino fresco. Por eso, al leer «Riesling» en una etiqueta, conviene mirar el origen o la descripción para saber cuánto dulzor tendrá.","Which country is the classic home of Riesling?":"¿Cuál es el país clásico de la Riesling?","Chile":"Chile","Germany is Riesling's classic home, making it from dry to sweet.":"Alemania es la patria clásica de la Riesling, de seca a dulce.","Riesling is the classic grape of Germany, where it is made across the full sweetness range, from dry to sweet. Fine dry Rieslings also come from Alsace in France and from Australia. Among the key white grapes, Italy is linked mainly with Pinot Grigio.":"La Riesling es la uva clásica de Alemania, donde se elabora en toda la gama de dulzor, de seco a dulce. También llegan excelentes Riesling secos de Alsacia, en Francia, y de Australia. Entre las grandes blancas, Italia se asocia sobre todo con el Pinot Grigio.","In which style do Alsace and Australia make Riesling?":"¿En qué estilo elaboran Riesling Alsacia y Australia?","Dry":"Seco","Sweet":"Dulce","Alsace and Australia are known for dry Riesling.":"Alsacia y Australia son conocidas por sus Riesling secos.","While Germany makes Riesling from dry to sweet, Alsace in France and Australia make it in a dry style. These are very fresh wines with citrus such as lime and lemon, floral notes and sometimes peach. Knowing the origin therefore helps you predict the sweetness.":"Mientras Alemania elabora Riesling de seco a dulce, Alsacia, en Francia, y Australia lo hacen en estilo seco. Son vinos muy frescos, con cítricos como lima y limón, notas florales y a veces melocotón. Conocer el origen ayuda, por tanto, a prever el dulzor.","Why does a sweet Riesling not taste cloying?":"¿Por qué un Riesling dulce no resulta empalagoso?","Its high acidity balances the sweetness":"Su acidez alta equilibra el dulzor","Oak flavours mask the sugar":"El roble tapa el azúcar","Tannin dries out the mouth":"El tanino seca la boca","High alcohol hides the sugar":"El alcohol alto oculta el azúcar","All Rieslings are high in acid, which counterbalances the sugar.":"Todos los Riesling son muy ácidos, y la acidez contrarresta el azúcar.","Riesling always has high acidity. In sweet or medium wines, that acidity balances the sugar and keeps each sip fresh. Riesling is usually not oaked, as a white wine it has almost no tannin, and sweet German Rieslings are often low in alcohol, so the other options do not apply.":"La Riesling siempre tiene una acidez alta. En los vinos dulces o semisecos, esa acidez equilibra el azúcar y mantiene fresco cada sorbo. La Riesling no suele criarse en roble, como blanco casi no tiene tanino y los Riesling dulces alemanes suelen tener poco alcohol.","Which aromas can a Riesling show?":"¿Qué aromas puede mostrar una Riesling?","Floral, lime, peach":"Flores, lima, melocotón","Blackcurrant, mint, bell pepper":"Grosella negra, menta, pimiento","Riesling ranges from floral and citrus aromas to stone fruit.":"La Riesling va de las flores y los cítricos a la fruta de hueso.","Riesling has pronounced aromas that can range from flowers and green apple to citrus such as lime and lemon, and on to peach and apricot. It is usually unoaked, so vanilla, cedar and smoke are not typical. Black pepper and blackcurrant belong to black grape varieties.":"La Riesling tiene aromas intensos que van de las flores y la manzana verde a cítricos como la lima y el limón, hasta el melocotón y el albaricoque. No suele criarse en roble, así que vainilla, cedro y ahumado no son típicos. Pimienta negra y grosella negra son de uvas tintas.","Which of the four key white grapes is most often matured in oak?":"¿Cuál de las cuatro grandes blancas se cría más a menudo en roble?","Chardonnay can be oaked; the other three usually are not.":"La Chardonnay puede criarse en roble; las otras tres normalmente no.","Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling are often fermented in stainless steel and usually not matured in oak, to protect their fruity aromas. Chardonnay, on the other hand, is often aged in oak, which adds vanilla: think of many white Burgundies or Californian Chardonnays.":"La Sauvignon Blanc, el Pinot Grigio y la Riesling suelen fermentar en acero inoxidable y normalmente no pasan por roble, para proteger su fruta. La Chardonnay, en cambio, se cría a menudo en barrica, que aporta vainilla: pensemos en muchos Borgoña blancos o en los Chardonnay californianos.","A wine list says «full-bodied, ripe tropical fruit and vanilla». Which wine is it?":"En una carta: «con cuerpo, fruta tropical madura y vainilla». ¿Qué vino es?","A Californian Chardonnay":"Un Chardonnay de California","A Chablis":"Un Chablis","An Italian Pinot Grigio":"Un Pinot Grigio italiano","An Alsace Riesling":"Un Riesling de Alsacia","Warm climate plus oak gives body, tropical fruit and vanilla.":"Clima cálido y roble dan cuerpo, fruta tropical y vainilla.","Ripe tropical fruit points to a warm climate, vanilla points to oak, and a full body completes the picture: this is the style of a Californian Chardonnay. Chablis is light and unoaked, Pinot Grigio is light with pear and lemon, and Alsace Riesling is dry, floral and unoaked.":"La fruta tropical madura indica un clima cálido, la vainilla indica roble y el cuerpo completa el cuadro: es el estilo de un Chardonnay californiano. El Chablis es ligero y sin madera, el Pinot Grigio es ligero con pera y limón, y el Riesling de Alsacia es seco, floral y sin roble.","Which white grape is used to make Champagne?":"¿Qué uva blanca se usa para elaborar Champagne?","Chardonnay is Champagne's white grape, often blended with Pinot Noir.":"La Chardonnay es la uva blanca del Champagne, a menudo con Pinot Noir.","Of the four key white grapes, only Chardonnay goes into Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir, a black grape. The result is a sparkling wine that is usually dry, with high acidity, green apple, lemon and notes of toasted bread. The other three grapes are not used for Champagne.":"De las cuatro grandes blancas, solo la Chardonnay entra en el Champagne, donde a menudo se mezcla con Pinot Noir, una uva tinta. El resultado es un espumoso normalmente seco, de acidez alta, con manzana verde, limón y notas de pan tostado. Las otras tres variedades no se usan para el Champagne.","A list says «Australia, dry, aromas of lime and blossom». Which grape is it?":"En una carta: «Australia, seco, aromas de lima y flores». ¿Qué uva es?","Lime and blossom in a dry Australian white point to Riesling.":"Lima y flores en un blanco seco australiano apuntan a la Riesling.","Australia makes Riesling in a dry style, with citrus such as lime and floral notes, carried by high acidity. Australian Chardonnay leans towards riper fruit and often vanilla; Sauvignon Blanc pairs citrus with herbaceous notes; and Pinot Grigio shows pear and lemon without marked floral aromas.":"Australia elabora Riesling en estilo seco, con cítricos como la lima y notas florales, sostenidos por una acidez alta. El Chardonnay australiano tiende a fruta más madura y a menudo vainilla; la Sauvignon Blanc une cítricos y notas herbáceas; y el Pinot Grigio tiene pera y limón, sin aromas florales marcados.","Which structure is typical of Cabernet Sauvignon?":"¿Qué estructura es típica del Cabernet Sauvignon?","High tannin and high acidity":"Tanino alto y acidez alta","Low tannin and high acidity":"Tanino bajo y acidez alta","Medium tannin and medium acidity":"Tanino medio y acidez media","Low tannin and low acidity":"Tanino bajo y acidez baja","Cabernet Sauvignon is high in both tannin and acidity.":"El Cabernet Sauvignon tiene tanto tanino como acidez altos.","Cabernet Sauvignon makes dry reds with high tannin and high acidity, and a medium to full body. Merlot has medium tannin and acidity, while Pinot Noir has high acidity but low to medium tannin. That high tannin is exactly why Cabernet is so often blended with Merlot.":"El Cabernet Sauvignon da tintos secos con tanino alto y acidez alta, de cuerpo medio a alto. El Merlot tiene tanino y acidez medios, y la Pinot Noir acidez alta pero tanino bajo a medio. Ese tanino alto explica precisamente por qué el Cabernet se mezcla tan a menudo con Merlot.","Which fruit is the signature aroma of Cabernet Sauvignon?":"¿Qué fruta es el aroma típico del Cabernet Sauvignon?","Pear":"Pera","Raspberry":"Frambuesa","Blackcurrant is Cabernet Sauvignon's hallmark aroma.":"La grosella negra es el aroma emblemático del Cabernet Sauvignon.","Cabernet Sauvignon smells of black fruit, above all blackcurrant and black cherry, often with notes of green bell pepper and mint. Strawberry and raspberry are red fruits typical of Pinot Noir or Beaujolais, while pear belongs to whites such as Pinot Grigio.":"El Cabernet Sauvignon huele a frutas negras, sobre todo grosella negra y cereza negra, a menudo con notas de pimiento verde y menta. La fresa y la frambuesa son frutas rojas típicas de la Pinot Noir o del Beaujolais, y la pera se asocia a blancos como el Pinot Grigio.","Which herbaceous notes can Cabernet Sauvignon show?":"¿Qué notas herbáceas puede tener el Cabernet Sauvignon?","Green bell pepper and mint":"Pimiento verde y menta","Black pepper and liquorice":"Pimienta negra y regaliz","Dried herbs and cloves":"Hierbas secas y clavo","Flowers and honey":"Flores y miel","Green pepper and mint often sit alongside Cabernet's blackcurrant.":"Pimiento verde y menta suelen acompañar a la grosella negra del Cabernet.","Besides blackcurrant and black cherry, Cabernet Sauvignon often shows herbaceous notes of green bell pepper and mint. Black pepper and liquorice are spices typical of Syrah/Shiraz, dried herbs are found in Chianti, and cloves come from oak. Those «green» notes are therefore a useful clue for recognising it.":"Además de grosella negra y cereza negra, el Cabernet Sauvignon muestra a menudo notas herbáceas de pimiento verde y menta. Pimienta negra y regaliz son especias típicas de la Syrah/Shiraz; las hierbas secas aparecen en el Chianti; y el clavo procede del roble. Esas notas «verdes» son, por tanto, una buena pista para reconocerlo.","Which aromas does oak add to a Cabernet Sauvignon?":"¿Qué aromas añade el roble a un Cabernet Sauvignon?","Cedar and vanilla":"Cedro y vainilla","Mint and green bell pepper":"Menta y pimiento verde","Blackcurrant and black cherry":"Grosella negra y cereza negra","Lemon and green apple":"Limón y manzana verde","Oak brings cedar and vanilla; fruit and herbaceous notes come from the grape.":"El roble aporta cedro y vainilla; la fruta y las notas herbáceas vienen de la uva.","Cabernet Sauvignon is often matured in oak, which adds cedar and vanilla notes. Blackcurrant, black cherry, mint and green bell pepper, on the other hand, come from the grape itself. Separating grape aromas from oak aromas helps you understand how the wine was made.":"El Cabernet Sauvignon se cría a menudo en roble, que añade notas de cedro y vainilla. La grosella negra, la cereza negra, la menta y el pimiento verde, en cambio, proceden de la propia uva. Distinguir los aromas de la uva de los de la madera ayuda a entender cómo se ha hecho el vino.","Why is Cabernet Sauvignon often blended with Merlot?":"¿Por qué se mezcla a menudo el Cabernet Sauvignon con Merlot?","Merlot softens the tannin and adds body":"El Merlot suaviza el tanino y da cuerpo","Merlot raises acidity and tannin":"El Merlot aumenta la acidez y el tanino","Merlot makes the wine sweet":"El Merlot hace el vino dulce","Merlot makes the colour lighter":"El Merlot aclara el color","Merlot softens Cabernet's high tannin and adds body.":"El Merlot suaviza el tanino alto del Cabernet y añade cuerpo.","Cabernet Sauvignon has a lot of tannin. Blending it with Merlot, which has medium tannin and acidity, gives a softer wine with more body. It works the other way round too: Cabernet gives Merlot extra tannin and acidity. Bordeaux is the most famous region for this blend.":"El Cabernet Sauvignon tiene mucho tanino. Al mezclarlo con Merlot, de tanino y acidez medios, se obtiene un vino más suave y con más cuerpo. También funciona al revés: el Cabernet aporta al Merlot tanino y acidez. Burdeos es la región más famosa por esta mezcla.","In Australia, Cabernet Sauvignon is sometimes blended with which grape?":"En Australia, ¿con qué uva se mezcla a veces el Cabernet Sauvignon?","Shiraz":"Shiraz","In Australia, Shiraz adds spicy aromas to Cabernet Sauvignon.":"En Australia, la Shiraz aporta aromas especiados al Cabernet Sauvignon.","Cabernet Sauvignon is widely grown in Australia, where it is sometimes blended with Shiraz, which adds spicy aromas. Pinot Noir is not usually blended when making red wine, and Riesling and Chardonnay are white grapes that do not go into red blends.":"El Cabernet Sauvignon se cultiva mucho en Australia, donde a veces se mezcla con Shiraz, que aporta aromas especiados. La Pinot Noir no suele mezclarse para hacer tintos, y la Riesling y la Chardonnay son uvas blancas que no entran en los tintos.","What structure does Merlot usually have?":"¿Qué estructura suele tener el Merlot?","Medium acidity and tannin, medium to full body":"Acidez y tanino medios, cuerpo medio a alto","High acidity and tannin, full body":"Acidez y tanino altos, mucho cuerpo","High acidity, low tannin, light body":"Acidez alta, tanino bajo, cuerpo ligero","Low acidity, high tannin, light body":"Acidez baja, tanino alto, cuerpo ligero","Merlot is soft: medium acidity and tannin, medium to full body.":"El Merlot es suave: acidez y tanino medios, cuerpo medio a alto.","Merlot makes wines that are generally dry, with a medium to full body and medium acidity and tannin. Cabernet Sauvignon has high tannin and acidity, while Pinot Noir has high acidity, low to medium tannin and a light to medium body. That is why Merlot feels softer.":"El Merlot da vinos generalmente secos, de cuerpo medio a alto, con acidez y tanino medios. El Cabernet Sauvignon tiene tanino y acidez altos, y la Pinot Noir acidez alta, tanino bajo a medio y cuerpo ligero a medio. Por eso el Merlot resulta más suave.","Which fruits are typically found in Merlot?":"¿Qué frutas se encuentran típicamente en el Merlot?","Strawberry and red plum through to blackberry and black plum":"De fresa y ciruela roja a mora y ciruela negra","Green apple, lemon and grapefruit":"Manzana verde, limón y pomelo","Apricot, peach and honey":"Albaricoque, melocotón y miel","Pear, flowers and lime":"Pera, flores y lima","Merlot ranges from red fruit to black fruit.":"El Merlot va de las frutas rojas a las negras.","Merlot can show red fruit such as strawberry and red plum, or black fruit such as blackberry and black plum. It is often matured in oak, which adds vanilla. The other options describe aromas of white wines such as Sauvignon Blanc, Sauternes or Riesling.":"El Merlot puede tener sabores de frutas rojas, como fresa y ciruela roja, o de frutas negras, como mora y ciruela negra. Suele criarse en roble, que añade vainilla. Las demás opciones describen aromas de blancos como Sauvignon Blanc, Sauternes o Riesling.","What does Cabernet Sauvignon add to a blend with Merlot?":"¿Qué aporta el Cabernet Sauvignon a una mezcla con Merlot?","Tannin and acidity":"Tanino y acidez","Sweetness and softness":"Dulzor y suavidad","Bubbles and freshness":"Burbujas y frescura","Pale colour and lightness":"Color claro y ligereza","Cabernet brings tannin and acidity; Merlot brings softness and body.":"El Cabernet aporta tanino y acidez; el Merlot, suavidad y cuerpo.","In the Bordeaux blend the two grapes complete each other. Merlot, with medium tannin and acidity, brings softness and body. Cabernet Sauvignon, with high tannin and acidity, gives the wine structure and freshness. The result is a dry, medium- to full-bodied red with black fruit, often with cedar from oak.":"En la mezcla de Burdeos las dos uvas se complementan. El Merlot, con tanino y acidez medios, aporta suavidad y cuerpo. El Cabernet Sauvignon, con tanino y acidez altos, da estructura y frescura. El resultado es un tinto seco, de cuerpo medio a alto, con fruta negra y a menudo cedro del roble.","Which countries make soft, fruity Merlot?":"¿Qué países elaboran Merlot suaves y afrutados?","Chile and California":"Chile y California","Portugal and Spain":"Portugal y España","Chile and California are known for soft, fruity Merlot.":"Chile y California son conocidos por sus Merlot suaves y afrutados.","Merlot is grown in many places; Chile and California use it for soft, fruity, easy-drinking wines, often with black plum and blackberry. Germany and Alsace are linked with Riesling, New Zealand and the Loire with Sauvignon Blanc, and Portugal with Port.":"El Merlot se cultiva en muchos lugares; en Chile y California se elaboran con él vinos suaves, afrutados y fáciles de beber, a menudo con ciruela negra y mora. Alemania y Alsacia se asocian a la Riesling, Nueva Zelanda y el Loira a la Sauvignon Blanc, y Portugal al Port.","Which region is most famous for Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon blends?":"¿Qué región es la más famosa por la mezcla Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon?","Bordeaux":"Burdeos (Bordeaux)","Burgundy":"Borgoña","Bordeaux is the home of the Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon blend.":"Burdeos es la cuna de la mezcla Merlot-Cabernet Sauvignon.","Bordeaux in France is the most famous region for blending Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon, a blend now common in many other countries too. Burgundy uses Pinot Noir for its reds and Chardonnay for its whites, while Champagne is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir.":"Burdeos, en Francia, es la región más famosa por la mezcla de Merlot y Cabernet Sauvignon, hoy habitual en muchos otros países. Borgoña usa Pinot Noir para sus tintos y Chardonnay para sus blancos, y el Champagne se elabora con Chardonnay y Pinot Noir.","Which description fits Pinot Noir?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a la Pinot Noir?","Light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin":"Cuerpo ligero a medio, acidez alta, tanino bajo a medio","Full body, medium acidity, high tannin":"Mucho cuerpo, acidez media, tanino alto","Full body, high acidity, high tannin":"Mucho cuerpo, acidez alta, tanino alto","Medium body, low acidity, medium tannin":"Cuerpo medio, acidez baja, tanino medio","Pinot Noir is a fresh, delicate red with modest tannin.":"La Pinot Noir es un tinto fresco y delicado, con poco tanino.","Pinot Noir makes reds that are usually dry, light to medium in body, with high acidity and low to medium tannin. It has red fruit aromas such as strawberry, red cherry and raspberry. A full body with high tannin describes Cabernet Sauvignon or Shiraz instead.":"La Pinot Noir da tintos normalmente secos, de cuerpo ligero a medio, con acidez alta y tanino bajo a medio. Tiene aromas de frutas rojas como fresa, cereza roja y frambuesa. Un cuerpo alto con tanino alto describe más bien al Cabernet Sauvignon o a la Shiraz.","Which fruit aromas are typical of Pinot Noir?":"¿Qué aromas de fruta son típicos de la Pinot Noir?","Strawberry, red cherry, raspberry":"Fresa, cereza roja, frambuesa","Blackcurrant, black cherry, mint":"Grosella negra, cereza negra, menta","Blackberry, black pepper, liquorice":"Mora, pimienta negra, regaliz","Pear, lemon, apple":"Pera, limón, manzana","Pinot Noir smells of red fruit.":"La Pinot Noir huele a frutas rojas.","Pinot Noir is the red-fruit grape: strawberry, red cherry and raspberry, often with vanilla and smoke when oaked. Blackcurrant and mint point to Cabernet Sauvignon; blackberry, black pepper and liquorice point to Syrah/Shiraz; and pear and lemon are white-wine aromas.":"La Pinot Noir es la uva de las frutas rojas: fresa, cereza roja y frambuesa, a menudo con vainilla y ahumado si pasa por roble. Grosella negra y menta apuntan al Cabernet Sauvignon; mora, pimienta negra y regaliz, a la Syrah/Shiraz; pera y limón son aromas de vinos blancos.","Which grape is used for red Burgundy?":"¿Con qué uva se elaboran los Borgoña tintos?","Syrah":"Syrah","Red Burgundy is made from Pinot Noir.":"Los Borgoña tintos se elaboran con Pinot Noir.","Burgundy (Bourgogne) uses Pinot Noir for its reds and Chardonnay for its whites. The reds are dry, light to medium-bodied, with high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit. Merlot and Cabernet Sauvignon are the grapes of Bordeaux, and Syrah is typical of the Northern Rhône.":"Borgoña usa Pinot Noir para los tintos y Chardonnay para los blancos. Los tintos son secos, ligeros a medios, con acidez alta, tanino bajo a medio y frutas rojas. Merlot y Cabernet Sauvignon son las uvas de Burdeos, y la Syrah es típica del norte del Ródano.","In which country is Pinot Noir the main black grape?":"¿En qué país es la Pinot Noir la principal uva tinta?","Australia":"Australia","South Africa":"Sudáfrica","In New Zealand, Pinot Noir is the leading black grape.":"En Nueva Zelanda, la Pinot Noir es la principal uva tinta.","Besides Burgundy, Pinot Noir is the main black grape of New Zealand, in regions such as Central Otago. Australia, Chile and South Africa are mentioned mainly for Cabernet Sauvignon, and Australia also for Shiraz. New Zealand is also famous for its Sauvignon Blanc.":"Además de Borgoña, la Pinot Noir es la principal uva tinta de Nueva Zelanda, con zonas como Central Otago. Australia, Chile y Sudáfrica se citan sobre todo por el Cabernet Sauvignon, y Australia también por la Shiraz. Nueva Zelanda es famosa además por su Sauvignon Blanc.","When making red wine, Pinot Noir is usually...":"Para los vinos tintos, la Pinot Noir normalmente se...","made on its own, without other grapes":"elabora sola, sin otras uvas","blended with Cabernet Sauvignon":"mezcla con Cabernet Sauvignon","blended with Shiraz":"mezcla con Shiraz","blended with Merlot":"mezcla con Merlot","For red wines, Pinot Noir is not usually blended.":"En los tintos, la Pinot Noir no suele mezclarse.","Unlike Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot and Shiraz, which are often blended with each other, Pinot Noir is usually made on its own when producing red wine. The one important blend to remember is Champagne, where Pinot Noir is combined with Chardonnay to make a sparkling wine.":"A diferencia del Cabernet Sauvignon, el Merlot y la Shiraz, que a menudo se mezclan entre sí, la Pinot Noir suele elaborarse sola en los tintos. La única mezcla importante que conviene recordar es la del Champagne, donde la Pinot Noir se une a la Chardonnay para hacer un espumoso.","What is Syrah called in Australia?":"¿Cómo se llama la Syrah en Australia?","Zinfandel":"Zinfandel","Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia are the same grape.":"Syrah en Francia y Shiraz en Australia son la misma uva.","The same grape has two names: Syrah in France and Shiraz in Australia. The name on the label therefore hints at the origin and often the style, fresher and more peppery in France, fuller and riper in Australia's warm regions. Merlot and Pinot Noir are different grapes.":"La misma uva tiene dos nombres: Syrah en Francia y Shiraz en Australia. El nombre de la etiqueta da, por tanto, una pista sobre el origen y a menudo sobre el estilo: más fresco y con pimienta en Francia, más corpulento y maduro en las zonas cálidas de Australia. Merlot y Pinot Noir son otras uvas.","Which spices are typical of Syrah/Shiraz?":"¿Qué especias son típicas de la Syrah/Shiraz?","Vanilla and coconut":"Vainilla y coco","White pepper and dried herbs":"Pimienta blanca y hierbas secas","Syrah/Shiraz pairs black fruit with black pepper and liquorice.":"La Syrah/Shiraz une fruta negra con pimienta negra y regaliz.","Syrah/Shiraz typically shows black fruit such as blackberry and black cherry, with spices such as black pepper and liquorice. Vanilla and coconut come from oak rather than the grape. Mint and green bell pepper are Cabernet Sauvignon notes, and white pepper is mentioned for Côtes du Rhône.":"Los sabores típicos de la Syrah/Shiraz son frutas negras como la mora y la cereza negra, con especias como la pimienta negra y el regaliz. La vainilla y el coco vienen del roble, no de la uva. Menta y pimiento verde son notas del Cabernet Sauvignon; la pimienta blanca se cita en el Côtes du Rhône.","What style does Northern Rhône Syrah often have?":"¿Qué estilo suele tener la Syrah del norte del Ródano?","Medium body, fresh blackberry and black pepper":"Cuerpo medio, mora fresca y pimienta negra","Full body, jammy black cherry":"Mucho cuerpo, cereza negra confitada","Light body, strawberry and raspberry":"Cuerpo ligero, fresa y frambuesa","Sweet, black plum and honey":"Dulce, ciruela negra y miel","Northern Rhône Syrah is fresher: medium body, blackberry and pepper.":"En el norte del Ródano la Syrah es más fresca: cuerpo medio, mora y pimienta.","France's Northern Rhône can produce medium-bodied Syrah with fresh blackberry and black pepper. In warm parts of Australia the grapes ripen further and Shiraz becomes full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice. Same grape, different climates, different styles. Climate explains the difference.":"El norte del Ródano, en Francia, puede dar Syrah de cuerpo medio, con mora fresca y pimienta negra. En las zonas cálidas de Australia la uva madura más y la Shiraz se vuelve de cuerpo alto, con cereza negra confitada y regaliz. La misma uva, climas distintos, estilos distintos. El clima explica la diferencia.","Why is Shiraz from warm parts of Australia often full-bodied?":"¿Por qué la Shiraz de las zonas cálidas de Australia suele tener mucho cuerpo?","The heat makes the grapes riper":"El calor hace que la uva madure más","The grapes are picked unripe":"La uva se vendimia sin madurar","The wine is made without skins":"El vino se hace sin hollejos","Unfermented juice is added":"Se añade zumo sin fermentar","More heat means riper, sweeter grapes and a fuller, riper wine.":"Más calor = uva más madura y azucarada = vino con más cuerpo y madurez.","In warm climates grapes ripen reliably and build up more sugar. That gives riper, fuller wines: Shiraz from warm Australian regions such as the Barossa Valley is full-bodied, with jammy black cherry and liquorice. In the cooler Northern Rhône, the style is medium-bodied instead.":"En climas cálidos la uva madura con regularidad y acumula más azúcar. Así salen vinos más maduros y con más cuerpo: la Shiraz de zonas cálidas de Australia, como el Barossa Valley, tiene mucho cuerpo, con cereza negra confitada y regaliz. En el norte del Ródano, más fresco, el estilo es de cuerpo medio.","Which notes does oak add to many Syrah/Shiraz wines?":"¿Qué notas añade el roble a muchos Syrah/Shiraz?","Vanilla or coconut":"Vainilla o coco","Black pepper or liquorice":"Pimienta negra o regaliz","Blackberry or black cherry":"Mora o cereza negra","Grass or asparagus":"Hierba o espárrago","Oak gives vanilla or coconut; black fruit and spice come from the grape.":"El roble da vainilla o coco; la fruta negra y las especias vienen de la uva.","Many Syrahs and Shirazes are matured in oak, which adds vanilla or coconut notes. Black fruit (blackberry, black cherry) and spice (black pepper, liquorice), on the other hand, are the grape's own aromas. Grass and asparagus are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc.":"Muchos Syrah y Shiraz se crían en roble, que añade notas de vainilla o de coco. La fruta negra (mora, cereza negra) y las especias (pimienta negra, regaliz), en cambio, son aromas propios de la uva. Hierba y espárrago son notas herbáceas típicas de la Sauvignon Blanc.","A list says «light-bodied, high acidity, strawberry and red cherry». Which grape?":"En una carta: «ligero, acidez alta, fresa y cereza roja». ¿Qué uva?","Light body, high acidity and red fruit point to Pinot Noir.":"Cuerpo ligero, acidez alta y frutas rojas apuntan a la Pinot Noir.","Of the four key black grapes, Pinot Noir is the lightest and freshest: light to medium body, high acidity, low to medium tannin and red fruit. Cabernet Sauvignon and Shiraz are fuller, with black fruit, while Merlot has medium acidity and a medium to full body.":"De las cuatro grandes tintas, la Pinot Noir es la más ligera y fresca: cuerpo ligero a medio, acidez alta, tanino bajo a medio y frutas rojas. El Cabernet Sauvignon y la Shiraz tienen más cuerpo y fruta negra, y el Merlot tiene acidez media y cuerpo medio a alto.","A list says «Australia, full-bodied, intense black cherry and liquorice». Which grape?":"En una carta: «Australia, con cuerpo, cereza negra intensa y regaliz». ¿Qué uva?","Black cherry and liquorice in a full Australian red point to Shiraz.":"Cereza negra y regaliz en un tinto australiano con cuerpo apuntan a la Shiraz.","Warm Australian regions such as the Barossa Valley make full-bodied Shiraz with ripe black cherry and liquorice. Pinot Noir is light with red fruit, Merlot is soft with plum and blackberry, and Riesling is a white grape, so none of them fits this description.":"Las zonas cálidas de Australia, como el Barossa Valley, producen Shiraz con mucho cuerpo, con cereza negra madura y regaliz. La Pinot Noir es ligera y de frutas rojas, el Merlot es suave con ciruela y mora, y la Riesling es una uva blanca.","Which black grape is used to make Champagne?":"¿Qué uva tinta se usa para elaborar Champagne?","Champagne often blends Pinot Noir with Chardonnay.":"El Champagne mezcla a menudo Pinot Noir y Chardonnay.","Of the four key black grapes, only Pinot Noir goes into Champagne, where it is often blended with Chardonnay. Although it is a black grape, its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a pale base wine. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon and Syrah are not Champagne grapes.":"De las cuatro grandes tintas, solo la Pinot Noir entra en el Champagne, donde a menudo se mezcla con Chardonnay. Aunque es una uva tinta, su zumo es incoloro: si se separan enseguida los hollejos, se obtiene una base clara. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon y Syrah no son uvas del Champagne.","In which regions is it common to grow black grapes like Cabernet Sauvignon?":"¿En qué regiones es habitual cultivar uvas tintas como el Cabernet Sauvignon?","Warm regions, where grapes ripen reliably":"Regiones cálidas, donde la uva madura con regularidad","Cool regions, where grapes struggle to ripen":"Regiones frescas, donde a la uva le cuesta madurar","Regions with no winter, where vines never rest":"Regiones sin invierno, donde la vid no descansa","Regions near the poles, with weak sunlight":"Regiones cerca de los polos, con luz débil","Warm climates ripen grapes well, so black grapes are commonly grown there.":"En climas cálidos la uva madura bien: allí es habitual cultivar uvas tintas.","Warm regions closer to the Equator, such as parts of Australia and California, have high temperatures and intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably and black grapes are commonly grown. In cool regions such as Germany and northern France, white grapes are grown more often.":"Las regiones cálidas, más cerca del ecuador, como partes de Australia y California, tienen temperaturas altas y sol intenso: la uva madura con regularidad y es habitual cultivar uvas tintas. En las regiones frescas, como Alemania y el norte de Francia, se cultivan más a menudo uvas blancas.","Still wine":"Vino tranquilo","Wine without bubbles; 8–15% abv, mostly 11.5–14%.":"Vino sin burbujas; 8–15 % vol., casi siempre 11,5–14 %.","Sparkling wine":"Vino espumoso","Bubbles of carbon dioxide from fermentation. E.g. Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.":"Burbujas de dióxido de carbono de la fermentación. Ej.: Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.","Fortified wine":"Vino fortificado","Wine with added alcohol, 15–22% abv. E.g. Sherry, Port.":"Vino con alcohol añadido, 15–22 % vol. Ej.: Sherry, Port.","Alcohol by volume: 10% means one tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"Porcentaje de alcohol en volumen: 10 % = una décima parte es alcohol.","Dry wine":"Vino seco","No or very little sugar: the yeast turned it all into alcohol.":"Nada o muy poco azúcar: las levaduras lo convirtieron todo en alcohol.","Comes from the juice, makes the mouth water, refreshes and balances sweetness.":"Viene del zumo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor.","From black grape skins; dries the mouth. High: red Bordeaux, Chianti.":"De los hollejos de uva tinta; seca la boca. Alto: Bordeaux tinto, Chianti.","How mouth-filling a wine is: light (Pinot Grigio), medium (Sancerre), full (Sauternes).":"Cuánto llena la boca: ligero (Pinot Grigio), medio (Sancerre), con cuerpo (Sauternes).","Black grapes, a few hours on the skins, then fermented without them.":"Uvas tintas, unas horas con los hollejos y luego fermentación sin ellos.","Cool-climate Chardonnay":"Chardonnay de clima fresco","High acidity, light to medium body, green apple and lemon (e.g. Chablis).":"Acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio, manzana verde y limón (ej. Chablis).","Warm-climate Chardonnay":"Chardonnay de clima cálido","Medium acidity, medium to full body, peach, pineapple, banana; often vanilla from oak.":"Acidez media, cuerpo medio a alto, melocotón, piña, plátano; a menudo vainilla del roble.","White Burgundy: which grape?":"Borgoña blanco: ¿qué uva?","Chardonnay; medium body, high acidity, lemon and peach, sometimes vanilla.":"Chardonnay; cuerpo medio, acidez alta, limón y melocotón, a veces vainilla.","Dry, pronounced aromas, high acidity; fruit from apple to grapefruit to passion fruit.":"Seco, aromas intensos, acidez alta; fruta de manzana a pomelo y fruta de la pasión.","Sauvignon Blanc herbaceous notes":"Notas herbáceas de la Sauvignon Blanc","Asparagus, green bell pepper, cut grass.":"Espárrago, pimiento verde, hierba cortada.","Key Sauvignon Blanc wines":"Vinos clave de Sauvignon Blanc","New Zealand Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre (Loire, France).":"Sauvignon Blanc de Nueva Zelanda y Sancerre (Loira, Francia).","Usually dry, light, medium to high acidity, pear and lemon; mainly Italy.":"Normalmente seco, ligero, acidez media a alta, pera y limón; sobre todo Italia.","Dry to sweet, always high acidity; floral, lime, lemon, peach, apricot.":"De seco a dulce, siempre acidez alta; flores, lima, limón, melocotón, albaricoque.","Riesling: where and in what style?":"Riesling: ¿dónde y en qué estilo?","Germany: dry to sweet. Alsace and Australia: dry.":"Alemania: de seco a dulce. Alsacia y Australia: seco.","Aromatic whites without oak":"Blancos aromáticos sin roble","Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio and Riesling: usually stainless steel, to keep the fruit.":"Sauvignon Blanc, Pinot Grigio y Riesling: normalmente acero inoxidable, para conservar la fruta.","Dry, high tannin and acidity, medium to full body; blackcurrant, green pepper, mint.":"Seco, tanino y acidez altos, cuerpo medio a alto; grosella negra, pimiento verde, menta.","Cabernet Sauvignon + oak":"Cabernet Sauvignon + roble","Cedar and vanilla notes.":"Notas de cedro y vainilla.","Dry, medium to full body, medium acidity and tannin; red and black fruit, vanilla from oak.":"Seco, cuerpo medio a alto, acidez y tanino medios; fruta roja y negra, vainilla del roble.","Bordeaux blend":"Mezcla de Burdeos","Cabernet Sauvignon (tannin, acidity) + Merlot (softness, body).":"Cabernet Sauvignon (tanino, acidez) + Merlot (suavidad, cuerpo).","Dry, light to medium, high acidity, low to medium tannin; strawberry, red cherry, raspberry.":"Seco, ligero a medio, acidez alta, tanino bajo a medio; fresa, cereza roja, frambuesa.","Where is Pinot Noir key?":"¿Dónde destaca la Pinot Noir?","Red Burgundy, New Zealand (main black grape) and Champagne with Chardonnay.":"Borgoña tinto, Nueva Zelanda (principal uva tinta) y Champagne con Chardonnay.","Syrah or Shiraz?":"¿Syrah o Shiraz?","Same grape: Syrah in France, Shiraz in Australia.":"La misma uva: Syrah en Francia, Shiraz en Australia.","Syrah/Shiraz: aromas":"Syrah/Shiraz: aromas","Blackberry, black cherry, black pepper, liquorice; oak: vanilla, coconut.":"Mora, cereza negra, pimienta negra, regaliz; roble: vainilla, coco.","Northern Rhône vs warm Australia":"Norte del Ródano vs Australia cálida","Rhône: medium body, fresh blackberry, black pepper. Australia: full, jammy black cherry, liquorice.":"Ródano: cuerpo medio, mora fresca, pimienta negra. Australia: con cuerpo, cereza negra confitada, regaliz.","Where is Cabernet Sauvignon widely grown?":"¿Dónde se cultiva mucho el Cabernet Sauvignon?","Bordeaux, California, Australia, Chile, South Africa.":"Burdeos, California, Australia, Chile, Sudáfrica.","Grapes, vines and climate":"La uva, la vid y el clima","How wine is made":"Cómo se hace el vino","Types and styles of wine":"Tipos y estilos de vino","The four key white grapes":"Las cuatro grandes blancas","The four key black grapes":"Las cuatro grandes tintas","Famous wines from the key grapes":"Vinos famosos de las uvas principales","Other wines to know":"Otros vinos que conocer","Storing and serving wine":"Conservar y servir el vino","Food and wine":"Comida y vino","Tasting: first steps":"Catar: primeros pasos","From vine to wine":"De la viña al vino","Types, styles and grapes":"Tipos, estilos y uvas","Store, serve, pair":"Conservar, servir, maridar"},"ar":{"Wine starts from a simple idea: crush grapes to free their sweet juice, then let that juice ferment. That is why wine can be described as fermented grape juice. To understand what ends up in the glass, it helps to start with the grape itself, which has two main parts: the skin on the outside and the pulp on the inside. Each one gives something different to the wine.":"El vino parte de una idea sencilla: se estrujan las uvas para liberar su jugo dulce y después se deja fermentar. Por eso el vino se puede definir como jugo de uva fermentado. Para entender lo que acabará en la copa, conviene empezar por la uva, que tiene dos partes principales: la piel por fuera y la pulpa por dentro. Cada una aporta algo distinto al vino.","The pulp is the soft, fleshy part of the grape and it holds the juice. That juice is made up mostly of water, sugar and acid. One important detail: the pulp has the same colour whether the grape is white or black. So the colour of a red wine does not come from the juice but from the skins, a key idea for understanding later how the different wines are made.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda y carnosa de la uva y es la que contiene el jugo. Ese jugo está formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Un detalle importante: la pulpa tiene el mismo color tanto en las uvas blancas como en las tintas. Por eso el color de un vino tinto no viene del jugo sino de las pieles, una idea clave para entender después cómo se elaboran los distintos vinos.","Wine is fermented grape juice.":"El vino es jugo de uva fermentado.","Pulp: juice made of water, sugar and acid.":"Pulpa: jugo de agua, azúcar y ácido.","Wine regions closer to the poles have a cool climate. Germany and northern France are typical examples. Average temperatures are low and the sunshine can be weaker than nearer the Equator; in some years the grapes even struggle to ripen. In cool climates, growing white grapes is common.":"Las regiones vitícolas más cercanas a los polos tienen un clima fresco. Alemania y el norte de Francia son ejemplos típicos. Allá las temperaturas medias son bajas y el sol puede ser más débil que cerca del ecuador; algunos años a la uva incluso le cuesta madurar. En los climas frescos es habitual cultivar uvas blancas.","The step that turns grape juice into wine is called alcoholic fermentation. The workers behind it are yeast, organisms so tiny you cannot see them with the naked eye. Yeast feed on the sugar in the juice and turn it into two products: alcohol and carbon dioxide, which is a gas. In short: sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide.":"El paso que convierte el jugo de uva en vino se llama fermentación alcohólica. Sus protagonistas son las levaduras, organismos tan pequeños que no se ven a simple vista. Las levaduras se alimentan del azúcar del jugo y lo transforman en dos productos: alcohol y dióxido de carbono, que es un gas. En resumen: azúcar + levadura → alcohol + dióxido de carbono.","In most cases fermentation carries on until the yeast have used up all the sugar, which gives a dry wine. The alcohol stays in the newly made wine, while the carbon dioxide usually escapes into the air. There are exceptions, such as sweet wines and sparkling wines, which you will meet when looking at the types and styles of wine.":"En la mayoría de los casos la fermentación continúa hasta que las levaduras se han comido todo el azúcar, y el resultado es un vino seco. El alcohol se queda en el vino recién hecho, mientras que el dióxido de carbono suele escaparse al aire. Hay excepciones, como los vinos dulces o los espumosos, que vas a ver al estudiar los tipos y estilos de vino.","The amount of alcohol in a wine is usually given as alcohol by volume, shortened to abv. A wine at 10% abv means that one tenth of the liquid is alcohol. Remember the link with the vineyard: it is the sugar the grapes built up while ripening that the yeast turn into alcohol.":"La cantidad de alcohol de un vino se suele indicar como porcentaje del volumen, abreviado % vol. Un vino de 10 % vol. significa que una décima parte del líquido es alcohol. Recordá el vínculo con el viñedo: es el azúcar que la uva acumuló al madurar lo que las levaduras convierten en alcohol.","White wine is usually made from white grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed, which releases some of the juice. Straight afterwards the crushed grapes are pressed, squeezing the skins to collect the rest of the juice. The key idea is that, for white wine, the juice is separated from the skins before fermentation begins.":"El vino blanco se suele hacer con uvas blancas. Tras la vendimia, la uva se estruja para liberar parte del jugo. Justo después, la uva estrujada pasa al prensado, que aprieta las pieles y recupera el jugo restante. La idea clave es que, en el blanco, el jugo se separa de las pieles antes de que empiece la fermentación.","Yeast are then added to the juice and fermentation starts. It can take place in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels. Once fermentation is over comes maturation, when the wine rests, again either in stainless steel or in oak. The final step is bottling, after which the wine is ready to reach the table.":"A continuación se añaden levaduras al jugo y empieza la fermentación. Puede hacerse en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble. Cuando termina la fermentación llega la crianza, en la que el vino reposa, de nuevo en acero o en roble. La última etapa es el embotellado, tras el cual el vino está listo para llegar a la mesa.","A useful point for the exam: white wine can also be made from black grapes. The colour of black grapes is all in the skin, and their juice is colourless. If black grapes are pressed gently before fermentation and the skins are removed straight away, the juice obtained is suitable for making a white wine.":"Un dato útil para el examen: también se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas. El color de las uvas tintas está todo en la piel y su jugo es incoloro. Si la uva tinta se prensa con suavidad antes de la fermentación y las pieles se retiran enseguida, se obtiene un jugo adecuado para elaborar un vino blanco.","Black grape juice is colourless, so it can make white wine.":"El jugo de uva tinta es incoloro: puede dar vino blanco.","Red wine is always made from black grapes. After picking, the grapes are crushed and, unlike white wine, the juice is not separated: juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This is the big difference from white winemaking, because it is the skins that will provide the colour and the tannins.":"El vino tinto se hace siempre con uvas tintas. Tras la vendimia la uva se estruja y, a diferencia del blanco, el jugo no se separa: jugo y pieles van juntos al recipiente de fermentación. Esta es la gran diferencia con el vino blanco, porque son precisamente las pieles las que darán el color y los taninos.","Yeast are added and fermentation begins. During this stage the juice and skins are mixed thoroughly so that colour and tannin are drawn out of the skins. The more thorough the contact, the more colour and structure the wine gains. When fermentation has finished, the new red wine is drained off the skins.":"Se añaden levaduras y empieza la fermentación. Durante esta fase, el jugo y las pieles se mezclan a fondo para extraer de las pieles el color y los taninos. Cuanto más intenso es el contacto, más color y estructura gana el vino. Cuando termina la fermentación, el vino nuevo se escurre, es decir, se separa de las pieles.","Mixing juice and skins extracts colour and tannin.":"Mezclar jugo y pieles extrae color y taninos.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, and at first the method is the same as for red: the grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the vessel together, yeast are added and fermentation starts. Colour begins to move from the skins into the juice, but rosé stands out for one clear choice: the contact is kept very short.":"El rosado también se hace con uvas tintas y, al principio, el método es el mismo que el del tinto: la uva se estruja, jugo y pieles van juntos al depósito, se añaden levaduras y empieza la fermentación. El color empieza a pasar de las pieles al jugo, pero el rosado se distingue por una decisión clara: el contacto dura muy poco.","After only a few hours the juice is drained off the skins. At that point it has picked up just a pink colour, and without the skins it cannot get any darker. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. It is the time spent in contact with the skins, a few hours rather than the whole fermentation, that explains why rosé is pink rather than red.":"Tras solo unas horas, el jugo se separa de las pieles. En ese momento solo ha tomado un color rosa y, sin las pieles, ya no puede oscurecerse más. La fermentación termina entonces sin las pieles. Es el tiempo de contacto con las pieles, unas horas en lugar de toda la fermentación, lo que explica por qué el rosado es rosa y no tinto.","Only a few hours on the skins: the juice turns just pink.":"Unas horas con las pieles: el jugo solo se vuelve rosa.","The third stage is the palate: take a small sip and move it around your mouth. Here you assess five structural characteristics. Sweetness depends on how much sugar is left in the wine, and most wines are dry. Acidity makes your mouth water and gives freshness. Tannin, typical of red wines, dries the mouth.":"La tercera etapa es la boca: se toma un sorbo pequeño y se mueve por la boca. Acá se valoran cinco características estructurales. El dulzor depende del azúcar que queda en el vino, y la mayoría de los vinos son secos. La acidez hace salivar y da frescura. El tanino, típico de los tintos, seca la boca.","Fermented grape juice":"Jugo de uva fermentado","Distilled grape juice":"Jugo de uva destilado","Concentrated grape juice":"Jugo de uva concentrado","Pasteurised grape juice":"Jugo de uva pasteurizado","Wine is made by fermenting the sweet juice of grapes.":"El vino se obtiene haciendo fermentar el jugo dulce de la uva.","To make wine, grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice. Alcoholic fermentation, carried out by yeast, then turns the sugar in that juice into alcohol. Without fermentation you would simply have grape juice; distilling or concentrating the juice is not part of the basic definition of wine.":"Para hacer vino se estrujan las uvas y se libera su jugo dulce. Después, la fermentación alcohólica, gracias a las levaduras, convierte el azúcar de ese jugo en alcohol. Sin fermentación solo quedaría jugo de uva; destilar o concentrar el jugo no forma parte de la definición básica del vino.","The juice":"En el jugo","The skin is what really sets black grapes apart from white ones: it is deeply coloured and contains tannins, which leave the mouth feeling dry. The pulp, by contrast, holds the juice, made of water, sugar and acid, and it is the same colour in all grapes.":"La piel es lo que distingue de verdad las uvas tintas de las blancas: tiene un color intenso y contiene taninos, que dejan sensación de sequedad en la boca. La pulpa, en cambio, contiene el jugo, formado por agua, azúcar y ácido, y tiene el mismo color en todas las uvas.","What is the juice in the pulp mainly made of?":"¿De qué está compuesto principalmente el jugo de la pulpa?","Grape juice is mostly water, sugar and acid.":"El jugo de uva es sobre todo agua, azúcar y ácido.","The pulp is the soft part of the grape and holds the juice, which is mostly water, sugar and acid. Tannin and colour are found in the skin instead. Alcohol and carbon dioxide only appear later, when yeast ferments the sugar in the juice.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda de la uva y contiene el jugo, formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Los taninos y el color están en la piel. El alcohol y el dióxido de carbono solo aparecen más tarde, cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar del jugo.","Inside, white and black grapes look very alike: the pulp is the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. This is exactly why a red wine gets its colour from the skins, and why a white wine can even be made from black grapes if the juice is separated from the skins straight away.":"Por dentro, las uvas blancas y tintas se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color sea cual sea el de la piel. Precisamente por eso el color de un vino tinto viene de las pieles, y por eso se puede hacer incluso un vino blanco con uvas tintas si se separa el jugo de las pieles enseguida.","Warm regions, closer to the Equator, have high average temperatures and more intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably. Growing black grapes is common there. In cool regions, closer to the poles, where grapes sometimes struggle to ripen at all, white grapes are more commonly grown.":"Las regiones cálidas, más cercanas al ecuador, tienen temperaturas medias altas y un sol más intenso, así que la uva madura con regularidad. Allá es habitual cultivar uvas tintas. En las regiones frescas, donde a veces a la uva le cuesta madurar, es más frecuente cultivar uvas blancas.","Cool regions lie closer to the poles: average temperatures are low and the sunlight can be less intense than near the Equator. In especially cool years the grapes may not ripen fully. This is one reason white grapes are commonly grown there.":"Las regiones frescas están más cerca de los polos: las temperaturas medias son bajas y la luz del sol puede ser menos intensa que cerca del ecuador. En los años especialmente frescos la uva puede no llegar a madurar del todo. Por eso allá se cultivan a menudo uvas blancas.","Yeast are what turn the sugar in the juice into alcohol.":"Son las levaduras las que convierten el azúcar del jugo en alcohol.","Without yeast, grape juice would stay juice. Yeast are microscopic organisms that feed on sugar and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Oak can be used to ferment or mature wine but is not essential, and carbon dioxide is a product of fermentation, not an ingredient.":"Sin levaduras, el jugo de uva seguiría siendo jugo. Las levaduras son organismos microscópicos que se alimentan del azúcar y lo transforman en alcohol y dióxido de carbono. El roble puede usarse para fermentar o criar el vino, pero no es imprescindible; el dióxido de carbono es un producto de la fermentación, no un ingrediente.","Yeast eat the sugar in the grape juice and turn it into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Sugar is therefore the starting point, not a product. The alcohol stays in the wine, while in most cases the carbon dioxide escapes into the atmosphere during fermentation.":"Las levaduras se comen el azúcar del jugo de uva y lo transforman en alcohol y dióxido de carbono. El azúcar es, por tanto, el punto de partida, no un producto. El alcohol se queda en el vino, mientras que el dióxido de carbono, en la mayoría de los casos, se escapa a la atmósfera durante la fermentación.","For white wine, crushed grapes are pressed before the juice ferments.":"En el blanco, la uva estrujada se prensa enseguida, antes de fermentar el jugo.","For white wine the order is: crushing, pressing, fermentation, maturation and bottling. Pressing collects the juice left in the crushed grapes, so that only the juice, without the skins, goes on to ferment. Draining, by contrast, is a typical step in making red and rosé wines.":"En el blanco, el orden es: estrujado, prensado, fermentación, crianza y embotellado. El prensado recupera el jugo que queda en la uva estrujada, para que solo el jugo, sin pieles, fermente. El escurrido, en cambio, es un paso típico del tinto y del rosado.","After crushing and pressing, yeast are added to the juice. Fermentation can happen in stainless steel tanks or in oak barrels; it is the winemaker's choice. The maturation that follows can also take place in either of these two kinds of container.":"Tras el estrujado y el prensado, se añaden levaduras al jugo. La fermentación puede hacerse en depósitos de acero inoxidable o en barricas de roble: es una elección de quien elabora el vino. La crianza posterior también puede hacerse en cualquiera de estos dos tipos de recipiente.","Their juice is colourless":"Su jugo es incoloro","Colour is only in the skin; black grape juice has no colour.":"El color está solo en la piel; el jugo de la uva tinta es incoloro.","Black grapes have coloured skins but colourless juice, just like the pulp of white grapes. If they are pressed gently before fermentation and the juice is separated from the skins straight away, the colour does not pass into the juice and a white wine can be made.":"Las uvas tintas tienen la piel de color, pero su jugo es incoloro, igual que la pulpa de las uvas blancas. Si se prensan con suavidad antes de la fermentación y el jugo se separa enseguida de las pieles, el color no pasa al jugo y se puede elaborar un vino blanco.","The juice together with the skins":"El jugo junto con las pieles","The juice alone, without skins":"Solo el jugo, sin pieles","The skins alone, without juice":"Solo las pieles, sin jugo","After black grapes are crushed, juice and skins go into the fermentation vessel together. This long contact is what draws colour and tannin out of the skins. For white wine, by contrast, the juice is separated from the skins by pressing before it ferments.":"Tras estrujar las uvas tintas, el jugo y las pieles van juntos al recipiente de fermentación. Este contacto prolongado es lo que permite extraer el color y los taninos de las pieles. En el blanco, por el contrario, el jugo se separa de las pieles con el prensado antes de fermentar.","Why are juice and skins mixed thoroughly during red wine fermentation?":"¿Por qué se mezclan a fondo jugo y pieles al fermentar el tinto?","The colour and tannin of red wine are found in the skins of black grapes. By mixing the skins well with the juice during fermentation, these substances pass into the wine. That is why a red wine has deep colour and a structure that dries the mouth, while a white does not.":"El color y los taninos del vino tinto están en la piel de las uvas tintas. Al mezclar bien las pieles con el jugo durante la fermentación, estas sustancias pasan al vino. Por eso un tinto tiene un color intenso y una estructura que seca la boca, y un blanco no.","For red wine the skins stay in contact with the juice for the whole fermentation, so they give plenty of colour and tannin. Only when fermentation is over is the new wine drained off the skins. Draining after just a few hours is, by contrast, the typical technique for rosé.":"En el tinto, las pieles se quedan en contacto con el jugo durante toda la fermentación, para que cedan mucho color y tanino. Solo cuando la fermentación ha terminado se escurre el vino nuevo de las pieles. Escurrir tras unas pocas horas es, en cambio, la técnica típica del rosado.","Red wine follows this sequence: crushing the black grapes, fermenting juice and skins together, draining the new wine, pressing the skins, maturation and bottling. Starting with crushing then pressing describes white winemaking instead, where pressing happens before fermentation and only the juice is fermented.":"El tinto sigue esta secuencia: estrujado de las uvas tintas, fermentación del jugo con las pieles, escurrido del vino nuevo, prensado de las pieles, crianza y embotellado. Empezar con estrujado y luego prensado describe el blanco, en el que el prensado va antes de la fermentación.","The pink colour comes from the skins of black grapes. The juice stays in contact with the skins for only a few hours, so it picks up just a little colour; it is then separated and finishes fermenting without the skins. White grapes do not have skins coloured enough to do this.":"El color rosa viene de la piel de las uvas tintas. El jugo está en contacto con las pieles solo unas horas, así que toma muy poco color; después se separa y termina de fermentar sin las pieles. Las uvas blancas no tienen la piel lo bastante coloreada para esto.","For a rosé, when is the juice drained from the skins?":"En un rosado, ¿cuándo se separa el jugo de las pieles?","Rosé starts out like a red: black grapes are crushed and fermentation begins with the skins. After only a few hours, though, the juice is drained off while it is still just pink. Fermentation then finishes without the skins. Draining at the end of fermentation would give a red wine instead.":"El rosado empieza como un tinto: uvas tintas estrujadas y fermentación con las pieles. Pero tras solo unas horas el jugo se separa, cuando todavía es solo rosa. La fermentación termina sin las pieles. Separarlo al final de la fermentación daría, en cambio, un vino tinto.","Rosé and red are both made from black grapes, whose pulp is the same colour as that of white grapes. The colour comes from the skins: for red they stay in the juice for the whole fermentation, for rosé only for a few hours. That is why rosé stays pink.":"El rosado y el tinto se hacen con uvas tintas, cuya pulpa tiene el mismo color que la de las uvas blancas. El color viene de las pieles: en el tinto se quedan en el jugo durante toda la fermentación; en el rosado, solo unas horas. Por eso el rosado se queda rosa.","Both wines go through crushing, adding yeast, fermentation, draining, maturation and bottling. For red, however, the skins stay until fermentation ends and are then pressed to recover the wine. For rosé the juice leaves the skins after a few hours, so this final pressing does not happen.":"Ambos vinos pasan por el estrujado, las levaduras, la fermentación, el escurrido, la crianza y el embotellado. En el tinto, sin embargo, las pieles se quedan hasta el final de la fermentación y después se prensan para recuperar el vino. En el rosado el jugo deja las pieles tras unas horas, así que ese prensado final no existe.","White grapes are pressed first so only the juice ferments.":"En el blanco se prensa enseguida para fermentar solo el jugo.","For white wine the grapes are crushed and then pressed, so the juice is separated from the skins and ferments on its own. For red, fermentation happens with the skins, which are only pressed after draining. For rosé the juice is drained off the skins after a few hours, with no final pressing.":"En el blanco, la uva se estruja y luego se prensa, de modo que el jugo se separa de las pieles y fermenta solo. En el tinto, la fermentación se hace con las pieles, que solo se prensan tras el escurrido. En el rosado, el jugo se escurre de las pieles tras unas horas, sin prensado final.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice and is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. It gives wine a refreshing character: too much makes it unpleasantly sharp, too little makes it lose freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth, while body describes how much the wine fills it.":"La acidez procede directamente del jugo de uva y se reconoce con facilidad porque hace salivar. Da al vino un carácter refrescante: demasiada lo vuelve agrio y demasiado poca le quita frescura. El tanino, en cambio, seca la boca, y el cuerpo describe cuánto la llena el vino.","Tannin is typical of red wines because it comes from the skins of black grapes, which stay in contact with the juice during fermentation. It is felt more than tasted: the mouth dries out. Acidity, by contrast, makes your mouth water.":"El tanino es típico de los tintos porque procede de la piel de las uvas tintas, que se quedan en contacto con el jugo durante la fermentación. Se nota más como una sensación que como un sabor: la boca se seca. La acidez, en cambio, hace salivar.","Soft part holding the juice: water, sugar and acid. Same colour in all grapes.":"Parte blanda con el jugo: agua, azúcar y ácido. Mismo color en todas las uvas.","Yes: the juice is colourless; press gently before fermentation.":"Sí: el jugo es incoloro; se prensa con suavidad antes de fermentar.","A wine's colour depends on two things: the grape variety and the way the wine is made. There are white grapes and black grapes, but inside they look very alike: the pulp is the same colour in both and the juice has no colour. All the colour of a black grape sits in its skin, which also holds the tannins.":"El color de un vino depende de dos cosas: la variedad de uva y la forma de elaborarlo. Hay uvas blancas y uvas tintas, pero por dentro se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color en ambas y el jugo es incoloro. Todo el color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo (la piel), que además contiene los taninos.","White wines are usually made from white grapes, as in Chablis or a Riesling. Yet black grapes can also give a white wine. The trick is to separate the skins from the juice before fermentation, for example by pressing gently: since the colour lives in the skins, the juice stays pale and the finished wine is white.":"Los vinos blancos suelen elaborarse con uvas blancas, como un Chablis o un Riesling. Sin embargo, también se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas. Basta con separar los hollejos del jugo antes de la fermentación, por ejemplo con un prensado suave: como el color está en la piel, el jugo sigue claro y el vino resulta blanco.","A red wine, on the other hand, must come from black grapes. During fermentation the skins stay in the juice and are mixed in thoroughly, so they pass colour and tannin into the wine. Once fermentation is over, the new wine is drained off the skins. Rioja from Spain and Cabernet Sauvignon wines are red examples.":"Un vino tinto, en cambio, tiene que hacerse con uvas tintas. Durante la fermentación los hollejos permanecen en el jugo y se mezclan bien con él, de modo que le ceden color y tanino. Cuando termina la fermentación, el vino se separa de los hollejos. El Rioja español y los vinos de Cabernet Sauvignon son ejemplos de tintos.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, but the skin contact is short: just a few hours. The juice, by then only pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins, giving a lightly coloured wine. White Zinfandel from California is a rosé example. Rosé wines are also only rarely aged in oak.":"El rosado también procede de uvas tintas, pero el contacto con los hollejos es breve: apenas unas horas. Después el jugo, solo ligeramente rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. El resultado es un vino de color suave. El White Zinfandel de California es un ejemplo de rosado. Además, los rosados rara vez se crían en roble.","Black grape colour is in the skin; the juice is colourless":"El color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo; el jugo es incoloro","Sweetness comes from sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry: to make one, the yeast must turn all the sugar in the juice into alcohol, leaving little or none behind. Dry examples include Chablis and Sauvignon Blanc wines among whites, and Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon wines among reds.":"El dulzor depende del azúcar que queda en el vino. La mayoría de los vinos son secos: para lograrlo, las levaduras tienen que convertir en alcohol todo el azúcar del jugo, de modo que queda muy poco o nada. Son secos, por ejemplo, el Chablis y los Sauvignon Blanc entre los blancos, y el Côtes du Rhône, el Chianti y los Cabernet Sauvignon entre los tintos.","Medium-sweet wines are mostly white or rosé. There are two main ways to make them: remove the yeast before it has turned all the sugar into alcohol, or blend some unfermented grape juice into a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, are good examples.":"Los vinos de dulzor medio son sobre todo blancos o rosados. Se elaboran de dos maneras: retirando las levaduras antes de que hayan transformado todo el azúcar, o añadiendo jugo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Algunos Riesling alemanes y el White Zinfandel, el rosado californiano, son buenos ejemplos.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. Too much tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its freshness. Chablis, Chianti and wines from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir all have high acidity.":"La acidez procede directamente del jugo de uva y es lo que hace que un vino resulte refrescante. Es fácil de reconocer porque hace salivar. Demasiada acidez hace que el vino sea desagradablemente ácido; demasiado poca y pierde su frescura. El Chablis, el Chianti y los vinos de Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon y Pinot Noir tienen acidez alta.","Medium: yeast removed early, or unfermented juice added":"Medio: levaduras retiradas antes, o jugo sin fermentar añadido","Acidity: from the juice, makes the mouth water, balances sweetness":"Acidez: viene del jugo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor","Nearly all still and sparkling wines sit between 11.5% and 14% abv. A few reach 15%, while others go as low as 8%. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a French red, is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. Remember that alcohol is produced when yeast ferment sugar.":"Casi todos los vinos tranquilos y espumosos tienen entre un 11,5 % y un 14 % vol. Algunos llegan al 15 % y otros bajan hasta el 8 %. El Châteauneuf-du-Pape, tinto francés, es un ejemplo de vino con mucho alcohol; el White Zinfandel californiano, de vino con poco. Recordá que el alcohol se forma cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar.","Wine can be fermented and/or matured in oak barrels. When it is, the wood adds notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The use of oak is sometimes mentioned on the label. If you pick up these aromas alongside the fruit, it is a good clue that the wine has spent time in barrel.":"El vino puede fermentar y/o criarse en barricas de roble. En ese caso la madera aporta notas de vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro y ahumado. A veces el uso de roble aparece en la etiqueta. Si notas estos aromas junto a la fruta, es una buena pista de que el vino pasó por barrica.","Chardonnay is also used to make Champagne, where it is often blended with Pinot Noir. In short, when you meet a Chardonnay, ask two questions: was the climate cool or warm (apple and lemon, or peach and pineapple)? And did the wine see oak (vanilla or not)? The answers tell you almost everything about its style.":"La Chardonnay también se utiliza para elaborar Champagne, donde a menudo se mezcla con Pinot Noir. En resumen, ante un Chardonnay hazte dos preguntas: ¿clima fresco o cálido (manzana y limón, o melocotón y piña)? ¿Pasó por roble (vainilla o no)? Las respuestas te dicen casi todo sobre su estilo.","Here too, winemaking choices are about protecting the fruit. Pinot Grigio is usually fermented in stainless steel tanks and not matured in oak. That way it keeps its fruity flavours and its lightness: oak, with its vanilla and toasty notes, would easily cover such delicate fruit.":"También acá las decisiones de bodega sirven para proteger la fruta. El Pinot Grigio suele fermentar en depósitos de acero inoxidable y no pasa por roble. Así conserva sus sabores afrutados y su ligereza: la madera, con su vainilla y sus notas tostadas, taparía una fruta tan delicada.","Unlike Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot, Pinot Noir is not usually blended with other grapes when making red wine; producers prefer to show its pure character. There is one important exception: in Champagne, Pinot Noir is often blended with Chardonnay. There the skins are removed straight away, so the juice stays pale.":"A diferencia del Cabernet Sauvignon y del Merlot, la Pinot Noir no suele mezclarse con otras uvas cuando se hace vino tinto: se prefiere mostrar su carácter puro. Hay, sin embargo, una excepción importante: en el Champagne, la Pinot Noir se mezcla a menudo con Chardonnay. Allá los hollejos se separan enseguida y el jugo se mantiene claro.","The skins stay in the juice during fermentation":"Los hollejos se quedan en el jugo durante la fermentación","Unfermented black grape juice is added":"Se añade jugo de uva tinta sin fermentar","The pulp of white and black grapes is the same colour and the juice is colourless. To make a red wine, black grapes are used and the skins are kept in contact with the juice throughout fermentation, mixed in well, so colour and tannin pass into the wine.":"La pulpa de las uvas blancas y tintas tiene el mismo color y el jugo es incoloro. Para hacer un tinto se usan uvas tintas y se dejan los hollejos en contacto con el jugo durante toda la fermentación, mezclándolos bien: así pasan al vino el color y el tanino.","Yes, by separating skins and juice before fermentation":"Sí, separando hollejos y jugo antes de fermentar","Black grape juice is colourless, so without the skins the wine stays white.":"El jugo de la uva tinta es incoloro: sin hollejos, el vino queda blanco.","All the colour of a black grape is in its skin. If the grapes are pressed gently and the skins are separated from the juice before fermentation, the juice stays pale and makes a white wine. This same idea is what allows Pinot Noir to be used in Champagne.":"Todo el color de la uva tinta está en su piel. Si las uvas se prensan con suavidad y los hollejos se separan del jugo antes de la fermentación, el jugo sigue claro y da un vino blanco. Es la misma idea que permite usar Pinot Noir en el Champagne.","The juice sits with black grape skins for a few hours, then is drained off.":"El jugo pasa unas horas con los hollejos de uva tinta y luego se separa.","Rosé comes from black grapes, like red wine, but the skin contact lasts only a few hours. The juice, now just pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins. If the skins stayed in until the end, the result would be a red wine instead.":"El rosado procede de uvas tintas, como el tinto, pero el contacto con los hollejos dura solo unas horas. El jugo, apenas rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. Si los hollejos se quedaran hasta el final, se obtendría un vino tinto.","Unfermented grape juice is added to the wine":"Se añade jugo de uva sin fermentar","Most wines are dry: the yeast keep working until they have turned all the sugar into alcohol. The other answers describe ways of keeping sugar in the wine: removing yeast or adding juice for medium wines, and adding alcohol for sweet fortified wines.":"La mayoría de los vinos son secos: las levaduras trabajan hasta convertir todo el azúcar en alcohol. Las demás respuestas describen formas de conservar azúcar: retirar las levaduras o añadir jugo en los vinos de dulzor medio, y añadir alcohol en los fortificados dulces.","Adding unfermented grape juice to a dry wine":"Añadir jugo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco","Leaving the skins in the juice for longer":"Dejar los hollejos más tiempo en el jugo","Unfermented juice brings sugar back into an already dry wine.":"El jugo sin fermentar aporta azúcar a un vino ya seco.","There are two routes to a medium-sweet wine: remove the yeast before they have eaten all the sugar, or add unfermented grape juice to a dry wine. Skins and oak affect colour, tannin and aromas, not the level of sweetness.":"Hay dos caminos para un vino de dulzor medio: retirar las levaduras antes de que consuman todo el azúcar, o añadir jugo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Los hollejos y el roble influyen en el color, el tanino y los aromas, no en el dulzor.","Adding unfermented grape juice to the wine":"Añadir jugo de uva sin fermentar","It adds tannin and therefore more body":"Agregá tanino y, por tanto, más cuerpo","Acidity comes from the grape juice and refreshes the wine. In sweet wines it acts as a counterweight to the sugar, which is why Sauternes and sweet Rieslings have high acidity. It does not change the colour, the tannin or the alcohol level. Without it, the wine would feel heavy.":"La acidez procede del jugo de uva y refresca el vino. En los dulces hace de contrapeso al azúcar: por eso el Sauternes y los Riesling dulces tienen acidez alta. No influye en el color, el tanino ni la graduación. Sin ella, el vino resultaría pesado.","The sugar in the juice":"El azúcar del jugo","Black grapes have coloured skins that contain tannins. When red wine ferments, the skins stay in the juice and release colour and tannin. How much tannin the wine ends up with depends on the grape and the winemaking: red Bordeaux has a lot, Beaujolais very little.":"Las uvas tintas tienen hollejos coloreados que contienen taninos. Al fermentar un tinto, los hollejos permanecen en el jugo y le ceden color y tanino. La cantidad final depende de la variedad y de la elaboración: el Bordeaux tinto tiene mucho; el Beaujolais, poco.","Beaujolais is a classic example of a low-tannin red, along with some Pinot Noir wines. Red Bordeaux and Chianti, by contrast, are standard examples of high-tannin reds, and Port, a sweet red fortified wine, also has high tannins. Remember that tannin leaves the mouth feeling dry.":"El Beaujolais es un ejemplo clásico de tinto con poco tanino, como algunos Pinot Noir. El Bordeaux tinto y el Chianti, en cambio, son ejemplos típicos de tintos muy tánicos, y el Port, vino fortificado tinto y dulce, también tiene taninos altos. Recordá que el tanino deja la boca seca.","Chablis comes from the coolest area of Burgundy. There the grapes ripen less, so they stay more acidic and give green apple and lemon flavours. The result is a dry white, light to medium in body, usually with no oak. Very ripe grapes would do the opposite and give lower acidity.":"El Chablis procede de la zona más fresca de Borgoña. Allá la uva madura menos, conserva más acidez y da sabores de manzana verde y limón. El resultado es un blanco seco, de cuerpo ligero a medio, normalmente sin roble. Una uva muy madura haría lo contrario y daría menos acidez.","Champagne, the famous French sparkling wine, is made from Chardonnay and Pinot Noir, often blended together. Pinot Noir is a black grape, but its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a white wine. Merlot and Riesling are not Champagne grapes.":"El Champagne, el famoso espumoso francés, se elabora con Chardonnay y Pinot Noir, a menudo mezcladas. La Pinot Noir es una uva tinta, pero su jugo es incoloro: si se separan enseguida los hollejos, se obtiene vino blanco. Merlot y Riesling no son uvas del Champagne.","Pinot Grigio usually makes dry, light-bodied wines with medium to high acidity and simple pear and lemon flavours. The other descriptions fit other wines: Sauternes (sweet, apricot and honey), an oaked warm-climate Chardonnay, and White Zinfandel. Think of it as a simple, fresh and easy white.":"El Pinot Grigio suele dar vinos secos, de cuerpo ligero, con acidez media a alta y sabores sencillos de pera y limón. Las otras descripciones encajan con otros vinos: el Sauternes (dulce, albaricoque y miel), un Chardonnay cálido con roble y el White Zinfandel. Pensá en un blanco sencillo y fresco.","Unfermented juice is added":"Se añade jugo sin fermentar","Of the four key black grapes, only Pinot Noir goes into Champagne, where it is often blended with Chardonnay. Although it is a black grape, its juice is colourless, so removing the skins straight away gives a pale base wine. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon and Syrah are not Champagne grapes.":"De las cuatro grandes tintas, solo la Pinot Noir entra en el Champagne, donde a menudo se mezcla con Chardonnay. Aunque es una uva tinta, su jugo es incoloro: si se separan enseguida los hollejos, se obtiene una base clara. Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon y Syrah no son uvas del Champagne.","Warm climates ripen grapes well, so black grapes are commonly grown there.":"En climas cálidos la uva madura bien: allá es habitual cultivar uvas tintas.","Comes from the juice, makes the mouth water, refreshes and balances sweetness.":"Viene del jugo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor."}};
